translate chinese strings:

    old "What? This isn't what I think it is, right?"
    new "What? This isn't what I think it is, right?\n什么？这不会就是我想的那回事吧？"

    old "Oh, it's exactly what you're thinking, [protag]."
    new "Oh, it's exactly what you're thinking, [protag].\n哦，正是你想的那回事，[protag]。"

    old "Nuala giggles happily and then presses up against me. Her eyelashes flutter before she closes her eyes and moves in for a kiss."
    new "Nuala giggles happily and then presses up against me. Her eyelashes flutter before she closes her eyes and moves in for a kiss.\nNuala开心地笑着，然后紧紧贴到我身上。她的睫毛颤动着，随后她闭上眼睛，凑过来索吻。"

    old "Seconds later, we're on the ground exchanging passionate kisses wherever our lips find purchase as a wild beast rests only a few meters away from us."
    new "Seconds later, we're on the ground exchanging passionate kisses wherever our lips find purchase as a wild beast rests only a few meters away from us.\n几秒之后，我们已双双倒地，唇齿交缠，热烈拥吻，而几米之外，一头野兽正静静地伏着。"

    old "If she were so inclined, Sheeba could jump on us and kill us in a instant. And maybe that dark thought makes the whole situation that more intense. It's a strangely erotic sensation that I've never felt before. Thanks to Nuala, this is a night I won't forget anytime soon."
    new "If she were so inclined, Sheeba could jump on us and kill us in a instant. And maybe that dark thought makes the whole situation that more intense. It's a strangely erotic sensation that I've never felt before. Thanks to Nuala, this is a night I won't forget anytime soon.\n如果她乐意，Sheeba随时能扑过来，一瞬间把我们撕碎。也许正是这个阴暗的念头，让眼前这一切更显炽烈。那是我从未体验过的奇异快感。多亏了Nuala，这个夜晚我一时半会儿都不会忘。"

    old "I'm having trouble sleeping tonight."
    new "I'm having trouble sleeping tonight.\n今晚我难以入眠。"

    old "I can't stop thinking about the upcoming mission. Only a few more days and we'll be face to face with the most dangerous creatures residing in N'Mar."
    new "I can't stop thinking about the upcoming mission. Only a few more days and we'll be face to face with the most dangerous creatures residing in N'Mar.\n我满脑子都是即将到来的任务。再过几天，我们就要正面面对栖居在N'Mar里的最危险的生物了。"

    old "We've completed difficult missions before, but that does little to ease my mind. This one is different. It will be our last mission and our most challenging one yet."
    new "We've completed difficult missions before, but that does little to ease my mind. This one is different. It will be our last mission and our most challenging one yet.\n我们以前也完成过艰难的任务，但那并不能让我安心多少。这一次不一样。这将是我们最后一项任务，也是迄今最具挑战的一项。"

    old "I fear for the safety of my companions-- Nuala in particular. Sure, she can handle herself, but if I lost her..."
    new "I fear for the safety of my companions-- Nuala in particular. Sure, she can handle herself, but if I lost her...\n我担心同伴们的安危——尤其是Nuala。当然，她能照顾好自己，可要是我失去了她……"

    old "You don't need to be afraid, my love. Not for me or any of your other companions. Everything will be fine."
    new "You don't need to be afraid, my love. Not for me or any of your other companions. Everything will be fine.\n你不必害怕，我的爱人。不必为我，也不必为你其他的同伴。一切都会好起来的。"

    old "I see Nuala. It's the first time we visited Grimoire together. I remember all the details clearly. The sounds, the light, her gestures..."
    new "I see Nuala. It's the first time we visited Grimoire together. I remember all the details clearly. The sounds, the light, her gestures...\n我看见了Nuala。那是我们第一次一起造访Grimoire。所有的细节我都记得清清楚楚。那声音、那光线、她的举止……"

    old "Is this a dream? Yes. Yes, it must be."
    new "Is this a dream? Yes. Yes, it must be.\n这是梦吗？是的。是的，一定是梦。"

    old "It is a dream. Or, maybe it's magic."
    new "It is a dream. Or, maybe it's magic.\n这是梦。又或者，是魔法。"

    old "I'm afraid, Nuala. For the first time in my life..."
    new "I'm afraid, Nuala. For the first time in my life...\n我害怕了，Nuala。我这辈子第一次……"

    old "For the first time in your life, huh? Oh, [protag], the fearless one!"
    new "For the first time in your life, huh? Oh, [protag], the fearless one!\n你这辈子第一次害怕，嗯？哦，[protag]，你这个天不怕地不怕的人！"

    old "I didn't mean it that way! Okay, I admit it. I've been afraid before-- many times. But... I've never feared losing someone important. I've feared for myself, for my own safety. I've felt fear when I was facing dangerous foes."
    new "I didn't mean it that way! Okay, I admit it. I've been afraid before-- many times. But... I've never feared losing someone important. I've feared for myself, for my own safety. I've felt fear when I was facing dangerous foes.\n我不是那个意思！好吧，我承认。我以前也害怕过——很多次。可是……我从没害怕过失去重要的人。我害怕的是自己，是自己的安危。面对危险敌人时，我也感到过恐惧。"

    old "But I've never had this feeling before. The fear of losing another person-- someone who is now a very important part of my life, a part of me... I..."
    new "But I've never had this feeling before. The fear of losing another person-- someone who is now a very important part of my life, a part of me... I...\n但我从未有过现在这种感觉。害怕失去另一个人——一个如今已成为我生命中极重要一部分的人，一个属于我的一部分……我……"

    old "Suddenly, I get another flashback. Now Nuala is eating a loaf of sweet bread, exactly like that day."
    new "Suddenly, I get another flashback. Now Nuala is eating a loaf of sweet bread, exactly like that day.\n突然间，我又闪过一段回忆。此刻Nuala正吃着一块甜面包，和那天一模一样。"

    old "Except that this time... she's eating it completely naked!"
    new "Except that this time... she's eating it completely naked!\n只不过这一次……她是一丝不挂地在吃！"

    old "So this is how you imagine me, huh? You little pig."
    new "So this is how you imagine me, huh? You little pig.\n原来你就是这么想象我的，嗯？你这头小色猪。"

    old "Ehm, it's only a dream!"
    new "Ehm, it's only a dream!\n呃，这只是个梦！"

    old "And she looks so lovely, exactly like that day. I think that was the moment that I truly fell in love with her."
    new "And she looks so lovely, exactly like that day. I think that was the moment that I truly fell in love with her.\n她看起来那么动人，和那天一模一样。我想，正是那一刻，我真正爱上了她。"

    old "I continue staring, watching as she gently presses her succulent lips against the loaf of sweet bread."
    new "I continue staring, watching as she gently presses her succulent lips against the loaf of sweet bread.\n我继续凝视着，看她轻轻地把那丰润的嘴唇贴到甜面包上。"

    old "What are you thinking, my love?"
    new "What are you thinking, my love?\n你在想什么，我的爱人？"

    old "The way you're eating that bread..."
    new "The way you're eating that bread...\n你吃面包的样子……"

    old "Hm? Like this?"
    new "Hm? Like this?\n嗯？像这样？"

    old "She smiles and slowly runs her tongue along the bread's surface, keeping her eyes fixed on me as she waits for my reaction."
    new "She smiles and slowly runs her tongue along the bread's surface, keeping her eyes fixed on me as she waits for my reaction.\n她微笑着，缓缓把舌头沿着面包表面舔过，眼睛始终盯着我，等着看我的反应。"

    old "As I feel the heat rise in my face, she lets out a slight moan."
    new "As I feel the heat rise in my face, she lets out a slight moan.\n我感到脸上发烫，她轻轻呻吟了一声。"

    old "If my mind wasn't thinking dirty thoughts before, it definitely is now."
    new "If my mind wasn't thinking dirty thoughts before, it definitely is now.\n就算刚才我的脑子还没往歪处想，现在也肯定在想了。"

    old "If you get that excited watching me eat bread, then I can't wait to see how excited you'll get when I--"
    new "If you get that excited watching me eat bread, then I can't wait to see how excited you'll get when I--\n看我吃个面包你都能这么兴奋，那我都等不及想看看，等我——的时候你会多兴奋。"

    old "Wh-woah!"
    new "Wh-woah!\n哇、哇哦！"

    old "Ah. Hello, [protag]."
    new "Ah. Hello, [protag].\n啊。你好，[protag]。"

    old "W-what are you doing here? Where I am? You were eating bread and-"
    new "W-what are you doing here? Where I am? You were eating bread and-\n你、你在这儿做什么？我这是在哪儿？你刚才在吃面包，然后——"

    old "Sorry, it looks like I woke you up. And what's this about me eating bread?"
    new "Sorry, it looks like I woke you up. And what's this about me eating bread?\n抱歉，看来是我把你吵醒了。你说我吃面包是怎么回事？"

    old "Ahem, nothing...But Nuala, you need to stop sneaking into my bedroom like this!"
    new "Ahem, nothing...But Nuala, you need to stop sneaking into my bedroom like this!\n咳咳，没什么……不过Nuala，你别老这样偷偷溜进我的卧室！"

    old "Sorry, [protag]. I didn't mean to wake you up."
    new "Sorry, [protag]. I didn't mean to wake you up.\n抱歉，[protag]。我不是有意吵醒你的。"

    old "She moves closer, inviting herself under my blankets. I feel the warmth of her body against my naked skin."
    new "She moves closer, inviting herself under my blankets. I feel the warmth of her body against my naked skin.\n她凑得更近，自顾自地钻进我的被窝。我感受到她的体温贴着我裸露的皮肤。"

    old "I couldn't sleep, so I came here. I apologize for interrupting the nice dream you seemed to be having."
    new "I couldn't sleep, so I came here. I apologize for interrupting the nice dream you seemed to be having.\n我睡不着，就过来了。很抱歉打断了你似乎正做着的那个好梦。"

    old "It, um.... It was a dream about you. Haha, it's a bit embarrassing, actually."
    new "It, um.... It was a dream about you. Haha, it's a bit embarrassing, actually.\n它，呃……那是个关于你的梦。哈哈，其实还挺难为情的。"

    old "Ooh? Then I definitely want to know more. Tell me everything, [protag]. But first..."
    new "Ooh? Then I definitely want to know more. Tell me everything, [protag]. But first...\n哦？那我更要听个仔细了。把一切都告诉我，[protag]。不过，先……"

    old "She starts kissing me and I kiss her back. A second later, she is on top of me, pushing my hands down into the pillow. I let her do as she wishes, quickly getting swept up in the passion of the act myself."
    new "She starts kissing me and I kiss her back. A second later, she is on top of me, pushing my hands down into the pillow. I let her do as she wishes, quickly getting swept up in the passion of the act myself.\n她开始吻我，我也回吻她。下一秒，她已跨坐在我身上，把我的双手按进枕头里。我任由她为所欲为，很快自己也被这激情席卷其中。"

    old "I'll tell her about the dream at some point, but there's no rush..."
    new "I'll tell her about the dream at some point, but there's no rush...\n我迟早会把这梦告诉她，不过不急……"

    old "As I arrive at the docks, I'm immediately struck by how different the sea is from the freshwater lakes and rivers I've seen before. The air is thick with humidity, and the sea's salty aroma fills my nose."
    new "As I arrive at the docks, I'm immediately struck by how different the sea is from the freshwater lakes and rivers I've seen before. The air is thick with humidity, and the sea's salty aroma fills my nose.\n一到码头，我就立刻被大海与以往见过的淡水湖、河流之间的巨大差异所震撼。空气里满是潮气，海水的咸腥味扑鼻而来。"

    old "I spot a man at the end of a dock wearing what looks like a captain's hat. He's barking orders and gesturing wildly. I wait for a moment to interrupt him."
    new "I spot a man at the end of a dock wearing what looks like a captain's hat. He's barking orders and gesturing wildly. I wait for a moment to interrupt him.\n我在码头尽头看到一个人，戴着一顶船长帽。他正扯着嗓子发号施令，手舞足蹈。我等他忙完才上前打断。"

    old "Excuse me..."
    new "Excuse me...\n打扰一下……"

    old "I'm here as a representative of the council of Grimoire. I was hoping to speak to someone in a strategic advisory role."
    new "I'm here as a representative of the council of Grimoire. I was hoping to speak to someone in a strategic advisory role.\n我是作为Grimoire议会的代表来的。我希望能跟一位担任战略顾问的人谈谈。"

    old "That would be me, I think. What is it that you're looking for?"
    new "That would be me, I think. What is it that you're looking for?\n我想那个人就是我了。你想打听什么？"

    old "It's regarding the blight of N'Mar."
    new "It's regarding the blight of N'Mar.\n是关于N'Mar的瘟疫。"

    old "Ah, so you're the one. I've heard someone was assembling an army. So what is it that brings you here?"
    new "Ah, so you're the one. I've heard someone was assembling an army. So what is it that brings you here?\n啊，原来就是你。我听说有人在集结一支军队。那么，是什么风把你吹到这儿来的？"

    old "The thought had occurred to me that the castle itself is on a peninsula. I was wondering if an assault by sea might be practical."
    new "The thought had occurred to me that the castle itself is on a peninsula. I was wondering if an assault by sea might be practical.\n我想到过，城堡本身就坐落在一个半岛上。我在想，从海上进攻是否可行。"

    old "Ah, I can see how you might think that, looking at a map. Sadly, I don't think our naval vessels will be of much use to you."
    new "Ah, I can see how you might think that, looking at a map. Sadly, I don't think our naval vessels will be of much use to you.\n啊，看了地图，我能理解你为什么会这么想。可惜，我觉得我们的海军舰艇对你帮不上多大忙。"

    old "The waters around N'Mar are treacherous, you see. The water around them is shallow and rocky. You might be able to maneuver through those waters with a fishing boat, or even a clipper, but a navy combat vessel is right out."
    new "The waters around N'Mar are treacherous, you see. The water around them is shallow and rocky. You might be able to maneuver through those waters with a fishing boat, or even a clipper, but a navy combat vessel is right out.\n你瞧，N'Mar周围的水域凶险得很。那片水域又浅又多礁石。你也许能开渔船、甚至快帆船穿过去，但海军的战舰就完全不行了。"

    old "That's all of your military-class vessels?"
    new "That's all of your military-class vessels?\n这就是你们所有的军用级舰艇了？"

    old "The captain shakes his head."
    new "The captain shakes his head.\n船长摇了摇头。"

    old "It wouldn't make sense for us to construct ships specifically to target an area like N'Mar. Most naval combat takes place on the open sea, or coastal towns that are designed specifically to accommodate ships."
    new "It wouldn't make sense for us to construct ships specifically to target an area like N'Mar. Most naval combat takes place on the open sea, or coastal towns that are designed specifically to accommodate ships.\n专门造针对N'Mar那种区域的船，对我们来说说不通。大多数海战都发生在开阔海域，或是那些专为停靠船只而建的沿海城镇。"

    old "Besides, we don't have a very large standing navy at the moment. Most of what we do is escorting merchant ships. In times of war, this is more critical, but in times of peace, it's mostly just piracy that we deal with. And pirates are peanuts compared to even a small naval battleship."
    new "Besides, we don't have a very large standing navy at the moment. Most of what we do is escorting merchant ships. In times of war, this is more critical, but in times of peace, it's mostly just piracy that we deal with. And pirates are peanuts compared to even a small naval battleship.\n此外，我们目前也没有一支庞大的常备海军。我们做的大多是护送商船。战时这事更加要紧，但和平时期，我们要对付的主要就是海盗。而海盗，跟哪怕最小型的海军战舰相比，都不过是小菜一碟。"

    old "So there aren't any military ships small enough to navigate those waters?"
    new "So there aren't any military ships small enough to navigate those waters?\n所以，没有任何军舰小到能在那片水域航行？"

    old "No sir. I wish I could help, but there just isn't any way we could support you with our existing vessels, and constructing a vessel designed specifically for that task would take months, not to mention the fact that you'd need to find a crew willing to embark on what would be, to be frank, a suicide mission."
    new "No sir. I wish I could help, but there just isn't any way we could support you with our existing vessels, and constructing a vessel designed specifically for that task would take months, not to mention the fact that you'd need to find a crew willing to embark on what would be, to be frank, a suicide mission.\n没有，先生。我也希望能帮上忙，但用我们现有的船只，实在没法支持你。而专门为这任务造一艘船，得花上好几个月，更别提你还得找到一船愿意出发的人——说白了，那可是一趟自杀任务。"

    old "No ma'am. I wish I could help, but there just isn't any way we could support you with our existing vessels, and constructing a vessel designed specifically for that task would take months, not to mention the fact that you'd need to find a crew willing to embark on what would be, to be frank, a suicide mission."
    new "No ma'am. I wish I could help, but there just isn't any way we could support you with our existing vessels, and constructing a vessel designed specifically for that task would take months, not to mention the fact that you'd need to find a crew willing to embark on what would be, to be frank, a suicide mission.\n没有，女士。我也希望能帮上忙，但用我们现有的船只，实在没法支持你。而专门为这任务造一艘船，得花上好几个月，更别提你还得找到一船愿意出发的人——说白了，那可是一趟自杀任务。"

    old "What do you mean, 'suicide mission?'"
    new "What do you mean, 'suicide mission?'\n你说的“自杀任务”是什么意思？"

    old "The waters around N'Mar are as choppy as hell itself. Even with a properly-sized vessel, you'd be hard-pressed to find a man willing to brave the elements. And that's completely setting aside the question of what's waiting for you on the other side. How many men do you figure would survive the waters only to be done in by the ghouls of that place?"
    new "The waters around N'Mar are as choppy as hell itself. Even with a properly-sized vessel, you'd be hard-pressed to find a man willing to brave the elements. And that's completely setting aside the question of what's waiting for you on the other side. How many men do you figure would survive the waters only to be done in by the ghouls of that place?\nN'Mar周围的水域颠簸得跟地狱一样。就算船的大小合适，你也很难找到一个愿意冒这种险的人。这还没算上对岸等着你的会是什么。你觉得有多少人能活着穿过那片水域，最后却栽在那地方的食尸鬼手里？"

    old "I've heard tale of ghouls capable of floating just below the surface until they find a ship to latch onto. They can't swim, or so story says, but they don't breathe either, which makes them a phantom menace in the water."
    new "I've heard tale of ghouls capable of floating just below the surface until they find a ship to latch onto. They can't swim, or so story says, but they don't breathe either, which makes them a phantom menace in the water.\n我听说过一种食尸鬼，能贴着水面下方漂浮，直到发现一艘可以攀附的船。它们不会游泳——至少传说是这么说的——但它们也不用呼吸，这让它们成了水里的幽灵般威胁。"

    old "My willingness aside, it's just not something that we're capable of doing, even if we wanted to. You'd need a smaller combat vessel."
    new "My willingness aside, it's just not something that we're capable of doing, even if we wanted to. You'd need a smaller combat vessel.\n撇开我的意愿不谈，就算我们想帮，这也不是我们能力所及的事。你需要一艘更小型的战斗舰船。"

    old "I see. Thanks for your time."
    new "I see. Thanks for your time.\n我明白了。多谢你抽空。"

    old "I wish I could be more helpful. I think all I can do at this point is wish you good luck."
    new "I wish I could be more helpful. I think all I can do at this point is wish you good luck.\n但愿我能帮上更多。我想此刻我能做的，只有祝你好运。"

    old "I walk off the dock with a feeling of dejection in my chest."
    new "I walk off the dock with a feeling of dejection in my chest.\n我走下码头，心中满是沮丧。"

    old "Excuse me."
    new "Excuse me.\n打扰一下。"

    old "I couldn't help but overhear your conversation just now."
    new "I couldn't help but overhear your conversation just now.\n刚才你们的谈话，我不小心听到了。"

    old "You 'just happened to overhear?' Sounds a bit suspicious to me, are you sure you weren't eavesdropping?"
    new "You 'just happened to overhear?' Sounds a bit suspicious to me, are you sure you weren't eavesdropping?\n你“碰巧听到”？听起来有点可疑啊，你确定你不是在偷听？"

    old "You looked like an interesting person, so I thought I'd stalk you for a bit. In the course of stalking you, I just happened to overhear a conversation you were having. Nothing suspicious about that, right?"
    new "You looked like an interesting person, so I thought I'd stalk you for a bit. In the course of stalking you, I just happened to overhear a conversation you were having. Nothing suspicious about that, right?\n你看着是个有趣的人，所以我想跟踪你一小会儿。就在跟踪你的过程中，我碰巧听到了你们的一段谈话。这没什么可疑的吧？"

    old "I must say, I'm flattered. It's not every day a man comes up to you and admits to stalking you."
    new "I must say, I'm flattered. It's not every day a man comes up to you and admits to stalking you.\n我真是受宠若惊，不是每天都有男人走到你面前，承认自己在跟踪你的。"

    old "Well, I guess that means you can count this day as one of the extraordinary ones."
    new "Well, I guess that means you can count this day as one of the extraordinary ones.\n嗯，我想这意味着你可以把今天算作不寻常的日子之一了。"

    old "What's so special about today?"
    new "What's so special about today?\n今天有什么特别之处？"

    old "Well, it's the day you met Jasper. That's my name, in case you didn't infer."
    new "Well, it's the day you met Jasper. That's my name, in case you didn't infer.\n嗯，今天是你遇见Jasper的日子。那是我的名字，万一你没猜出来的话。"

    old "A pleasure to meet you, Jasper."
    new "A pleasure to meet you, Jasper.\n幸会，Jasper。"

    old "Likewise, [protag]."
    new "Likewise, [protag].\n彼此彼此，[protag]。"

    old "You know my name?"
    new "You know my name?\n你知道我的名字？"

    old "Of course I do. I wouldn't be a very good stalker if I wasn't. You're [protag] of Grimoire, and you're representing the council of Grimoire. You're looking for a way to assault N'Mar by sea."
    new "Of course I do. I wouldn't be a very good stalker if I wasn't. You're [protag] of Grimoire, and you're representing the council of Grimoire. You're looking for a way to assault N'Mar by sea.\n我当然知道。要不是这样，我也算不上称职的跟踪者了。你是Grimoire的[protag]，代表Grimoire议会而来。你在找一条从海上攻打N'Mar的路子。"

    old "Most men wouldn't start a conversation with someone by admitting to stalking to them."
    new "Most men wouldn't start a conversation with someone by admitting to stalking to them.\n大多数男人不会一上来就承认自己在跟踪对方，以此开启谈话。"

    old "Well, I'm not most men."
    new "Well, I'm not most men.\n嗯，我不是大多数男人。"

    old "I don't even know your name."
    new "I don't even know your name.\n可我连你的名字都不知道。"

    old "I'm Jasper. And you're [protag], as I'm sure you know I know."
    new "I'm Jasper. And you're [protag], as I'm sure you know I know.\n我是Jasper。而你是[protag]，我很确定你知道我晓得这一点。"

    old "I do know, but couldn't you at least pretend you don't already know everything about me?"
    new "I do know, but couldn't you at least pretend you don't already know everything about me?\n我是知道，可你就不能至少假装一下，别对我的一切都了如指掌吗？"

    old "Oh, I wouldn't say I know everything about you. Just that you're [protag], representative of Grimoire's council, looking for a way to assault N'Mar by sea."
    new "Oh, I wouldn't say I know everything about you. Just that you're [protag], representative of Grimoire's council, looking for a way to assault N'Mar by sea.\n哦，我可不敢说对你的一切都了如指掌。我不过知道你是[protag]，是Grimoire议会的代表，正想找条从海上攻打N'Mar的路子罢了。"

    old "Is that all you overheard?"
    new "Is that all you overheard?\n你偷听到的就这些？"

    old "You also seem to be a very thoughtful person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it."
    new "You also seem to be a very thoughtful person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it.\n你看起来还是个很体贴周到的人。这倒不是我偷听到的，是我自己推断出来的。"

    old "You also seem to be a very patient person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it."
    new "You also seem to be a very patient person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it.\n你看起来还是个很有耐心的人。这也不是我偷听到的，只是我碰巧推断出来的。"

    old "You also seem to be a very strong-willed person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it."
    new "You also seem to be a very strong-willed person. That, I didn't overhear, I just happened to infer it.\n你看起来还是个意志坚定的人。这也不是我偷听到的，只是我碰巧推断出来的。"

    old "You also seem to be a very expressive person. That's just my own observation, not something that was mentioned in the conversation."
    new "You also seem to be a very expressive person. That's just my own observation, not something that was mentioned in the conversation.\n你看起来还是个感情丰富的人。这是我自己的观察，可不是谈话里提到的。"

    old "But as interesting as you are as a person, I think the most important thing I overheard is that you're in need of a ship. A ship ready for combat, small enough to navigate the rocky crag that surrounds the N'Mar peninsula."
    new "But as interesting as you are as a person, I think the most important thing I overheard is that you're in need of a ship. A ship ready for combat, small enough to navigate the rocky crag that surrounds the N'Mar peninsula.\n不过，无论你这个人多有意思，我觉得我偷听到的最重要的一点是：你需要一艘船。一艘能作战、小到能穿过环绕N'Mar半岛的嶙峋礁石区的船。"

    old "What about that do you find so interesting?"
    new "What about that do you find so interesting?\n这又有什么让你觉得那么有意思的？"

    old "I happen to know of such a ship."
    new "I happen to know of such a ship.\n我碰巧知道这样一艘船。"

    old "And yet the captain didn't know of it."
    new "And yet the captain didn't know of it.\n可那位船长却不知道。"

    old "[protag], there are certain things that the navy doesn't notice, and some things that they choose to remain willfully ignorant of."
    new "[protag], there are certain things that the navy doesn't notice, and some things that they choose to remain willfully ignorant of.\n[protag]，有些事海军注意不到，还有些事，他们选择故意视而不见。"

    old "Let's just say that this ship I'm talking about, most of what it does isn't legal, strictly speaking."
    new "Let's just say that this ship I'm talking about, most of what it does isn't legal, strictly speaking.\n这么说吧，我说的这艘船，严格来讲，干的营生大多不合法。"

    old "I'm don't know what you take me as, Jasper, but if you're suggesting what I think you are, I'm not interested."
    new "I'm don't know what you take me as, Jasper, but if you're suggesting what I think you are, I'm not interested.\n我不知道你把我当成什么人了，Jasper，但如果你暗示的是我所想的那种事，那我没兴趣。"

    old "Suit yourself. I'm not looking to goad or pressure you into anything. But if you do change your mind, pay me a visit. I hang around these docks often."
    new "Suit yourself. I'm not looking to goad or pressure you into anything. But if you do change your mind, pay me a visit. I hang around these docks often.\n随你。我并不想怂恿你或逼你做什么。不过，要是你改了主意，就来找我。我常在这一带码头转悠。"

    old "You expect me to come back here looking for you?"
    new "You expect me to come back here looking for you?\n你要我回到这儿来找你？"

    old "No, I just expect you to come back. Serendipitously meeting people is my area of expertise, so you can leave that part to me."
    new "No, I just expect you to come back. Serendipitously meeting people is my area of expertise, so you can leave that part to me.\n不，我只是期望你会回来。与人不期而遇正是我的专长，那部分就交给我吧。"

    old "Jasper turns and begins to walk away."
    new "Jasper turns and begins to walk away.\nJasper转身，开始走开。"

    old "Have a nice day, [protag]. Hope to see you back here again."
    new "Have a nice day, [protag]. Hope to see you back here again.\n祝你今天愉快，[protag]。希望还能在这儿见到你。"

    old "I'm not in a position to refuse offers of assistance, Jasper. What exactly is it that you're offering me?"
    new "I'm not in a position to refuse offers of assistance, Jasper. What exactly is it that you're offering me?\n我没资格拒绝别人的援手，Jasper。你到底想给我什么？"

    old "I'm not exactly in a position to make deals. But I can offer you an introduction with someone who can."
    new "I'm not exactly in a position to make deals. But I can offer you an introduction with someone who can.\n我其实也没资格谈什么交易。不过，我可以把你介绍给一个能谈的人。"

    old "I'd like to meet them."
    new "I'd like to meet them.\n我想见见他们。"

    old "Today's not a good day. They're all out at sea right now. But come back some other day, before dusk. I'll be waiting when you're ready."
    new "Today's not a good day. They're all out at sea right now. But come back some other day, before dusk. I'll be waiting when you're ready.\n今天日子不合适。他们这会儿都出海去了。改天再来吧，赶在黄昏前。你准备好了，我就在这儿等着。"

    old "Alright, Jasper."
    new "Alright, Jasper.\n好吧，Jasper。"

    old "I arrive at the docks just as the sun is cresting the horizon. I scan around, but don't see anything."
    new "I arrive at the docks just as the sun is cresting the horizon. I scan around, but don't see anything.\n太阳刚从地平线探出头时，我到了码头。我四下张望，却什么也没看到。"

    old "Jasper! You startled me."
    new "Jasper! You startled me.\nJasper！你吓我一跳。"

    old "Just one of my many talents."
    new "Just one of my many talents.\n这不过是我众多本事中的一项。"

    old "I'm surprised to see you back here, [protag]. Didn't you say something about not doing business with criminals?"
    new "I'm surprised to see you back here, [protag]. Didn't you say something about not doing business with criminals?\n看到你回到这儿，我很意外，[protag]。你不是说过什么不跟罪犯做生意之类的话吗？"

    old "Well, I'm still in need of a ship. You offered to set me up with one. I thought I should at least find out what the offer is before I decline it."
    new "Well, I'm still in need of a ship. You offered to set me up with one. I thought I should at least find out what the offer is before I decline it.\n嗯，我仍需要一艘船。你主动提出给我牵线。我想至少该先弄清楚是什么提议，再决定要不要拒绝。"

    old "Well, I'm glad you came back. I'm not the one to make the offer, though. I'm not exactly what you'd describe as the brains of the operation."
    new "Well, I'm glad you came back. I'm not the one to make the offer, though. I'm not exactly what you'd describe as the brains of the operation.\n嗯，很高兴你回来了。不过，开价的人不是我。我算不上这桩生意里出谋划策的那号人物。"

    old "So what does that make you? The slimy, slick hands of the operation?"
    new "So what does that make you? The slimy, slick hands of the operation?\n那你算什么？这桩生意里油滑圆滑的“手”？"

    old "That's a good way to describe what I do."
    new "That's a good way to describe what I do.\n这倒是对我活计的好形容。"

    old "I need you to come with me."
    new "I need you to come with me.\n我需要你跟我来。"

    old "I follow Jasper to the end of the dock, where he leads me to a small rowboat."
    new "I follow Jasper to the end of the dock, where he leads me to a small rowboat.\n我跟着Jasper走到码头尽头，他把我领到一艘小划艇前。"

    old "You want me to get into that thing?"
    new "You want me to get into that thing?\n你要我坐上那玩意儿？"

    old "That's how we're getting to our next destination, yes."
    new "That's how we're getting to our next destination, yes.\n没错，这就是我们去下一站的方式。"

    old "I get into the boat and sit across from Jasper."
    new "I get into the boat and sit across from Jasper.\n我上了船，坐在Jasper对面。"

    old "Alright. You want me to take an oar?"
    new "Alright. You want me to take an oar?\n好了。要我搭把手划桨吗？"

    old "No need, I'm rowing. I wouldn't be a very good host if I expected you to do that labor. And I'm the one who knows where we're going."
    new "No need, I'm rowing. I wouldn't be a very good host if I expected you to do that labor. And I'm the one who knows where we're going.\n不必，我来划。要是指望你干这力气活，我这个东道主可就不称职了。再说，只有我知道要去哪儿。"

    old "Something about this makes me feel uneasy..."
    new "Something about this makes me feel uneasy...\n这事让我隐隐有些不安……"

    old "Don't worry. This boat doesn't look like much, but I've taken it out into this harbor hundreds of times before. I'll get us to our destination safe and sound."
    new "Don't worry. This boat doesn't look like much, but I've taken it out into this harbor hundreds of times before. I'll get us to our destination safe and sound.\n别担心。这船看着不怎么样，但我驾着它进出这片港湾已经不下几百回了。我会把咱们平安送到目的地。"

    old "It's not so much the size of the boat as much as the fact that I'm going out to sea, alone, with a self-professed criminal."
    new "It's not so much the size of the boat as much as the fact that I'm going out to sea, alone, with a self-professed criminal.\n倒不是船的大小，而是我要跟一个自认是罪犯的人，独自出海这件事。"

    old "Is this how people get murdered? Because this feels like how people get murdered."
    new "Is this how people get murdered? Because this feels like how people get murdered.\n人就是这样被谋害的吗？因为这感觉就像人会被人谋害的那种情形。"

    old "I see. You're worried that once we've paddled out to sea, I might attempt something...untoward."
    new "I see. You're worried that once we've paddled out to sea, I might attempt something...untoward.\n我懂了。你担心一旦我们把船划到海上，我可能会做出什么……不轨之举。"

    old "I have an idea."
    new "I have an idea.\n我有个主意。"

    old "Jasper takes out a knife. I flinch, but he presents the knife to me, handle first."
    new "Jasper takes out a knife. I flinch, but he presents the knife to me, handle first.\nJasper掏出一把刀。我本能地一缩，但他把刀柄朝我递了过来。"

    old "Take it."
    new "Take it.\n拿着。"

    old "I take the knife from Jasper. It's a nasty-looking dagger."
    new "I take the knife from Jasper. It's a nasty-looking dagger.\n我从Jasper手里接过刀。那是一把看着就凶的匕首。"

    old "Jasper gets into the rowboat and grabs hold of the oars."
    new "Jasper gets into the rowboat and grabs hold of the oars.\nJasper登上划艇，握住了桨。"

    old "You look limber enough that you could put that knife through my neck at a moment's notice, yes? And my hands are a bit busy with the oars. I'd say you have me at a disadvantage. If I try anything funny, you can just jab that knife right through my jugular."
    new "You look limber enough that you could put that knife through my neck at a moment's notice, yes? And my hands are a bit busy with the oars. I'd say you have me at a disadvantage. If I try anything funny, you can just jab that knife right through my jugular.\n你身手足够灵活，随时都能把刀捅进我脖子里，对吧？我的手又忙着划桨。我看是我处于劣势。我要敢耍花招，你尽管把刀捅进我颈动脉里。"

    old "Now, can you trust me?"
    new "Now, can you trust me?\n现在，你能信任我了吗？"

    old "You make a compelling argument."
    new "You make a compelling argument.\n你的理由很充分。"

    old "Good. Then get in."
    new "Good. Then get in.\n好。那就上船吧。"

    old "I get in after Jasper, keeping a tight grip on the knife. I don't think I'll have to use it, but I'm better off safe than sorry."
    new "I get in after Jasper, keeping a tight grip on the knife. I don't think I'll have to use it, but I'm better off safe than sorry.\n我跟着Jasper上了船，手里紧攥着那把刀。我想我大概用不上它，但小心总没坏处。"

    old "I look out over the sea. The boat rocks gently at first, but the rocking intensifies the further we get from the dock. I place both of my hands on the sides of the boat to steady myself."
    new "I look out over the sea. The boat rocks gently at first, but the rocking intensifies the further we get from the dock. I place both of my hands on the sides of the boat to steady myself.\n我望向海面。起初船只是轻轻摇晃，可离码头越远，摇晃得越厉害。我把双手撑在船舷上稳住自己。"

    old "Getting a little seasick?"
    new "Getting a little seasick?\n有点晕船了？"

    old "Just trying to keep my balance."
    new "Just trying to keep my balance.\n只是想保持平衡。"

    old "How do you feel about the sea, [protag]?"
    new "How do you feel about the sea, [protag]?\n你对大海是什么感觉，[protag]？"

    old "Personally, I feel a connection to the sea, even though I've spent most of my life on land. Something about the wide open water just seems incredibly romantic."
    new "Personally, I feel a connection to the sea, even though I've spent most of my life on land. Something about the wide open water just seems incredibly romantic.\n就我个人来说，我对大海有种亲近感，尽管我大半辈子都生活在陆地上。辽阔开阔的水面，有种说不出的浪漫。"

    old "Is it the sea that you're falling in love with, or the man you're sitting with?"
    new "Is it the sea that you're falling in love with, or the man you're sitting with?\n让你坠入爱河的，是大海，还是与你同坐的那个男人？"

    old "It's the sea. Definitely the sea."
    new "It's the sea. Definitely the sea.\n是大海。绝对是大海。"

    old "Ouch."
    new "Ouch.\n哎哟。"

    old "Nothing against you personally, Jasper. But it's hard for a single man to hold a candle to the sea when it comes to impressing and enrapturing me."
    new "Nothing against you personally, Jasper. But it's hard for a single man to hold a candle to the sea when it comes to impressing and enrapturing me.\n我对你本人没有意见，Jasper。不过，要说打动我、迷住我，一个男人可比不过大海。"

    old "You're right, I must be falling for you."
    new "You're right, I must be falling for you.\n你说得对，我一定是爱上你了。"

    old "For the sake of my ego, I'm going to presume you're not just saying that in jest. After all, two handsome men, trapped at sea in a small boat together...what could possibly be more romantic?"
    new "For the sake of my ego, I'm going to presume you're not just saying that in jest. After all, two handsome men, trapped at sea in a small boat together...what could possibly be more romantic?\n为了我这点自尊，我就当你不是在开玩笑。毕竟，两个英俊的男人一起被困在海上的小船上……还能有比这更浪漫的事吗？"

    old "Oh dear. Am I going to have to break another heart?"
    new "Oh dear. Am I going to have to break another heart?\n天哪。我这是又要伤一颗心了吗？"

    old "You do seem like the type of man who's broken a young girl's heart before."
    new "You do seem like the type of man who's broken a young girl's heart before.\n你看起来确实是那种伤过年轻姑娘心的男人。"

    old "Too many to count. I hope you won't hold it against me, as I take no pleasure in it."
    new "Too many to count. I hope you won't hold it against me, as I take no pleasure in it.\n多得数不清。希望你别因此记恨我，毕竟我从中并无乐趣。"

    old "It's not that I don't enjoy female company...but I'm what you might call a 'man's man,' in a certain sense."
    new "It's not that I don't enjoy female company...but I'm what you might call a 'man's man,' in a certain sense.\n倒不是我不喜欢女人的陪伴……只不过在某种意义上，我是你们所说的那种“男人的男人”。"

    old "Jasper offers a feeble smile."
    new "Jasper offers a feeble smile.\nJasper挤出一个无力的微笑。"

    old "Me and the sea don't have much history together. I know it well enough to say that I don't like it. The last time I was on a boat I felt sick to my stomach the entire trip."
    new "Me and the sea don't have much history together. I know it well enough to say that I don't like it. The last time I was on a boat I felt sick to my stomach the entire trip.\n我和大海没什么交情。我对它的了解，足以让我说一句：我不喜欢它。上次坐船，整个航程我胃里都翻江倒海。"

    old "Perhaps you and the sea just happened to get off on the wrong foot."
    new "Perhaps you and the sea just happened to get off on the wrong foot.\n也许你和大海只是开头就处得不对付。"

    old "It's hard to get off on the right foot when the ship's deck refuses to stay stationary."
    new "It's hard to get off on the right foot when the ship's deck refuses to stay stationary.\n当甲板不肯安安稳稳待着的时候，想开个好头可难了。"

    old "Sounds like you need to work on your sense of balance. Like anything else, learning to keep your footing on a rocking ship is an acquired skill. Practice makes perfect, don't you know."
    new "Sounds like you need to work on your sense of balance. Like anything else, learning to keep your footing on a rocking ship is an acquired skill. Practice makes perfect, don't you know.\n听起来你得练练平衡感了。跟别的本事一样，在摇晃的船上站稳脚跟也是一门要练出来的功夫。熟能生巧，你没听过吗。"

    old "I'm not really sure. I'm not what you'd call a seafaring [manwoman]. I guess we'll find out how well I take to the sea."
    new "I'm not really sure. I'm not what you'd call a seafaring [manwoman]. I guess we'll find out how well I take to the sea.\n我不太确定。我也算不上你所说的那种常年在海上漂泊的[manwoman]。看来我们会见识到我到底多能适应大海。"

    old "Well, if it puts you at ease to know, the sea doesn't care how you feel about it. What matters is how kindly the sea takes to you."
    new "Well, if it puts you at ease to know, the sea doesn't care how you feel about it. What matters is how kindly the sea takes to you.\n嗯，如果说出来能让你安心的话——大海才不在乎你对它是什么感觉。要紧的是它待你有多友善。"

    old "I'm not sure that telling someone that things are beyond their power is the best way to put them at ease."
    new "I'm not sure that telling someone that things are beyond their power is the best way to put them at ease.\n我不太确定，告诉别人事情由不得他们做主，会是让人安心的最佳方式。"

    old "Isn't it? I find that most people like letting someone else take responsibility. Followers are more common than leaders."
    new "Isn't it? I find that most people like letting someone else take responsibility. Followers are more common than leaders.\n不是吗？我发现大多数人更愿意让别人来担责。追随者比领导者更常见。"

    old "Which group do you fall into?"
    new "Which group do you fall into?\n你属于哪一类？"

    old "Oh, I'm a follower, through and through. I don't mind taking initiative from time to time, but I never had the head for bigger picture things."
    new "Oh, I'm a follower, through and through. I don't mind taking initiative from time to time, but I never had the head for bigger picture things.\n哦，我彻头彻尾是个追随者。偶尔主动挑个头我也不介意，只是我从来就没有放眼大局的头脑。"

    old "On the horizon, I spot the shape of a ship, and as we near it, I can make out the form of a black flag atop its mast. The image of a skull is imprinted on the flag."
    new "On the horizon, I spot the shape of a ship, and as we near it, I can make out the form of a black flag atop its mast. The image of a skull is imprinted on the flag.\n在地平线上，我望见了一艘船的轮廓。等我们靠近，我已能辨认出桅杆顶端一面黑旗的形状。旗上印着一个骷髅。"

    old "That's not a very inviting emblem."
    new "That's not a very inviting emblem.\n那可不是个多友好的标志。"

    old "It's not supposed to be. If you're intimidated by it, then it's serving its purpose."
    new "It's not supposed to be. If you're intimidated by it, then it's serving its purpose.\n本来就没打算友好。要是它把你唬住了，那它的目的就达到了。"

    old "Its purpose is to intimidate me?"
    new "Its purpose is to intimidate me?\n它的目的就是吓唬我？"

    old "Well, not you, specifically."
    new "Well, not you, specifically.\n嗯，不特指你。"

    old "Just what kind of an operation are you running here?"
    new "Just what kind of an operation are you running here?\n你在这儿经营的到底是哪门子营生？"

    old "Perhaps your questions are best answered by the captain. We'll be on board soon enough."
    new "Perhaps your questions are best answered by the captain. We'll be on board soon enough.\n你的问题，或许最好由船长来回答。我们很快就上船了。"

    old "As I set foot on the deck, I keep a hand on the side of the ship to keep my balance."
    new "As I set foot on the deck, I keep a hand on the side of the ship to keep my balance.\n踏上甲板时，我一只手扶着船舷以保持平衡。"

    old "Are you doing okay over there?"
    new "Are you doing okay over there?\n你那边还好吗？"

    old "Just trying to make sure I don't lose my footing."
    new "Just trying to make sure I don't lose my footing.\n只是尽量别让自己站不稳。"

    old "Within several moments, I grow accustomed to the pattern of the ship's rocking and swaying, and can take several steps forward without falling."
    new "Within several moments, I grow accustomed to the pattern of the ship's rocking and swaying, and can take several steps forward without falling.\n没过多久，我便习惯了船身摇晃摆动的节奏，能向前走几步而不致摔倒。"

    old "Jasper, who's this?"
    new "Jasper, who's this?\nJasper，这位是？"

    old "Captain! This is [protag], the one I was telling you about before."
    new "Captain! This is [protag], the one I was telling you about before.\n船长！这位就是[protag]，我先前跟您提过的那位。"

    old "Ah, yes. The [manwoman] from Grimoire. Hello, [protag]."
    new "Ah, yes. The [manwoman] from Grimoire. Hello, [protag].\n啊，是的。来自Grimoire的那位[manwoman]。你好，[protag]。"

    old "Hello, uh, captain."
    new "Hello, uh, captain.\n你好，呃，船长。"

    old "You can call me Senya. 'Captain' is how my subordinates address me, and even then, it's not even a formal title. It's what you might call a self-appointed office."
    new "You can call me Senya. 'Captain' is how my subordinates address me, and even then, it's not even a formal title. It's what you might call a self-appointed office.\n你可以叫我Senya。“船长”是我的手下对我的称呼，而且那甚至都不是什么正式头衔。算是我自封的职位吧。"

    old "What exactly are you?"
    new "What exactly are you?\n你们究竟是做什么的？"

    old "Senya gestures to the men on deck."
    new "Senya gestures to the men on deck.\nSenya朝甲板上的手下们比了比。"

    old "These are the Bastards of the Sea, and I am their captain."
    new "These are the Bastards of the Sea, and I am their captain.\n这些是Bastards of the Sea，而我是他们的船长。"

    old "Bastards of the Sea?"
    new "Bastards of the Sea?\nBastards of the Sea？"

    old "Some of us are literal bastards who never knew our fathers. Others have chosen to forsake their families for the embrace of the sea. We have no loyalty to any family or nation. We have only one love: the sea."
    new "Some of us are literal bastards who never knew our fathers. Others have chosen to forsake their families for the embrace of the sea. We have no loyalty to any family or nation. We have only one love: the sea.\n我们当中有些人是货真价实的私生子，从没见过自己的父亲。另一些人则选择抛弃家人，投入大海的怀抱。我们不效忠于任何家族或国家，我们唯一的挚爱就是：大海。"

    old "And how exactly do you maintain your livelihood?"
    new "And how exactly do you maintain your livelihood?\n那你们究竟靠什么维持生计？"

    old "That's a fair question. As we owe no loyalty to any nation, we're not shy about stealing from the rich and giving to ourselves, when the opportunity presents itself."
    new "That's a fair question. As we owe no loyalty to any nation, we're not shy about stealing from the rich and giving to ourselves, when the opportunity presents itself.\n问得公平。既然我们不欠任何国家忠诚，那么机会出现时，我们也从不羞于劫富——然后济我们自己。"

    old "But we are not mere parasites who exist only by preying on other men: we share a symbiotic relationship with the sea. Our presence discourages those who might poach whales and otherwise threaten the marine life, and in return the sea offers its bounty to us. Some days, we are pirates. Other days, we are fisherman."
    new "But we are not mere parasites who exist only by preying on other men: we share a symbiotic relationship with the sea. Our presence discourages those who might poach whales and otherwise threaten the marine life, and in return the sea offers its bounty to us. Some days, we are pirates. Other days, we are fisherman.\n但我们并不是只靠捕食他人为生的寄生虫：我们与大海是一种共生关系。有我们的存在，那些想偷猎鲸鱼、或以其他方式威胁海洋生物的人就不敢造次；作为回报，大海也把它的馈赠赐予我们。有些日子，我们是海盗；另一些日子，我们是渔夫。"

    old "If a man spends a thousand days building a bridge, and one day he murders a man, he's known as a murderer, not a bridge-builder. You may have interests other than piracy, but you are still pirates."
    new "If a man spends a thousand days building a bridge, and one day he murders a man, he's known as a murderer, not a bridge-builder. You may have interests other than piracy, but you are still pirates.\n一个人花一千天造桥，只要有一天杀了人，他就会被称为杀人犯，而不是造桥的人。你们或许在劫掠之外还有别的营生，但你们终究还是海盗。"

    old "That's a fair accusation. But words mean little to me, as you might imagine from a woman who's chosen to name her cohort 'The Bastards of the Sea.' We're well aware of what we are, [protag]."
    new "That's a fair accusation. But words mean little to me, as you might imagine from a woman who's chosen to name her cohort 'The Bastards of the Sea.' We're well aware of what we are, [protag].\n这个指控很公道。不过言辞对我意义不大，你从一个给自己的队伍取名“Bastards of the Sea”的女人身上应该也想象得到。我们很清楚自己是什么人，[protag]。"

    old "So you're more than just criminals."
    new "So you're more than just criminals.\n所以你们不只是罪犯。"

    old "Indeed we are, though the empire will likely see us as nothing but a lousy group of pirates."
    new "Indeed we are, though the empire will likely see us as nothing but a lousy group of pirates.\n确实如此，尽管在帝国眼里，我们八成不过是一帮不入流的海盗。"

    old "Still, the point stands. We have interests beyond theft. We could, if we wanted to, call you our prisoner and demand ransom from Grimoire. But I'm much more interested in meeting a mutually beneficial arrangement. You came to us for a reason, and I'm curious to hear what exactly that reason is."
    new "Still, the point stands. We have interests beyond theft. We could, if we wanted to, call you our prisoner and demand ransom from Grimoire. But I'm much more interested in meeting a mutually beneficial arrangement. You came to us for a reason, and I'm curious to hear what exactly that reason is.\n话虽如此，道理还是那个道理。我们的利益不止于偷盗。只要我们愿意，现在就可以把你当俘虏，向Grimoire索要赎金。但我更想达成一个对双方都有利的安排。你来我们这里自有原因，我很想听听，那原因究竟是什么。"

    old "Are you aware of the mist that's been covering the plains around N'Mar?"
    new "Are you aware of the mist that's been covering the plains around N'Mar?\n你知道一直笼罩着N'Mar周边平原的那片迷雾吗？"

    old "I've heard of it, yes, but the plains around N'Mar are of less interest to me than the waters around the N'Mar peninsula. That area has been shrouded in mist as well."
    new "I've heard of it, yes, but the plains around N'Mar are of less interest to me than the waters around the N'Mar peninsula. That area has been shrouded in mist as well.\n我听说过，是的，不过比起N'Mar平原，我更关心N'Mar半岛周边的水域。那片区域也同样被迷雾笼罩着。"

    old "The mist is spreading, and it carries with it N'Mar's corruption. We believe that if we don't put a stop to it, soon the entire continent will be covered with N'Mar's blight. We need to end the evil at its source. We're taking the fight directly to the front gates of N'Mar's castle."
    new "The mist is spreading, and it carries with it N'Mar's corruption. We believe that if we don't put a stop to it, soon the entire continent will be covered with N'Mar's blight. We need to end the evil at its source. We're taking the fight directly to the front gates of N'Mar's castle.\n迷雾正在蔓延，随之而来的是N'Mar的腐化。我们相信，若不止住它，整个大陆很快都会被N'Mar的瘟疫吞没。我们必须从源头终结这股邪恶。我们要把战线直接推到N'Mar城堡的大门前。"

    old "The wonderful thing about living my life at sea is that I don't have to worry about the affairs of man on land. Let the land rot, and I'll still have the water. You've explained why the mist covering N'Mar matters to you. Now explain why it should matter to me."
    new "The wonderful thing about living my life at sea is that I don't have to worry about the affairs of man on land. Let the land rot, and I'll still have the water. You've explained why the mist covering N'Mar matters to you. Now explain why it should matter to me.\n一辈子生活在海上的妙处就在于，我不用操心陆地上那些人的事。让陆地烂掉好了，反正我还有这片海。你已经解释了N'Mar的迷雾为什么对你重要。现在解释一下，它为什么该对我重要。"

    old "We're invading the castle of N'Mar. Were you to join us in the invasion, you would have the chance to help yourself to whatever spoils lie within."
    new "We're invading the castle of N'Mar. Were you to join us in the invasion, you would have the chance to help yourself to whatever spoils lie within.\n我们要攻打N'Mar的城堡。你要是加入我们，就有机会把里面的战利品随便往自己兜里装。"

    old "Now you have my interest. What riches can we expect to find, exactly?"
    new "Now you have my interest. What riches can we expect to find, exactly?\n现在你勾起我的兴趣了。我们到底能指望找到什么财富？"

    old "Who knows? But I have it on good authority that vampires have a taste for the finer things in life. They always appear to be so well-dressed."
    new "Who knows? But I have it on good authority that vampires have a taste for the finer things in life. They always appear to be so well-dressed.\n谁知道呢？不过据可靠消息，vampires可是很懂得享受生活中那些好东西的。他们看上去总是衣着光鲜。"

    old "Ha! You may be correct, [protag]."
    new "Ha! You may be correct, [protag].\n哈！也许你说得对，[protag]。"

    old "It sounds to me like all you have right now is a hunch. But I've more than once boarded a cargo ship on the hunch that it might contain something worth stealing, and my hunches are were generally right. I get the feeling that if you win at N'Mar, I'll want to be a part of that."
    new "It sounds to me like all you have right now is a hunch. But I've more than once boarded a cargo ship on the hunch that it might contain something worth stealing, and my hunches are were generally right. I get the feeling that if you win at N'Mar, I'll want to be a part of that.\n在我看来，你现在有的不过是直觉。可我不止一次凭着一股直觉登上一艘货船，觉得里面也许有值得一偷的东西，而我的直觉一般都挺准。我有种感觉，要是你在N'Mar打赢了，我会想成为其中的一份子。"

    old "But that's a big 'if.' I've no desire to commit my men to an invasion that's doomed to fail."
    new "But that's a big 'if.' I've no desire to commit my men to an invasion that's doomed to fail.\n但那可是个很大的“如果”。我可不想把手下的人投入到一场注定失败的进攻里。"

    old "I'm betting that the invasion succeeds."
    new "I'm betting that the invasion succeeds.\n我赌这次进攻会成功。"

    old "And that's all good and well for you. I'm sure that you're betting the lives of others on your success as well. I may very well make the same bet. But before I'm willing to do that, I want to have some assurance of your competence."
    new "And that's all good and well for you. I'm sure that you're betting the lives of others on your success as well. I may very well make the same bet. But before I'm willing to do that, I want to have some assurance of your competence.\n这对你来说自然是好事。我相信你也是拿别人的性命在赌你的成功。我也很可能做同样的赌注。但在我愿意下注之前，我想先对你的实力有些把握。"

    old "I want to put you to the test. See what you're made of. And maybe get a little something out of it for myself, too."
    new "I want to put you to the test. See what you're made of. And maybe get a little something out of it for myself, too.\n我想考验考验你，看看你有几斤几两。顺便，也许还能为我自己捞点好处。"

    old "What do you have in mind?"
    new "What do you have in mind?\n你有什么打算？"

    old "Let's explore the waters around the N'Mar peninsula. Consider it a practice run for the assault you want to run."
    new "Let's explore the waters around the N'Mar peninsula. Consider it a practice run for the assault you want to run.\n我们去N'Mar半岛周边的水域探一探。就当是你想发动的那场进攻的预演。"

    old "Not today, though. We've got...plans. I can't be any more specific than that. Come back some other day and I'll make the time."
    new "Not today, though. We've got...plans. I can't be any more specific than that. Come back some other day and I'll make the time.\n不过不是今天。我们另有……安排。再具体我就不能说了。改天再来，我会腾出时间。"

    old "Oh, one more thing. When you come back, bring a few friends. No telling what might be waiting out there for us, and besides, if I'm going to bet on the success of your invasion, it'll be a test of both you and whatever companions you decide to take along."
    new "Oh, one more thing. When you come back, bring a few friends. No telling what might be waiting out there for us, and besides, if I'm going to bet on the success of your invasion, it'll be a test of both you and whatever companions you decide to take along.\n哦，还有一件事。你回来时，带几个朋友。谁也不知道那儿会有什么在等着我们，再说了，既然我要押注你进攻能成，那这也是对你和你挑选的同伴们的一次考验。"

    old "How many friends I can bring?"
    new "How many friends I can bring?\n我能带几个朋友？"

    old "Let's say six. Not that I don't trust you, but I can't allow you to bring a small army on board and threaten to overthrow my ship's crew. Besides, too many people on deck will cause chaos and do more harm than good. Bring your best weapons and be ready to fight."
    new "Let's say six. Not that I don't trust you, but I can't allow you to bring a small army on board and threaten to overthrow my ship's crew. Besides, too many people on deck will cause chaos and do more harm than good. Bring your best weapons and be ready to fight.\n就六个吧。倒不是我不信任你，只是我不能让你把一支小军队带上船，反过来威胁要掀翻我的船员。再说，甲板上人太多会乱成一团，弊大于利。带上你最好的武器，准备好战斗。"

    old "Alright, Senya. I'll be back soon."
    new "Alright, Senya. I'll be back soon.\n好，Senya。我很快就回来。"

    old "Good. Jasper, can you escort [protag] back to shore?"
    new "Good. Jasper, can you escort [protag] back to shore?\n很好。Jasper，你能送[protag]回岸上吗？"

    old "On it, captain."
    new "On it, captain.\n遵命，船长。"

    old "Oh, and one last thing. Next time? Come at the end of the day. This is going to be a nighttime operation."
    new "Oh, and one last thing. Next time? Come at the end of the day. This is going to be a nighttime operation.\n哦，还有最后一件事。下次来？傍晚时分再来。这将是一次夜间行动。"

    old "The sun has almost set by the time we arrive at the Grimoire docks, but it's still bright enough for me to make out the shape of Jasper waving at me from the end of the pier."
    new "The sun has almost set by the time we arrive at the Grimoire docks, but it's still bright enough for me to make out the shape of Jasper waving at me from the end of the pier.\n我们抵达Grimoire码头时，太阳几乎已经落山，不过天还够亮，我能看清Jasper在栈桥尽头朝我挥手的身影。"

    old "You've brought company. Hello, I'm Jasper."
    new "You've brought company. Hello, I'm Jasper.\n你带了同伴来。大家好，我是Jasper。"

    old "Hello, handsome."
    new "Hello, handsome.\n你好啊，帅哥。"

    old "Ha! A pirate. We need one in our team!"
    new "Ha! A pirate. We need one in our team!\n哈！海盗。我们队里正缺一个呢！"

    old "<blushes> Hello, I'm Dasyra."
    new "<blushes> Hello, I'm Dasyra.\n<blushes> 你好，我是Dasyra。"

    old "Oh. Hello, Jasper."
    new "Oh. Hello, Jasper.\n哦。你好，Jasper。"

    old "Shall we get going?"
    new "Shall we get going?\n我们出发吧？"

    old "Yes, let's. My boat is at the end of the dock."
    new "Yes, let's. My boat is at the end of the dock.\n好，走吧。我的船在码头尽头。"

    old "Welcome back, [protag]. Are you and your companions ready for this?"
    new "Welcome back, [protag]. Are you and your companions ready for this?\n欢迎回来，[protag]。你和你的同伴们准备好了吗？"

    old "I'm not sure exactly what it is we're supposed to be ready for."
    new "I'm not sure exactly what it is we're supposed to be ready for.\n我不太确定我们究竟该为做什么而准备。"

    old "This is a reconnaissance mission. If we knew exactly what was out there, we wouldn't need to investigate, now would we?"
    new "This is a reconnaissance mission. If we knew exactly what was out there, we wouldn't need to investigate, now would we?\n这是一次侦察任务。要是我们早知道外面有什么，就用不着去探查了，对吧？"

    old "We're headed for the N'Mar peninsula, yes?"
    new "We're headed for the N'Mar peninsula, yes?\n我们要去N'Mar半岛，对吧？"

    old "Yes. Navigating the waters by moonlight will be tricky, but by the time we arrive there, I expect our eyes will have all had a chance to adjust to the darkness."
    new "Yes. Navigating the waters by moonlight will be tricky, but by the time we arrive there, I expect our eyes will have all had a chance to adjust to the darkness.\n是的。借着月光在那片水域航行会相当棘手，不过等我们到那儿时，我想大家的眼睛也都该适应黑暗了。"

    old "I understand that we don't have much information to go on, but anything you can tell me would be helpful."
    new "I understand that we don't have much information to go on, but anything you can tell me would be helpful.\n我明白我们可依据的情报不多，但你能告诉我的任何事都会有帮助。"

    old "I'd think that this is something you have more experience with than me. After all, haven't you been patrolling around the plains of N'Mar? Tell me how N'Mar's plains compare to normal land, and maybe we'll have some idea of how N'Mar's waters compare to normal waters."
    new "I'd think that this is something you have more experience with than me. After all, haven't you been patrolling around the plains of N'Mar? Tell me how N'Mar's plains compare to normal land, and maybe we'll have some idea of how N'Mar's waters compare to normal waters.\n我想，这方面你比我更有经验。毕竟，你不是一直在N'Mar平原一带巡逻吗？告诉我N'Mar的平原和普通陆地有何不同，也许我们就能大概知道，N'Mar的水域与普通水域有何不同。"

    old "Well, it's misty."
    new "Well, it's misty.\n嗯，那里雾蒙蒙的。"

    old "Yes, which is why we're doing this at night. Trying to navigate the mists in daylight can be enough to blind a man. The mists, they're not like normal fog. Something about them refracts the light, rather than blocking it."
    new "Yes, which is why we're doing this at night. Trying to navigate the mists in daylight can be enough to blind a man. The mists, they're not like normal fog. Something about them refracts the light, rather than blocking it.\n没错，这正是我们选择夜里行动的原因。想在白天穿过那片迷雾，足以把人晃瞎。那迷雾跟普通的雾不一样。它不知怎的会折射光线，而不是遮挡光线。"

    old "You seem to know a lot about the mist already."
    new "You seem to know a lot about the mist already.\n你似乎对那迷雾已经了解得不少了。"

    old "I know enough about the mist to keep well away. You've been inside the mist. Tell me, what lurks around N'Mar's plains?"
    new "I know enough about the mist to keep well away. You've been inside the mist. Tell me, what lurks around N'Mar's plains?\n我对迷雾的了解，足以让我远远避开它。你进过迷雾里。告诉我，N'Mar平原周围潜伏着什么？"

    old "Ghouls roam the area. Zombies, skeletons, and beasts of that ilk."
    new "Ghouls roam the area. Zombies, skeletons, and beasts of that ilk.\n食尸鬼在那一带游荡。还有僵尸、骷髅，以及诸如此类的怪物。"

    old "Interesting. Where do you suppose they come from?"
    new "Interesting. Where do you suppose they come from?\n有意思。你猜它们是从哪儿来的？"

    old "I wish we knew."
    new "I wish we knew.\n但愿我们知道。"

    old "But think about what a skeleton is. You and I, we have skeletons inside of us. So do beasts. So do fish. I think that you need to be a bit more precise when you tell me there are walking skeletons shambling around N'Mar. They're human skeletons, aren't they?"
    new "But think about what a skeleton is. You and I, we have skeletons inside of us. So do beasts. So do fish. I think that you need to be a bit more precise when you tell me there are walking skeletons shambling around N'Mar. They're human skeletons, aren't they?\n但想想骷髅是什么。你和我，我们身体里都有骷髅。野兽也一样，鱼也一样。我想，你告诉我N'Mar周围有会走路的骷髅在游荡时，得说得更精确一点。它们是人类骷髅，对吧？"

    old "Yes. I suppose it would be correct to say that the undead all have the makings of what we might associate with people."
    new "Yes. I suppose it would be correct to say that the undead all have the makings of what we might associate with people.\n是的。我想可以这么说，那些亡灵都长着我们会联想到人的样子。"

    old "So, I wonder what we'll encounter out at sea, if anything."
    new "So, I wonder what we'll encounter out at sea, if anything.\n所以，我在想，到了海上我们会遇到什么——如果真有什么的话。"

    old "Well, supposing that N'Mar's ghouls are reanimated corpses, I imagine we'll find fewer of them out at sea."
    new "Well, supposing that N'Mar's ghouls are reanimated corpses, I imagine we'll find fewer of them out at sea.\n嗯，假设N'Mar的食尸鬼是复活的尸体，我想在海上遇到的会少一些。"

    old "Let's hope so. We're almost there."
    new "Let's hope so. We're almost there.\n但愿如此。我们快到了。"

    old "We're nearing the peninsula."
    new "We're nearing the peninsula.\n我们正接近半岛。"

    old "Just how far out are we going to go?"
    new "Just how far out are we going to go?\n我们究竟要开到多远？"

    old "If I think that we're approaching a point of no return, we go back, and we consider the mission a failure. Unless that point of no return happens to be the peninsula itself."
    new "If I think that we're approaching a point of no return, we go back, and we consider the mission a failure. Unless that point of no return happens to be the peninsula itself.\n如果我觉得我们快到无法回头的地步了，我们就掉头回去，把这任务当作失败。除非那个无法回头的点恰好就是半岛本身。"

    old "So what do we consider a success?"
    new "So what do we consider a success?\n那我们怎样才算成功？"

    old "I want to see the castle of N'Mar."
    new "I want to see the castle of N'Mar.\n我想看到N'Mar的城堡。"

    old "Just seeing it? That's all?"
    new "Just seeing it? That's all?\n就只是看到它？仅此而已？"

    old "Seeing the castle means getting pretty damn close, especially in this fog."
    new "Seeing the castle means getting pretty damn close, especially in this fog.\n要看到城堡，就意味着得靠得相当近，尤其是在这样的雾里。"

    old "Make no mistake, [protag]. The purpose of this mission is to gather information. Nothing more, nothing less. I intend to chart these waters, and the longer we stay, the more information we can gather, and the closer we get to having a full picture of what it takes to invade N'Mar by sea."
    new "Make no mistake, [protag]. The purpose of this mission is to gather information. Nothing more, nothing less. I intend to chart these waters, and the longer we stay, the more information we can gather, and the closer we get to having a full picture of what it takes to invade N'Mar by sea.\n别搞错了，[protag]。这次任务的目的就是收集情报，不多也不少。我打算绘制这片水域的海图；我们待得越久，能收集到的情报就越多，也就越能看清从海上入侵N'Mar到底需要什么。"

    old "But we can leave at any time. If I think the lives of my crew are in jeopardy, I'm going to pull out. We can come back some other day if we need to."
    new "But we can leave at any time. If I think the lives of my crew are in jeopardy, I'm going to pull out. We can come back some other day if we need to.\n但我们随时可以撤离。要是我觉得船员们的性命受到威胁，我就会撤。有需要的话，改天再来就是。"

    old "As the boat coasts through the waters, I hear a terrible moaning sound, like one I've heard before on the plains of N'Mar."
    new "As the boat coasts through the waters, I hear a terrible moaning sound, like one I've heard before on the plains of N'Mar.\n船在水面上滑行时，我听到一阵可怕的呻吟声，就像我先前在N'Mar平原上听到过的那种。"

    old "I hear zombies."
    new "I hear zombies.\n我听到了僵尸的声音。"

    old "What do you intend to do about it?"
    new "What do you intend to do about it?\n你打算怎么办？"

    old "I don't know, I can't see anything out here. But they sound too close to be on land."
    new "I don't know, I can't see anything out here. But they sound too close to be on land.\n我不知道，这儿我什么都看不见。但它们的动静太近了，不像是从陆地上传来的。"

    old "I hear a scratching noise, like nails on wood."
    new "I hear a scratching noise, like nails on wood.\n我听到一阵刮擦声，像是指甲刮在木头上。"

    old "Yelling erupts from the rear of the ship."
    new "Yelling erupts from the rear of the ship.\n喊叫声从船尾爆发出来。"

    old "Monsters!"
    new "Monsters!\n有怪物！"

    old "Captain, we've got monsters at the bow!"
    new "Captain, we've got monsters at the bow!\n船长，船头有怪物！"

    old "[protag], Jasper, go!"
    new "[protag], Jasper, go!\n[protag]，Jasper，快上！"

    old "We run to the rear of the ship, where several zombies have already managed to climb on board."
    new "We run to the rear of the ship, where several zombies have already managed to climb on board.\n我们冲向船尾，那里已经有几具僵尸爬上了船。"

    old "Let's go!"
    new "Let's go!\n我们上！"

    old "How did they..."
    new "How did they...\n它们是怎么……"

    old "They must have crawled on board."
    new "They must have crawled on board.\n它们一定是爬上船的。"

    old "Is anyone hurt?"
    new "Is anyone hurt?\n有人受伤吗？"

    old "[protag], are you good to keep going? I want to keep exploring these waters, but if anyone is hurt and needs to return to land, just say the word."
    new "[protag], are you good to keep going? I want to keep exploring these waters, but if anyone is hurt and needs to return to land, just say the word.\n[protag]，你还能继续吗？我想继续探查这片水域，不过要是有人受伤、需要回岸上，说一声就行。"

    old "I'm not sure how much more of this we can take, Senya."
    new "I'm not sure how much more of this we can take, Senya.\n我不确定我们还能撑多久，Senya。"

    old "And I don't intend to stay around and find out. Let's go back, [protag]."
    new "And I don't intend to stay around and find out. Let's go back, [protag].\n我也不打算留下来弄清这个。我们回去吧，[protag]。"

    old "Fall back!"
    new "Fall back!\n后撤！"

    old "Let's retreat!"
    new "Let's retreat!\n我们撤退！"

    old "Is this what it feels like to be invincible? It feels like nothing can stop us."
    new "Is this what it feels like to be invincible? It feels like nothing can stop us.\n这就是无敌的感觉吗？仿佛什么也挡不住我们。"

    old "[protag], I'm amazed that we've managed to make it this far. But my men are exhausted. You look like you could use some rest too. I think we should pull back now."
    new "[protag], I'm amazed that we've managed to make it this far. But my men are exhausted. You look like you could use some rest too. I think we should pull back now.\n[protag]，真没想到我们能走到这一步。但我的手下已经精疲力竭，你看上去也需要歇歇了。我想我们现在该撤了。"

    old "Let's pull back, then. You are the captain, after all."
    new "Let's pull back, then. You are the captain, after all.\n那就撤吧。毕竟你是船长。"

    old "We've gotten this far. We can't turn back now."
    new "We've gotten this far. We can't turn back now.\n我们都走到这一步了，现在不能回头。"

    old "The decision isn't up to you, [protag]. I am the captain of this ship. You might be ready to press on, but I have my men to worry about."
    new "The decision isn't up to you, [protag]. I am the captain of this ship. You might be ready to press on, but I have my men to worry about.\n这由不得你，[protag]。我才是这艘船的船长。你可能已经准备好继续前进，但我还有手下要操心。"

    old "You promised..."
    new "You promised...\n你答应过的……"

    old "Worry not, [protag]. Your efforts weren't in vain. With your help so far, we've managed to chart these waters more effectively than I ever could have hoped."
    new "Worry not, [protag]. Your efforts weren't in vain. With your help so far, we've managed to chart these waters more effectively than I ever could have hoped.\n别担心，[protag]。你的努力没有白费。有了你迄今的帮助，我们绘制这片水域海图的进展，比我预想的还要好。"

    old "We didn't make it to the N'Mar peninsula, but we did get some valuable information."
    new "We didn't make it to the N'Mar peninsula, but we did get some valuable information.\n我们没能抵达N'Mar半岛，但确实得到了一些宝贵的情报。"

    old "So, about our agreement..."
    new "So, about our agreement...\n那么，关于我们的约定……"

    old "You want my help invading N'Mar, I haven't forgotten. But until I'm sure that we can make it there safely, I can't guarantee our participation."
    new "You want my help invading N'Mar, I haven't forgotten. But until I'm sure that we can make it there safely, I can't guarantee our participation.\n你想让我帮忙入侵N'Mar，这我没忘。但在确信我们能安全抵达之前，我无法保证我们的参与。"

    old "So where do we go from here?"
    new "So where do we go from here?\n那我们接下来怎么办？"

    old "Thanks to today's scouting mission, we now have a better understanding of the waters around N'Mar. With your help, I think we could fully chart those waters. At that point, I'd be content to commit to the invasion."
    new "Thanks to today's scouting mission, we now have a better understanding of the waters around N'Mar. With your help, I think we could fully chart those waters. At that point, I'd be content to commit to the invasion.\n多亏了今天的侦察，我们现在对N'Mar周边水域有了更清楚的了解。有你的帮助，我想我们能把那片水域完全绘制出来。到那时，我就愿意投身这场进攻。"

    old "What exactly are you saying?"
    new "What exactly are you saying?\n你究竟想说什么？"

    old "Help me help you, [protag]. Help me scout the waters around N'Mar, and I'll help you invade. Come back some other night. I think we all need some rest."
    new "Help me help you, [protag]. Help me scout the waters around N'Mar, and I'll help you invade. Come back some other night. I think we all need some rest.\n帮我就是帮你自己，[protag]。帮我侦察N'Mar周边水域，我就帮你进攻。改天夜里再来。我想我们都需要休息。"

    old "Captain..."
    new "Captain...\n船长……"

    old "Ah, yes. [protag], if you haven't noticed, Jasper has taken a real interest in you."
    new "Ah, yes. [protag], if you haven't noticed, Jasper has taken a real interest in you.\n啊，对了。[protag]，你也许已经注意到了，Jasper对你可是相当上心。"

    old "For awhile, I struggled to see what it was in you that made him feel so strongly. But I must admit, watching you two fight alongside one another made me think that Jasper seems more at home standing by your side than by mine."
    new "For awhile, I struggled to see what it was in you that made him feel so strongly. But I must admit, watching you two fight alongside one another made me think that Jasper seems more at home standing by your side than by mine.\n有段时间，我一直看不出你身上是什么让他如此倾心。但我不得不承认，看着你们俩并肩作战，我觉得Jasper站在你身边，比站在我身边更自在。"

    old "What are you saying?"
    new "What are you saying?\n你在说什么？"

    old "[protag], you offered us the aid of your companions tonight in assisting my crew. Now I'm prepared to return the favor. Jasper still has responsibilities on board this ship, but I can excuse him to accompany on your missions."
    new "[protag], you offered us the aid of your companions tonight in assisting my crew. Now I'm prepared to return the favor. Jasper still has responsibilities on board this ship, but I can excuse him to accompany on your missions.\n[protag]，今晚你让你的同伴们帮了我的船员。现在轮到我回报了。Jasper在船上还有职责，但我可以准他的假，让他随你出任务。"

    old "I'm ready to follow you into the plains of N'Mar. That is, if you'll have me."
    new "I'm ready to follow you into the plains of N'Mar. That is, if you'll have me.\n我准备好跟你进N'Mar平原了。当然，得你愿意收留我才行。"

    old "I'm not in a position to refuse help. If we need you, I'll be sure to let you know."
    new "I'm not in a position to refuse help. If we need you, I'll be sure to let you know.\n我没有立场拒绝帮助。若我们需要你，我一定会告诉你。"

    old "I'm glad to lend a hand. And if you happen to be in the vicinity of the docks, you can pay me a visit sometime. I'm curious about what sort of person you are, and I get the feeling that you're similarly curious about me. I think we'd have a lot to talk about."
    new "I'm glad to lend a hand. And if you happen to be in the vicinity of the docks, you can pay me a visit sometime. I'm curious about what sort of person you are, and I get the feeling that you're similarly curious about me. I think we'd have a lot to talk about.\n我很乐意搭把手。而且，你要是碰巧到码头附近，不妨来看看我。我很好奇你是怎样的人，而我有种感觉，你对我也同样好奇。我想我们能聊的会有很多。"

    old "Alright, Jasper. I'll see you some other time."
    new "Alright, Jasper. I'll see you some other time.\n好，Jasper。改日再见。"

    old "Hello, [protag]. I see you've brought help."
    new "Hello, [protag]. I see you've brought help.\n你好，[protag]。我看你带来了帮手。"

    old "Let's go exploring, Senya."
    new "Let's go exploring, Senya.\n我们去探路吧，Senya。"

    old "This is the last area left to explore!"
    new "This is the last area left to explore!\n这是最后一个待探索的区域了！"

    old "We have [senya_charting] areas left to explore."
    new "We have [senya_charting] areas left to explore.\n我们还剩[senya_charting]个区域要探索。"

    old "Monsters on deck! Monsters on deck!"
    new "Monsters on deck! Monsters on deck!\n甲板上有怪物！甲板上有怪物！"

    old "Careful, I spotted a draugh."
    new "Careful, I spotted a draugh.\n小心，我发现了一只draugh。"

    old "What's a draugh?"
    new "What's a draugh?\ndraugh是什么？"

    old "It's a vampire exposed to dark magic. An abomination. A mindless, ferocious, fast creature."
    new "It's a vampire exposed to dark magic. An abomination. A mindless, ferocious, fast creature.\n那是一种被黑暗魔法侵蚀的vampire。一个可憎之物，一种没有心智、凶猛又迅捷的生物。"

    old "Doesn't sound good."
    new "Doesn't sound good.\n听起来不妙。"

    old "Retreat! Everyone retreat!"
    new "Retreat! Everyone retreat!\n撤退！所有人撤退！"

    old "I'm sorry, I thought we could handle this."
    new "I'm sorry, I thought we could handle this.\n抱歉，我以为我们能应付得了。"

    old "Luckily we managed to push the undead back on water and escape. But I think you'll agree that for today it is enough."
    new "Luckily we managed to push the undead back on water and escape. But I think you'll agree that for today it is enough.\n幸好我们把这些亡灵逼回了水里，逃了出来。不过我想你会同意，今天到此为止就够了。"

    old "Yes, let's get back to Grimoire docks."
    new "Yes, let's get back to Grimoire docks.\n好，我们回Grimoire码头吧。"

    old "Good. Come back some other time and we continue exploring. One of these days we're sure to make it to N'Mar."
    new "Good. Come back some other time and we continue exploring. One of these days we're sure to make it to N'Mar.\n好。改天再来，我们继续探索。总有一日，我们一定能抵达N'Mar。"

    old "Are we good to keep going, or do we need to turn back?"
    new "Are we good to keep going, or do we need to turn back?\n我们还能继续前进吗，还是得掉头？"

    old "Let's keep going. No reason to turn back now."
    new "Let's keep going. No reason to turn back now.\n继续前进吧。现在没有回头的理由。"

    old "Sorry, Senya. We need to turn back."
    new "Sorry, Senya. We need to turn back.\n抱歉，Senya。我们得掉头回去。"

    old "No need to apologize. We've made good progress today. Come back some other time and we continue exploring. One of these days we're sure to make it to N'Mar."
    new "No need to apologize. We've made good progress today. Come back some other time and we continue exploring. One of these days we're sure to make it to N'Mar.\n不必道歉。我们今天进展不错。改天再来，我们继续探索。总有一日，我们一定能抵达N'Mar。"

    old "This was the last area! Our path to N'Mar should be free now!"
    new "This was the last area! Our path to N'Mar should be free now!\n这就是最后一个区域了！我们通往N'Mar的路现在应该畅通无阻了！"

    old "There's something ahead of us. Looks big."
    new "There's something ahead of us. Looks big.\n前方有东西。看着块头不小。"

    old "I squint, trying to see through the mist."
    new "I squint, trying to see through the mist.\n我眯起眼，试图透过迷雾看清。"

    old "I don't see it."
    new "I don't see it.\n我看不到。"

    old "Look harder. Broaden your view."
    new "Look harder. Broaden your view.\n再看仔细些。把视野放宽。"

    old "I cast my gaze to the left and to the right. Then I look up and see a glinting eye. It's at that moment I realize..."
    new "I cast my gaze to the left and to the right. Then I look up and see a glinting eye. It's at that moment I realize...\n我左右扫视，随后抬头，看见一只闪闪发亮的眼睛。就在那一刻，我意识到……"

    old "It's huge!"
    new "It's huge!\n好大！"

    old "We're in no condition to fight a beast of this size. Let's turn back and regroup."
    new "We're in no condition to fight a beast of this size. Let's turn back and regroup.\n以我们现在的状态，可斗不过这种体型的巨兽。我们掉头，重新整顿吧。"

    old "What was that thing?"
    new "What was that thing?\n那是什么东西？"

    old "I've heard tales of this beast before. Giant eyes, massive tentacles. They called it the Kraken. I never imagined I'd see it with my own eyes."
    new "I've heard tales of this beast before. Giant eyes, massive tentacles. They called it the Kraken. I never imagined I'd see it with my own eyes.\n我以前听过这种巨兽的传说。巨大的眼睛，庞大的触手。人们管它叫Kraken。我从没想过会亲眼见到它。"

    old "We were close to N'Mar. I could feel it in my bones. I feel like that beast is the last thing standing between us and the castle."
    new "We were close to N'Mar. I could feel it in my bones. I feel like that beast is the last thing standing between us and the castle.\n我们离N'Mar已经很近了。我骨子里都感觉得到。我觉得那头巨兽，就是挡在我们和城堡之间的最后一道障碍。"

    old "If we want to have any chance of successfully invading N'Mar, we'll have to fell that beast. We're going to need your help to do it, [protag]."
    new "If we want to have any chance of successfully invading N'Mar, we'll have to fell that beast. We're going to need your help to do it, [protag].\n若想有任何成功入侵N'Mar的机会，我们就必须打倒那头巨兽。要做到这一点，我们需要你的帮助，[protag]。"

    old "Let's go back to land. Give my crew a chance to rest, and yourself a chance to think about how to tackle this beast. Bring your best warriors with you. It's not going to be an easy fight."
    new "Let's go back to land. Give my crew a chance to rest, and yourself a chance to think about how to tackle this beast. Bring your best warriors with you. It's not going to be an easy fight.\n我们回陆地吧。让我的船员歇一歇，也让你自己想想该怎么对付这头巨兽。带上你最精锐的战士。这场仗不会轻松。"

    old "Are you ready?"
    new "Are you ready?\n你准备好了吗？"

    old "[protag], I've got an idea I'd like to share with you."
    new "[protag], I've got an idea I'd like to share with you.\n[protag]，我有个想法想跟你商量。"

    old "Go ahead and tell me."
    new "Go ahead and tell me.\n说来听听。"

    old "The Kraken is big. Almost as big as this ship itself."
    new "The Kraken is big. Almost as big as this ship itself.\nKraken体型巨大，几乎跟这艘船本身一样大。"

    old "So I've seen."
    new "So I've seen.\n这我已经见识过了。"

    old "We can use that to our advantage. We have artillery and cannons. The cannons are too slow and inaccurate to be used effectively against a shambling skeleton or a zombie. But against a monster as big as a ship..."
    new "We can use that to our advantage. We have artillery and cannons. The cannons are too slow and inaccurate to be used effectively against a shambling skeleton or a zombie. But against a monster as big as a ship...\n我们可以利用这一点。我们有火炮和大炮。大炮太慢又不够准，拿来对付踉跄的骷髅或僵尸派不上用场。但要对付像船那么大的怪物……"

    old "You think we can damage the Kraken with cannon fire."
    new "You think we can damage the Kraken with cannon fire.\n你觉得我们能靠炮火伤到Kraken。"

    old "That's what I'm thinking."
    new "That's what I'm thinking.\n我正是这么想的。"

    old "I like that idea."
    new "I like that idea.\n我喜欢这个主意。"

    old "There's another thing that will be different about fighting the Kraken. Zombies, ghouls, skeletons, they all were attacking the people on deck. But the Kraken..."
    new "There's another thing that will be different about fighting the Kraken. Zombies, ghouls, skeletons, they all were attacking the people on deck. But the Kraken...\n与Kraken战斗还有另一点不同。僵尸、食尸鬼、骷髅，它们攻击的都是甲板上的人。可Kraken……"

    old "The Kraken can attack the ship itself."
    new "The Kraken can attack the ship itself.\nKraken能攻击船本身。"

    old "The Kraken isn't big enough to drag the ship under the sea, or at least I hope it's not. But it could do enough damage to the ship to cripple it."
    new "The Kraken isn't big enough to drag the ship under the sea, or at least I hope it's not. But it could do enough damage to the ship to cripple it.\nKraken还没大到能把船拖进海底——至少我希望没有。但它足以重创船只，让船瘫痪。"

    old "If the Kraken is smart, it will go after our artillery as soon as it realizes it's under attack from cannon fire. Do your best to protect it."
    new "If the Kraken is smart, it will go after our artillery as soon as it realizes it's under attack from cannon fire. Do your best to protect it.\n要是Kraken够聪明，它一旦发觉自己正遭到炮火攻击，就会冲着我们的火炮下手。务必保护好火炮。"

    old "And if it tries to sink the ship...don't let that happen."
    new "And if it tries to sink the ship...don't let that happen.\n还有，如果它想弄沉这艘船……别让那种事发生。"

    old "Don't let the ship sink. Sounds like good advice."
    new "Don't let the ship sink. Sounds like good advice.\n别让船沉了。听起来是个好建议。"

    old "We're nearing it now. Are you ready?"
    new "We're nearing it now. Are you ready?\n我们正逼近它了。你准备好了吗？"

    old "I'm as ready as I'll ever be."
    new "I'm as ready as I'll ever be.\n我早就准备好了。"

    old "Here it comes."
    new "Here it comes.\n它来了。"

    old "Looks like we managed to beat it."
    new "Looks like we managed to beat it.\n看来我们成功把它打败了。"

    old "Of course we did. We wouldn't be very good at our jobs if a little sea monster was enough to stop us."
    new "Of course we did. We wouldn't be very good at our jobs if a little sea monster was enough to stop us.\n那当然。要是区区一只小海怪就能拦住我们，那我们这行也干得太差了。"

    old "Ha! I like your attitude, [protag]. Though, it was more than just a little sea monster."
    new "Ha! I like your attitude, [protag]. Though, it was more than just a little sea monster.\n哈！我喜欢你这股劲儿，[protag]。不过，它可不只是只小海怪。"

    old "True, true. It was nearly as big as your ship. But then, it's not a very big ship."
    new "True, true. It was nearly as big as your ship. But then, it's not a very big ship.\n没错，没错。它都快有你船那么大了。不过话说回来，你这船也不算大。"

    old "And that's why we're working together."
    new "And that's why we're working together.\n所以我们要联手啊。"

    old "Some days, you just manage to survive, if only by the skin of your teeth."
    new "Some days, you just manage to survive, if only by the skin of your teeth.\n有些日子，你不过勉强活了下来，就差那么一丁点儿。"

    old "Well, it's not every day that you come up against the stuff of legend."
    new "Well, it's not every day that you come up against the stuff of legend.\n嗯，跟传说中的怪物交手，可不是天天都有的事。"

    old "Oh, if you're looking to take on legendary beasts, just wait until you see what's lurking inside of N'Mar. Vampires...well, if you're lucky, you'll never have to see one."
    new "Oh, if you're looking to take on legendary beasts, just wait until you see what's lurking inside of N'Mar. Vampires...well, if you're lucky, you'll never have to see one.\n哦，如果你想对付传说中的野兽，就等着看N'Mar里潜伏着什么吧。Vampires……嗯，运气好的话，你一辈子都不用亲眼见到一只。"

    old "I see what looks like land in the distance. Land, with a large structure."
    new "I see what looks like land in the distance. Land, with a large structure.\n我看见远处似乎有陆地。陆地上还有一座庞大的建筑。"

    old "That's it. That's the castle. It's so close I feel we could strike it's walls with an arrow, had we an archer."
    new "That's it. That's the castle. It's so close I feel we could strike it's walls with an arrow, had we an archer.\n那就是城堡。近得我都觉得，要是有个弓箭手，一箭就能射到它的墙上。"

    old "We don't have archers, but we do have cannons. And when the invasion day comes, we'll be prepared to use one."
    new "We don't have archers, but we do have cannons. And when the invasion day comes, we'll be prepared to use one.\n我们没有弓箭手，但我们有大炮。等进攻之日来临，我们就会准备好用它。"

    old "You and your crew think you'll be able to make it out here, unassisted?"
    new "You and your crew think you'll be able to make it out here, unassisted?\n你和你的船员们觉得你们能独自到这儿来吗？"

    old "Don't you worry, [protag]. You've been helpful in charting these waters, but now that we know our way around, and the Kraken is gone, I think me and my men can handle things. Leave the assault by sea to us."
    new "Don't you worry, [protag]. You've been helpful in charting these waters, but now that we know our way around, and the Kraken is gone, I think me and my men can handle things. Leave the assault by sea to us.\n别担心，[protag]。绘制这片水域的海图，你帮了大忙，可如今我们已经认路了，Kraken也不在了，我想我和手下的人应付得来。海上的进攻就交给我们吧。"

    old "Alright. I'll be leading the assault by land."
    new "Alright. I'll be leading the assault by land.\n好。陆路的进攻由我率领。"

    old "I look forward to working together in the future. And maybe claiming some of whatever treasure is locked inside for myself."
    new "I look forward to working together in the future. And maybe claiming some of whatever treasure is locked inside for myself.\n我期待以后能与你并肩作战。顺便也许能给自己捞点锁在里面的财宝。"

    old "[protag]! I was thinking it was about time you came to visit me!"
    new "[protag]! I was thinking it was about time you came to visit me!\n[protag]！我还想着你也该来看我了！"

    old "How did you know it was me?"
    new "How did you know it was me?\n你怎么知道是我？"

    old "Oh, actually I've been following you since you stepped into the swamp territory."
    new "Oh, actually I've been following you since you stepped into the swamp territory.\n哦，其实从你踏进沼泽地开始，我就一直跟着你。"

    old "What? So, when I had to stop and go behind that bush for..."
    new "What? So, when I had to stop and go behind that bush for...\n什么？那……我停下来，绕到灌木丛后面去……的时候？"

    old "Don't worry! I respect people's privacy. I just looked away when you had that...business."
    new "Don't worry! I respect people's privacy. I just looked away when you had that...business.\n别担心！我尊重别人的隐私。你办那……事的时候，我只是转开了视线。"

    old "Sylrissa was following me hidden. I'm not sure I like it."
    new "Sylrissa was following me hidden. I'm not sure I like it.\nSylrissa一直偷偷跟着我。我不太喜欢这样。"

    old "Where did that sudden outburst come from?"
    new "Where did that sudden outburst come from?\n你怎么突然说这些？"

    old "That kind of behavior isn't appropriate, Sylrissa. If you're supposed to be an ally, or even a friend that I'd come to visit, why do you feel the need to stalk me like that?"
    new "That kind of behavior isn't appropriate, Sylrissa. If you're supposed to be an ally, or even a friend that I'd come to visit, why do you feel the need to stalk me like that?\n这种行为不太妥当，Sylrissa。如果你是我的盟友，甚至是我会来看望的朋友，你又为什么觉得非得那样跟踪我？"

    old "But...it's because I'm your friend that I watched you. I wanted to keep you safe."
    new "But...it's because I'm your friend that I watched you. I wanted to keep you safe.\n可是……正因为我是你的朋友，我才会看着你。我想护你周全。"

    old "Really? Because being watched doesn't make me feel very safe."
    new "Really? Because being watched doesn't make me feel very safe.\n真的吗？可被人盯着，并没能让我感到多安全。"

    old "Ah, but anyone meaning you harm would feel even less safe, [protag]. If some enemy attacked you by surprise, they wouldn't expect someone like me to be lurking in the shadows."
    new "Ah, but anyone meaning you harm would feel even less safe, [protag]. If some enemy attacked you by surprise, they wouldn't expect someone like me to be lurking in the shadows.\n啊，不过任何想害你的人只会觉得更不安全，[protag]。要是有敌人偷袭你，他们可想不到会有我这样的人潜伏在暗处。"

    old "So, thanks to my speed and swiftness, I could have backstabbed them before they had a chance to do you any harm."
    new "So, thanks to my speed and swiftness, I could have backstabbed them before they had a chance to do you any harm.\n所以，多亏我这身速度，我大可以在他们伤到你之前就绕到背后捅死他们。"

    old "Hmpf. I'm not sure I'm buying it, but I guess it could make sense. Just don't do it again, OK?"
    new "Hmpf. I'm not sure I'm buying it, but I guess it could make sense. Just don't do it again, OK?\n哼。我不太吃你这一套，不过也算说得通。只是下不为例，好吗？"

    old "Alright, [protag]. If you feel that strongly about it...I promise."
    new "Alright, [protag]. If you feel that strongly about it...I promise.\n好吧，[protag]。既然你这么在意……我答应你。"

    old "Absolutely! Yes, that was the reason."
    new "Absolutely! Yes, that was the reason.\n正是！对，就是这个原因。"

    old "Sylrissa grins."
    new "Sylrissa grins.\nSylrissa咧嘴一笑。"

    old "People get vulnerable when they think they're in control of a situation. Imagine, some bandits, ambushing you."
    new "People get vulnerable when they think they're in control of a situation. Imagine, some bandits, ambushing you.\n人一旦以为自己掌控了局面，就会露出破绽。想象一下，几个强盗伏击你。"

    old "Maybe they're two or three. Against you, alone. They think they've already won, they look at you like a wolf on his prey."
    new "Maybe they're two or three. Against you, alone. They think they've already won, they look at you like a wolf on his prey.\n也许他们有两三个。对付你孤身一人。他们以为自己已经赢了，看你的眼神，就像一头盯上猎物的狼。"

    old "And this is where I'd make my grand entrance, right behind them. A few seconds and a few slices later, their dead bodies would be floating down the river."
    new "And this is where I'd make my grand entrance, right behind them. A few seconds and a few slices later, their dead bodies would be floating down the river.\n这时候就该我隆重登场了，就出现在他们身后。几秒钟、几刀下去，他们的尸体就会顺着河漂走。"

    old "When you talk like that, it's almost poetic."
    new "When you talk like that, it's almost poetic.\n你这么一说，倒有几分诗意了。"

    old "I know! I really am an artist."
    new "I know! I really am an artist.\n我知道！我真的是个艺术家。"

    old "Although...you were describing death."
    new "Although...you were describing death.\n虽然……你描述的是死亡。"

    old "I'm the kind of atist who paints in blood."
    new "I'm the kind of atist who paints in blood.\n我是那种用鲜血作画的艺术家。"

    old "This is starting to get more and more morbid..."
    new "This is starting to get more and more morbid...\n这话题越来越病态了……"

    old "Anyway, I only came here to make sure you were all right. And it seems you are."
    new "Anyway, I only came here to make sure you were all right. And it seems you are.\n总之，我来这儿只是想确认你没事。看来你确实没事。"

    old "Well, I miss Enok. But I know that when the opportunity arises, I'll go looking for him. And rescue him, if all goes well."
    new "Well, I miss Enok. But I know that when the opportunity arises, I'll go looking for him. And rescue him, if all goes well.\n嗯，我很想念Enok。但我知道，等机会一到，我就会去找他。如果一切顺利，就把他救出来。"

    old "If he's still alive..."
    new "If he's still alive...\n如果他还在世的话……"

    old "I'm sure of it. He doesn't look like it, but he is a tough naga."
    new "I'm sure of it. He doesn't look like it, but he is a tough naga.\n我敢肯定。他看起来不像，但他是个硬气的naga。"

    old "All of you nagas are tough."
    new "All of you nagas are tough.\n你们这些nagas都挺硬朗的。"

    old "So, what have you been doing, Sylrissa?"
    new "So, what have you been doing, Sylrissa?\n那么，你最近都在做什么，Sylrissa？"

    old "There's not much to do around the swamp. But I don't mind it here. It...seems to be the best place for a person like me. Except for the times when I need to come with you in the arena or in some mission."
    new "There's not much to do around the swamp. But I don't mind it here. It...seems to be the best place for a person like me. Except for the times when I need to come with you in the arena or in some mission.\n沼泽附近没什么可做的。不过我不介意待在这里。这里……似乎是像我这样的人最合适的归宿。除了有时得跟你去竞技场、或是执行什么任务的时候。"

    old "Oh? I thought you might like to spend more time traveling outside the swamp."
    new "Oh? I thought you might like to spend more time traveling outside the swamp.\n哦？我还以为你会想多花点时间到沼泽外走走。"

    old "I do. However, the stares of the humans in Grimoire when we walk in the streets... or when we fight in some arena..."
    new "I do. However, the stares of the humans in Grimoire when we walk in the streets... or when we fight in some arena...\n我想啊。可是，走在街上时，或者在某些竞技场里战斗时，Grimoire那些人类盯着我们看的目光……"

    old "I never thought about that."
    new "I never thought about that.\n我从没想过这些。"

    old "I don't blame them. Probably they've never seen a naga before in their lives. Still, it's a bit...unsettling. They don't like me. And I don't like people who don't like me."
    new "I don't blame them. Probably they've never seen a naga before in their lives. Still, it's a bit...unsettling. They don't like me. And I don't like people who don't like me.\n我不怪他们。也许他们这辈子都没见过naga。不过，还是有点……让人心里发毛。他们不喜欢我，我也不喜欢不喜欢我的人。"

    old "I understand. Well, if you're alright with calling the swamp your home, then I suppose I'll leave well enough alone."
    new "I understand. Well, if you're alright with calling the swamp your home, then I suppose I'll leave well enough alone.\n我理解。嗯，如果你愿意把沼泽当作自己的家，那我想我也就不好多说什么了。"

    old "Yes. However, you [protag]... you're always welcome here."
    new "Yes. However, you [protag]... you're always welcome here.\n是的。不过，你，[protag]……你在这里永远都受欢迎。"

    old "Thank you. I'm glad to have you as a ally, Sylrissa. Although...as for the swamp..."
    new "Thank you. I'm glad to have you as a ally, Sylrissa. Although...as for the swamp...\n谢谢。有你这样的盟友，我很高兴，Sylrissa。只不过……说到这沼泽……"

    old "What, you don't like it? What about it?"
    new "What, you don't like it? What about it?\n怎么，你不喜欢？它哪儿不好？"

    old "The odor here is quite...strong."
    new "The odor here is quite...strong.\n这里的气味实在……太冲了。"

    old "I know! Isn't it delightful?"
    new "I know! Isn't it delightful?\n我知道！是不是很美妙？"

    old "I was thinking the opposite. It smells like rotting meat mixed with the vomit of buzzards that tried eating that meat."
    new "I was thinking the opposite. It smells like rotting meat mixed with the vomit of buzzards that tried eating that meat.\n我想的恰恰相反。闻起来像腐烂的肉，混着那些想啃这腐肉的秃鹫吐出来的东西。"

    old "I know! It's so nice!"
    new "I know! It's so nice!\n我知道！多好啊！"

    old "...perhaps we should lay this topic to rest. I'm beginning to see why you and I have differing opinions about the swamp."
    new "...perhaps we should lay this topic to rest. I'm beginning to see why you and I have differing opinions about the swamp.\n……也许我们该换个话题了。我开始明白，为什么你我对沼泽的看法如此不同。"

    old "It's the air around here. It sticks to your skin and makes you feel sweaty. It's even worse than being in a desert."
    new "It's the air around here. It sticks to your skin and makes you feel sweaty. It's even worse than being in a desert.\n是这附近的空气。它黏在皮肤上，让人浑身汗津津的。比待在沙漠里还难受。"

    old "Really? That's my favorite part of the swamp, [protag]. It keeps my skin nice and moist, even when I'm out of the water."
    new "Really? That's my favorite part of the swamp, [protag]. It keeps my skin nice and moist, even when I'm out of the water.\n真的吗？这正是我最喜欢沼泽的地方，[protag]。它让我的皮肤保持水润，哪怕我不在水里也一样。"

    old "Well, I guess a naga would say that."
    new "Well, I guess a naga would say that.\n嗯，我想naga都会这么说。"

    old "I don't have many memories of the swamp, and most of them are bad ones."
    new "I don't have many memories of the swamp, and most of them are bad ones.\n我对这片沼泽没有多少回忆，而且大多是糟糕的回忆。"

    old "I know Enok was a close friend to you. But...I like to think he was my friend, as well."
    new "I know Enok was a close friend to you. But...I like to think he was my friend, as well.\n我知道Enok是你的挚友。不过……我愿意相信他也是我的朋友。"

    old "Sylrissa nods understandingly."
    new "Sylrissa nods understandingly.\nSylrissa会意地点点头。"

    old "You got to have some positive memories of Enok in this swamp. But whenever I come here, I'm reminded of...well, you know."
    new "You got to have some positive memories of Enok in this swamp. But whenever I come here, I'm reminded of...well, you know.\n在这片沼泽里，你肯定也留下过关于Enok的美好回忆。只是每次我来到这里，就会想起……嗯，你懂的。"

    old "I understand, [protag]. I don't wish to relive that memory either. But whenever I go back to where I last saw Enok, I can't chase those thoughts from my head."
    new "I understand, [protag]. I don't wish to relive that memory either. But whenever I go back to where I last saw Enok, I can't chase those thoughts from my head.\n我理解，[protag]。我也不愿重温那段记忆。可每当我回到最后见到Enok的地方，那些念头就怎么也挥之不去。"

    old "I feel like I should go."
    new "I feel like I should go.\n我想我该走了。"

    old "Aww, leaving already?"
    new "Aww, leaving already?\n啊呀，这就要走了？"

    old "I'm sorry I don't have more time. But I'll be back soon!"
    new "I'm sorry I don't have more time. But I'll be back soon!\n抱歉，我没有更多时间了。不过我会很快回来的！"

    old "Almost as soon as I reach the swamp, I run into an excited looking Sylrissa."
    new "Almost as soon as I reach the swamp, I run into an excited looking Sylrissa.\n我刚到沼泽，就撞上了满脸兴奋的Sylrissa。"

    old "[protag]! I was just leaving to go find you!"
    new "[protag]! I was just leaving to go find you!\n[protag]！我正要出门去找你呢！"

    old "Wait. You were coming... to Grimoire?"
    new "Wait. You were coming... to Grimoire?\n等等。你本来要去……Grimoire？"

    old "Sorry. I know it would have been a risk coming there on my own, but I had to find you. I think Enok is still alive!"
    new "Sorry. I know it would have been a risk coming there on my own, but I had to find you. I think Enok is still alive!\n抱歉。我知道一个人去那儿会有风险，但我必须找到你。我觉得Enok还活着！"

    old "Really? You scouted the area and spotted him or something?"
    new "Really? You scouted the area and spotted him or something?\n真的？你去那一带侦察，看见他了还是怎么？"

    old "Well, no. But... I saw him."
    new "Well, no. But... I saw him.\n呃，不是。不过……我看见他了。"

    old "Saw him?"
    new "Saw him?\n看见他？"

    old "Yes, last night, when I had trouble sleeping."
    new "Yes, last night, when I had trouble sleeping.\n是的，就在昨晚，我睡不着的时候。"

    old "Don't take this the wrong way, but... are you sure it wasn't just a dream?"
    new "Don't take this the wrong way, but... are you sure it wasn't just a dream?\n别误会，可是……你确定那不只是个梦？"

    old "What! Of course I'm sure!"
    new "What! Of course I'm sure!\n什么！我当然确定！"

    old "Sylrissa..."
    new "Sylrissa...\nSylrissa……"

    old "Sylrissa's demeanor suddenly turns agressive as she closes the gap between us in mere seconds. If she was going to attack me, I wouldn't have had a chance to stop her. Her speed is really something else."
    new "Sylrissa's demeanor suddenly turns agressive as she closes the gap between us in mere seconds. If she was going to attack me, I wouldn't have had a chance to stop her. Her speed is really something else.\nSylrissa的神情骤然变得凶狠起来，短短几秒就逼近到我面前。要是她真要攻击我，我根本来不及阻止她。她的速度确实非同寻常。"

    old "I imagine most people in my position would be scared, but I'm not. As angry as she is, I still trust that she won't actually hurt me."
    new "I imagine most people in my position would be scared, but I'm not. As angry as she is, I still trust that she won't actually hurt me.\n我想，换作我这种情况的大多数人都会害怕，但我没有。尽管她如此生气，我仍相信她不会真的伤害我。"

    old "When you're done hissing at me and want to explain, I'm listening."
    new "When you're done hissing at me and want to explain, I'm listening.\n等你朝我发完脾气，想解释的时候，我在听。"

    old "Right. I apologize."
    new "Right. I apologize.\n好。我道歉。"

    old "It's just that... when it's about Enok, I sometimes lose my temper. But it wasn't a dream, [protag]. I'm sure it wasn't."
    new "It's just that... when it's about Enok, I sometimes lose my temper. But it wasn't a dream, [protag]. I'm sure it wasn't.\n只是……一涉及到Enok，我有时就会失控。但那不是梦，[protag]。我确定不是。"

    old "Sylrissa stops and blinks at me, completely caught off guard by my comment. For someone who's such a flirt, you'd think she'd be more prepared for something like this."
    new "Sylrissa stops and blinks at me, completely caught off guard by my comment. For someone who's such a flirt, you'd think she'd be more prepared for something like this.\nSylrissa停了下来，朝我眨眨眼，被我的话弄得完全措手不及。像她这么爱撩的人，按理说该对这种事早有准备才是。"

    old "Once she has a second to process what just happened, a slight blush creeps into her cheeks as she bursts into laughter."
    new "Once she has a second to process what just happened, a slight blush creeps into her cheeks as she bursts into laughter.\n等她回过神来，脸颊泛起一抹红晕，随即放声大笑。"

    old "I'm sorry. I got carried away. It happens sometimes when it's about Enok."
    new "I'm sorry. I got carried away. It happens sometimes when it's about Enok.\n对不起。我太激动了。一涉及到Enok，我有时就会这样。"

    old "I understand. You care about him a lot."
    new "I understand. You care about him a lot.\n我理解。你很在乎他。"

    old "Yes. And believe me when I say that I'm sure it wasn't a dream."
    new "Yes. And believe me when I say that I'm sure it wasn't a dream.\n是的。而且请你相信我，我确定那不是梦。"

    old "It looked so real! It was like a sort of vision. A blurred vision, but it was enough for me to understand that he was being held captive inside a tent."
    new "It looked so real! It was like a sort of vision. A blurred vision, but it was enough for me to understand that he was being held captive inside a tent.\n它看起来那么真实！就像某种幻象。虽然画面模糊，但足以让我明白，他被囚禁在一顶帐篷里。"

    old "So you...'saw' Enok inside a tent?"
    new "So you...'saw' Enok inside a tent?\n所以，你……在帐篷里“看见”了Enok？"

    old "It was more like I was him. Like if I could see things through his eyes."
    new "It was more like I was him. Like if I could see things through his eyes.\n更像是我就变成了他。仿佛我能透过他的眼睛看东西。"

    old "If I'm being honest, I'm having a hard time believing that this is more than wishful thinking. On the other hand, it's my job to keep my team together and part of that means dealing with their issues- imagined or otherwise- before they become bigger problems down the line."
    new "If I'm being honest, I'm having a hard time believing that this is more than wishful thinking. On the other hand, it's my job to keep my team together and part of that means dealing with their issues- imagined or otherwise- before they become bigger problems down the line.\n老实说，我很难相信这不仅仅是一厢情愿。但另一方面，让团队保持团结是我的职责，这也就意味着，要在伙伴们的问题——无论是真是假——演变成更大的麻烦之前加以处理。"

    old "What else did you see?"
    new "What else did you see?\n你还看到了什么？"

    old "I was lying on my side which means Enok must still be without his tail. Hm. He's probably bound and gagged too so that he can't cast spells. They must have figured out that he's a battlemage."
    new "I was lying on my side which means Enok must still be without his tail. Hm. He's probably bound and gagged too so that he can't cast spells. They must have figured out that he's a battlemage.\n在幻象里我侧躺着，这说明Enok一定还没长出尾巴。嗯，他八成还被绑着、堵着嘴，好让他没法施法。他们肯定已经发现他是个战斗法师了。"

    old "Well, even if he could cast spells, he wouldn't be able to put up much resistance without his tail."
    new "Well, even if he could cast spells, he wouldn't be able to put up much resistance without his tail.\n嗯，就算他能施法，没有尾巴，他也撑不起多大抵抗。"

    old "You're wrong. Enok can cast a very powerful regeneration spell. Our tails regrow naturally over time, but with his spell the process is much faster. It only takes only a few minutes."
    new "You're wrong. Enok can cast a very powerful regeneration spell. Our tails regrow naturally over time, but with his spell the process is much faster. It only takes only a few minutes.\n你错了。Enok能施放一种极强大的再生法术。我们的尾巴本来就会随时间自然再生，但有了他的法术，这个过程会快得多。只需要短短几分钟。"

    old "How do you know?"
    new "How do you know?\n你怎么知道？"

    old "This sort of thing has happened before. He's saved my life more than once."
    new "This sort of thing has happened before. He's saved my life more than once.\n这种事以前发生过。他不止一次救过我的命。"

    old "I see. Still... if he was tied and gagged, that vision doesn't make sense. If Enok can't cast spells right now, it couldn't have been his doing."
    new "I see. Still... if he was tied and gagged, that vision doesn't make sense. If Enok can't cast spells right now, it couldn't have been his doing.\n我明白了。可是……如果他当时被绑着、堵着嘴，那幻象就说不通了。若Enok现在没法施法，那就不可能是他做的。"

    old "[protag], I don't know how to explain it, but I'm sure it was him. And even if wasn't him, I still have to try following this lead."
    new "[protag], I don't know how to explain it, but I'm sure it was him. And even if wasn't him, I still have to try following this lead.\n[protag]，我不知道该怎么解释，但我确定那就是他。就算不是他，我也得试着追查这条线索。"

    old "What lead? A tent in the jungle? There must be hundreds of them!"
    new "What lead? A tent in the jungle? There must be hundreds of them!\n什么线索？丛林里的一顶帐篷？那样的帐篷肯定有成百上千顶！"

    old "Oh, yeah. Sorry. There's one detail I forgot to mention."
    new "Oh, yeah. Sorry. There's one detail I forgot to mention.\n哦，对。抱歉。有个细节我忘了说。"

    old "The tent was open and I managed to get a glimpse of the outside. I saw a big temple; the temple of Chzulu."
    new "The tent was open and I managed to get a glimpse of the outside. I saw a big temple; the temple of Chzulu.\n帐篷是敞开的，我趁机瞥了一眼外面。我看到一座大庙——Chzulu神庙。"

    old "What? That's pretty far north of here. And, on top of that, it's full of lizardmen. It's not exactly a safe place to go poking around."
    new "What? That's pretty far north of here. And, on top of that, it's full of lizardmen. It's not exactly a safe place to go poking around.\n什么？那在这儿的正北边，远得很。而且那里到处是lizardmen，可不是个能随便乱闯的安全地方。"

    old "I also noticed something else: some of the lizardmen were more of a reddish color. They weren't green like normal lizardmen."
    new "I also noticed something else: some of the lizardmen were more of a reddish color. They weren't green like normal lizardmen.\n我还注意到另一点：有些lizardmen偏红色。它们不像普通lizardmen那样是绿色的。"

    old "Red lizardmen!?"
    new "Red lizardmen!?\n红色的lizardmen！？"

    old "Hey. You look troubled. I take it that's not a good sign?"
    new "Hey. You look troubled. I take it that's not a good sign?\n嘿。你脸色不对。看来那不是什么好兆头？"

    old "It is not. I've never had to deal with them myself since my job as a debt collector didn't exactly have me running around swamps, but I've heard a lot of bad things about them."
    new "It is not. I've never had to deal with them myself since my job as a debt collector didn't exactly have me running around swamps, but I've heard a lot of bad things about them.\n不，不是。我本人从没遇上过它们，因为我这收债人的活计可不至于让我在沼泽地里到处乱跑，但关于它们的坏话我听过不少。"

    old "No, it isn't. I've never met them personally, but other merchants weren't as lucky as me. The ones that ran into them usually turned up dead and without limbs attached to their bodies."
    new "No, it isn't. I've never met them personally, but other merchants weren't as lucky as me. The ones that ran into them usually turned up dead and without limbs attached to their bodies.\n不，不是。我本人从没遇上过它们，可别的商人就没我这么走运了。撞上它们的人，通常被发现时已经死了，而且四肢都不在身上。"

    old "I once composed a ballad based on the tales of a paladin who survived an encounter with a group of them. Though, if I'm being honest, I doubt that the paladin's account had any truth to it. It'd be nigh impossible for someone to take on three of those lizardmen on his own."
    new "I once composed a ballad based on the tales of a paladin who survived an encounter with a group of them. Though, if I'm being honest, I doubt that the paladin's account had any truth to it. It'd be nigh impossible for someone to take on three of those lizardmen on his own.\n我曾经根据一位圣骑士的传闻写过一首叙事诗，那人在一群它们的包围中幸存了下来。不过说实话，我怀疑那圣骑士的说法有几分是真的。一个人单枪匹马对付三个那种lizardmen，几乎是不可能的。"

    old "They were particularly famous in the alchemy circle of the magic academy where I studied because their blood has peculiar properties. It costs a fortune too because it's so dangerous to collect."
    new "They were particularly famous in the alchemy circle of the magic academy where I studied because their blood has peculiar properties. It costs a fortune too because it's so dangerous to collect.\n在我求学的魔法学院的炼金圈里，它们特别出名，因为它们的血液有着奇异的特性。那血也贵得吓人，因为采集起来危险至极。"

    old "They're called lizardmen devourers. You can distinguish them from the other, regular, lizardmen because they have a red carapace and are bigger and more lethal."
    new "They're called lizardmen devourers. You can distinguish them from the other, regular, lizardmen because they have a red carapace and are bigger and more lethal.\n它们叫做lizardmen devourers。要跟其他普通的lizardmen区分开来很简单——它们长着红色的甲壳，体型更大，也更致命。"

    old "They believe that by eating their prey alive, they gain the favor of the god of death, Chzulu."
    new "They believe that by eating their prey alive, they gain the favor of the god of death, Chzulu.\n它们相信活生生地吞下猎物，就能博得死神Chzulu的垂青。"

    old "That's... crazy. Even for me."
    new "That's... crazy. Even for me.\n这……太疯狂了。就连我也觉得。"

    old "Strange. I was expecting a joke from you at this point."
    new "Strange. I was expecting a joke from you at this point.\n真奇怪。我还以为这会儿你会开个玩笑呢。"

    old "As I said, it's crazy. Who would eat something without cooking it first? Raw meat tastes terrible."
    new "As I said, it's crazy. Who would eat something without cooking it first? Raw meat tastes terrible.\n我说了，这很疯狂。谁会不先煮熟就吃啊？生肉难吃死了。"

    old "That's better."
    new "That's better.\n这才像你。"

    old "Anyway, I plan to follow my instinct on this one. I feel something. Something like... Hm. It's hard to explain. A connection? Like a voice is telling me to go there."
    new "Anyway, I plan to follow my instinct on this one. I feel something. Something like... Hm. It's hard to explain. A connection? Like a voice is telling me to go there.\n总之，这件事我打算跟着直觉走。我感觉到某种东西。像是……嗯。很难说清。一种联结？就像有个声音在告诉我，去那里。"

    old "Wait, you're seriously planning to go towards the Chzulu temple on your own?"
    new "Wait, you're seriously planning to go towards the Chzulu temple on your own?\n等等，你真打算独自前往Chzulu神庙？"

    old "No, not alone. You're coming with me."
    new "No, not alone. You're coming with me.\n不，不是独自一人。你跟我一起去。"

    old "Ah, good. Wait- me?!"
    new "Ah, good. Wait- me?!\n啊，好。等等——我？！"

    old "Yes, you. You can even ask that amazon lady, Leena. She's an icy bitch, but she does know how to kill things."
    new "Yes, you. You can even ask that amazon lady, Leena. She's an icy bitch, but she does know how to kill things.\n没错，就是你。你甚至可以叫上那位amazon女士Leena。她这人冷冰冰的，不过杀起东西来确实是把好手。"

    old "Wait. Hold on. I don't think it's a good idea to bring anyone else with you-I mean, with us. It's too risky to go there in large numbers. That'll just attract more attention and there won't be any getting out of there if we're fighting off all the lizardemen in the swamp."
    new "Wait. Hold on. I don't think it's a good idea to bring anyone else with you-I mean, with us. It's too risky to go there in large numbers. That'll just attract more attention and there won't be any getting out of there if we're fighting off all the lizardemen in the swamp.\n等等。慢着。我觉得还是别再带别人了——我是说，别跟我们一起去。人太多去那儿太冒险了。那样只会引来更多注意，而且我们要是跟沼泽里所有的lizardmen打起来，就别想从那里脱身了。"

    old "This will work much better as a quick search and rescue mission. Avoiding as many fights as we can is the only way I see us accomplishing this."
    new "This will work much better as a quick search and rescue mission. Avoiding as many fights as we can is the only way I see us accomplishing this.\n这更适合当作一次快速的搜救行动。尽可能少打斗，是我能想到的完成这件事的唯一办法。"

    old "I got it: avoid fighting."
    new "I got it: avoid fighting.\n我懂了：避免打斗。"

    old "I look at her and notice the way she says 'avoid fighting'. Yeah, that's probably not going to happen with her."
    new "I look at her and notice the way she says 'avoid fighting'. Yeah, that's probably not going to happen with her.\n我看着她，注意到她说“避免打斗”时的语气。嗯，有她在，这恐怕是不可能了。"

    old "I let out a sigh and resign myself."
    new "I let out a sigh and resign myself.\n我叹了口气，认命了。"

    old "I know I'm going to regret this but, yes, I'll accompany you."
    new "I know I'm going to regret this but, yes, I'll accompany you.\n我知道我会后悔的，不过，好吧，我陪你去。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]! Let me just grab my swords and-"
    new "Thank you, [protag]! Let me just grab my swords and-\n谢谢你，[protag]！我这就去拿我的双剑，然后——"

    old "Wait! Not now!! I need some time to prepare myself. You know, grab some potions, get better gear. This isn't going to be easy."
    new "Wait! Not now!! I need some time to prepare myself. You know, grab some potions, get better gear. This isn't going to be easy.\n等等！不是现在！我需要点时间准备。你知道的，带些药水，换身更好的装备。这趟可不容易。"

    old "I guess that makes sense. But please, don't wait too long. As much as I hate to admit it, I can't do this alone."
    new "I guess that makes sense. But please, don't wait too long. As much as I hate to admit it, I can't do this alone.\n也有道理。但请你别拖太久。尽管我很不愿意承认，可这事我一个人办不成。"

    old "I'll try to be back soon, Sylrissa."
    new "I'll try to be back soon, Sylrissa.\n我会尽快回来的，Sylrissa。"

    old "I'll be here waiting for you."
    new "I'll be here waiting for you.\n我会在这里等你。"

    old "I reach the usual spot to find Sylrissa already waiting for me. The first thing I notice is that she's already equipped for battle and ready to leave."
    new "I reach the usual spot to find Sylrissa already waiting for me. The first thing I notice is that she's already equipped for battle and ready to leave.\n我到了老地方，发现Sylrissa已经在等我了。我注意到的第一件事，就是她已全副武装，随时准备出发。"

    old "I suppose you want to leave immediately."
    new "I suppose you want to leave immediately.\n我想你是想马上出发。"

    old "Indeed. I haven't had any more visions since last time we spoke and I'm growing impatient."
    new "Indeed. I haven't had any more visions since last time we spoke and I'm growing impatient.\n没错。自上次我们谈过之后，我再没看到过幻象，我越来越等不及了。"

    old "I understand. But please, listen to me first. We don't know the area well as the lizardmen. We need to be careful, okay?"
    new "I understand. But please, listen to me first. We don't know the area well as the lizardmen. We need to be careful, okay?\n我理解。但请你先听我说。我们对那一带的了解远不如lizardmen。我们必须小心行事，好吗？"

    old "I will be you shadow. You won't even notice me."
    new "I will be you shadow. You won't even notice me.\n我会成为你的影子。你甚至都察觉不到我。"

    old "Good. However, since you're the one that saw the vision, you're probably the one that should lead the way. Maybe you'll recognize some details as we move north."
    new "Good. However, since you're the one that saw the vision, you're probably the one that should lead the way. Maybe you'll recognize some details as we move north.\n好。不过，既然看到幻象的是你，大概也该由你来带路。也许我们往北走时，你会认出某些细节。"

    old "Ah, that makes sense. Alright. Follow me closely."
    new "Ah, that makes sense. Alright. Follow me closely.\n啊，有道理。好。跟紧我。"

    old "We start walking and, after several hours, the jungle scenery gradually replaces the swamp's. Curiously, there is no fog here. This area seems completely unaffected by whatever magic is behind N'Mar."
    new "We start walking and, after several hours, the jungle scenery gradually replaces the swamp's. Curiously, there is no fog here. This area seems completely unaffected by whatever magic is behind N'Mar.\n我们开始赶路。几个小时后，丛林景色逐渐取代了沼泽风光。奇怪的是，这里没有雾。这片区域似乎完全不受N'Mar背后那股魔法的影响。"

    old "Is something wrong?"
    new "Is something wrong?\n有什么不对劲吗？"

    old "No. Not exactly. I just noticed that there's no fog here."
    new "No. Not exactly. I just noticed that there's no fog here.\n不。也不完全是。我只是注意到，这里没有雾。"

    old "Hm. You're right. I wonder why?"
    new "Hm. You're right. I wonder why?\n嗯。你说得对。不知道是为什么？"

    old "Who knows? Maybe since the lizardmen worship the god of death, they're immune? Or maybe whoever is behind N'Mar isn't interested in conquering or corrupting this area."
    new "Who knows? Maybe since the lizardmen worship the god of death, they're immune? Or maybe whoever is behind N'Mar isn't interested in conquering or corrupting this area.\n谁知道呢？也许因为lizardmen崇拜死神，所以对雾免疫？又或者，N'Mar背后的黑手对征服或腐化这片区域不感兴趣。"

    old "After more walking, we can see the Chzulu temple in the distance. It's large size makes it impossible to miss. We must be close to the place in Sylrissa's vision."
    new "After more walking, we can see the Chzulu temple in the distance. It's large size makes it impossible to miss. We must be close to the place in Sylrissa's vision.\n又走了一段路，我们已能望见远处的Chzulu神庙。它规模宏大，想看不见都难。我们一定离Sylrissa幻象中的那个地方很近了。"

    old "We make our way up a small hill to get a better view of the surroundings but before I reach the top, Sylrissa puts her arm out in front of me, effectively blocking me from moving forward. I shiver as her soft skin brushes my arm."
    new "We make our way up a small hill to get a better view of the surroundings but before I reach the top, Sylrissa puts her arm out in front of me, effectively blocking me from moving forward. I shiver as her soft skin brushes my arm.\n我们爬上一座小山，想看清周围的地形，可还没等我到山顶，Sylrissa就把手臂横在我面前，硬是拦住了我前进的脚步。她柔软的皮肤擦过我的手臂，我微微一颤。"

    old "There. That tent."
    new "There. That tent.\n那儿。那顶帐篷。"

    old "It's the one you saw? Are you sure?"
    new "It's the one you saw? Are you sure?\n就是你看到的那顶？你确定吗？"

    old "No, I am not. But look, red lizardmen."
    new "No, I am not. But look, red lizardmen.\n不，我不确定。可是你看，红色的lizardmen。"

    old "Devourers! I count at least 3 of them."
    new "Devourers! I count at least 3 of them.\nDevourers！我数了数，至少有3只。"

    old "It could just be a coincidence, but I doubt it. There aren't that many devourers around. I think it's worth investigating."
    new "It could just be a coincidence, but I doubt it. There aren't that many devourers around. I think it's worth investigating.\n也许只是巧合，但我很怀疑。附近的devourers可不多。我觉得值得一查。"

    old "The good news is that the encampment is quite far from the others. That should give us some time before reinforcements are able to arrive if things go terribly wrong for us."
    new "The good news is that the encampment is quite far from the others. That should give us some time before reinforcements are able to arrive if things go terribly wrong for us.\n好消息是，这处营地离其他营地相当远。要是一旦出了大岔子，这应该能给我们争取到援军赶到前的时间。"

    old "Yes, but remember that if this isn't the right place and we blow our cover, it'll be too dangerous to come back."
    new "Yes, but remember that if this isn't the right place and we blow our cover, it'll be too dangerous to come back.\n是的，但记住，如果这里不是要找的地方，而我们的行踪又暴露了，那再想回来就太危险了。"

    old "Damn. I don't know what to do. We have only have one real shot at this and if Enok isn't in that tent..."
    new "Damn. I don't know what to do. We have only have one real shot at this and if Enok isn't in that tent...\n该死。我不知道该怎么办。我们只有这一次真正出手的机会，要是Enok不在那个帐篷里……"

    old "She looks seriously worried. I know she's hoping that I'll be able to come up with a solution, but that's easier said than done. I guess the first step is getting more information. What's the best way to do that though?"
    new "She looks seriously worried. I know she's hoping that I'll be able to come up with a solution, but that's easier said than done. I guess the first step is getting more information. What's the best way to do that though?\n她看起来忧心忡忡。我知道她希望我能想出个办法，可说比做容易。我想第一步是获取更多情报。但最好的方式又是什么呢？"

    old "I say we get closer to the camp. Maybe hide behind a rock, eavesdrop."
    new "I say we get closer to the camp. Maybe hide behind a rock, eavesdrop.\n我说我们靠近那营地。也许躲到岩石后面，偷听一下。"

    old "Missha Takaka-na."
    new "Missha Takaka-na.\nMissha Takaka-na。"

    old "It means 'suck my balls' in lizardmen."
    new "It means 'suck my balls' in lizardmen.\n在lizardmen语里，意思是“舔我的蛋蛋”。"

    old "And... you're telling me this exactly why?"
    new "And... you're telling me this exactly why?\n而且……你告诉我这个，究竟是为什么？"

    old "Because it's the only phrase I know in lizard. So, unless you know how to speak lizard fluently, what's the benefit of eavesdropping on them?"
    new "Because it's the only phrase I know in lizard. So, unless you know how to speak lizard fluently, what's the benefit of eavesdropping on them?\n因为这是我会的唯一一句蜥蜴语。所以，除非你能流利地说蜥蜴语，不然偷听他们说话有什么用？"

    old "...fair point."
    new "...fair point.\n……说得在理。"

    old "Still. I guess it's possible to get some kind of clue. Maybe they know a bit of the common tongue so that they can communicate with prisoners."
    new "Still. I guess it's possible to get some kind of clue. Maybe they know a bit of the common tongue so that they can communicate with prisoners.\n不过，我想还是有可能找到些线索的。也许他们会一点通用语，好跟俘虏沟通。"

    old "In any case, it's bound to be better than staying hidden up here."
    new "In any case, it's bound to be better than staying hidden up here.\n不管怎样，总比一直躲在这儿强。"

    old "That decided, Sylrissa and I quietly move down the hill. We then duck behind a boulder that's large enough to hide us from the lizardmen. At least, we hope."
    new "That decided, Sylrissa and I quietly move down the hill. We then duck behind a boulder that's large enough to hide us from the lizardmen. At least, we hope.\n打定主意后，我和Sylrissa悄悄下了山。然后我们躲到一块大石头后面，那石头大得足以挡住lizardmen的视线。至少，我们希望如此。"

    old "<whispering> Hear anything?"
    new "<whispering> Hear anything?\n<whispering> 听到什么了吗？"

    old "<whispering> No."
    new "<whispering> No.\n<whispering> 没有。"

    old "We settle in and play the waiting game. We're only there for several minutes, but those minutes seem like an eternity. Finally, someone speaks. Unfortunately, it's more lizard language. We have to wait a bit longer before our efforts are rewarded."
    new "We settle in and play the waiting game. We're only there for several minutes, but those minutes seem like an eternity. Finally, someone speaks. Unfortunately, it's more lizard language. We have to wait a bit longer before our efforts are rewarded.\n我们安顿下来，开始静静等待。我们在那儿只待了几分钟，那几分钟却漫长得像永恒。终于，有人开口了。可惜说的还是蜥蜴语。我们还得再等上一会儿，努力才会有回报。"

    old "The naga battlemage. I heard some rumors that you captured him."
    new "The naga battlemage. I heard some rumors that you captured him.\n那个naga战斗法师。我听到些传言，说你们抓住了他。"

    old "<whispering> I know this voice!"
    new "<whispering> I know this voice!\n<whispering> 我认得这个声音！"

    old "Hmm. Yaya. We have. That tent, there."
    new "Hmm. Yaya. We have. That tent, there.\n唔。呀呀。是抓到了。那个帐篷，就在那儿。"

    old "Strangely enough, I don't need to hold Sylrissa still. She seems to be waiting for that mysterious voice to talk again."
    new "Strangely enough, I don't need to hold Sylrissa still. She seems to be waiting for that mysterious voice to talk again.\n说来奇怪，我根本不用按住Sylrissa。她似乎在等着那个神秘的声音再次开口。"

    old "How much?"
    new "How much?\n多少钱？"

    old "Not for sale."
    new "Not for sale.\n不卖。"

    old "I didn't come all the way here to go back empty handed. There may be three of you, but I'm a naga blademaster. I can kill you all without breaking a sweat."
    new "I didn't come all the way here to go back empty handed. There may be three of you, but I'm a naga blademaster. I can kill you all without breaking a sweat.\n我大老远跑过来，可不想空手而归。你们是有三个人，可我是naga剑术大师。把你们全杀了都不带流汗的。"

    old "<whispering> It's him! I knew that voice was familiar!"
    new "<whispering> It's him! I knew that voice was familiar!\n<whispering> 是他！我就说这声音耳熟！"

    old "<whispering> Who is he?"
    new "<whispering> Who is he?\n<whispering> 他是谁？"

    old "<whispering> Hazel. One of the best naga fighters. He trained me personally."
    new "<whispering> Hazel. One of the best naga fighters. He trained me personally.\n<whispering> 是Hazel。最顶尖的naga战士之一。他亲自训练过我。"

    old "<whispering> What he is doing here? It sounds like he wants Enok, but why?"
    new "<whispering> What he is doing here? It sounds like he wants Enok, but why?\n<whispering> 他在这儿做什么？听起来他想要Enok，可为什么呢？"

    old "<whispering> He wants to kill Enok. And me too. Remember what I told you when we first met? We escaped our tribe and the usual punishment for that is death."
    new "<whispering> He wants to kill Enok. And me too. Remember what I told you when we first met? We escaped our tribe and the usual punishment for that is death.\n<whispering> 他想杀了Enok，还有我。还记得我们初次见面时我跟你说过的吗？我们逃离了部落，而逃族的惯例惩罚就是处死。"

    old "Our discussion is interrupted by the sound of swords! They're fighting!"
    new "Our discussion is interrupted by the sound of swords! They're fighting!\n我们的谈话被剑刃交击之声打断！他们打起来了！"

    old "This is our chance! We must run and free Enok!"
    new "This is our chance! We must run and free Enok!\n机会来了！我们得冲过去救出Enok！"

    old "Sylrissa nods, and she jumps out from behind the rock. Both the naga and the lizardmen turn to her, surprised. While she has their attention, I run towards the tent..."
    new "Sylrissa nods, and she jumps out from behind the rock. Both the naga and the lizardmen turn to her, surprised. While she has their attention, I run towards the tent...\nSylrissa点点头，从石头后面跳了出去。那个naga和lizardmen都惊讶地转向她。趁她吸引住他们的注意，我朝帐篷跑去……"

    old "Are you sure? There are 4 lizardmen, plus Hazel."
    new "Are you sure? There are 4 lizardmen, plus Hazel.\n你确定吗？那儿有4个lizardmen，再加上Hazel。"

    old "I am a powerful [manwoman], Sylrissa. You should know that by now. Anyway, I should be able to break through them and run inside the tent. You only need to keep them off my tail for a minute."
    new "I am a powerful [manwoman], Sylrissa. You should know that by now. Anyway, I should be able to break through them and run inside the tent. You only need to keep them off my tail for a minute.\n我可是个强大的[manwoman]，Sylrissa。到如今你应该知道了。总之，我应当能冲破他们，跑进帐篷。你只需要帮我拖住他们一分钟。"

    old "I make my entrance on the scene, catching everyone by surprise. As they're focusing on me, I see Sylrissa starting to sneak in behind them."
    new "I make my entrance on the scene, catching everyone by surprise. As they're focusing on me, I see Sylrissa starting to sneak in behind them.\n我在现场登场，惊得所有人措手不及。趁他们都把注意力集中在我身上，我看见Sylrissa开始从他们身后悄悄潜入。"

    old "I run and push the two lizardmen to the ground before they can react. With a quick change of direction, I'm able to avoid Hazel's attack. From there, I start running full speed towards the tent..."
    new "I run and push the two lizardmen to the ground before they can react. With a quick change of direction, I'm able to avoid Hazel's attack. From there, I start running full speed towards the tent...\n我冲上前，趁两个lizardmen还没反应过来就把他们扑倒在地。紧接着一个急转，躲开了Hazel的攻击。从那之后，我开始全速冲向帐篷……"

    old "...and I manage to get inside! I immediately spot Enok on the ground, tied and gagged as in Sylrissa's suspected from her vision. I quickly free him."
    new "...and I manage to get inside! I immediately spot Enok on the ground, tied and gagged as in Sylrissa's suspected from her vision. I quickly free him.\n……而我成功冲了进去！我立刻看到Enok倒在地上，被绑着、堵着嘴，正如Sylrissa从幻象中推测的那样。我赶紧给他松绑。"

    old "...however, I trip over something on the ground and fall down, close to Sylrissa."
    new "...however, I trip over something on the ground and fall down, close to Sylrissa.\n……然而，我被地上的什么东西绊了一下，摔倒了，正好摔在Sylrissa附近。"

    old "Normally I like when people fall at my 'feet' but this isn't exactly the best time for that!"
    new "Normally I like when people fall at my 'feet' but this isn't exactly the best time for that!\n平时我挺喜欢有人拜倒在我“脚下”的，可现在真不是时候！"

    old "Sylrissa! After all this time, I finally find you. It's time to end this once for all."
    new "Sylrissa! After all this time, I finally find you. It's time to end this once for all.\nSylrissa！找了这么久，我终于找到你了。是时候把这一切做个了断了。"

    old "Behind you!"
    new "Behind you!\n你身后！"

    old "Hazel flips back with his blades and kills two lizardmen. Unfortunately for him, he's not quite fast enough to avoid their weapons. The lizardmens' spears skewer Hazel and I can tell that these are wounds he won't be recovering from."
    new "Hazel flips back with his blades and kills two lizardmen. Unfortunately for him, he's not quite fast enough to avoid their weapons. The lizardmens' spears skewer Hazel and I can tell that these are wounds he won't be recovering from.\nHazel挥动双刃一个后翻，砍死了两个lizardmen。可惜他还是不够快，没能躲开对方的武器。lizardmen的长矛刺穿了Hazel，我看得出，这些伤他是挺不过去了。"

    old "Blugh... this isn't fair...it should have been a fight between the three of us..."
    new "Blugh... this isn't fair...it should have been a fight between the three of us...\n呸……这不公平……这本该是我们三人之间的一场决斗……"

    old "...I'm sorry, Hazel. I'd have liked to fight you fairly as well."
    new "...I'm sorry, Hazel. I'd have liked to fight you fairly as well.\n……对不起，Hazel。我也希望能跟你堂堂正正地打一场。"

    old "I... I..."
    new "I... I...\n我……我……"

    old "He's dead. Go, [protag]! Before more lizardmen come! I'll keep these ones at bay!"
    new "He's dead. Go, [protag]! Before more lizardmen come! I'll keep these ones at bay!\n他死了。快去，[protag]！趁更多lizardmen赶到之前！这几个我来挡住！"

    old "Remembering the mission, I run inside and find Enok. He is on the ground, tied and gagged exactly as Sylrissa suspected from her vision. I quickly free him."
    new "Remembering the mission, I run inside and find Enok. He is on the ground, tied and gagged exactly as Sylrissa suspected from her vision. I quickly free him.\n想起此行的任务，我冲进里面找到了Enok。他倒在地上，被绑着、堵着嘴，跟Sylrissa从幻象中推测的一模一样。我赶紧给他松绑。"

    old "It seems my little trick worked. Thank you, [protag]! I started to think-"
    new "It seems my little trick worked. Thank you, [protag]! I started to think-\n看来我的小把戏奏效了。谢谢你，[protag]！我都开始以为——"

    old "There's no time! We'll talk later, we need to get out of here now!"
    new "There's no time! We'll talk later, we need to get out of here now!\n没时间了！回头再说，我们现在必须离开这里！"

    old "Right. Let me just fix my... tail problem."
    new "Right. Let me just fix my... tail problem.\n好。先让我解决一下……尾巴的问题。"

    old "Enok begins casting a regeneration spell. It starts working instantly and, in less than a minute, Enok's tail has recovered completely."
    new "Enok begins casting a regeneration spell. It starts working instantly and, in less than a minute, Enok's tail has recovered completely.\nEnok开始施放再生法术。法术立刻生效，不到一分钟，Enok的尾巴就完全长好了。"

    old "Enok then grabs his staff and gets up, saying:"
    new "Enok then grabs his staff and gets up, saying:\n随后Enok抓起法杖站起身来，说道："

    old "I'm ready now. Let's go."
    new "I'm ready now. Let's go.\n我准备好了。我们走。"

    old "When we exit the tent, we immediately notice that most of the lizardmen are dead, their bodies strewn about the camp in a grotesque fashion. Sylrissa is still holding her ground, but I notice a trickle of blood running down her side as she faces Hazel and two remaining lizardmen. We need to help her!"
    new "When we exit the tent, we immediately notice that most of the lizardmen are dead, their bodies strewn about the camp in a grotesque fashion. Sylrissa is still holding her ground, but I notice a trickle of blood running down her side as she faces Hazel and two remaining lizardmen. We need to help her!\n我们一出帐篷，就发现大部分lizardmen已经死了，尸体横七竖八地散落在营地各处，景象可怖。Sylrissa仍在坚守阵地，但我注意到她面对Hazel和剩下的两个lizardmen时，身侧淌下一道血痕。我们必须去帮她！"

    old "We go outside, just in time to help Sylrissa who is trying her best to keep four lizardmen at bay."
    new "We go outside, just in time to help Sylrissa who is trying her best to keep four lizardmen at bay.\n我们赶到外面，正好赶上帮Sylrissa——她正拼命抵挡四个lizardmen。"

    old "Finally! These devourers really are formidable opponents!"
    new "Finally! These devourers really are formidable opponents!\n终于来了！这些devourers还真是难缠的对手！"

    old "What? We need to get closer!"
    new "What? We need to get closer!\n什么？我们得靠得更近些！"

    old "Trust me. If we get close, we might hear something useful, but it's more likely that we'll just end up being spotted. I don't need to remind you what happens if they catch us."
    new "Trust me. If we get close, we might hear something useful, but it's more likely that we'll just end up being spotted. I don't need to remind you what happens if they catch us.\n相信我。我们靠得近了，也许能听到些有用的，但更可能是我们反而暴露了自己。被他们抓住会有什么下场，不用我提醒你吧。"

    old "Hmm. I don't like it. I hate the idea of just standing here while Enok's life is in danger."
    new "Hmm. I don't like it. I hate the idea of just standing here while Enok's life is in danger.\n嗯。我不喜欢这样。我讨厌就这么干站着，看着Enok身处险境。"

    old "I don't like it either, but if we move hastily-"
    new "I don't like it either, but if we move hastily-\n我也不喜欢，可要是我们贸然行动——"

    old "Stand down! Someone is coming."
    new "Stand down! Someone is coming.\n别动！有人来了。"

    old "I follow her gaze to see another naga, alone, approaching the camp from the same path we took to get here."
    new "I follow her gaze to see another naga, alone, approaching the camp from the same path we took to get here.\n我顺着她的目光望去，看见另一个naga独自一人，正沿着我们来时的那条路朝营地走来。"

    old "Wait...Hazel?!"
    new "Wait...Hazel?!\n等等……Hazel？！"

    old "You know him?"
    new "You know him?\n你认识他？"

    old "Yeah..."
    new "Yeah...\n认识……"

    old "It's kind of a long story. I told you that we left the naga community, right? Well, what Enok and I did is considered treason and the usual punishment for treason is death."
    new "It's kind of a long story. I told you that we left the naga community, right? Well, what Enok and I did is considered treason and the usual punishment for treason is death.\n说来话长。我跟你说过我们离开了naga社群，对吧？嗯，Enok和我做的事被视为叛逃，而叛逃的惯例惩罚就是处死。"

    old "And that guy, Hazel, has held a grudge against both of us for a long time now. He's an excellent fighter too. If he knew we were here, he'd definitely try to kill us."
    new "And that guy, Hazel, has held a grudge against both of us for a long time now. He's an excellent fighter too. If he knew we were here, he'd definitely try to kill us.\n而那个Hazel，早就对我们俩怀恨在心了。他还是个出色的战士。要是他知道我们在这儿，肯定会对我们下杀手。"

    old "But he doesn't know we're here, right? Do you think he followed us?"
    new "But he doesn't know we're here, right? Do you think he followed us?\n但他不知道我们在这儿，对吧？你觉得他是跟踪我们来的？"

    old "I doubt it. We've been careful. I think he is headed to the camp. Yes, see? He's not changing course."
    new "I doubt it. We've been careful. I think he is headed to the camp. Yes, see? He's not changing course.\n我怀疑不是。我们一直很小心。我想他是要去营地。看，是吧？他都没有改道。"

    old "This is good news! If he's here that must mean that Enok is too. It's the only reason he'd be here in lizardman territory!"
    new "This is good news! If he's here that must mean that Enok is too. It's the only reason he'd be here in lizardman territory!\n这是好消息！他出现在这儿，说明Enok一定也在这儿。这是他出现在lizardman地盘上的唯一理由！"

    old "Hmm. This is interesting. The lizardmen won't hand Enok over peacefully. I think we could use this to our advantage."
    new "Hmm. This is interesting. The lizardmen won't hand Enok over peacefully. I think we could use this to our advantage.\n嗯。有意思。lizardmen不会乖乖交出Enok。我想我们可以利用这一点。"

    old "Really? How?"
    new "Really? How?\n真的？怎么利用？"

    old "He doesn't know me. I could convince him to help us, involuntarily. You said he is a good fighter, right?"
    new "He doesn't know me. I could convince him to help us, involuntarily. You said he is a good fighter, right?\n他不认识我。我可以“说服”他帮我们——让他自己都没察觉。你说他是个好战士，对吧？"

    old "I think I can fool him using my wits."
    new "I think I can fool him using my wits.\n我想凭我的聪明才智骗过他。"

    old "Meanwhile, you can sneak inside the tent and free Enok. Once he's healed, join us and we'll kill everyone. Hazel too, if needed."
    new "Meanwhile, you can sneak inside the tent and free Enok. Once he's healed, join us and we'll kill everyone. Hazel too, if needed.\n与此同时，你潜入帐篷救出Enok。等他恢复过来，就过来跟我们汇合，我们把所有人全干掉。必要的话，Hazel也别放过。"

    old "Hm. It might work. Be careful though, [protag]. Hazel is not stupid."
    new "Hm. It might work. Be careful though, [protag]. Hazel is not stupid.\n嗯。也许行得通。不过要当心，[protag]。Hazel可不蠢。"

    old "I'll tell him that I want Enok too and that the lizardmen are about to kill him. That should be enough to get him to help me take out the lizardmen."
    new "I'll tell him that I want Enok too and that the lizardmen are about to kill him. That should be enough to get him to help me take out the lizardmen.\n我会告诉他，我也想要Enok，而lizardmen马上就要杀了他。这应该足以让他帮我对付那些lizardmen。"

    old "Well, he is known for being hot-headed. He could easily lose his temper if you tell him that. You'll need to be convincing though."
    new "Well, he is known for being hot-headed. He could easily lose his temper if you tell him that. You'll need to be convincing though.\n嗯，他可是出了名的火爆脾气。你这么一说，他很可能就炸了。不过你得演得够像才行。"

    old "I'll do my best. Meanwhile, you'll sneak into the tent and rescue Enok."
    new "I'll do my best. Meanwhile, you'll sneak into the tent and rescue Enok.\n我会尽力的。与此同时，你溜进帐篷救出Enok。"

    old "Are we clear?"
    new "Are we clear?\n我们说定了？"

    old "Yes. Let's just hope that Enok is really inside that tent. Even if every detail seems to match, it still might not be..."
    new "Yes. Let's just hope that Enok is really inside that tent. Even if every detail seems to match, it still might not be...\n说定了。只希望Enok真的在那顶帐篷里。就算每个细节都对得上，也仍有可能不是……"

    old "There's only one way to find out, right? Let's go."
    new "There's only one way to find out, right? Let's go.\n要弄清，只有一条路可走，对吧？我们走。"

    old "I take a shortcut and pretend to stumble randomly into Hazel. As soon as he sees me, he draws his sword, ready to attack."
    new "I take a shortcut and pretend to stumble randomly into Hazel. As soon as he sees me, he draws his sword, ready to attack.\n我抄了近道，假装不小心撞上了Hazel。他一看见我，就拔剑出鞘，准备动手。"

    old "Easy now. There's no need to fight. Actually, this might even be a fortunate turn of events seeing as I could definitely use a hand here."
    new "Easy now. There's no need to fight. Actually, this might even be a fortunate turn of events seeing as I could definitely use a hand here.\n放轻松。没必要动武。其实，这说不定还是件走运的事，因为我正需要人搭把手。"

    old "You want me to help you?"
    new "You want me to help you?\n你要我帮你？"

    old "I would appreciate it. You see, there's another naga here named Enok. He's being held prisoner in that tent over there."
    new "I would appreciate it. You see, there's another naga here named Enok. He's being held prisoner in that tent over there.\n那我感激不尽。你看，这儿还有个叫Enok的naga。他被关在那边的帐篷里。"

    old "Interesting. I'm listening."
    new "Interesting. I'm listening.\n有意思。我在听。"

    old "He owes my employer a large sum of money and I'm here to get it back."
    new "He owes my employer a large sum of money and I'm here to get it back.\n他欠我雇主一大笔钱，我是来讨债的。"

    old "A debt collector I suppose?"
    new "A debt collector I suppose?\n我猜，你是收债的？"

    old "You see, I'm a merchant. Enok stole from my caravan a few weeks ago. Most of the goods were replaceable, but he also took a family heirloom of mine. It has a great deal of sentimental value to me and I need to get it back."
    new "You see, I'm a merchant. Enok stole from my caravan a few weeks ago. Most of the goods were replaceable, but he also took a family heirloom of mine. It has a great deal of sentimental value to me and I need to get it back.\n你看，我是个商人。几周前，Enok偷了我的商队。大部分货物丢了还能再补，可他还拿走了我家的一件传家宝。那东西对我意义重大，我必须拿回来。"

    old "I'm a bard. I ventured up here to get some inspiration for my next ballad, the dancing lizard, and ended up overhearing some of the lizardmen talking about him. From what I heard, he seems like someone I'd like to talk to."
    new "I'm a bard. I ventured up here to get some inspiration for my next ballad, the dancing lizard, and ended up overhearing some of the lizardmen talking about him. From what I heard, he seems like someone I'd like to talk to.\n我是个吟游诗人。我冒险跑到这儿来，是想为我下一首叙事诗《跳舞的蜥蜴》找点灵感，结果偶然听到几个lizardmen在谈论他。从我听到的来看，他像是个我想聊上一聊的人。"

    old "Enok is a powerful battlemage. I'm of the order of the Sanctimonious Mages from Haros and it's my duty is to make sure that Enok cannot harm anyone in future."
    new "Enok is a powerful battlemage. I'm of the order of the Sanctimonious Mages from Haros and it's my duty is to make sure that Enok cannot harm anyone in future.\nEnok是个强大的战斗法师。我出身Haros的Sanctimonious Mages修会，我的职责就是确保Enok今后无法再伤害任何人。"

    old "What? Another naga? Don't you dare try to stop me!"
    new "What? Another naga? Don't you dare try to stop me!\n什么？又来一个naga？你休想拦我！"

    old "Stop you, from what?"
    new "Stop you, from what?\n拦你？拦你做什么？"

    old "Enok! I need answers from him! And I'm not letting some stupid lizardmen kill him first!"
    new "Enok! I need answers from him! And I'm not letting some stupid lizardmen kill him first!\nEnok！我得从他那儿问出答案！我可不会让那些蠢lizardmen先把他杀了！"

    old "Kill him? The lizardmen have him?"
    new "Kill him? The lizardmen have him?\n杀他？lizardmen抓了他？"

    old "Yes, they're holding him in that camp straight ahead!"
    new "Yes, they're holding him in that camp straight ahead!\n没错，他们就把他关在正前方那个营地里！"

    old "Hmm. That matches up with my own information."
    new "Hmm. That matches up with my own information.\n嗯。这跟我自己的情报吻合。"

    old "It's the truth. So if you're one of his friend trying to stop me..."
    new "It's the truth. So if you're one of his friend trying to stop me...\n这是实话。所以，如果你是他朋友，想拦我……"

    old "I'm not. I want him dead."
    new "I'm not. I want him dead.\n我不是。我要他死。"

    old "Oh."
    new "Oh.\n哦。"

    old "Well, good! Perhaps we can come to an arrangement then. He has some information that I need so I have to talk to him first, but after that I don't care what happens to him. If you want to kill him, kill him."
    new "Well, good! Perhaps we can come to an arrangement then. He has some information that I need so I have to talk to him first, but after that I don't care what happens to him. If you want to kill him, kill him.\n好，很好！那我们也许可以谈个条件。他身上有我需要的情报，所以我得先跟他谈谈，谈完之后他怎么样我都不在乎。你想杀他就杀吧。"

    old "I remain silent, waiting for Hazel to say something. Then he speaks up."
    new "I remain silent, waiting for Hazel to say something. Then he speaks up.\n我保持沉默，等Hazel开口。随后他说话了。"

    old "You know, I've always been good at telling when people are lying to me."
    new "You know, I've always been good at telling when people are lying to me.\n你知道，我一直很擅长分辨别人有没有在骗我。"

    old "And you, you're telling me the truth. And, as much as I hate to admit it, I could use a hand with those lizardmen. You're welcome to join me, but remember, Enok is mine."
    new "And you, you're telling me the truth. And, as much as I hate to admit it, I could use a hand with those lizardmen. You're welcome to join me, but remember, Enok is mine.\n而你，你说的是实话。而且，尽管我不愿承认，对付那些lizardmen我还真需要个帮手。欢迎你加入我，但记住，Enok是我的。"

    old "Sounds good. As long as I get to talk with him first, I have no issue with that."
    new "Sounds good. As long as I get to talk with him first, I have no issue with that.\n听起来不错。只要我能先跟他谈谈，我对此没有异议。"

    old "Our alliance formed, we move towards the camp. Seeing as Hazel makes no effort to hide himself, I have to assume that his plan doesn't involve being stealthy."
    new "Our alliance formed, we move towards the camp. Seeing as Hazel makes no effort to hide himself, I have to assume that his plan doesn't involve being stealthy.\n结盟之后，我们朝营地进发。既然Hazel丝毫不想隐藏自己，我只能假定他的计划里没有“隐蔽”这一项。"

    old "Where's Enok? Show him to me now or die!"
    new "Where's Enok? Show him to me now or die!\nEnok在哪儿？马上把他交出来，不然就死！"

    old "I pretend to join him, but I keep my distance. Hazel's direct approach attracts three lizardmen to him. The fourth one is a bit sharper and manages to spot me. Still, I guess I can't complain. Fighting one is better than fighting four."
    new "I pretend to join him, but I keep my distance. Hazel's direct approach attracts three lizardmen to him. The fourth one is a bit sharper and manages to spot me. Still, I guess I can't complain. Fighting one is better than fighting four.\n我假装与他并肩作战，但始终和他保持距离。Hazel这种直来直去的打法引来了三个lizardmen。第四个机灵些，发现了我的踪迹。不过，我也没什么可抱怨的。打一个总比打四个强。"

    old "And I only need to hold out until Sylrissa rescues Enok. Hopefully, that's sooner than later."
    new "And I only need to hold out until Sylrissa rescues Enok. Hopefully, that's sooner than later.\n而且我只要撑到Sylrissa救出Enok就行了。但愿越快越好。"

    old "I turn and see both Sylrissa and Enok running towards me, killing any lizardmen that cross their path."
    new "I turn and see both Sylrissa and Enok running towards me, killing any lizardmen that cross their path.\n我转过身，看到Sylrissa和Enok一起朝我跑来，一路斩杀挡道的lizardmen。"

    old "By now, Hazel has figured out that I'm not his ally. He backs away from me and tries to rally the lizardmen to his cause."
    new "By now, Hazel has figured out that I'm not his ally. He backs away from me and tries to rally the lizardmen to his cause.\n事到如今，Hazel已经识破我不是他的盟友。他退离我身边，试图鼓动lizardmen跟他联手。"

    old "Stupid lizards, don't you see who your real enemy is?"
    new "Stupid lizards, don't you see who your real enemy is?\n蠢蜥蜴们，你们还看不出谁才是你们真正的敌人吗？"

    old "The lizardmen pause for a moment before deciding that they stand a better chance joining up with Hazel to fight the three of us, even if it's clearly a very temporary alliance."
    new "The lizardmen pause for a moment before deciding that they stand a better chance joining up with Hazel to fight the three of us, even if it's clearly a very temporary alliance.\nlizardmen们迟疑了一下，随即认定跟Hazel联手对付我们三个胜算更大，尽管这显然只是一时权宜的结盟。"

    old "And you... You are definitely lying. Did you really think that I wouldn't spot that bitch Sylrissa up the hill?"
    new "And you... You are definitely lying. Did you really think that I wouldn't spot that bitch Sylrissa up the hill?\n而你……你绝对在撒谎。难道你真以为我会没发现山上的那个该死的Sylrissa？"

    old "Wh-what are you-"
    new "Wh-what are you-\n你、你在说什么——"

    old "Silence! Nobody gets away with trying to fool me!"
    new "Silence! Nobody gets away with trying to fool me!\n闭嘴！敢耍我的人，一个都别想好过！"

    old "Wow. He is angry. And there's no way that his shouts haven't alerted the lizardmen to our presence. This is bad."
    new "Wow. He is angry. And there's no way that his shouts haven't alerted the lizardmen to our presence. This is bad.\n哇。他气坏了。他这么一吼，lizardmen不可能还没察觉到我们的存在。这下糟了。"

    old "I can only hope that Sylrissa is taking advantage of the situation and is freeing Enok right now."
    new "I can only hope that Sylrissa is taking advantage of the situation and is freeing Enok right now.\n我只能寄希望于Sylrissa正利用这个局面，此刻正在救出Enok。"

    old "I start running towards the camp and, as I expected, four lizardmen charge towards us."
    new "I start running towards the camp and, as I expected, four lizardmen charge towards us.\n我开始朝营地跑去，正如我所料，四个lizardmen向我们冲了过来。"

    old "I'll kill you all!"
    new "I'll kill you all!\n我要把你们全杀了！"

    old "I am surrounded, on one side there's Hazel and, on the other, four lizardmen. I don't think I'll be able to hold them off until Sylrissa can help me either. This might really be the end for me."
    new "I am surrounded, on one side there's Hazel and, on the other, four lizardmen. I don't think I'll be able to hold them off until Sylrissa can help me either. This might really be the end for me.\n我被包围了，一边是Hazel，另一边是四个lizardmen。我怕是也撑不到Sylrissa来帮我了。这回可能真的要完了。"

    old "Just as I think it's over, a blazing ball of fire bursts from the direction of the tent. Two of the lizardmen scream as they're skin begins to crackle under flames as the spell burns them alive."
    new "Just as I think it's over, a blazing ball of fire bursts from the direction of the tent. Two of the lizardmen scream as they're skin begins to crackle under flames as the spell burns them alive.\n就在我以为一切都完了的时候，一团炽烈的火球从帐篷方向轰然炸出。两个lizardmen惨叫着，皮肤在烈焰下噼啪作响，被那法术活活烧死。"

    old "Enok! You're free!"
    new "Enok! You're free!\nEnok！你自由了！"

    old "Indeed, I am. I thought the least I could do is give you a warm welcome."
    new "Indeed, I am. I thought the least I could do is give you a warm welcome.\n没错，我自由了。我想我至少得给你来个“热情”的欢迎。"

    old "I see also Sylrissa coming behind him. They both turn their gaze to Hazel."
    new "I see also Sylrissa coming behind him. They both turn their gaze to Hazel.\n我还看见Sylrissa跟在他身后。两人不约而同地把目光投向Hazel。"

    old "Hazel. Finally we meet. It's time to end this."
    new "Hazel. Finally we meet. It's time to end this.\nHazel。我们终于见面了。是时候做个了断了。"

    old "I take my place next to Enok and Sylrissa. Seeing that the odds have changed, the lizardmen stop and look at the three of us and then at Hazel."
    new "I take my place next to Enok and Sylrissa. Seeing that the odds have changed, the lizardmen stop and look at the three of us and then at Hazel.\n我站到Enok和Sylrissa身旁。眼见形势逆转，lizardmen们停下脚步，看看我们三个，又看看Hazel。"

    old "I have no quarrel with you. I just want the nagas dead. Wait, I stand corrected: the nagas and the [prace] dead!"
    new "I have no quarrel with you. I just want the nagas dead. Wait, I stand corrected: the nagas and the [prace] dead!\n我跟你们无冤无仇。我只想要这两个nagas死。等等，我说错了：是nagas和这个[prace]都该死！"

    old "It looks like I just got onto Hazel's kill list. The lizardmen make their decision and join forces with Hazel to attack us."
    new "It looks like I just got onto Hazel's kill list. The lizardmen make their decision and join forces with Hazel to attack us.\n看来我刚上了Hazel的必杀名单。lizardmen们拿定主意，与Hazel联手向我们发起进攻。"

    old "As the fight ends, we hear more noise off the distance. We killed all of the lizardmen in this small camp, but more are about to come any minute now!"
    new "As the fight ends, we hear more noise off the distance. We killed all of the lizardmen in this small camp, but more are about to come any minute now!\n战斗刚结束，我们就听到远处传来更多动静。我们杀光了这个小营地的所有lizardmen，但更多的援兵随时会到！"

    old "Let's leave this place!"
    new "Let's leave this place!\n我们离开这个地方！"

    old "You don't need to tell me twice."
    new "You don't need to tell me twice.\n用不着你说第二遍。"

    old "I'll make sure that they won't be following us."
    new "I'll make sure that they won't be following us.\n我会确保他们没法跟上来。"

    old "With an incredible effort, Enok casts fire magic, using it to form a high wall of fire behind us and completely blocking off the path. Sure, if they go far enough, they can walk around it, but Enok's wall is more than enough to give us a solid advantage against our pursuers."
    new "With an incredible effort, Enok casts fire magic, using it to form a high wall of fire behind us and completely blocking off the path. Sure, if they go far enough, they can walk around it, but Enok's wall is more than enough to give us a solid advantage against our pursuers.\nEnok拼尽全力施放火焰魔法，在我们身后筑起一道高高的火墙，彻底封住了来路。当然，他们绕得够远也能绕过去，但Enok这道火墙足以让我们在甩开追兵上占尽先机。"

    old "After a few hours spent carefully passing through the swamp, we're back at our usual spot by the river, free of lizardmen and finally able to relax."
    new "After a few hours spent carefully passing through the swamp, we're back at our usual spot by the river, free of lizardmen and finally able to relax.\n小心翼翼地穿过沼泽几个小时后，我们回到了河边那个老地方。没有了lizardmen的威胁，我们终于能松口气了。"

    old "But it was fun! And... Enok is safe now."
    new "But it was fun! And... Enok is safe now.\n不过还是很有趣的！而且……Enok现在安全了。"

    old "I have one question for you, Enok. When I rescued you, you mentioned something about your 'little trick'. I suppose it means that Sylrissa's vision was your doing?"
    new "I have one question for you, Enok. When I rescued you, you mentioned something about your 'little trick'. I suppose it means that Sylrissa's vision was your doing?\n我有个问题想问你，Enok。我救你出来时，你提到了你的“小把戏”。我想，Sylrissa看到的幻象是你的手笔？"

    old "Indeed, it was."
    new "Indeed, it was.\n确实如此。"

    old "Enok is being strangely quiet about it. For someone who likes to brag and talk how awesome he is, it's strange."
    new "Enok is being strangely quiet about it. For someone who likes to brag and talk how awesome he is, it's strange.\nEnok对此反常地沉默。对一个喜欢自吹自擂、总说自己多厉害的人来说，这很反常。"

    old "But how did you cast that spell? You were all tied up. You couldn't use your hands or even speak..."
    new "But how did you cast that spell? You were all tied up. You couldn't use your hands or even speak...\n可你是怎么施法的？你被绑得结结实实。既用不了手，也说不了话……"

    old "That...ahem..."
    new "That...ahem...\n那个……咳咳……"

    old "Enok? [protag] risked [hisher] life to save us! Don't hide anything from us."
    new "Enok? [protag] risked [hisher] life to save us! Don't hide anything from us.\nEnok？[protag]可是冒着[hisher]生命危险来救我们的！别瞒着我们。"

    old "It was... dark magic. It doesn't always work. It requires a powerful link between two people. The other person really need to care about you, must dream about you, for it to work."
    new "It was... dark magic. It doesn't always work. It requires a powerful link between two people. The other person really need to care about you, must dream about you, for it to work.\n是……黑暗魔法。它不总是灵验。它需要两个人之间有很强的联结。对方必须真心在乎你、必须梦见你，法术才会起效。"

    old "What you mean?"
    new "What you mean?\n你什么意思？"

    old "Haha, perhaps [protag] was right then. I really dreamed it."
    new "Haha, perhaps [protag] was right then. I really dreamed it.\n哈哈，那也许[protag]说对了。我确实梦到了。"

    old "Yes, but it's a very vivid dream, seems real. The target person is able to see with your own eyes, albeit for a small fraction of time."
    new "Yes, but it's a very vivid dream, seems real. The target person is able to see with your own eyes, albeit for a small fraction of time.\n是的，不过那是个非常逼真的梦，跟真的一样。被联结的人能借你的眼睛看见东西，尽管只有短短一瞬间。"

    old "A spell you could cast without seeing the target? That's impressive."
    new "A spell you could cast without seeing the target? That's impressive.\n一种不用看见目标就能施放的法术？真了不起。"

    old "I know people have different opinions regarding dark magic, but if I'm alive now, it's only because of it. And you of course. And Sylrissa who dreamed about me."
    new "I know people have different opinions regarding dark magic, but if I'm alive now, it's only because of it. And you of course. And Sylrissa who dreamed about me.\n我知道人们对黑暗魔法看法不一，但如果说我现在还活着，那全是因为它。当然，也因为你。还有梦见我的Sylrissa。"

    old "Sylrissa smiles at Enok, who responds by taking her into a hug. Sylrissa returns the hug by wrapping her own arms around him. Taking a closer look, I spot relieved tears streaming down Enok's face. Even Sylrissa seems touched by this moment."
    new "Sylrissa smiles at Enok, who responds by taking her into a hug. Sylrissa returns the hug by wrapping her own arms around him. Taking a closer look, I spot relieved tears streaming down Enok's face. Even Sylrissa seems touched by this moment.\nSylrissa对Enok微笑，Enok则以一个拥抱回应。Sylrissa也张开双臂回抱住他。仔细一看，我发现Enok脸上淌下了如释重负的泪水。连Sylrissa似乎也被这一刻打动了。"

    old "I'll go ahead and leave now. It looks like you two could use some privacy."
    new "I'll go ahead and leave now. It looks like you two could use some privacy.\n我先走了。看来你们俩需要些独处的空间。"

    old "Wait, [protag]!"
    new "Wait, [protag]!\n等等，[protag]！"

    old "Enok releases Sylrissa and approaches me, a sincere smile on his face. He cups my head with his soft hands and stares into my eyes. He continues to gaze at me steadily, but doesn't say anything."
    new "Enok releases Sylrissa and approaches me, a sincere smile on his face. He cups my head with his soft hands and stares into my eyes. He continues to gaze at me steadily, but doesn't say anything.\nEnok放开Sylrissa，走到我面前，脸上带着真诚的笑容。他用柔软的双手捧起我的脸，凝视着我的眼睛。他就那样静静地看着我，一言不发。"

    old "I don't know why, but it feels like an invitation for me to move closer to him and give him a quick kiss on his cheek. I'm careful to keep the kiss friendly, since I'm unsure how Sylrissa would react to something more forward."
    new "I don't know why, but it feels like an invitation for me to move closer to him and give him a quick kiss on his cheek. I'm careful to keep the kiss friendly, since I'm unsure how Sylrissa would react to something more forward.\n不知为何，那感觉像是在邀请我靠近他，在他脸颊上飞快地亲一下。我小心地让这个吻保持在友好的分寸上，因为我不确定Sylrissa对更进一步的举动会作何反应。"

    old "Enok seems a bit surprised. Now that it's done, I wonder if I misinterpreted the situation."
    new "Enok seems a bit surprised. Now that it's done, I wonder if I misinterpreted the situation.\nEnok似乎有点意外。既然已经做了，我不禁怀疑自己是不是会错了意。"

    old "Sorry, I just-"
    new "Sorry, I just-\n抱歉，我只是——"

    old "There's nothing to apologize for."
    new "There's nothing to apologize for.\n没什么好道歉的。"

    old "I peek behind him and see Sylrissa smiling. Thankfully, she doesn't seem bothered by what I did."
    new "I peek behind him and see Sylrissa smiling. Thankfully, she doesn't seem bothered by what I did.\n我朝他身后瞥了一眼，看到Sylrissa在笑。幸好，她似乎并不介意我方才的举动。"

    old "For a moment I thought was a bad idea and that Sylrissa might have been jealous."
    new "For a moment I thought was a bad idea and that Sylrissa might have been jealous.\n有那么一瞬，我还以为这主意糟透了，Sylrissa可能会吃醋。"

    old "Oh, not at all, [protag]. Nice things are made to be shared, right? And Enok's cheeks are definitely nice."
    new "Oh, not at all, [protag]. Nice things are made to be shared, right? And Enok's cheeks are definitely nice.\n哦，一点也不，[protag]。好东西就是用来分享的，对吧？而且Enok的脸颊确实很棒。"

    old "Well, I guess if you put it that way..."
    new "Well, I guess if you put it that way...\n嗯，你要这么说的话……"

    old "I give Enok a quick hug and then pull back."
    new "I give Enok a quick hug and then pull back.\n我飞快地抱了Enok一下，然后退开。"

    old "Welcome back to the swamps, Enok."
    new "Welcome back to the swamps, Enok.\n欢迎回到沼泽，Enok。"

    old "Ah, the swamps. Home sweet home."
    new "Ah, the swamps. Home sweet home.\n啊，沼泽。甜蜜的家。"

    old "I try to keep my composure, but I guess the idea of someone calling these swamps home is too much. They notice my face and start laughing."
    new "I try to keep my composure, but I guess the idea of someone calling these swamps home is too much. They notice my face and start laughing.\n我努力保持镇定，可大概“有人把这片沼泽称作家”这件事实在太逗了。他们瞧见我的表情，都笑了起来。"

    old "We all laugh and forgive all the stress and sweat of the past few hours. It's nice. Honestly, I wish I got to have more moments like this."
    new "We all laugh and forgive all the stress and sweat of the past few hours. It's nice. Honestly, I wish I got to have more moments like this.\n我们全都笑了起来，把过去几个小时的紧张和汗水都抛到脑后。真好。说实话，我真希望能多拥有一些这样的时刻。"

    old "Thank you for rescuing me, [protag]. I mean it."
    new "Thank you for rescuing me, [protag]. I mean it.\n谢谢你救了我，[protag]。我是认真的。"

    old "You know, there aren't a lot of people who whould go out of their way to rescue someone they barely knew-- especially when they're in the middle of such an important mission."
    new "You know, there aren't a lot of people who whould go out of their way to rescue someone they barely knew-- especially when they're in the middle of such an important mission.\n你知道，没有多少人会费尽周折去救一个几乎不认识的人——尤其是在执行如此重要任务的当口。"

    old "Let's just say that Sylrissa was convincing."
    new "Let's just say that Sylrissa was convincing.\n这么说吧，Sylrissa很有说服力。"

    old "Haha, you like to joke, [protag]. But I am dead serious now. I used to think that Sylrissa was the only one in this whole world that cared about me. But now I see that I was wrong. You have my eternal gratitude, [protag]."
    new "Haha, you like to joke, [protag]. But I am dead serious now. I used to think that Sylrissa was the only one in this whole world that cared about me. But now I see that I was wrong. You have my eternal gratitude, [protag].\n哈哈，你爱开玩笑，[protag]。可我现在是极其认真的。我过去总以为，这世上关心我的只有Sylrissa一人。但现在我明白自己错了。我永远感激你，[protag]。"

    old "I smile and Enok puts one of his hands on my shoulder. With a fierce gaze focused on me he adds:"
    new "I smile and Enok puts one of his hands on my shoulder. With a fierce gaze focused on me he adds:\n我笑了笑，Enok把一只手搭在我肩上。他目光灼灼地盯着我，补充道："

    old "I'm ready to join you and face whatever evil is lurking into N'Mar. From today on, you can count on my help too. Whenever you need me, I'll come help you."
    new "I'm ready to join you and face whatever evil is lurking into N'Mar. From today on, you can count on my help too. Whenever you need me, I'll come help you.\n我准备好加入你，去面对N'Mar里潜伏的邪恶了。从今天起，你也可以指望我的帮助。只要你需要，我随时会来助你。"

    old "Thank you, Enok. I will remember your offer."
    new "Thank you, Enok. I will remember your offer.\n谢谢你，Enok。你的心意我会记住。"

    old "I spend a few more minutes enjoying their company but, eventually, duty calls and I can't justify lingering longer. I leave the two nagas behind for now, knowing that I'll probably be seeing them again soon."
    new "I spend a few more minutes enjoying their company but, eventually, duty calls and I can't justify lingering longer. I leave the two nagas behind for now, knowing that I'll probably be seeing them again soon.\n我又多待了几分钟，享受他们的陪伴，但最终职责在身，我也没理由再久留。我暂时告别这两位nagas，心知大概很快又会见到他们。"

    old "Sylrissa slithers towards me at a startling speed. I instinctively and embarrassingly panic for a moment as she pounces on me. I have to take a step back to avoid being toppled by her hug."
    new "Sylrissa slithers towards me at a startling speed. I instinctively and embarrassingly panic for a moment as she pounces on me. I have to take a step back to avoid being toppled by her hug.\nSylrissa以惊人的速度朝我滑行而来。她朝我扑过来时，我本能地、也狼狈地慌乱了一瞬。我不得不后退一步，免得被她的拥抱扑倒。"

    old "Hello to you too, Sylrissa."
    new "Hello to you too, Sylrissa.\n你也好，Sylrissa。"

    old "Sylrissa responds with an amused chuckle."
    new "Sylrissa responds with an amused chuckle.\nSylrissa以一声好笑的轻笑回应。"

    old "You know, if this is the way you welcome people, I'll have to make a point of coming around more often."
    new "You know, if this is the way you welcome people, I'll have to make a point of coming around more often.\n你知道，要是你都是这样欢迎人的，那我可得多来几趟了。"

    old "Her smile broadens and her amber eyes meet mine as she pulls back, releasing me from her hug."
    new "Her smile broadens and her amber eyes meet mine as she pulls back, releasing me from her hug.\n她退开身子，放开拥抱，笑意更浓，琥珀色的眼眸与我的目光相遇。"

    old "It occurs to me that I've never just taken the time to stop and look at her eyes-- at least, not carefully. Now that I am, I can see that they contain several brilliant shades of mezmerizing yellows and oranges."
    new "It occurs to me that I've never just taken the time to stop and look at her eyes-- at least, not carefully. Now that I am, I can see that they contain several brilliant shades of mezmerizing yellows and oranges.\n我忽然意识到，自己从未真正停下来好好看过她的眼睛——至少没有仔细看过。如今细看之下，我发现她的双眸里交叠着好几种明艳的、令人着迷的黄色与橙色。"

    old "I guess I end up staring a little too long since Sylrissa's happy expression shifts into a concerned one."
    new "I guess I end up staring a little too long since Sylrissa's happy expression shifts into a concerned one.\n大概我盯着看的时间太长了，Sylrissa脸上的笑意渐渐变成了关切。"

    old "What is it? Is something wrong?"
    new "What is it? Is something wrong?\n怎么啦？出什么事了吗？"

    old "Oh, no! Nothing like that. I just..."
    new "Oh, no! Nothing like that. I just...\n哦，没有！不是那样的。我只是……"

    old "W-wait! You mean that? You're not joking?"
    new "W-wait! You mean that? You're not joking?\n等、等等！你是认真的？没开玩笑？"

    old "I'm serious. You have beautiful eyes, Sylrissa."
    new "I'm serious. You have beautiful eyes, Sylrissa.\n我是认真的。你的眼睛很美，Sylrissa。"

    old "Sylrissa grins as a slight blush creeps into her cheeks."
    new "Sylrissa grins as a slight blush creeps into her cheeks.\nSylrissa咧嘴一笑，脸颊泛起淡淡红晕。"

    old "It seems that that small compliment meant a lot to her. I'm glad, of course, but I would've thought that she'd be used to hearing things like that."
    new "It seems that that small compliment meant a lot to her. I'm glad, of course, but I would've thought that she'd be used to hearing things like that.\n看来那一句小小的夸赞对她意义重大。我当然很高兴，不过我原以为她早已习惯听到这样的话。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]! That's the first time anyone has said anything like that to me."
    new "Thank you, [protag]! That's the first time anyone has said anything like that to me.\n谢谢你，[protag]！这还是第一次有人对我说这种话。"

    old "Yes, why?"
    new "Yes, why?\n是啊，怎么？"

    old "I just find that kind of odd. I mean, complimenting someone's physical features is pretty common in a romantic relationship, isn't it?"
    new "I just find that kind of odd. I mean, complimenting someone's physical features is pretty common in a romantic relationship, isn't it?\n我只是觉得这有点奇怪。我是说，夸赞恋人的外貌，在恋爱关系里不是挺常见的吗？"

    old "You must have had at least a few of those in the past. At least, before you left your tribe."
    new "You must have had at least a few of those in the past. At least, before you left your tribe.\n你过去肯定至少有过几段吧。至少在你离开部落之前。"

    old "Even as an [prace], I can see Sylrissa's appeal. I can't imagine her own kind would have overlooked her."
    new "Even as an [prace], I can see Sylrissa's appeal. I can't imagine her own kind would have overlooked her.\n即便身为[prace]，我也能看出Sylrissa的魅力。我无法想象她的同类会无视她。"

    old "Even as a [prace], I can see Sylrissa's appeal. I can't imagine her own kind would have overlooked her."
    new "Even as a [prace], I can see Sylrissa's appeal. I can't imagine her own kind would have overlooked her.\n即便身为[prace]，我也能看出Sylrissa的魅力。我无法想象她的同类会无视她。"

    old "I just noticed that you and Enok have the same eye color."
    new "I just noticed that you and Enok have the same eye color.\n我刚注意到，你和Enok的眼睛是同一种颜色。"

    old "Is it a rare color or do most naga's share that same yellow-orange hue?"
    new "Is it a rare color or do most naga's share that same yellow-orange hue?\n这是种罕见的颜色，还是大多数naga都是这种黄橙色？"

    old "Ah, I see. Orange and yellow are the most common eye colors for nagas. They're are rarer colors like red, violet, blue, gold--"
    new "Ah, I see. Orange and yellow are the most common eye colors for nagas. They're are rarer colors like red, violet, blue, gold--\n啊，原来如此。橙色和黄色是nagas最常见的眼睛颜色。还有些更稀有的颜色，比如红色、紫色、蓝色、金色——"

    old "So a wide variety of colors?"
    new "So a wide variety of colors?\n所以颜色很多样？"

    old "Exactly. But mostly yellow and orange."
    new "Exactly. But mostly yellow and orange.\n正是。不过大多是黄色和橙色。"

    old "So, basically, my eyes aren't that special."
    new "So, basically, my eyes aren't that special.\n所以，基本上，我的眼睛也没那么特别。"

    old "They're still nice though."
    new "They're still nice though.\n不过还是很漂亮。"

    old "Sylrissa smiles slightly at the compliment."
    new "Sylrissa smiles slightly at the compliment.\n听到这夸赞，Sylrissa微微一笑。"

    old "It quickly fades however as Sylrissa shyly tucks a strand of hair behind her ear. Wait... Is she embarrassed?"
    new "It quickly fades however as Sylrissa shyly tucks a strand of hair behind her ear. Wait... Is she embarrassed?\n不过那笑容很快就消失了，Sylrissa羞涩地把一缕头发别到耳后。等等……她是害羞了？"

    old "You know, the way you were looking at my eyes before..."
    new "You know, the way you were looking at my eyes before...\n你知道，你刚才看我的眼神……"

    old "Ah, sorry! I didn't mean to make you uncomfortable."
    new "Ah, sorry! I didn't mean to make you uncomfortable.\n啊，抱歉！我不是故意让你不自在的。"

    old "Oh. No! You have it wrong. It didn't make me uncomfortable. I... Well, I thought it was nice. That sort of thing has never happened to me before."
    new "Oh. No! You have it wrong. It didn't make me uncomfortable. I... Well, I thought it was nice. That sort of thing has never happened to me before.\n哦。不！你误会了。那没有让我不自在。我……嗯，我觉得那挺好的。那种事以前从没发生在我身上过。"

    old "That's never happened to you before?"
    new "That's never happened to you before?\n你以前从没遇到过这种事？"

    old "That seems strange to me."
    new "That seems strange to me.\n这让我觉得挺奇怪的。"

    old "Not even with a romantic partner?"
    new "Not even with a romantic partner?\n连跟恋人在一起时也没有过？"

    old "Not really. Um, you probably don't know, but nagas aren't exactly known for... being romantic."
    new "Not really. Um, you probably don't know, but nagas aren't exactly known for... being romantic.\n不太有。嗯，你可能不知道，nagas这族并不以……浪漫著称。"

    old "We just... ahem. In a lot of ways, we're more similar to animals than humans, you know?"
    new "We just... ahem. In a lot of ways, we're more similar to animals than humans, you know?\n我们只是……咳咳。在很多方面，我们其实比人类更像动物，你懂吧？"

    old "You're going to have to be clearer than that."
    new "You're going to have to be clearer than that.\n你得说得再明白点才行。"

    old "I insist, but I admit that I'm mostly doing it because it's fun to see Sylrissa getting so embarrassed trying to talk about it. This certainly isn't a sight I get to see every day. I have to make the most of it."
    new "I insist, but I admit that I'm mostly doing it because it's fun to see Sylrissa getting so embarrassed trying to talk about it. This certainly isn't a sight I get to see every day. I have to make the most of it.\n我继续追问，不过我承认，我多半是出于乐趣——看着Sylrissa为了说这事而窘迫不已，实在有趣。这样的景象可不是每天都能见到的。我得好好把握。"

    old "Sex. I'm talking about sex, alright? Specifically for procreation. And for fun too, I guess. But for love... That's not something nagas usually do."
    new "Sex. I'm talking about sex, alright? Specifically for procreation. And for fun too, I guess. But for love... That's not something nagas usually do.\n性。我在说性，行了吧？尤其是为了繁衍后代。当然，也为了寻欢作乐。但为了爱情……那不是nagas通常会做的事。"

    old "I mean, I guess it does happen, but it's really rare."
    new "I mean, I guess it does happen, but it's really rare.\n我是说，我想这种情况确实存在，但真的很少见。"

    old "Oh. Wow."
    new "Oh. Wow.\n哦。哇。"

    old "Yup."
    new "Yup.\n对。"

    old "If you don't already know, us nagas are all bisexual. I mean, I guess it's always possible that there's an exception to that rule, but having male and female partners is expected. Sometimes during mating season, we all gather together and... Well, it lasts for days."
    new "If you don't already know, us nagas are all bisexual. I mean, I guess it's always possible that there's an exception to that rule, but having male and female partners is expected. Sometimes during mating season, we all gather together and... Well, it lasts for days.\n你可能还不知道，我们nagas全都是双性恋。我是说，这条规则里大概也会有例外，但拥有男性和女性伴侣都是很平常的事。有时到了交配季节，我们会聚在一起……嗯，一折腾就是好几天。"

    old "Is it exclusively for nagas? For example, could an [prace] join in?"
    new "Is it exclusively for nagas? For example, could an [prace] join in?\n那是nagas专属的吗？比如说，[prace]能参加吗？"

    old "Is it exclusively for nagas? For example, could a [prace] join in?"
    new "Is it exclusively for nagas? For example, could a [prace] join in?\n那是nagas专属的吗？比如说，[prace]能加入吗？"

    old "Sylrissa laughs. However, I can sense a bit of sadness in her smile."
    new "Sylrissa laughs. However, I can sense a bit of sadness in her smile.\nSylrissa笑了。不过，我能从她的笑容里感受到一丝悲伤。"

    old "I guess it would sound like fun when I put it like that, huh? Well, I guess it was the first few times. But after awhile..."
    new "I guess it would sound like fun when I put it like that, huh? Well, I guess it was the first few times. But after awhile...\n我那么一说，听起来是挺有意思的，对吧？嗯，头几次确实也算有趣。但时间一长……"

    old "It's not fun anymore."
    new "It's not fun anymore.\n就不再有趣了。"

    old "Sylrissa shakes her head."
    new "Sylrissa shakes her head.\nSylrissa摇了摇头。"

    old "You don't have any connection to your partners. You don't even know who you're mating with and they just forget about you afterward anyway."
    new "You don't have any connection to your partners. You don't even know who you're mating with and they just forget about you afterward anyway.\n你跟伴侣之间没有任何联结。你甚至都不知道自己在跟谁交配，而事后他们转眼就把你忘了。"

    old "After awhile, you start to lose your sense of self. It's like... How do I put it? You're not a person anymore. You're just a thing. Some kind of souless toy that everyone gets to abuse. It's... terrible."
    new "After awhile, you start to lose your sense of self. It's like... How do I put it? You're not a person anymore. You're just a thing. Some kind of souless toy that everyone gets to abuse. It's... terrible.\n时间一长，你会开始失去自我。就像……我该怎么说呢？你不再是一个人。你只是一件东西。某种任谁都能摆布、没有灵魂的玩物。那……糟透了。"

    old "After a while, I imagine it'd get old. It sounds like it'd be more like exercise than anything else."
    new "After a while, I imagine it'd get old. It sounds like it'd be more like exercise than anything else.\n我想，时间久了也就腻了。听起来那更像是一种运动，而不像别的什么。"

    old "And, sorry if I insist, but I really can't believe that nobody falls in love. There has to at least be some kind of relationship similar to that, right?"
    new "And, sorry if I insist, but I really can't believe that nobody falls in love. There has to at least be some kind of relationship similar to that, right?\n还有，抱歉我这么坚持，但我实在难以相信没有人会坠入爱河。至少总该有某种类似爱情的关系吧？"

    old "As I said, it happens, but it's very rare. Personally, I've never been in any kind of long term relationship and it's the same for Enok."
    new "As I said, it happens, but it's very rare. Personally, I've never been in any kind of long term relationship and it's the same for Enok.\n正如我说的，这种情况确实存在，但非常罕见。就我个人而言，我从未有过任何长期关系，Enok也一样。"

    old "It wasn't just the unnecessary cruelness that drove us away from our old tribe. It was also that lack of connection. Romantic or otherwise."
    new "It wasn't just the unnecessary cruelness that drove us away from our old tribe. It was also that lack of connection. Romantic or otherwise.\n让我们离开旧部落的，不只是那没必要的残酷。还有那种联结的缺失。不管是爱情上的，还是其他方面的。"

    old "I'm sorry, Sylrissa. That sounds... unpleasant."
    new "I'm sorry, Sylrissa. That sounds... unpleasant.\n我很抱歉，Sylrissa。那听起来……很不好受。"

    old "Thanks. Just remember: Enok and I are different, [protag]. I hope that you never forget that."
    new "Thanks. Just remember: Enok and I are different, [protag]. I hope that you never forget that.\n谢谢。只要记住：Enok和我是不同的，[protag]。我希望你永远别忘了这一点。"

    old "Trust me. You don't need to worry about that."
    new "Trust me. You don't need to worry about that.\n相信我。这点你不用担心。"

    old "I noticed that you two were different from the moment I met you. Both of you are special, even by... non-naga standards."
    new "I noticed that you two were different from the moment I met you. Both of you are special, even by... non-naga standards.\n从遇见你们的第一刻起，我就注意到你们俩与众不同。你们俩都很特别，即便按……非naga的标准来看。"

    old "Sylrissa beams at me. All the underlying sadness that previously permeated our conversation seems to have vanished."
    new "Sylrissa beams at me. All the underlying sadness that previously permeated our conversation seems to have vanished.\nSylrissa朝我展颜一笑。先前弥漫在我们对话里的那些隐约悲伤，似乎都消散了。"

    old "I'm glad to hear it."
    new "I'm glad to hear it.\n听你这么说，我很高兴。"

    old "Now that I can leave the conversation on a positive note, I decide to take my leave. As much as I'd like to keep talking with Sylrissa, I do have other things I need to get done."
    new "Now that I can leave the conversation on a positive note, I decide to take my leave. As much as I'd like to keep talking with Sylrissa, I do have other things I need to get done.\n既然能带着这样的好心情结束谈话，我便决定告辞。尽管我很想继续和Sylrissa聊下去，但我确实还有别的事要做。"

    old "I have to go now, but we'll talk again soon, Sylrissa."
    new "I have to go now, but we'll talk again soon, Sylrissa.\n我现在得走了，不过我们很快会再聊的，Sylrissa。"

    old "Good. I'm looking forward to it."
    new "Good. I'm looking forward to it.\n好。我很期待。"

    old "I head to the swamps to visit Sylrissa again. Oddly, I don't have to go far too find her. Instead of finding her deeper in, I run into her at the edge of the swamp, near Grimoire's fields."
    new "I head to the swamps to visit Sylrissa again. Oddly, I don't have to go far too find her. Instead of finding her deeper in, I run into her at the edge of the swamp, near Grimoire's fields.\n我又去沼泽地看望Sylrissa。奇怪的是，我没走多远就碰到了她。她没在沼泽深处，而是在沼泽边缘、靠近Grimoire田地的地方与我相遇。"

    old "Oh, [protag], I was just on my way to to visit you!"
    new "Oh, [protag], I was just on my way to to visit you!\n哦，[protag]，我正要去看你呢！"

    old "You were on your way to visit me?"
    new "You were on your way to visit me?\n你正要来看我？"

    old "Yes. You're always coming to visit me. I thought it'd be nice to return the favor and come see you instead this time."
    new "Yes. You're always coming to visit me. I thought it'd be nice to return the favor and come see you instead this time.\n是的。总是你来看我。我想这回也该轮到我来回报一下，主动来看看你。"

    old "So there isn't a problem or anything? There's no reason you needed to see me so soon?"
    new "So there isn't a problem or anything? There's no reason you needed to see me so soon?\n所以，没出什么事吧？你没有什么要紧事非得这么快见我？"

    old "Apart from enjoying your fine company? No. There's nothing you need to worry about."
    new "Apart from enjoying your fine company? No. There's nothing you need to worry about.\n除了想享受一下你的陪伴之外？没有。你什么都不用担心。"

    old "That's a first. Not that I'm complaining."
    new "That's a first. Not that I'm complaining.\n这还是头一遭。不过我不是在抱怨。"

    old "I appreciate that, Sylrissa. Still... I thought you didn't like civilized places like Grimoire. This is kind of surprising."
    new "I appreciate that, Sylrissa. Still... I thought you didn't like civilized places like Grimoire. This is kind of surprising.\n我很感激，Sylrissa。不过……我还以为你不喜欢Grimoire这样文明的地方。这可真让人意外。"

    old "Well, I do feel most at home in the swamp. Of course, in the past I used to feel just as at home with my tribe even though we we're doing... terrible things."
    new "Well, I do feel most at home in the swamp. Of course, in the past I used to feel just as at home with my tribe even though we we're doing... terrible things.\n嗯，我确实在沼泽里感觉最自在。当然，过去我在部落里也曾一样自在，哪怕我们那时在做……可怕的事。"

    old "People change, [protag]."
    new "People change, [protag].\n人是会变的，[protag]。"

    old "As long as it's for the better, that's a good thing."
    new "As long as it's for the better, that's a good thing.\n只要是往好的方向变，那就是好事。"

    old "Sylrissa nods."
    new "Sylrissa nods.\nSylrissa点点头。"

    old "However, now that we're here and I've found you... I'm not sure I want to go to Grimoire anymore."
    new "However, now that we're here and I've found you... I'm not sure I want to go to Grimoire anymore.\n不过，既然我们到了这儿，也找到你了……我不确定自己还想不想去Grimoire了。"

    old "Sylrissa lowers her gaze, unable to look me in the eye. It's rare to see her so insecure. In battle she fights with such fierce determination, and yet, something like this makes her act fragile."
    new "Sylrissa lowers her gaze, unable to look me in the eye. It's rare to see her so insecure. In battle she fights with such fierce determination, and yet, something like this makes her act fragile.\nSylrissa垂下目光，不敢直视我的眼睛。很少见到她如此没安全感。战斗中她是那样决绝凶猛，可这种事却让她显得如此脆弱。"

    old "Is the thought of going to Grimoire really that terrifying to her?"
    new "Is the thought of going to Grimoire really that terrifying to her?\n去Grimoire这个念头，真的让她如此恐惧吗？"

    old "I don't want to push her into something she's uncomfortable with, but I don't want her to feel like she has to stay in the swamp forever either."
    new "I don't want to push her into something she's uncomfortable with, but I don't want her to feel like she has to stay in the swamp forever either.\n我不想逼她去做让她不自在的事，但我也不想让她觉得自己非得永远留在沼泽里。"

    old "I consider my options for another second before saying..."
    new "I consider my options for another second before saying...\n我又斟酌了片刻，然后说道……"

    old "Sylrissa raises her head and smiles at me. However, it seems a little forced this time, as if she's doing it only to please me."
    new "Sylrissa raises her head and smiles at me. However, it seems a little forced this time, as if she's doing it only to please me.\nSylrissa抬起头对我微笑。不过，这次的笑显得有些勉强，仿佛只是为了让我高兴。"

    old "I think she knows that she'll have to face her fear at some point but, for today at least, she can put that off a bit longer."
    new "I think she knows that she'll have to face her fear at some point but, for today at least, she can put that off a bit longer.\n我想她明白，总有一天她得直面这份恐惧，但至少今天，她还可以再拖一拖。"

    old "Honestly, though? I wouldn't mind spending time with you in a... more comfortable place. By my standards, anyway."
    new "Honestly, though? I wouldn't mind spending time with you in a... more comfortable place. By my standards, anyway.\n不过说真的？我倒不介意在一个……更舒服的地方和你共度时光。按我的标准来说的话。"

    old "I'll never understand what's wrong with you. The swamp is a warm, cozy place. I can't imagine there being a place that would be preferable to it."
    new "I'll never understand what's wrong with you. The swamp is a warm, cozy place. I can't imagine there being a place that would be preferable to it.\n我永远搞不懂你有什么毛病。沼泽是又温暖又惬意的地方。我想象不出还有哪儿能比它更好。"

    old "Is she serious? I never know when she's talking about the swamp. It's not exactly a place I find welcoming."
    new "Is she serious? I never know when she's talking about the swamp. It's not exactly a place I find welcoming.\n她是认真的吗？她什么时候提到沼泽我都拿不准。那实在不是个让我觉得受欢迎的地方。"

    old "Maybe Sylrissa's feelings towards Grimoire are similar to mine regarding the swamps."
    new "Maybe Sylrissa's feelings towards Grimoire are similar to mine regarding the swamps.\n也许Sylrissa对Grimoire的感觉，就像我对沼泽的感觉一样。"

    old "Sylrissa sighs."
    new "Sylrissa sighs.\nSylrissa叹了口气。"

    old "You... you're probably right."
    new "You... you're probably right.\n你……你也许是对的。"

    old "I don't want to push you or anything, but I think that you might benefit from taking a break from the swamp from time to time. There's a lot more of the world to experience, you know?"
    new "I don't want to push you or anything, but I think that you might benefit from taking a break from the swamp from time to time. There's a lot more of the world to experience, you know?\n我不是想逼你或怎样，但我觉得时不时离开沼泽歇一歇，对你会有好处。这世界还有更多值得去体验的东西，你知道吗？"

    old "N-not that I don't absolutely love the swamp or anything."
    new "N-not that I don't absolutely love the swamp or anything.\n并、并不是说我有多不爱沼泽还是怎样。"

    old "Hm? You don't like the delicious smells that come from it?"
    new "Hm? You don't like the delicious smells that come from it?\n嗯？你不喜欢它散发出的那些美妙气味吗？"

    old "You're lucky that we meet near a river where it doesn't smell like the other parts of the swamp. Otherwise, I wouldn't come visit you as often."
    new "You're lucky that we meet near a river where it doesn't smell like the other parts of the swamp. Otherwise, I wouldn't come visit you as often.\n你算幸运的，我们见面的地方在河边，那儿闻起来不像沼泽其他地方那样。不然我可不会这么常来看你。"

    old "Sylrissa looks behind me, her eyes locked to the path leading to Grimoire."
    new "Sylrissa looks behind me, her eyes locked to the path leading to Grimoire.\nSylrissa望向我身后，目光紧锁在通往Grimoire的那条路上。"

    old "Well, I guess I'm willing to try."
    new "Well, I guess I'm willing to try.\n好吧，我想我愿意试试。"

    old "To start with, why don't we just try moving a bit closer? I know a good spot among the hills surrounding Grimoire. It isn't very high, but there's a nice view of the city from there."
    new "To start with, why don't we just try moving a bit closer? I know a good spot among the hills surrounding Grimoire. It isn't very high, but there's a nice view of the city from there.\n先这样吧，我们何不试着再靠近一点？我知道Grimoire周围丘陵间有个好去处。那儿不算很高，但能俯瞰到很美的城市景色。"

    old "That sounds nice. It's almost sunset though, do you think it's safe?"
    new "That sounds nice. It's almost sunset though, do you think it's safe?\n听起来不错。不过都快日落了，你觉得安全吗？"

    old "I'd say so. The N'Mar mists are still far to the north. Besides, being the capitol of the Human Empire has its benefits. There's always several guard patrols protecting the surrounding areas."
    new "I'd say so. The N'Mar mists are still far to the north. Besides, being the capitol of the Human Empire has its benefits. There's always several guard patrols protecting the surrounding areas.\n我觉得安全。N'Mar的迷雾还远在北方。再说了，作为人类帝国的首都自有它的好处——周边总有几支巡逻队守护。"

    old "I also hear there might be a powerful female naga in the area that you'd have to be a fool to mess with."
    new "I also hear there might be a powerful female naga in the area that you'd have to be a fool to mess with.\n我还听说，这附近可能有个强大的女naga，谁敢招惹她，谁就是傻瓜。"

    old "Sylrissa perks up."
    new "Sylrissa perks up.\nSylrissa来了精神。"

    old "I know that part is true at least."
    new "I know that part is true at least.\n至少这一点是真的。"

    old "So, what do you say? Are you up for it?"
    new "So, what do you say? Are you up for it?\n怎么样？你愿意试试吗？"

    old "Yes. Your powers of persuasion have convinced me. Lead the way, [protag]."
    new "Yes. Your powers of persuasion have convinced me. Lead the way, [protag].\n好。你的说服力打动了我。带路吧，[protag]。"

    old "Together, we walk towards the place I mentioned. We talk a bit along the way, but most of our journey is silent which is something really odd for Sylrissa."
    new "Together, we walk towards the place I mentioned. We talk a bit along the way, but most of our journey is silent which is something really odd for Sylrissa.\n我们一起朝我提到的那个地方走去。路上我们聊了几句，但大部分时间都沉默着，这对Sylrissa来说实在反常。"

    old "I think she's more stressed about this little trip than she's letting on."
    new "I think she's more stressed about this little trip than she's letting on.\n我想，她对这趟小出游的紧张程度，比她表现出来的更甚。"

    old "Well, here we are. What do you think?"
    new "Well, here we are. What do you think?\n好了，我们到了。你觉得怎么样？"

    old "It's... nice."
    new "It's... nice.\n挺……挺好的。"

    old "I can tell she's just being polite at this point. Maybe if I can get her to relax, she'll be able to enjoy herself more."
    new "I can tell she's just being polite at this point. Maybe if I can get her to relax, she'll be able to enjoy herself more.\n我看得出来，她此刻只是在客套。也许我能让她放松下来，她就能更尽兴一些。"

    old "Let's sit... Er, wait, does that make sense for nagas?"
    new "Let's sit... Er, wait, does that make sense for nagas?\n我们坐下吧……呃，等等，对nagas来说“坐下”这说法成立吗？"

    old "Nagas can 'sit down' too, despite having a tail, thank you."
    new "Nagas can 'sit down' too, despite having a tail, thank you.\nNagas虽然有尾巴，也能“坐下”，多谢关心。"

    old "Sylrissa smiles and pushes me as I am sitting down, making me roll onto my side. I get up again and sit near her."
    new "Sylrissa smiles and pushes me as I am sitting down, making me roll onto my side. I get up again and sit near her.\nSylrissa笑着，趁我坐下时推了我一把，害我滚到一边。我又爬起来，坐回她身旁。"

    old "Heheh. Sorry. I couldn't help myself."
    new "Heheh. Sorry. I couldn't help myself.\n嘿嘿。抱歉。我实在忍不住。"

    old "As long as you're enjoying yourself, I guess. Though you may have to fear retaliation in the future."
    new "As long as you're enjoying yourself, I guess. Though you may have to fear retaliation in the future.\n只要你开心就好吧。不过，往后你可得小心我的报复。"

    old "Sylrissa lets out another chuckle as she settles in."
    new "Sylrissa lets out another chuckle as she settles in.\nSylrissa安顿下来时，又轻笑了一声。"

    old "A slight wind blows, rustling the grass in wave like motions. From our place on top of the hill, we can see the whole town. It's surrounded by large walls with only the occasional high roofs and buildings peeking over it."
    new "A slight wind blows, rustling the grass in wave like motions. From our place on top of the hill, we can see the whole town. It's surrounded by large walls with only the occasional high roofs and buildings peeking over it.\n微风轻拂，草浪层层起伏。从我们所在的山顶，可以望见整座城镇。它被高墙环绕，只有零星几处高耸的屋顶和建筑从墙头探出来。"

    old "Since it's sunset, the guards start to light the lamp posts and people begin settling in for the night, leaving their own light sources in the windows of their homes."
    new "Since it's sunset, the guards start to light the lamp posts and people begin settling in for the night, leaving their own light sources in the windows of their homes.\n时值日落，卫兵们开始点亮路灯，人们也纷纷准备歇息，在自家窗前留下点点灯火。"

    old "Seeing Grimoire lit up like this, away from all the bustle and noise of the actual city, is something I genuinely enjoy."
    new "Seeing Grimoire lit up like this, away from all the bustle and noise of the actual city, is something I genuinely enjoy.\n像这样远远望着灯火通明的Grimoire，远离城中真正的喧嚣与嘈杂，是我真心享受的事。"

    old "I extend my hand to take hers but when I touch her, she jolts in surprise."
    new "I extend my hand to take hers but when I touch her, she jolts in surprise.\n我伸出手去牵她的手，可刚一碰到，她就惊得一颤。"

    old "Eep!"
    new "Eep!\n呀！"

    old "Ah, I'm sorry! I didn't mean..."
    new "Ah, I'm sorry! I didn't mean...\n啊，对不起！我不是有意……"

    old "Now that she's had a second to process what I'd tried to do, she relaxes a bit."
    new "Now that she's had a second to process what I'd tried to do, she relaxes a bit.\n等她回过神来，明白我方才想做什么，她稍稍放松了些。"

    old "Ah, no. It's my fault. I wasn't expecting you to do that so I overreacted."
    new "Ah, no. It's my fault. I wasn't expecting you to do that so I overreacted.\n啊，不。是我的错。我没想到你会那么做，所以反应过度了。"

    old "But, um, I would like to hold your hand. I-If you still want to, of course."
    new "But, um, I would like to hold your hand. I-If you still want to, of course.\n不过，嗯，我确实想牵你的手。当、当然，如果你还愿意的话。"

    old "I smile to myself. Sylrissa is being really cute right now."
    new "I smile to myself. Sylrissa is being really cute right now.\n我不禁微笑。此刻的Sylrissa真的好可爱。"

    old "You know, that startled sound you just made was kind of adorable."
    new "You know, that startled sound you just made was kind of adorable.\n你知道，你刚才那声惊呼还挺可爱的。"

    old "Sylrissa shoves me, making me fall onto my side once more. I probably deserved that."
    new "Sylrissa shoves me, making me fall onto my side once more. I probably deserved that.\nSylrissa推了我一把，害我又倒向一边。这多半是我活该。"

    old "She then offers me her hand to help me up, which I take."
    new "She then offers me her hand to help me up, which I take.\n随后她向我伸出手拉我起身，我握住了。"

    old "From there, we sit in silence and admire the view, our hand entertwined."
    new "From there, we sit in silence and admire the view, our hand entertwined.\n之后，我们静静地坐着欣赏景色，双手交缠。"

    old "Occasionally, I turn to look at her only to find her pretending to be looking at Grimoire. Then, it's her turn. I sense her looking at me as I keep my eyes focused in front of me."
    new "Occasionally, I turn to look at her only to find her pretending to be looking at Grimoire. Then, it's her turn. I sense her looking at me as I keep my eyes focused in front of me.\n我偶尔转头看她，总发现她装出在看Grimoire的样子。接着轮到她了。我目不斜视地盯着前方，却能感觉到她在看我。"

    old "It makes me feel like a teenager again, back when I had my first dates and was just starting to delve into what it was like to be in a romantic relationship."
    new "It makes me feel like a teenager again, back when I had my first dates and was just starting to delve into what it was like to be in a romantic relationship.\n这让我仿佛又回到了少年时代，那会儿我刚经历最初的约会，刚开始摸索恋爱的滋味。"

    old "I guess for Sylrissa, it really is. I can't help but think that I'm lucky to see her fumbling her way through her first experience the way I had back then. There's something truly endearing about it."
    new "I guess for Sylrissa, it really is. I can't help but think that I'm lucky to see her fumbling her way through her first experience the way I had back then. There's something truly endearing about it.\n我想对Sylrissa来说，这确实是头一回。我不禁觉得自己很幸运，能看着她像当年的我一样，笨拙地经历着她的第一次。那模样实在惹人怜爱。"

    old "It's beautiful, isn't it?"
    new "It's beautiful, isn't it?\n很美，不是吗？"

    old "I hate to admit it, but it is."
    new "I hate to admit it, but it is.\n虽然不愿承认，但确实很美。"

    old "See? The swamp isn't the only place where you can find nice things."
    new "See? The swamp isn't the only place where you can find nice things.\n看到了吧？沼泽可不是唯一能找到美好事物的地方。"

    old "I never doubted that. After all, there's Nuala in the desert and Vaeril in the forest so there are definitely 'nice things' outside the swamps."
    new "I never doubted that. After all, there's Nuala in the desert and Vaeril in the forest so there are definitely 'nice things' outside the swamps.\n我从没怀疑过。毕竟，沙漠里有Nuala，森林里有Vaeril，所以沼泽之外当然也有“美好的事物”。"

    old "She smirks at me while saying it. I'm fairly certain it's on purpose too. She's trying to make me jealous."
    new "She smirks at me while saying it. I'm fairly certain it's on purpose too. She's trying to make me jealous.\n她说这话时朝我坏笑。我相当确定她是故意的。她在试着让我吃醋。"

    old "Well, thank you for not including me on your list."
    new "Well, thank you for not including me on your list.\n嗯，谢谢你没把我算进你的名单里。"

    old "My voice is seeped in sarcasm. Even the most oblivious person in the world would have a hard time missing it."
    new "My voice is seeped in sarcasm. Even the most oblivious person in the world would have a hard time missing it.\n我的语气里满是讽刺。哪怕是世上最迟钝的人，也很难听不出来。"

    old "Haha, I knew that'd get to you! You tried to make me envious about Grimoire, so I had to get even. Sorry."
    new "Haha, I knew that'd get to you! You tried to make me envious about Grimoire, so I had to get even. Sorry.\n哈哈，我就知道这招对你管用！你想让我羡慕Grimoire，那我只好扳回一城。抱歉啦。"

    old "She doesn't look sorry at all. Then again, I suppose that's part of her charm."
    new "She doesn't look sorry at all. Then again, I suppose that's part of her charm.\n她看起来一点歉意都没有。不过话说回来，我想这也是她的魅力之一。"

    old "The night is falling quickly, so we eventually decide it's time to leave. As I assured Sylrissa earlier, it'd be safe to stay longer, but I'm sure she's been away from the swamp long enough and I have my duties to get back to."
    new "The night is falling quickly, so we eventually decide it's time to leave. As I assured Sylrissa earlier, it'd be safe to stay longer, but I'm sure she's been away from the swamp long enough and I have my duties to get back to.\n夜幕降临得很快，我们最终决定是时候离开了。正如我先前向Sylrissa保证过的，多待一会儿也安全，但我确信她离开沼泽已经够久了，而我也得回去处理自己的事务。"

    old "[protag], I want to thank you."
    new "[protag], I want to thank you.\n[protag]，我想谢谢你。"

    old "For showing you Grimoire at sunset?"
    new "For showing you Grimoire at sunset?\n谢谢你带你看日落时分的Grimoire？"

    old "Well, yes. There is that. But, more importantly, I want to thank you for sharing this moment with me."
    new "Well, yes. There is that. But, more importantly, I want to thank you for sharing this moment with me.\n嗯，是的。那也算一桩。但更重要的是，我想谢谢你愿意与我分享这一刻。"

    old "I know you're a busy person. There are a lot of ways you could have spent this time. Even so, you still chose to spend it with me-- to show me a silly thing, unrelated to our mission."
    new "I know you're a busy person. There are a lot of ways you could have spent this time. Even so, you still chose to spend it with me-- to show me a silly thing, unrelated to our mission.\n我知道你很忙。这段时光你本可以有无数种打发的方式。可你还是选择和我一起度过——带我看一件与任务无关的傻傻的小事。"

    old "You know, in my previous line of work, I was always in a hurry. Go there, take money, go elsewhere, drop off money. Repeat."
    new "You know, in my previous line of work, I was always in a hurry. Go there, take money, go elsewhere, drop off money. Repeat.\n你知道，我以前那份活计，总是来去匆匆。到这儿，收钱；再去别处，把钱放下。周而复始。"

    old "There wasn't a lot of time for moments like the one we just shared. I needed it as much as you."
    new "There wasn't a lot of time for moments like the one we just shared. I needed it as much as you.\n像刚才那样的时刻，向来没什么机会拥有。我和你一样需要它。"

    old "As a merchant, I've seen more sunrises than sunsets. It's kind of nice to be able to switch it up every now and then."
    new "As a merchant, I've seen more sunrises than sunsets. It's kind of nice to be able to switch it up every now and then.\n身为商人，我见过的日出比日落多。偶尔能换换口味，也挺不错的。"

    old "Well, if you're going to be a merchant, you need to travel from town to town. That involves getting up early to make the most of the daylight you have."
    new "Well, if you're going to be a merchant, you need to travel from town to town. That involves getting up early to make the most of the daylight you have.\n嗯，要做商人，就得辗转于各个城镇之间。这意味着要早起，好充分利用白天的时光。"

    old "And even if you're hanging around town, you have to get up to set up your stall before the city awakens and people start wandering the streets."
    new "And even if you're hanging around town, you have to get up to set up your stall before the city awakens and people start wandering the streets.\n就算只是在城里待着，你也得赶在城市苏醒、人们上街走动之前起身去支摊。"

    old "Because of that, I used to wake up when it was still night. I'd always end up seeing the sun rise while I was setting up or talking to some other merchant."
    new "Because of that, I used to wake up when it was still night. I'd always end up seeing the sun rise while I was setting up or talking to some other merchant.\n正因如此，我过去常常天还没亮就醒来。最后总是在支摊或和别的商人闲聊时，看着太阳升起。"

    old "Waking up early, huh? Ugh. I usually like to sleep until midday."
    new "Waking up early, huh? Ugh. I usually like to sleep until midday.\n早起啊？呃。我通常喜欢一觉睡到中午。"

    old "Heh. Of course. I should have expected that answer from you."
    new "Heh. Of course. I should have expected that answer from you.\n嘿。当然。我早该料到你会这么答。"

    old "I wouldn't be much of a bard if I didn't stop to be inspired by the occasional sunset, would I?"
    new "I wouldn't be much of a bard if I didn't stop to be inspired by the occasional sunset, would I?\n要是不偶尔停下来，从落日中汲取灵感，我也算不上什么合格的吟游诗人了，对吧？"

    old "In any case, spending time with you has given me some ideas for one of the songs I'm composing. As soon as we depart, I'll write them down so I don't forget."
    new "In any case, spending time with you has given me some ideas for one of the songs I'm composing. As soon as we depart, I'll write them down so I don't forget.\n总之，与你共度的时光给了我正在谱写的一首歌不少灵感。等我们一分别，我就把它们记下来，免得忘记。"

    old "Well, that's nice and all, but that's not exactly related to our mission, is it?"
    new "Well, that's nice and all, but that's not exactly related to our mission, is it?\n嗯，这固然挺好，不过那跟我们眼下的任务没多大关系吧？"

    old "You're not wrong, but you aren't completely right either."
    new "You're not wrong, but you aren't completely right either.\n你没说错，但也不全对。"

    old "It's true that me writing a song won't help us defeat whatever evil is lurking in N'Mar. However, it could inspire future generations."
    new "It's true that me writing a song won't help us defeat whatever evil is lurking in N'Mar. However, it could inspire future generations.\n确实，我写首歌帮不了我们打败N'Mar里潜伏的邪恶。不过，它能鼓舞后世之人。"

    old "Words and ideas have a power uniquely their own. When all is hopeless, they cut through the darkness and remind us that even against incredible odds, evil has been overcome before and it can be overcome again."
    new "Words and ideas have a power uniquely their own. When all is hopeless, they cut through the darkness and remind us that even against incredible odds, evil has been overcome before and it can be overcome again.\n言语与思想自有其独特的力量。当一切陷入绝望时，它们能划破黑暗，提醒我们：即便面对不可思议的逆境，邪恶也曾经被战胜过，而它还能再次被战胜。"

    old "A song that resonates with someone can clear their doubts and remind them that they aren't powerless, that they do have the ability to change their fates if they find their courage and embrace hope."
    new "A song that resonates with someone can clear their doubts and remind them that they aren't powerless, that they do have the ability to change their fates if they find their courage and embrace hope.\n一首能引起共鸣的歌，能驱散人心中的疑虑，提醒他们自己并非无能为力——只要鼓起勇气、拥抱希望，他们就有能力改变自己的命运。"

    old "And, if nothing else, it's an entertaining way to pass down our history."
    new "And, if nothing else, it's an entertaining way to pass down our history.\n而且，退一万步说，它也是传承我们历史的一种有趣方式。"

    old "Heh. That was...interesting. You really are an interesting person, [protag]."
    new "Heh. That was...interesting. You really are an interesting person, [protag].\n嘿。这还真……有意思。你果然是个有趣的人，[protag]。"

    old "Well, if nothing else, you have a better understanding of the city now."
    new "Well, if nothing else, you have a better understanding of the city now.\n嗯，不管怎样，你现在对这座城市有了更深的了解。"

    old "True. I did notice its structure. There's a main gate on the south, and another to the north, I think."
    new "True. I did notice its structure. There's a main gate on the south, and another to the north, I think.\n没错。我确实注意到了它的布局。南边有座正门，北边还有一座，我想。"

    old "You are correct. You have a good eye, Sylrissa. What else?"
    new "You are correct. You have a good eye, Sylrissa. What else?\n你说得对。你观察力不错，Sylrissa。还有呢？"

    old "The wall surrounding it is tall. If enemies were to attack it, you could make good use of archers up there. On the other hand, archers would be almost useless against zombies and skeletons."
    new "The wall surrounding it is tall. If enemies were to attack it, you could make good use of archers up there. On the other hand, archers would be almost useless against zombies and skeletons.\n环绕它的城墙很高。如果有敌人来攻，可以好好利用城头上的弓箭手。不过话说回来，弓箭手对付僵尸和骷髅几乎派不上用场。"

    old "Good observation. See? We already got good information that will be useful to our mission."
    new "Good observation. See? We already got good information that will be useful to our mission.\n观察得很好。瞧见没？我们已经得到对任务有用的情报了。"

    old "So you brought me here...for a lesson?"
    new "So you brought me here...for a lesson?\n所以，你带我来这儿……是为了给我上课？"

    old "Oh, no. That wasn't my intention at all. I really did enjoy this moment."
    new "Oh, no. That wasn't my intention at all. I really did enjoy this moment.\n哦，不。我完全没有那个意思。我是真的很享受这一刻。"

    old "I guess I was just demonstrating that even moments like these can be useful in regards to our mission."
    new "I guess I was just demonstrating that even moments like these can be useful in regards to our mission.\n我想我只是在说明，即便是这样的时刻，对我们的任务也有益处。"

    old "Well, now I really need to get back to the swamp. Enok will be waiting for me."
    new "Well, now I really need to get back to the swamp. Enok will be waiting for me.\n好了，现在我真的得回沼泽去了。Enok该在等我了。"

    old "Waiting for you? I'm almost jealous now."
    new "Waiting for you? I'm almost jealous now.\n等你？我都要吃醋了。"

    old "We're only good friends, [protag]. He is waiting for me for dinner. He went fishing when I left and has probably cooked whatever he caught by now. He likes to roast fresh fish and add spices he finds around the swamp."
    new "We're only good friends, [protag]. He is waiting for me for dinner. He went fishing when I left and has probably cooked whatever he caught by now. He likes to roast fresh fish and add spices he finds around the swamp.\n我们只是好朋友，[protag]。他在等我吃晚饭。我出门时他去钓鱼了，这会儿八成已经把他钓到的东西做好了。他喜欢把新鲜的鱼烤来吃，再撒上他在沼泽里找到的香料。"

    old "Hm. That actually sounds kind of delicious."
    new "Hm. That actually sounds kind of delicious.\n嗯。那听起来还真挺美味的。"

    old "He is a surprisingly good cook. Next time we'll invite you over too!"
    new "He is a surprisingly good cook. Next time we'll invite you over too!\n他厨艺好得出乎意料。下次我们也会请你来的！"

    old "I'd like that. Anyway, take care, Sylrissa. I'll see you soon."
    new "I'd like that. Anyway, take care, Sylrissa. I'll see you soon.\n我很乐意。总之，保重，Sylrissa。回头见。"

    old "We part ways, and I start to feel a weird sensation in my chest. It's a sort of disappointment or regret? Like a need I had was met, but not fully satisfied."
    new "We part ways, and I start to feel a weird sensation in my chest. It's a sort of disappointment or regret? Like a need I had was met, but not fully satisfied.\n我们分别后，我心中涌起一种奇怪的感觉。是某种失落，还是遗憾？就像一个得到部分满足、却又没有完全满足的渴求。"

    old "I guess if I'm honest with myself, I would have liked to stay up on that hill with Sylrissa a bit longer. I wonder if it's the same for her."
    new "I guess if I'm honest with myself, I would have liked to stay up on that hill with Sylrissa a bit longer. I wonder if it's the same for her.\n我想，如果对自己诚实一点，我其实想和Sylrissa在那山丘上再多待一会儿。不知道她是否也有同感。"

    old "I got a message from Sylrissa earlier this morning in which she formally invited me over for lunch. After hearing about Enok's cooking from her the last time, I must admit that I'm eager to try it."
    new "I got a message from Sylrissa earlier this morning in which she formally invited me over for lunch. After hearing about Enok's cooking from her the last time, I must admit that I'm eager to try it.\n今天一早我收到Sylrissa的讯息，她正式邀请我去吃午饭。上回从她那儿听说了Enok的厨艺之后，我不得不承认，我挺想尝尝的。"

    old "Ah, [protag]! Just in time. I was just about to start roasting the fish on the fire!"
    new "Ah, [protag]! Just in time. I was just about to start roasting the fish on the fire!\n啊，[protag]！来得正好。我正要开始把鱼架到火上烤呢！"

    old "I got up early to search for spices to use. I found some good ones too."
    new "I got up early to search for spices to use. I found some good ones too.\n我起了个大早去找要用的香料，还真找到些不错的。"

    old "Oh, [protag]. I've been meaning to ask: do you like your food spicy or mild? I can make it whichever way you prefer."
    new "Oh, [protag]. I've been meaning to ask: do you like your food spicy or mild? I can make it whichever way you prefer.\n哦，[protag]。我一直想问你：你喜欢吃辣一点还是清淡一点？我可以照你的口味来做。"

    old "I'm good with either. Just make it however you're making it for Sylrissa and yourself."
    new "I'm good with either. Just make it however you're making it for Sylrissa and yourself.\n我两种都行。就照你给Sylrissa和你自己做的那样做就好。"

    old "Okay. I'll do that then."
    new "Okay. I'll do that then.\n好。那我就照做。"

    old "Enok hums to himself as he slathers the fish with the spices he's found. He does it quickly and confidently, seemingly knowing exactly how much of each spice he should use."
    new "Enok hums to himself as he slathers the fish with the spices he's found. He does it quickly and confidently, seemingly knowing exactly how much of each spice he should use.\nEnok一边哼着小曲，一边把他找到的香料抹到鱼上。他动作利落又自信，似乎对每种香料该放多少都了然于胸。"

    old "Did you catch the fish in the river we usually meet up at?"
    new "Did you catch the fish in the river we usually meet up at?\n这鱼是在我们平常碰头的那条河里钓的吗？"

    old "I did, as a matter of fact."
    new "I did, as a matter of fact.\n事实上，确实是。"

    old "It was easier than usual today too for some reason. Maybe they were jumping at the chance to be eaten by Grimoire's envoy."
    new "It was easier than usual today too for some reason. Maybe they were jumping at the chance to be eaten by Grimoire's envoy.\n不知怎的，今天也比往常容易。也许它们正争着抢着要被Grimoire的使者吃掉呢。"

    old "Heh. Somehow I doubt that."
    new "Heh. Somehow I doubt that.\n嘿。我怎么就那么不信呢。"

    old "Enok laughs and then turns his attention back to his cooking long enough to put the fish on the fire."
    new "Enok laughs and then turns his attention back to his cooking long enough to put the fish on the fire.\nEnok笑了一声，随即把注意力转回烹饪上，把鱼放到了火上。"

    old "I don't know what mix of spices he used, but it smells good already."
    new "I don't know what mix of spices he used, but it smells good already.\n我不知道他用的是哪几种香料的搭配，但已经闻起来很香了。"

    old "I can tell that cooking is a real passion for you, Enok."
    new "I can tell that cooking is a real passion for you, Enok.\n我看得出，烹饪是你真正的热爱，Enok。"

    old "Oh, yes. Enok loves cooking. He especially likes trying out new things. He hates routine in every aspect of life. Right, Enok?"
    new "Oh, yes. Enok loves cooking. He especially likes trying out new things. He hates routine in every aspect of life. Right, Enok?\n哦，没错。Enok热爱烹饪。他尤其喜欢尝试新东西。他讨厌生活每个方面的循规蹈矩。对吧，Enok？"

    old "Absolutely. This is a new recipe we're trying, by the way. I've wanted to try it for awhile now, but I never managed to find the right mix of ingredients before."
    new "Absolutely. This is a new recipe we're trying, by the way. I've wanted to try it for awhile now, but I never managed to find the right mix of ingredients before.\n正是。顺便说一句，这是我们在试的一道新菜谱。我想试它已经有一阵子了，可之前总也凑不齐合适的配料。"

    old "I guess, technically. But phrasing it that way makes me sound evil."
    new "I guess, technically. But phrasing it that way makes me sound evil.\n严格来说，我想是的。但那么说让我听起来像个坏蛋。"

    old "Think of it more like... you're an explorer, discovering a whole new sensational dish before anyone else in all of Aravorn!"
    new "Think of it more like... you're an explorer, discovering a whole new sensational dish before anyone else in all of Aravorn!\n不如这么想……你是个探险家，抢在Aravorn所有人之前，发现了一道全新的惊艳菜肴！"

    old "Well, at the very least, Enok isn't lacking enthusiasm. His confidence is kind of inspiring."
    new "Well, at the very least, Enok isn't lacking enthusiasm. His confidence is kind of inspiring.\n好吧，至少Enok从不缺热情。他的自信还挺鼓舞人的。"

    old "Sylrissa sneaks up behind me. She wraps her arms around me, placing them around my abdomen as she leans in and whispers in my ear."
    new "Sylrissa sneaks up behind me. She wraps her arms around me, placing them around my abdomen as she leans in and whispers in my ear.\nSylrissa悄悄溜到我身后。她环抱住我，双臂搂住我的腰，凑过来在我耳边低语。"

    old "It's not too late to escape, [protag]. There's still time to avoid being corrupted by us evil nagas."
    new "It's not too late to escape, [protag]. There's still time to avoid being corrupted by us evil nagas.\n现在逃跑还不算太晚，[protag]。还来得及，免得被我们这些邪恶的nagas给带坏。"

    old "I can feel her body vibrate against my back as she lets out a small chuckle."
    new "I can feel her body vibrate against my back as she lets out a small chuckle.\n她轻声一笑，我能感觉到她的身体贴着我的后背轻轻颤动。"

    old "What are you two talking about?"
    new "What are you two talking about?\n你们俩在说什么？"

    old "Nothing. I just convinced [protag] not to run away."
    new "Nothing. I just convinced [protag] not to run away.\n没什么。我只是说服了[protag]别逃跑。"

    old "As if that was ever an option. There's no way [protag] would be able to leave after smelling my cooking."
    new "As if that was ever an option. There's no way [protag] would be able to leave after smelling my cooking.\n说得好像那算个选项似的。闻到我的菜香，[protag]才不可能走得了呢。"

    old "Oh? Well, thank you for reminding me."
    new "Oh? Well, thank you for reminding me.\n哦？嗯，谢谢你的提醒。"

    old "Sylrissa releases me and then slides over to Enok, turning her attention to the food he's cooking."
    new "Sylrissa releases me and then slides over to Enok, turning her attention to the food he's cooking.\nSylrissa松开我，滑到Enok身边，把注意力转向他正在做的菜。"

    old "I can't help but wonder if I missed out on something. Maybe she would have liked me to play along a bit more."
    new "I can't help but wonder if I missed out on something. Maybe she would have liked me to play along a bit more.\n我不禁琢磨自己是不是错过了什么。也许她本希望我再多配合她玩闹一下。"

    old "So, [protag], what do you think? It smells pretty good, right?"
    new "So, [protag], what do you think? It smells pretty good, right?\n那么，[protag]，你觉得怎么样？闻起来挺香的，对吧？"

    old "Thank you for your vote of confidence, [protag]. You won't regret it."
    new "Thank you for your vote of confidence, [protag]. You won't regret it.\n谢谢你的信任，[protag]。你不会后悔的。"

    old "I've never produced anything... what's the word in common tongue? Ah, yes. Inedible. I've never produced anything inedible. Sylrissa can attest to that."
    new "I've never produced anything... what's the word in common tongue? Ah, yes. Inedible. I've never produced anything inedible. Sylrissa can attest to that.\n我做出来的东西从没有……通用语里那词怎么说来着？啊，对了。“难以下咽”。我做出来的东西从没有难以下咽过。Sylrissa可以作证。"

    old "He's selling himself short. His dishes are more than edible-- they're downright fantastic."
    new "He's selling himself short. His dishes are more than edible-- they're downright fantastic.\n他这是自谦了。他的菜何止能吃——简直是美味绝伦。"

    old "I see. Well, I'm excited. I can't wait to try it."
    new "I see. Well, I'm excited. I can't wait to try it.\n我明白了。嗯，我很期待。都等不及想尝尝了。"

    old "Sylrissa comes near me, placing her hand on my arm."
    new "Sylrissa comes near me, placing her hand on my arm.\nSylrissa走近我，把手搭在我的手臂上。"

    old "You're in for a real treat, [protag]."
    new "You're in for a real treat, [protag].\n你这次有口福了，[protag]。"

    old "We let Enok get back to his cooking and, after a few more minutes, the food's delicious smell is stronger than ever. I hope it's done soon. My stomach is growling in anticipation."
    new "We let Enok get back to his cooking and, after a few more minutes, the food's delicious smell is stronger than ever. I hope it's done soon. My stomach is growling in anticipation.\n我们让Enok回去继续做菜。又过了几分钟，食物的香气愈发浓郁。真希望快点做好，我的肚子已经饿得咕咕叫了。"

    old "Don't worry, [protag]. The fish are almost done."
    new "Don't worry, [protag]. The fish are almost done.\n别担心，[protag]。鱼快好了。"

    old "It smells amazing, Enok."
    new "It smells amazing, Enok.\n闻起来棒极了，Enok。"

    old "Thank you. Oh, by the way, this recipe comes from Zoltar. Do you know where that is?"
    new "Thank you. Oh, by the way, this recipe comes from Zoltar. Do you know where that is?\n谢谢。哦，对了，这道菜谱来自Zoltar。你知道那在哪儿吗？"

    old "Of course. I traveled quite a bit for my previous job. I've actually been to Zoltar a couple of times."
    new "Of course. I traveled quite a bit for my previous job. I've actually been to Zoltar a couple of times.\n当然。我以前那份工作要到处跑。我其实去过Zoltar几次。"

    old "Wow. I'm surprised. Zoltar is really far away. I wonder how it is there."
    new "Wow. I'm surprised. Zoltar is really far away. I wonder how it is there.\n哇。真让人惊讶。Zoltar可远得很。不知道那儿怎么样。"

    old "Some places are similar to Issanis. Others are more...wild. There are more dangers there, I think. Races like minotaurs, centaurs, wealdings-"
    new "Some places are similar to Issanis. Others are more...wild. There are more dangers there, I think. Races like minotaurs, centaurs, wealdings-\n有些地方和Issanis相似。另一些则更……蛮荒。我想那边的危险也更多。有minotaurs、centaurs、wealdings这样的种族——"

    old "Wealdlings? What are wealdlings? I know about minotaurs and centaurs, but that last one is unfamiliar to me."
    new "Wealdlings? What are wealdlings? I know about minotaurs and centaurs, but that last one is unfamiliar to me.\nWealdlings？Wealdlings是什么？我知道minotaurs和centaurs，但最后那种我没听说过。"

    old "Let's see... How to explain? Wealdlings are a race of people that look like a mix between humans and animals. Felines mostly."
    new "Let's see... How to explain? Wealdlings are a race of people that look like a mix between humans and animals. Felines mostly.\n让我想想……该怎么解释呢？Wealdlings是一个种族，长得像人类和动物的混合体。大多是猫科。"

    old "Oh? That sounds interesting."
    new "Oh? That sounds interesting.\n哦？听起来很有意思。"

    old "Haha, it is. I couldn't believe it the first time I saw one. I was gaping, wide-eyed, and thinking, 'what the hell is that?' It was so--"
    new "Haha, it is. I couldn't believe it the first time I saw one. I was gaping, wide-eyed, and thinking, 'what the hell is that?' It was so--\n哈哈，确实。我第一次见到时简直不敢相信。我目瞪口呆，心里想着：“这他妈是什么东西？”那真是——"

    old "Before I finish the sentence, I stop short, realizing what I'm doing."
    new "Before I finish the sentence, I stop short, realizing what I'm doing.\n话没说完，我戛然而止，意识到自己在做什么。"

    old "I'm describing a mixed race in an unkind way in front of a two half human, half snake people. How could I be so stupid?"
    new "I'm describing a mixed race in an unkind way in front of a two half human, half snake people. How could I be so stupid?\n我竟在两个半人半蛇的人面前，以不友善的方式描述一个混血种族。我怎么会蠢成这样？"

    old "I-I'm sorry. That came out wrong. I mean, I was shocked when I saw them, but... I could have phrased it better."
    new "I-I'm sorry. That came out wrong. I mean, I was shocked when I saw them, but... I could have phrased it better.\n对、对不起。我那么说很失礼。我是说，我看到他们时是很震惊，不过……我本可以说得更得体些。"

    old "It's fine, [protag]. We're used to it. And we know that you didn't mean it in a bad way, like others usually do. Right, Sylrissa?"
    new "It's fine, [protag]. We're used to it. And we know that you didn't mean it in a bad way, like others usually do. Right, Sylrissa?\n没关系，[protag]。我们习惯了。而且我们知道你并不是像其他人那样存有恶意。对吧，Sylrissa？"

    old "I shift my gaze towards Sylrissa, who remains silent instead of answering. Her own eyes are focused on the flickering flames coming from our campfire."
    new "I shift my gaze towards Sylrissa, who remains silent instead of answering. Her own eyes are focused on the flickering flames coming from our campfire.\n我把目光转向Sylrissa，她却沉默不语。她的眼睛紧盯着我们篝火里跳动的火焰。"

    old "Without a word, she grabs her sword and slinks off towards the jungle."
    new "Without a word, she grabs her sword and slinks off towards the jungle.\n她一言不发，抓起剑，朝丛林悄无声息地溜去。"

    old "Hm."
    new "Hm.\n嗯。"

    old "What... where is she going? Is she going to be okay?"
    new "What... where is she going? Is she going to be okay?\n她……她去哪儿了？她不会有事吧？"

    old "Yeah. She'll be alright. She just going to go cut some things to blow off some steam. You know, trees, fruits. She'll come back once she's done."
    new "Yeah. She'll be alright. She just going to go cut some things to blow off some steam. You know, trees, fruits. She'll come back once she's done.\n没事。她会好好的。她只是去砍点东西撒撒气。你知道的，砍砍树啊、果子啊。砍完了她就会回来。"

    old "I made her really mad, didn't I?"
    new "I made her really mad, didn't I?\n我把她惹得很生气，对吧？"

    old "You didn't do it on purpose. She does know that, deep down."
    new "You didn't do it on purpose. She does know that, deep down.\n你不是故意的。她心里明白这一点。"

    old "It's just... What you said... It probably reminded her of some things from her past. Bad things."
    new "It's just... What you said... It probably reminded her of some things from her past. Bad things.\n只是……你说的那些话……大概勾起了她过去的一些事。不好的事。"

    old "What kind of bad things?"
    new "What kind of bad things?\n什么样的坏事？"

    old "That's... Not really my place to say."
    new "That's... Not really my place to say.\n这……实在不该由我来说。"

    old "If you want to know, you should talk to her yourself."
    new "If you want to know, you should talk to her yourself.\n如果你想知道，就自己去跟她谈谈。"

    old "Enok takes a second to look at the roasting fish before saying:"
    new "Enok takes a second to look at the roasting fish before saying:\nEnok看了一眼烤鱼，然后说道："

    old "It'll be about ten or twelve minutes before the food is ready. Go talk to Sylrissa, okay? And then come back with her so we can all eat together like we planned."
    new "It'll be about ten or twelve minutes before the food is ready. Go talk to Sylrissa, okay? And then come back with her so we can all eat together like we planned.\n食物大概还要十到十二分钟才好。去跟Sylrissa谈谈，好吗？然后带她一起回来，我们好按计划一起吃饭。"

    old "Right."
    new "Right.\n好。"

    old "I follow Enok's advice and go after Sylrissa. It's not hard to track her considering the sheer amount of destruction she's left in her wake. It's like following the trail of a tornado."
    new "I follow Enok's advice and go after Sylrissa. It's not hard to track her considering the sheer amount of destruction she's left in her wake. It's like following the trail of a tornado.\n我听从Enok的建议，去找Sylrissa。考虑到她身后留下的一片狼藉，追踪她并不难。简直就像循着龙卷风的轨迹走。"

    old "Aaaaargh!"
    new "Aaaaargh!\n啊啊啊啊——！"

    old "When I finally catch up to her, I see her furiously cutting into a tree. She gives it one final cut before it snaps and falls to the ground with a loud crash."
    new "When I finally catch up to her, I see her furiously cutting into a tree. She gives it one final cut before it snaps and falls to the ground with a loud crash.\n等我终于追上她时，只见她正愤怒地砍着一棵树。她最后补上一刀，那树应声折断，轰然倒地。"

    old "She's really mad. I'd better approach her carefully."
    new "She's really mad. I'd better approach her carefully.\n她气得不轻。我最好小心地接近她。"

    old "Just go away, [protag]! I don't want to see your stupid face right now!"
    new "Just go away, [protag]! I don't want to see your stupid face right now!\n走开，[protag]！我现在不想看到你这张蠢脸！"

    old "Sylrissa, stop this immediately!"
    new "Sylrissa, stop this immediately!\nSylrissa，马上住手！"

    old "You don't get to give me orders! Not right now! This isn't part of our mission to save N'Mar. This is something personal!"
    new "You don't get to give me orders! Not right now! This isn't part of our mission to save N'Mar. This is something personal!\n你没资格命令我！至少现在没有！这跟我们拯救N'Mar的任务无关。这是私事！"

    old "If I offended you somehow, I apologize."
    new "If I offended you somehow, I apologize.\n如果我有什么冒犯到你的地方，我道歉。"

    old "Apologize? You think that's enough for what you did to us!?"
    new "Apologize? You think that's enough for what you did to us!?\n道歉？你以为一句道歉，就抵得过你们对我们做的一切吗！？"

    old "What is she is talking about? Enok was right. This isn't about what I said. Not really. It's about something bigger that happened in her past."
    new "What is she is talking about? Enok was right. This isn't about what I said. Not really. It's about something bigger that happened in her past.\n她在说什么？Enok说得对。这事跟我刚才说的无关。不是的。是跟她过去发生的某件更大的事有关。"

    old "Us?"
    new "Us?\n“我们”？"

    old "You... the Empire..."
    new "You... the Empire...\n你们……帝国……"

    old "Hey, the fact that I'm a human doesn't automatically make me a friend or supporter of the Empire, you know?"
    new "Hey, the fact that I'm a human doesn't automatically make me a friend or supporter of the Empire, you know?\n嘿，我是人类这件事，可不会自动让我成为帝国的朋友或支持者，你知道吗？"

    old "The Empire? I'm not a human, in case you temporarily forgot. I've nothing to do with them."
    new "The Empire? I'm not a human, in case you temporarily forgot. I've nothing to do with them.\n帝国？我可不是人类，万一你一时忘了的话。我跟他们毫无瓜葛。"

    old "I-I needed to do this...the memories..."
    new "I-I needed to do this...the memories...\n我、我必须这么做……那些回忆……"

    old "That's enough. Tell me everything, now!"
    new "That's enough. Tell me everything, now!\n够了。现在，把一切都告诉我！"

    old "Sylrissa, please! Calm down!"
    new "Sylrissa, please! Calm down!\nSylrissa，拜托！冷静下来！"

    old "You... you're like all of the others, aren't you? Deep down, you hate me."
    new "You... you're like all of the others, aren't you? Deep down, you hate me.\n你……你和那些人一样，对吧？内心深处，你恨我。"

    old "What? How can you say it? Especially after what we've gone through together lately!"
    new "What? How can you say it? Especially after what we've gone through together lately!\n什么？你怎么能这么说？尤其是我们最近一起经历了那么多之后！"

    old "You only need to keep me happy. You need my skills for your mission. That's the only reason why you've been acting the way you have been-- like you care about me. But I know, I know it's just a façade."
    new "You only need to keep me happy. You need my skills for your mission. That's the only reason why you've been acting the way you have been-- like you care about me. But I know, I know it's just a façade.\n你只需要让我开心。你的任务需要我的本事。这就是你一直那样待我的唯一原因——装出一副关心我的样子。但我知道，我知道那只是装出来的。"

    old "That's not true, Sylrissa and you know it. You have to know it."
    new "That's not true, Sylrissa and you know it. You have to know it.\n不是这样的，Sylrissa，而且你心里清楚。你不可能不知道。"

    old "I want to help you. What happened? Why are you so angry about what I said?"
    new "I want to help you. What happened? Why are you so angry about what I said?\n我想帮你。到底发生了什么？你为什么对我刚才说的话那么生气？"

    old "Have you heard the joke about the dwarf who had a naga girlfriend?"
    new "Have you heard the joke about the dwarf who had a naga girlfriend?\n你听过那个关于dwarf找了个naga女友的笑话吗？"

    old "So, the dwarf's friends are curious so they all ask him how it is having a naga as a girlfriend."
    new "So, the dwarf's friends are curious so they all ask him how it is having a naga as a girlfriend.\n于是，dwarf的朋友们很好奇，都问他有个naga女友是什么感觉。"

    old "And he replies: Well, it has its ups and downs. For example, when she suddenly moves towards you, you never know if she's going to hug you or eat you alive."
    new "And he replies: Well, it has its ups and downs. For example, when she suddenly moves towards you, you never know if she's going to hug you or eat you alive.\n他回答说：嗯，有起有伏吧。比如，她突然朝你扑过来时，你永远不知道她是要拥抱你，还是要活吞了你。"

    old "But besides that... It's very cool."
    new "But besides that... It's very cool.\n不过除此之外……挺酷的。"

    old "...pft."
    new "...pft.\n……噗。"

    old "What kind of joke is that?"
    new "What kind of joke is that?\n这算哪门子笑话？"

    old "One I just made up right now. It's... a work in progress."
    new "One I just made up right now. It's... a work in progress.\n我刚刚现编的。这……还在打磨中。"

    old "Well, it was was terrible."
    new "Well, it was was terrible.\n嗯，糟透了。"

    old "It still got you to laugh though."
    new "It still got you to laugh though.\n可你还是笑了。"

    old "No way. There's no way I'd laugh at something that bad."
    new "No way. There's no way I'd laugh at something that bad.\n不可能。那么烂的笑话，我才不会笑。"

    old "Heh. Well, it at least calmed you down, right?"
    new "Heh. Well, it at least calmed you down, right?\n嘿。至少它让你冷静下来了，对吧？"

    old "Do you want to tell me what happened just now? There has to be more to this outburst than my lack of tact, right?"
    new "Do you want to tell me what happened just now? There has to be more to this outburst than my lack of tact, right?\n你想告诉我刚才怎么了吗？你突然爆发，总不会只是因为我说话欠妥吧？"

    old "Sylrissa's shoulders slump and she lets out a tired sigh."
    new "Sylrissa's shoulders slump and she lets out a tired sigh.\nSylrissa的肩膀垮了下来，疲惫地叹了口气。"

    old "All right, I'll tell you."
    new "All right, I'll tell you.\n好吧，我告诉你。"

    old "Good. I'm listening. You can trust me, Sylrissa, whatever it is."
    new "Good. I'm listening. You can trust me, Sylrissa, whatever it is.\n好，我在听。你可以信任我，Sylrissa，无论是什么事。"

    old "This all happened years ago. I was just a teenager. There were much more of us back then..."
    new "This all happened years ago. I was just a teenager. There were much more of us back then...\n这都是多年前的事了。那时我还只是个少女。我们当时的人比现在多得多……"

    old "One day, the Empire, along with some mages of Horus, decided that it was time to do something about 'the naga menace' so they enlisted the help of a group that called themselves the 'Witch Hunters'."
    new "One day, the Empire, along with some mages of Horus, decided that it was time to do something about 'the naga menace' so they enlisted the help of a group that called themselves the 'Witch Hunters'.\n有一天，帝国连同Horus的一些法师，认定是时候对“naga之患”采取行动了，于是他们招募了一个自称为“Witch Hunters”的组织来帮忙。"

    old "The group's name was a bit misleading, of course. They didn't just hunt witches. Anyone the Empire told them to hunt was fair game. Unfortunately for me, that meant nagas were fair game."
    new "The group's name was a bit misleading, of course. They didn't just hunt witches. Anyone the Empire told them to hunt was fair game. Unfortunately for me, that meant nagas were fair game.\n当然，这个组织的名字有点误导人。他们不只是猎杀女巫。凡是帝国下令追猎的对象，都可以任由他们处置。不幸的是，对我来说，这意味着nagas也成了可以任由处置的目标。"

    old "I tried to fight back, but I was young and inexperienced at the time. They beat me into submission and captured me. There was nothing I could do to stop them."
    new "I tried to fight back, but I was young and inexperienced at the time. They beat me into submission and captured me. There was nothing I could do to stop them.\n我试图反抗，但当时我又年轻又没经验。他们把我打服，然后抓走了我。我什么也做不了。"

    old "Sylrissa holds herself, eyes wide as her fingertips dig into her arms."
    new "Sylrissa holds herself, eyes wide as her fingertips dig into her arms.\nSylrissa抱住自己，双眼圆睁，指尖深深掐进自己的手臂。"

    old "I can still feel it even now. That paralzying fear that overtook me when their leader, Raven, captured me. I thought that they would kill me, but they didn't. I guess that would have been too merciful."
    new "I can still feel it even now. That paralzying fear that overtook me when their leader, Raven, captured me. I thought that they would kill me, but they didn't. I guess that would have been too merciful.\n直到现在，我仍能感受到那种恐惧。当他们的头领Raven抓住我时，那股令人瘫软的恐惧攫住了我。我以为他们会杀了我，可他们没有。我想，那对他们来说太仁慈了。"

    old "They used me for experiments instead."
    new "They used me for experiments instead.\n他们转而拿我做实验。"

    old "Experiments?"
    new "Experiments?\n实验？"

    old "Sylrissa nods, a grave expression on her face."
    new "Sylrissa nods, a grave expression on her face.\nSylrissa点点头，一脸凝重。"

    old "After I was captured, I was brought to Horus. They held me prisoner in a room inside the Wizard's Guild. There, one of the mages took a special interest in me. Gregorius. I don't know much besides his name and his face, but those details are seared into my memory."
    new "After I was captured, I was brought to Horus. They held me prisoner in a room inside the Wizard's Guild. There, one of the mages took a special interest in me. Gregorius. I don't know much besides his name and his face, but those details are seared into my memory.\n我被俘后被带到了Horus。他们把我关在Wizard's Guild里的一间屋子里。在那儿，有个法师对我产生了特别的兴趣。Gregorius。除了他的名字和长相，我对他所知不多，可这些细节早已烙进我的记忆里。"

    old "Oh God. I really don't like where this is heading. I can understand why she was mad now."
    new "Oh God. I really don't like where this is heading. I can understand why she was mad now.\n天哪。我真不喜欢事情往这个方向发展。现在我明白她为什么那么生气了。"

    old "I'll spare you the details, [protag]. You don't need to know how he cut my tail every week to see it regrow, how he hurt me, physically and psychologically."
    new "I'll spare you the details, [protag]. You don't need to know how he cut my tail every week to see it regrow, how he hurt me, physically and psychologically.\n细节我就不多说了，[protag]。你不必知道他是怎么每周割掉我的尾巴，看着它重新长出来；也不必知道他是如何在身体上、心理上伤害我的。"

    old "I grit my teeth, unable to decide which feeling is more dominant: sadness for Sylrissa or anger at the people who did that to her. Instead of giving power to either emotion, I get her to continue."
    new "I grit my teeth, unable to decide which feeling is more dominant: sadness for Sylrissa or anger at the people who did that to her. Instead of giving power to either emotion, I get her to continue.\n我咬紧牙关，说不清哪种情绪更占上风：是对Sylrissa的心疼，还是对伤害她的那些人的愤怒。我没有让任何一方占据上风，而是让她继续说下去。"

    old "What happened then? How did you escape?"
    new "What happened then? How did you escape?\n后来呢？你是怎么逃出来的？"

    old "That's the weird part. I don't remember. I remember falling asleep one night, and waking up the next day in the swamps."
    new "That's the weird part. I don't remember. I remember falling asleep one night, and waking up the next day in the swamps.\n这正是奇怪的地方。我不记得了。我只记得有天夜里睡了过去，第二天醒来时，人已经在沼泽里了。"

    old "That's... crazy."
    new "That's... crazy.\n这……太离奇了。"

    old "Sylrissa's expression switches back to the fierce, determined gaze I'm used to."
    new "Sylrissa's expression switches back to the fierce, determined gaze I'm used to.\nSylrissa的神情又变回了我所熟悉的那种凶猛而坚定的样子。"

    old "After that, I went back to my tribe. I wanted revenge, you know? For what they did for me. So I began training, every day. Harder and harder to become the best naga fighter in my tribe-- in the whole swamp-- so that no one could make me feel helpless ever again."
    new "After that, I went back to my tribe. I wanted revenge, you know? For what they did for me. So I began training, every day. Harder and harder to become the best naga fighter in my tribe-- in the whole swamp-- so that no one could make me feel helpless ever again.\n那之后，我回到了部落。我想报仇，你知道吗？为他们对我所做的一切。于是我开始了日复一日的训练。我练得越来越狠，只为成为部落里——乃至整个沼泽里——最强的naga战士，这样谁也别想再让我感到无助。"

    old "Mission accomplished, I'd say."
    new "Mission accomplished, I'd say.\n依我看，这目标你算是达成了。"

    old "Hmph. Thanks. But when the day came to take my revenge, I didn't do anything."
    new "Hmph. Thanks. But when the day came to take my revenge, I didn't do anything.\n哼。谢谢。可真到要报仇的那天，我却什么都没做。"

    old "Because I realized it was impossible. How could a naga like me enter Horus unnoticed? The only reason I can enter Grimoire is because of you, because people are becoming familiar with my face, with who I am."
    new "Because I realized it was impossible. How could a naga like me enter Horus unnoticed? The only reason I can enter Grimoire is because of you, because people are becoming familiar with my face, with who I am.\n因为我意识到那不可能。像我这样的naga，怎么可能悄无声息地潜入Horus？我能进入Grimoire，仅仅是因为你——因为人们开始熟悉我的脸，熟悉我是谁。"

    old "But, normally, Enok and I would be arrested on sight, if not worse."
    new "But, normally, Enok and I would be arrested on sight, if not worse.\n但正常情况下，Enok和我一露面就会被抓，甚至更糟。"

    old "I think the Empire has become more tolerant of other races these days-- even if what the nagas are doing in the Unforgiving Swamps isn't exactly helping."
    new "I think the Empire has become more tolerant of other races these days-- even if what the nagas are doing in the Unforgiving Swamps isn't exactly helping.\n我想，如今帝国对其他种族已经宽容了许多——尽管nagas在Unforgiving Swamps里的所作所为实在帮不上什么忙。"

    old "I don't like what they're doing. But, I don't like what the Empire did to me either. I want your help, [protag]."
    new "I don't like what they're doing. But, I don't like what the Empire did to me either. I want your help, [protag].\n我不喜欢他们现在的所作所为。但我也同样不喜欢帝国对我做的事。我需要你的帮助，[protag]。"

    old "My help? For what?"
    new "My help? For what?\n我的帮助？做什么？"

    old "I want to go to Horus and find Gregorius. I want to get my revenge."
    new "I want to go to Horus and find Gregorius. I want to get my revenge.\n我想去Horus找到Gregorius。我要报仇。"

    old "Revenge? You mean..."
    new "Revenge? You mean...\n报仇？你是说……"

    old "I want to ask him some questions. And if his answers aren't good, I'm going to kill him."
    new "I want to ask him some questions. And if his answers aren't good, I'm going to kill him.\n我想问他几个问题。要是他的回答让我不满意，我就杀了他。"

    old "I can understand where Sylrissa is coming from, but I'm still not sure this is the right course of action. Apparently, I hesitate a little too long since Sylrissa ends up going off on me."
    new "I can understand where Sylrissa is coming from, but I'm still not sure this is the right course of action. Apparently, I hesitate a little too long since Sylrissa ends up going off on me.\n我能理解Sylrissa的出发点，但我仍不确定这是否是正确之举。显然我犹豫得太久了，Sylrissa终究朝我发作了。"

    old "Don't tell me you're defending that man? After I told you what he did to me?"
    new "Don't tell me you're defending that man? After I told you what he did to me?\n别告诉我你在袒护那个男人？在我告诉过你他对我做了什么之后？"

    old "Maybe I should have gone into details! You'd never be able to take his side if you knew!"
    new "Maybe I should have gone into details! You'd never be able to take his side if you knew!\n也许我该把细节都说出来！你要是知道，就绝不可能站在他那一边！"

    old "I'm not taking his side, Sylrissa!"
    new "I'm not taking his side, Sylrissa!\n我没站在他那一边，Sylrissa！"

    old "I can't forgive what he did to you. Even so..."
    new "I can't forgive what he did to you. Even so...\n我无法原谅他对你做过的事。即便如此……"

    old "Are you going to help me or not?"
    new "Are you going to help me or not?\n你到底帮不帮我？"

    old "But, Sylrissa... Do you understand what you're asking?"
    new "But, Sylrissa... Do you understand what you're asking?\n可是，Sylrissa……你明白你在要求什么吗？"

    old "I know it's a lot. But you're the only way I'm going to get into Horus undisturbed. You're the Envoy of Grimoire after all."
    new "I know it's a lot. But you're the only way I'm going to get into Horus undisturbed. You're the Envoy of Grimoire after all.\n我知道这要求很过分。但你是我能不受干扰进入Horus的唯一途径。毕竟你是Grimoire的使者。"

    old "I let out a long sigh. I don't know. This feels wrong. But so does leaving Sylrissa's tormentor unpunished."
    new "I let out a long sigh. I don't know. This feels wrong. But so does leaving Sylrissa's tormentor unpunished.\n我长叹一口气。我不知道。这么做感觉不对。但让折磨Sylrissa的人逍遥法外，同样让我觉得不对。"

    old "I'll think about it. That's all I can promise for now, Sylrissa."
    new "I'll think about it. That's all I can promise for now, Sylrissa.\n我会考虑的。眼下我能答应的只有这些，Sylrissa。"

    old "I'm not going to be your partner in a potential assassination attempt, Sylrissa! Especially a member of the Wizards Guild of Horus!"
    new "I'm not going to be your partner in a potential assassination attempt, Sylrissa! Especially a member of the Wizards Guild of Horus!\n我不会陪你搞什么可能沦为暗杀的行动，Sylrissa！更何况目标是Horus的Wizards Guild成员！"

    old "Why? Are you scared?"
    new "Why? Are you scared?\n为什么？你怕了？"

    old "Yes, Sylrissa. I'm scared."
    new "Yes, Sylrissa. I'm scared.\n是的，Sylrissa。我怕。"

    old "This isn't some simple task you're asking. If I help you and we get caught, the Empire would never trust me again. And they'd be right to do so."
    new "This isn't some simple task you're asking. If I help you and we get caught, the Empire would never trust me again. And they'd be right to do so.\n你要求的可不是什么简单差事。要是我帮你、我们被抓了，帝国就再也不会信任我。而且他们那么做也理所当然。"

    old "Our mission at N'Mar is too important to risk that."
    new "Our mission at N'Mar is too important to risk that.\n我们在N'Mar的任务太重要了，冒不起这个险。"

    old "You can't ask me to risk the lives of everyone for your personal revenge, Sylrissa."
    new "You can't ask me to risk the lives of everyone for your personal revenge, Sylrissa.\n你不能要求我为了你的私人恩怨，拿所有人的性命去冒险，Sylrissa。"

    old "I'm sorry, but my answer is no. Please, try to understand."
    new "I'm sorry, but my answer is no. Please, try to understand.\n抱歉，但我的答案是“不”。请你试着理解。"

    old "..maybe you're right."
    new "..maybe you're right.\n……也许你是对的。"

    old "I think we should get back now, assuming you are okay with that."
    new "I think we should get back now, assuming you are okay with that.\n我想我们现在该回去了，希望你不介意。"

    old "Yeah... I'm okay with that."
    new "Yeah... I'm okay with that.\n嗯……我不介意。"

    old "I do feel a bit better after talking with you, [protag]."
    new "I do feel a bit better after talking with you, [protag].\n跟你聊过之后，我确实感觉好多了，[protag]。"

    old "Sylrissa looks at me and smiles, but it's a sad smile. As if the bad memories are still at the forefront of her mind, continuously hurting her even now."
    new "Sylrissa looks at me and smiles, but it's a sad smile. As if the bad memories are still at the forefront of her mind, continuously hurting her even now.\nSylrissa看着我，露出一个微笑，但那是个悲伤的微笑。仿佛那些糟糕的回忆仍盘踞在她心头，直到现在仍不断刺痛着她。"

    old "We go back and eat Enok's cooking."
    new "We go back and eat Enok's cooking.\n我们回去，吃了Enok做的饭。"

    old "It's better than I could have hoped, but the earlier conversation with Sylrissa is still effecting the overall mood. None of us talk much and I don't try to push it."
    new "It's better than I could have hoped, but the earlier conversation with Sylrissa is still effecting the overall mood. None of us talk much and I don't try to push it.\n饭菜比我期望的还要好，但先前与Sylrissa的那番谈话仍影响着整体的气氛。我们都不怎么说话，我也没有强求。"

    old "After lunch is over, I leave the swamp."
    new "After lunch is over, I leave the swamp.\n午饭结束后，我离开了沼泽。"

    old "Ever since Sylrissa mentioned wanting to go to Horus to face the man who tormented her, I've been having a hard time focusing on my other tasks."
    new "Ever since Sylrissa mentioned wanting to go to Horus to face the man who tormented her, I've been having a hard time focusing on my other tasks.\n自从Sylrissa提起想回Horus去找那个折磨过她的人算账之后，我一直很难把心思放在其他事情上。"

    old "I keep thinking about it, even at the most inopportune times. I can't afford to have it keep distracting me like this any longer which is why I've decided to put a stop to it."
    new "I keep thinking about it, even at the most inopportune times. I can't afford to have it keep distracting me like this any longer which is why I've decided to put a stop to it.\n即使在最不合时宜的时候，我也总在想这件事。我不能再让它这样一直分散我的注意力了，所以我决定就此打住。"

    old "Today, I'm seeing Sylrissa to clear this matter up once and for all."
    new "Today, I'm seeing Sylrissa to clear this matter up once and for all.\n今天，我要去见Sylrissa，把这件事彻底了结。"

    old "[protag]?"
    new "[protag]?\n[protag]？"

    old "Hello, Sylrissa."
    new "Hello, Sylrissa.\n你好，Sylrissa。"

    old "Hello to you too. I wasn't expecting you today."
    new "Hello to you too. I wasn't expecting you today.\n你也好。我没想到你今天会来。"

    old "Where's Enok? Fishing again?"
    new "Where's Enok? Fishing again?\nEnok呢？又去钓鱼了？"

    old "Nope. Not this time. This time he's hunting something bigger. I'm not exactly sure what he was after, but I think I heard him mumbling something about needing basilisk meat for one of his recipes."
    new "Nope. Not this time. This time he's hunting something bigger. I'm not exactly sure what he was after, but I think I heard him mumbling something about needing basilisk meat for one of his recipes.\n不。这次不是。这次他去猎更大的东西了。我不太确定他到底想抓什么，但我想我听到他嘟囔着说，做菜需要蛇怪肉。"

    old "Basilisk meat, huh?"
    new "Basilisk meat, huh?\n蛇怪肉，是吗？"

    old "Yes. I imagine he'll make a 'stunning' dish with it."
    new "Yes. I imagine he'll make a 'stunning' dish with it.\n是啊。我想他会用它做出一道“令人石化”的菜。"

    old "She looks at me eagerly, waiting for me to laugh."
    new "She looks at me eagerly, waiting for me to laugh.\n她热切地看着我，等着我笑出来。"

    old "Did you get it? Basilisk? Stone gaze? Stunning?"
    new "Did you get it? Basilisk? Stone gaze? Stunning?\n你听懂了吗？蛇怪？石化凝视？石化？"

    old "You do know what a Basilisk is, right?"
    new "You do know what a Basilisk is, right?\n你知道蛇怪是什么吧？"

    old "Honestly, her overexplaining it to me is funnier than the actual joke. I do end up letting an accidental laugh."
    new "Honestly, her overexplaining it to me is funnier than the actual joke. I do end up letting an accidental laugh.\n说实话，她给我解释得那么细，比笑话本身还好笑。结果我还是没忍住，笑了出来。"

    old "There we go!"
    new "There we go!\n看吧，笑了！"

    old "Well, I'm glad to see that your sense of humour is back, Sylrissa."
    new "Well, I'm glad to see that your sense of humour is back, Sylrissa.\n嗯，我很高兴看到你的幽默感又回来了，Sylrissa。"

    old "I'm not exactly here to have fun this time though. I wanted to talk you about what you asked me to do the last time..."
    new "I'm not exactly here to have fun this time though. I wanted to talk you about what you asked me to do the last time...\n不过，我这次来可不只是为了玩。我想跟你谈谈你上次拜托我的事……"

    old "My last sentence immediately catches Sylrissa's attention. She claps her hand to the front of her chest and looks at me expectantly."
    new "My last sentence immediately catches Sylrissa's attention. She claps her hand to the front of her chest and looks at me expectantly.\n我最后一句话立刻引起了Sylrissa的注意。她把一只手按在胸前，满怀期待地看着我。"

    old "I'm doing this for you, Sylrissa."
    new "I'm doing this for you, Sylrissa.\n我这么做是为了你，Sylrissa。"

    old "For me!? How can you be doing this for me?"
    new "For me!? How can you be doing this for me?\n为了我？！你怎么会是为了我？"

    old "I honestly don't think that facing that man again will help you."
    new "I honestly don't think that facing that man again will help you.\n说实话，我不觉得再去面对那个男人对你有好处。"

    old "It'll only bring back bad memories and, even if you do kill him, I don't think you'll get the closure you're looking for. There's no outcome that'd make up for what you went through."
    new "It'll only bring back bad memories and, even if you do kill him, I don't think you'll get the closure you're looking for. There's no outcome that'd make up for what you went through.\n那只会勾起痛苦的回忆，而且就算你杀了他，我也不认为你能得到你想要的了结。什么样的结局，都无法弥补你经历过的那些事。"

    old "I think stirring up those old feelings will only take you to a darker place than the one you're in now."
    new "I think stirring up those old feelings will only take you to a darker place than the one you're in now.\n我觉得，重新翻起那些旧情绪，只会把你拖进比现在更黑暗的境地。"

    old "Shouldn't I be the one to decide that though? This isn't fair, [protag]!"
    new "Shouldn't I be the one to decide that though? This isn't fair, [protag]!\n可那不该由我自己来决定吗？这不公平，[protag]！"

    old "Please Sylrissa, I ask it in the name of our... friendship. Forget about this whole thing. It's the best thing for you."
    new "Please Sylrissa, I ask it in the name of our... friendship. Forget about this whole thing. It's the best thing for you.\n求你了，Sylrissa，我以我们之间的……友谊的名义请求你。把这件事忘了吧。这样对你最好。"

    old "But I--"
    new "But I--\n可是我——"

    old "Focus on the mission, on the people around you who love you for who you are. Your future is with us. Forget the past. There's nothing there for you now."
    new "Focus on the mission, on the people around you who love you for who you are. Your future is with us. Forget the past. There's nothing there for you now.\n把心思放在任务上，放在那些爱着你本来模样的伙伴身上。你的未来和我们在一起。忘掉过去吧。那里已经没有什么值得你留恋的了。"

    old "I... Okay, [protag]. I will try."
    new "I... Okay, [protag]. I will try.\n我……好吧，[protag]。我会试试的。"

    old "I'm sure you can do it, Sylrissa."
    new "I'm sure you can do it, Sylrissa.\n我相信你一定能做到，Sylrissa。"

    old "I hope you're right."
    new "I hope you're right.\n希望你是对的。"

    old "She'll need some time to process, so I give her a hug goodbye and then take my leave."
    new "She'll need some time to process, so I give her a hug goodbye and then take my leave.\n她需要一点时间来消化，于是我拥抱了她一下道别，然后告辞离开。"

    old "I know she would have liked my help, but I meant what I said. I don't think it'll do her any good to meet that man."
    new "I know she would have liked my help, but I meant what I said. I don't think it'll do her any good to meet that man.\n我知道她原本会希望我帮她，但我说的都是真心话。我觉得去见那个男人对她没有任何好处。"

    old "It was too risky anyway. If we'd been caught... Well, we'd be compromising our whole mission. I can't do that just to satisfy Sylrissa's need for revenge."
    new "It was too risky anyway. If we'd been caught... Well, we'd be compromising our whole mission. I can't do that just to satisfy Sylrissa's need for revenge.\n而且那太冒险了。要是被抓住了……嗯，我们整个任务都会泡汤。我不能只是为了满足Sylrissa复仇的念头就那样做。"

    old "R-really? You'll help me?"
    new "R-really? You'll help me?\n真、真的吗？你会帮我？"

    old "That's what I said."
    new "That's what I said.\n我刚才就是这么说的。"

    old "I still don't think that this is a great idea, but if you really feel that you need to face this Gregorius guy, well, I'm in."
    new "I still don't think that this is a great idea, but if you really feel that you need to face this Gregorius guy, well, I'm in.\n我仍然不觉得这是个好主意，但如果你真的觉得自己必须去面对这个叫Gregorius的家伙，那好吧，算我一个。"

    old "Thank you, [protag]! You don't know how much this means to me!"
    new "Thank you, [protag]! You don't know how much this means to me!\n谢谢你，[protag]！你不知道这对我有多重要！"

    old "I just hope I don't end up regretting this later."
    new "I just hope I don't end up regretting this later.\n我只希望以后不会后悔。"

    old "Anyway, are you ready now?"
    new "Anyway, are you ready now?\n总之，你现在准备好了吗？"

    old "N-now?"
    new "N-now?\n现、现在？"

    old "Yes. We should do this before I come to my senses and change my mind. Unless, of course, you've changed your mind."
    new "Yes. We should do this before I come to my senses and change my mind. Unless, of course, you've changed your mind.\n对。趁我还没清醒过来反悔，我们最好现在就去。当然，除非你已经改主意了。"

    old "Not at all!"
    new "Not at all!\n才没有！"

    old "I'm coming with you two."
    new "I'm coming with you two.\n我跟你们俩一起去。"

    old "Enok's voice startles both of us as he emerges from the vegetation."
    new "Enok's voice startles both of us as he emerges from the vegetation.\nEnok从树丛里钻出来，他的声音把我们俩都吓了一跳。"

    old "How much of that did you just hear?"
    new "How much of that did you just hear?\n你刚才听到了多少？"

    old "Enough. I guess it's a good thing that my hunt didn't go as planned."
    new "Enough. I guess it's a good thing that my hunt didn't go as planned.\n听到的够多了。看来我这次打猎没按计划进行，反而是件好事。"

    old "It's going to be dangerous, Enok."
    new "It's going to be dangerous, Enok.\n那会很危险，Enok。"

    old "Which is why you're going to need my help."
    new "Which is why you're going to need my help.\n所以你们才更需要我帮忙。"

    old "Besides, you want answers right? I have a spell that should be able to help with that."
    new "Besides, you want answers right? I have a spell that should be able to help with that.\n再说了，你们想要答案，对吧？我有个咒语应该能帮上忙。"

    old "What kind of spell?"
    new "What kind of spell?\n什么样的咒语？"

    old "A spell that can tell us if Gregorius is telling us the truth."
    new "A spell that can tell us if Gregorius is telling us the truth.\n一个能告诉我们Gregorius说的是不是真话的咒语。"

    old "How? By reading his mind or something?"
    new "How? By reading his mind or something?\n怎么判断？读他的心思之类的吗？"

    old "It's nothing as grand as that. The magic will just react if he's lying. That's all."
    new "It's nothing as grand as that. The magic will just react if he's lying. That's all.\n没那么厉害。只要他撒谎，魔法就会有反应。仅此而已。"

    old "Ah, I see. That's still pretty impressive though. You can really cast something like that?"
    new "Ah, I see. That's still pretty impressive though. You can really cast something like that?\n啊，我明白了。不过那还是很了不起。你真的能施放那种咒语？"

    old "Not under normal conditions, but there should be a pretty significant concentration of magic present at the Wizards Guild that I can tap into. I'm confident that it'll work."
    new "Not under normal conditions, but there should be a pretty significant concentration of magic present at the Wizards Guild that I can tap into. I'm confident that it'll work.\n正常情况下不行，不过Wizards Guild里应该聚集着相当浓厚的魔力，我可以借助那股力量。我相信能成功。"

    old "A spell like that should make things much easier."
    new "A spell like that should make things much easier.\n有那种咒语，事情应该会顺利很多。"

    old "Even if it doesn't end up working, it'll be good to have the back up. I'm sure two nagas will create a more intimidating presence than one if we have to resort to threats."
    new "Even if it doesn't end up working, it'll be good to have the back up. I'm sure two nagas will create a more intimidating presence than one if we have to resort to threats.\n就算最后不起作用，多个后援也好。要是真到了不得不靠威胁的地步，我相信两个naga站在一起，肯定比一个更有威慑力。"

    old "And an extra party member wouldn't go amiss if we end up having to make a hasty retreat. Though, hopefully we don't get to the point where that's necessary."
    new "And an extra party member wouldn't go amiss if we end up having to make a hasty retreat. Though, hopefully we don't get to the point where that's necessary.\n而万一我们不得不仓促撤退，多一个队友也不是坏事。不过，希望别真走到那一步。"

    old "That would be for the best."
    new "That would be for the best.\n那样最好。"

    old "Are you ready Enok? We're in a hurry."
    new "Are you ready Enok? We're in a hurry.\n你准备好了吗，Enok？我们赶时间。"

    old "Just let me grab my staff and spellbook. Then I'll be ready to go."
    new "Just let me grab my staff and spellbook. Then I'll be ready to go.\n让我拿上我的手杖和法术书。然后就可以出发了。"

    old "Even if I could, why would I do that? I already know what kind of thoughts you have about me, [protag]."
    new "Even if I could, why would I do that? I already know what kind of thoughts you have about me, [protag].\n就算我能，我为什么要那么做？我早就知道你对我的看法了，[protag]。"

    old "Wait. Was he just flirting with me? The mischievous grin on his face certainly seems to support that theory."
    new "Wait. Was he just flirting with me? The mischievous grin on his face certainly seems to support that theory.\n等等。他刚刚是在跟我调情吗？他脸上那抹促狭的笑容，似乎印证了这个猜想。"

    old "It's only natural for you to think that I'm the most amazing male specimen you've ever seen."
    new "It's only natural for you to think that I'm the most amazing male specimen you've ever seen.\n你会觉得我是你见过的最棒的男性，再自然不过了。"

    old "Err, yes. Exactly. I couldn't have said it better."
    new "Err, yes. Exactly. I couldn't have said it better.\n呃，对，没错。你说得太对了。"

    old "Enok laughs, seemingly pleased with my response."
    new "Enok laughs, seemingly pleased with my response.\nEnok笑了起来，似乎对我的回应很满意。"

    old "Anyway, let me grab my staff and I'll follow you to Horus."
    new "Anyway, let me grab my staff and I'll follow you to Horus.\n总之，让我拿上手杖，然后我就跟你们去Horus。"

    old "This place is more impressive than I remember. Of course, most of my time was spent in a dark basement. They called it an alchemist's workshop, but it was a dark basement."
    new "This place is more impressive than I remember. Of course, most of my time was spent in a dark basement. They called it an alchemist's workshop, but it was a dark basement.\n这地方比我印象中还要气派。当然，我大部分时间都待在一间阴暗的地下室里。他们管那叫炼金工坊，可那不过是间阴暗的地下室。"

    old "What? I'm just calling it like I saw it."
    new "What? I'm just calling it like I saw it.\n怎么了？我只是实话实说而已。"

    old "Do you at least remember what Gregorius' face looks like?"
    new "Do you at least remember what Gregorius' face looks like?\n你至少还记得Gregorius长什么样吧？"

    old "Sylrissa's expression darkens at the mention of his name."
    new "Sylrissa's expression darkens at the mention of his name.\n一提到他的名字，Sylrissa的脸色就沉了下来。"

    old "Of course. I could never forget his face, his cold eyes watching me as he had my tail cut for his sick experiments."
    new "Of course. I could never forget his face, his cold eyes watching me as he had my tail cut for his sick experiments.\n当然记得。我永远也忘不了他的脸，忘不了他做那些变态实验时，用冰冷的眼睛盯着我割下我尾巴的样子。"

    old "There it is, the Wizards Guild. One of the biggest ones in all of Aravorn. We need to be extra careful now."
    new "There it is, the Wizards Guild. One of the biggest ones in all of Aravorn. We need to be extra careful now.\n就是那里，Wizards Guild。整个Aravorn最大的几个协会之一。我们现在得格外小心。"

    old "We reach the entrance where two enormous golems stand guard. What a bizarre place."
    new "We reach the entrance where two enormous golems stand guard. What a bizarre place.\n我们来到入口，两尊巨大的魔像在那里把守。真是个古怪的地方。"

    old "Halt! State your business with the Wizards Guild!"
    new "Halt! State your business with the Wizards Guild!\n站住！说清你们来Wizards Guild有何贵干！"

    old "We need to see the mage, Gregorius."
    new "We need to see the mage, Gregorius.\n我们要见法师Gregorius。"

    old "Do you have an appointment?"
    new "Do you have an appointment?\n你们有预约吗？"

    old "I take a step forward, trying to appear confident, but the golem moves to intercept my path."
    new "I take a step forward, trying to appear confident, but the golem moves to intercept my path.\n我向前迈了一步，想显得从容一些，但那魔像却移了过来，挡住我的去路。"

    old "Wait. What is your name?"
    new "Wait. What is your name?\n等等。你叫什么名字？"

    old "There's no appointment scheduled for someone of that name."
    new "There's no appointment scheduled for someone of that name.\n预约名单上没有这个名字。"

    old "The registry."
    new "The registry.\n登记册。"

    old "I look behind the second golem and see text literally floating in the air. After a reading a few lines, I can tell that the words are a list of names."
    new "I look behind the second golem and see text literally floating in the air. After a reading a few lines, I can tell that the words are a list of names.\n我朝第二尊魔像身后看去，只见文字真的飘浮在空中。读了几行之后，我看出那是一串名字的名单。"

    old "Well, I guess that explains it. This is the first time I've seen magic used for something like this. I'm kind of impressed and a little annoyed."
    new "Well, I guess that explains it. This is the first time I've seen magic used for something like this. I'm kind of impressed and a little annoyed.\n嗯，我想这算是解释得通了。这还是我头一回见到魔法被用在这种事情上。我既有点佩服，又有点恼火。"

    old "Uh, there must be some kind of mistake-"
    new "Uh, there must be some kind of mistake-\n呃，一定是哪里搞错了——"

    old "Sorry, my friend got confused. The appointment was actually made under 'Envoy of Grimoire', which is [protag]'s current title. It's right there as you can see."
    new "Sorry, my friend got confused. The appointment was actually made under 'Envoy of Grimoire', which is [protag]'s current title. It's right there as you can see.\n抱歉，我朋友弄混了。预约其实是登记在“Envoy of Grimoire”名下的，那是[protag]现在的头衔。你看，就在那儿。"

    old "The golems look at Enok, then at the registry, and then back at us before moving aside and letting us pass."
    new "The golems look at Enok, then at the registry, and then back at us before moving aside and letting us pass.\n两尊魔像看看Enok，又看看登记册，然后看看我们，最后让到一旁放我们通过。"

    old "<whispering> How is this possible?!"
    new "<whispering> How is this possible?!\n<whispering>这怎么可能？！"

    old "<whispering> The magical protection on the registry is actually pretty basic. It was easy enough to tamper with using my own magic. From there, it was all just a matter of adding your title to it."
    new "<whispering> The magical protection on the registry is actually pretty basic. It was easy enough to tamper with using my own magic. From there, it was all just a matter of adding your title to it.\n<whispering>那登记册上的魔法防护其实相当基础。用我自己的魔法，想在上面动手脚轻而易举。之后嘛，只要把你的头衔加上去就行了。"

    old "Well, I'm impressed."
    new "Well, I'm impressed.\n嗯，我服了。"

    old "Thanks. It is my job to impress people after all."
    new "Thanks. It is my job to impress people after all.\n谢了。毕竟我的工作就是让人印象深刻。"

    old "Envoy of Grimoire?"
    new "Envoy of Grimoire?\nEnvoy of Grimoire？"

    old "Yes, I'm [protag]. You've probably heard of me."
    new "Yes, I'm [protag]. You've probably heard of me.\n是的，我就是[protag]。你大概听说过我。"

    old "Yes. Your identity is well known even here. You have permission to enter."
    new "Yes. Your identity is well known even here. You have permission to enter.\n是的。你的大名即便在这里也无人不知。你们可以进去了。"

    old "The two golems move aside and let us enter the building."
    new "The two golems move aside and let us enter the building.\n两尊魔像让到一边，放我们进入大楼。"

    old "See? Told you. You only need to say the magic words and you're in! Easy."
    new "See? Told you. You only need to say the magic words and you're in! Easy.\n看到没？跟你说过了。你只要说出那句咒语一样的名字，就能进去！简单吧。"

    old "Let's just hope that the rest of our mission goes as smoothly as this."
    new "Let's just hope that the rest of our mission goes as smoothly as this.\n只希望我们接下来的任务也能像这样顺利。"

    old "We walk the long corridors for several minutes and I can't help but wonder if the building for the Wizards Guild is actually as big as the whole town. Suddenly, Sylrissa stops short, a troubled looking expression on her face."
    new "We walk the long corridors for several minutes and I can't help but wonder if the building for the Wizards Guild is actually as big as the whole town. Suddenly, Sylrissa stops short, a troubled looking expression on her face.\n我们在长长的走廊里走了好几分钟，我不禁怀疑，这栋Wizards Guild的大楼是不是真有整座城镇那么大。突然，Sylrissa猛地停下脚步，脸上浮现出不安的神情。"

    old "It's here. I recognize this corridor. The room where he experimented on me... It's on the right, downstairs."
    new "It's here. I recognize this corridor. The room where he experimented on me... It's on the right, downstairs.\n就是这里。我认得这条走廊。他拿我做实验的那个房间……就在楼下，靠右手边。"

    old "They didn't even bother to blindfold you while carrying you here?"
    new "They didn't even bother to blindfold you while carrying you here?\n他们把你带过来的时候，甚至都懒得蒙住你的眼睛？"

    old "There wasn't much point in doing that. I wasn't supposed to get out of here alive in the first place."
    new "There wasn't much point in doing that. I wasn't supposed to get out of here alive in the first place.\n那样做没什么意义。反正我本来就不可能活着离开这里。"

    old "Yet you did, Sylrissa."
    new "Yet you did, Sylrissa.\n可你还是活下来了，Sylrissa。"

    old "What are you implying?"
    new "What are you implying?\n你这话是什么意思？"

    old "I already told you several times. Nobody could have rescued you from the outside. It had to have been someone on the inside who allowed you to escape. And considering the state you were in, I feel like it had to be on purpose."
    new "I already told you several times. Nobody could have rescued you from the outside. It had to have been someone on the inside who allowed you to escape. And considering the state you were in, I feel like it had to be on purpose.\n我跟你说过好几次了。没有人能从外面把你救出来。一定是内部有人放你逃走。而且考虑到你当时的状况，我觉得那肯定是故意的。"

    old "Have you seen this place? You'd need an army to even think about infiltrating it. The only reason we've gotten this far is because of [protag]'s reputation."
    new "Have you seen this place? You'd need an army to even think about infiltrating it. The only reason we've gotten this far is because of [protag]'s reputation.\n你见过这地方吗？想潜入这里，你起码得带上一支军队。我们能走到这一步，全靠[protag]的名声。"

    old "Enok seems pretty intent on disagreeing with Sylrissa despite the gentle and calm manner he's using to do so. I can tell that he really does believe that Sylrissa was let go on purpose. Interesting."
    new "Enok seems pretty intent on disagreeing with Sylrissa despite the gentle and calm manner he's using to do so. I can tell that he really does believe that Sylrissa was let go on purpose. Interesting.\nEnok虽然语气温和平静，但看得出来，他铁了心要反驳Sylrissa。我能看出，他确实相信Sylrissa是被人故意放走的。有意思。"

    old "This situation might not be as straightforward as Sylrissa believes..."
    new "This situation might not be as straightforward as Sylrissa believes...\n情况也许并不像Sylrissa想的那么简单……"

    old "What do we do now? We know where the 'experiment chamber' is now, but we don't know if Gregorius is actually down there."
    new "What do we do now? We know where the 'experiment chamber' is now, but we don't know if Gregorius is actually down there.\n我们现在怎么办？我们知道那个“实验间”的位置了，但不知道Gregorius是不是真的就在下面。"

    old "I think I can solve that problem."
    new "I think I can solve that problem.\n我想这个问题我能解决。"

    old "Excuse me, my good man?"
    new "Excuse me, my good man?\n打扰一下，这位小哥？"

    old "Enok slides over to a young man I assume is an apprentice and starts talking with him. I'm not sure if it's magic or his natural charm, but the apprentice's cheeks turn a bright shade of red as Enok speaks with him."
    new "Enok slides over to a young man I assume is an apprentice and starts talking with him. I'm not sure if it's magic or his natural charm, but the apprentice's cheeks turn a bright shade of red as Enok speaks with him.\nEnok滑向一个我猜是学徒的年轻人，跟他攀谈起来。不知道是魔法的功劳还是他天生的魅力，随着Enok同他说话，那学徒的脸颊泛起一片通红。"

    old "A couple of minutes later, Enok returns to us with the information we were looking for."
    new "A couple of minutes later, Enok returns to us with the information we were looking for.\n几分钟后，Enok带着我们想要的情报回到我们身边。"

    old "Gregorius is in the workshop downstairs right now."
    new "Gregorius is in the workshop downstairs right now.\nGregorius现在就在楼下的工坊里。"

    old "Perfect!"
    new "Perfect!\n太好了！"

    old "What if he is not alone?"
    new "What if he is not alone?\n万一他不是一个人呢？"

    old "We're taking the risk."
    new "We're taking the risk.\n我们冒这个险。"

    old "Without waiting for a response from either of us, Sylrissa bolts down stairs. I look at Enok who sighs. We have no choice but to follow her now."
    new "Without waiting for a response from either of us, Sylrissa bolts down stairs. I look at Enok who sighs. We have no choice but to follow her now.\n不等我们俩任何一人回应，Sylrissa就冲下了楼梯。我看了看Enok，他叹了口气。我们别无选择，只能跟着她走。"

    old "As soon as we get to the workshop, I make a point of locating Sylrissa."
    new "As soon as we get to the workshop, I make a point of locating Sylrissa.\n我们一进工坊，我立刻打定主意先找到Sylrissa的位置。"

    old "There's a stiffness in her posture and a dangerous aura eminating from her. She's like a wild animal. I've seen her angry plenty of times, but never quite like this."
    new "There's a stiffness in her posture and a dangerous aura eminating from her. She's like a wild animal. I've seen her angry plenty of times, but never quite like this.\n她的姿态紧绷，周身散发着一股危险的气息。她就像一头野兽。我见过她生气很多次，但从来没见过她这副模样。"

    old "Hm? Is someone there?"
    new "Hm? Is someone there?\n嗯？有人在那儿吗？"

    old "Gregorius' eyes widen in shock as Sylrissa slides into the light and reveals herself. I quickly look around the room to confirm that Gregorius is the only one in the room besides us. Luckily, he seems to be alone."
    new "Gregorius' eyes widen in shock as Sylrissa slides into the light and reveals herself. I quickly look around the room to confirm that Gregorius is the only one in the room besides us. Luckily, he seems to be alone.\n当Sylrissa滑入亮处现身时，Gregorius惊得瞪大了眼睛。我迅速扫视房间，确认这屋里除了我们之外只有Gregorius一个人。幸运的是，他似乎是独自一人。"

    old "Y-you?!"
    new "Y-you?!\n你、是你？！"

    old "Surprised to see me? Did you really think I'd just roll over and die before I made you pay for what you've done?"
    new "Surprised to see me? Did you really think I'd just roll over and die before I made you pay for what you've done?\n见到我很惊讶？难道你真以为，在我让你为所做的一切付出代价之前，我会乖乖等死？"

    old "I don't... What's going on?"
    new "I don't... What's going on?\n我不……这是怎么回事？"

    old "Gregorius takes a step back. At first, I think it's out of fear, but too late I realize what his actual goal is. Before we can respond, he hits a button on the wall."
    new "Gregorius takes a step back. At first, I think it's out of fear, but too late I realize what his actual goal is. Before we can respond, he hits a button on the wall.\nGregorius后退了一步。起初我以为他是出于恐惧，但等我意识到他真正的目的时，已经太迟了。我们还没来得及反应，他就按下了墙上的一个按钮。"

    old "Two hidden panels along on the wall open up, releasing two golems that immediately charge towards us!"
    new "Two hidden panels along on the wall open up, releasing two golems that immediately charge towards us!\n墙上有两块隐藏的面板打开，放出两尊魔像，立刻朝我们冲了过来！"

    old "Your petty tricks won't save you!"
    new "Your petty tricks won't save you!\n你的小把戏救不了你！"

    old "What are you doing here? What do you want?"
    new "What are you doing here? What do you want?\n你在这里做什么？你想干什么？"

    old "W-wait a moment. You're [protag]! The Envoy of Grimoire! We've met before! I was on the council. Apolimesho is a good friend of mine! Please, tell this monster to stop!"
    new "W-wait a moment. You're [protag]! The Envoy of Grimoire! We've met before! I was on the council. Apolimesho is a good friend of mine! Please, tell this monster to stop!\n等、等一下。你是[protag]！Envoy of Grimoire！我们以前见过面！我当时在议会里。Apolimesho是我的好朋友！求你了，叫这个怪物住手！"

    old "That was a poor choice of words."
    new "That was a poor choice of words.\n这个词用得太糟了。"

    old "You're the monster! I--"
    new "You're the monster! I--\n你才是怪物！我——"

    old "Sylrissa, stop!"
    new "Sylrissa, stop!\nSylrissa，住手！"

    old "Just as Sylrissa lunges at Gregorius, Enok casts a freezing spell to stop her. She tries to fight it, but the icy crystals forming around her body hold her in place."
    new "Just as Sylrissa lunges at Gregorius, Enok casts a freezing spell to stop her. She tries to fight it, but the icy crystals forming around her body hold her in place.\n就在Sylrissa扑向Gregorius的当口，Enok施放了一道冰冻咒语拦住她。她拼命挣扎，但围着她身体凝结起来的冰晶把她牢牢定在原地。"

    old "Damn you, Enok! I can't--"
    new "Damn you, Enok! I can't--\n该死的，Enok！我没法——"

    old "We came here for answers, remember? Don't you want to know why this happened to you?"
    new "We came here for answers, remember? Don't you want to know why this happened to you?\n我们是来寻求答案的，记得吗？你难道不想知道，这一切为什么会发生在你身上？"

    old "Sylrissa grits her teeth, but says nothing. That's as much of a yes as we're going to get from her right now."
    new "Sylrissa grits her teeth, but says nothing. That's as much of a yes as we're going to get from her right now.\nSylrissa咬紧牙关，却一言不发。眼下从她那里，这就算是答应了吧。"

    old "We have some questions for you, Gregorius, and you'd better answer them honestly because I'm going to cast the Eye of the Gorgon spell on you."
    new "We have some questions for you, Gregorius, and you'd better answer them honestly because I'm going to cast the Eye of the Gorgon spell on you.\nGregorius，我们有几个问题要问你，你最好老实回答，因为我要对你施放Eye of the Gorgon咒语。"

    old "What? How is that possible? That spell is dark magic! It's forbidden! It's cursed!"
    new "What? How is that possible? That spell is dark magic! It's forbidden! It's cursed!\n什么？怎么可能？那个咒语是黑魔法！是被禁止的！是受诅咒的！"

    old "What can I say? I'm kind of a rebel."
    new "What can I say? I'm kind of a rebel.\n我能说什么呢？我这个人有点叛逆。"

    old "Anyway, I'm sure I don't need to tell an educated man such as yourself what this spell does."
    new "Anyway, I'm sure I don't need to tell an educated man such as yourself what this spell does.\n总之，我想不必由我告诉你这样的饱学之士，这个咒语会有什么效果。"

    old "Wait a moment, Enok, what do you mean? The spell only forces him to tell the truth, right?"
    new "Wait a moment, Enok, what do you mean? The spell only forces him to tell the truth, right?\n等一下，Enok，你这是什么意思？这个咒语不是只会强迫他说真话吗？"

    old "That's what Enok told me, but the terror on Gregorius' face tells me there's a more sinister aspect to this spell."
    new "That's what Enok told me, but the terror on Gregorius' face tells me there's a more sinister aspect to this spell.\nEnok是这么跟我说的，但Gregorius脸上那副惊恐的神色告诉我，这个咒语还有更阴险的一面。"

    old "I'm sorry, [protag]. I wasn't completely honest with you."
    new "I'm sorry, [protag]. I wasn't completely honest with you.\n对不起，[protag]。我没有完全跟你说实话。"

    old "There are two versions of the spell I'm using. Yes, one will force the target to tell the truth. The other, which is said to have been crafted by Morax herself, will make the target's head explode if he tells a lie."
    new "There are two versions of the spell I'm using. Yes, one will force the target to tell the truth. The other, which is said to have been crafted by Morax herself, will make the target's head explode if he tells a lie.\n我要用的这个咒语有两个版本。没错，其中一个会强迫目标说真话。而另一个，据说是Morax亲手创造的，只要目标撒谎，就会让他的脑袋爆炸。"

    old "I don't want to die!"
    new "I don't want to die!\n我不想死！"

    old "Then you should probably tell the truth."
    new "Then you should probably tell the truth.\n那你最好还是说实话。"

    old "The spell Enok cast on Sylrissa fades and, while she still looks grumpy, she has calmed down a bit. She at least seems interested in what Gregorius has to say."
    new "The spell Enok cast on Sylrissa fades and, while she still looks grumpy, she has calmed down a bit. She at least seems interested in what Gregorius has to say.\nEnok施在Sylrissa身上的咒语渐渐消散，虽然她看起来还是气鼓鼓的，但总算冷静了一些。至少她似乎对Gregorius要说的话来了兴趣。"

    old "I'm not good at asking questions. Go ahead, [protag]. I'll decide what to do after I hear his answers."
    new "I'm not good at asking questions. Go ahead, [protag]. I'll decide what to do after I hear his answers.\n我不擅长问问题。你来问吧，[protag]。等听完他的回答，我再决定怎么办。"

    old "Be careful, [protag]. This spell requires a lot of magic to work. I believe that the other mages here will eventually sense it. We should limit it to three questions. Any more than that and we'll probably be found out and arrested."
    new "Be careful, [protag]. This spell requires a lot of magic to work. I believe that the other mages here will eventually sense it. We should limit it to three questions. Any more than that and we'll probably be found out and arrested.\n小心，[protag]。这个咒语需要大量魔力才能维持。我相信这里的其他法师最终会察觉到它。我们最多只能问三个问题。再问下去，我们很可能就会被发现、被逮捕。"

    old "Right. Three questions... I'd better make them count."
    new "Right. Three questions... I'd better make them count.\n好。三个问题……我最好让每个问题都问到点子上。"

    old "What? She was just one test subjects they brought us!"
    new "What? She was just one test subjects they brought us!\n什么？她只是他们给我们送来的试验对象之一！"

    old "You mean that you didn't pick her in particular? Because she was a young, defenseless naga?"
    new "You mean that you didn't pick her in particular? Because she was a young, defenseless naga?\n你是说你并不是特意选中她的？不是因为她是个年轻又毫无反抗之力的naga？"

    old "Well..."
    new "Well...\n这个嘛……"

    old "Exploding head. Remember."
    new "Exploding head. Remember.\n脑袋会爆炸。别忘了。"

    old "Ah, Yes! Yes, of course. We did tell the Witch Hunters to bring us young subjects for our tests. Obviously, they were easier to hold captive and... to experiment with."
    new "Ah, Yes! Yes, of course. We did tell the Witch Hunters to bring us young subjects for our tests. Obviously, they were easier to hold captive and... to experiment with.\n啊，是！是，当然。我们确实让Witch Hunters给我们送来年轻的试验对象。显然，他们更容易囚禁，也更容易……拿来实验。"

    old "But it wasn't like we targeted her in particular! She wasn't special. She was just one of many."
    new "But it wasn't like we targeted her in particular! She wasn't special. She was just one of many.\n但我们并不是特意针对她！她并不特别。她只是众多试验对象中的一个。"

    old "I glance Sylrissa's way. There's no mistaking the disgust on her face as she keeps her eyes focused on Gregorius."
    new "I glance Sylrissa's way. There's no mistaking the disgust on her face as she keeps her eyes focused on Gregorius.\n我朝Sylrissa瞥了一眼。她的眼睛始终盯着Gregorius，脸上的厌恶之情表露无遗。"

    old "My only goal was to help others! Really!"
    new "My only goal was to help others! Really!\n我唯一的目标就是帮助他人！真的！"

    old "Help others?"
    new "Help others?\n帮助他人？"

    old "Yes. I was studying the extraordinary regenerative properties of your tails. I was hoping to synthetize a potion to cure other races using the same principles. For example, soldiers who'd lost their limbs in battles."
    new "Yes. I was studying the extraordinary regenerative properties of your tails. I was hoping to synthetize a potion to cure other races using the same principles. For example, soldiers who'd lost their limbs in battles.\n是的。我在研究你们尾巴那非凡的再生能力。我本想用同样的原理合成一种药剂，去治愈其他种族。比如，在战斗中失去四肢的士兵。"

    old "Did you succeed?"
    new "Did you succeed?\n你成功了吗？"

    old "Partially, yes. The potion we created... It doesn't always succeed. We haven't ascertained the reason why, but some subjects recover completely while others experience no changes whatsoever."
    new "Partially, yes. The potion we created... It doesn't always succeed. We haven't ascertained the reason why, but some subjects recover completely while others experience no changes whatsoever.\n算是部分成功了。我们造出的药剂……并不总是奏效。我们还没查明原因，但有些试验对象完全康复了，另一些则毫无变化。"

    old "So you didn't accomplish anything reliable."
    new "So you didn't accomplish anything reliable.\n所以你并没有做出任何可靠的东西。"

    old "How dare you! Reliable or not, you have no idea how many lives my research managed to save. My own niece among them!"
    new "How dare you! Reliable or not, you have no idea how many lives my research managed to save. My own niece among them!\n你竟敢这么说！可靠与否先不论，你根本不知道我的研究挽救了多少生命。其中就有我自己的侄女！"

    old "She lost her leg when she was captured by naga bandits! If it hadn't been for the studies we conducted on you and the others..."
    new "She lost her leg when she was captured by naga bandits! If it hadn't been for the studies we conducted on you and the others...\n她被naga强盗抓走时丢了一条腿！要不是我们在你和其他人身上做的研究……"

    old "The potion worked and she regained her leg, thank Tayrion. She can walk and run like the other children now."
    new "The potion worked and she regained her leg, thank Tayrion. She can walk and run like the other children now.\n药剂起效了，她的腿重新长了出来，感谢Tayrion。她现在能像其他孩子一样走路奔跑了。"

    old "Sylrissa lowers her gaze, as if thinking over what she just heard."
    new "Sylrissa lowers her gaze, as if thinking over what she just heard.\nSylrissa垂下目光，仿佛在消化她刚刚听到的话。"

    old "Enok looks at Gregorius and makes an exploding gesture with his hands."
    new "Enok looks at Gregorius and makes an exploding gesture with his hands.\nEnok看着Gregorius，用双手比了个爆炸的手势。"

    old "Boom!"
    new "Boom!\n砰！"

    old "Alright, alright! Yes. We experimented on other nagas."
    new "Alright, alright! Yes. We experimented on other nagas.\n好，好！是的。我们对其他naga也做过实验。"

    old "You experimented on them? That's what you keep telling yourself? No. You tortured them. You tortured us."
    new "You experimented on them? That's what you keep telling yourself? No. You tortured them. You tortured us.\n你对她们做过实验？你就是这么自我安慰的？不。你是在折磨她们。你折磨了我们。"

    old "Do you think I took pleasure in that? No. It was for science."
    new "Do you think I took pleasure in that? No. It was for science.\n你以为我从中得到乐趣了吗？不。那是为了科学。"

    old "I think I need to cut you in half now. For science, of course."
    new "I think I need to cut you in half now. For science, of course.\n我想我现在该把你劈成两半了。当然，也是为了科学。"

    old "Calm down, Sylrissa."
    new "Calm down, Sylrissa.\n冷静点，Sylrissa。"

    old "No. I am not. This is my workshop. I work here. I find it easier to work underground, away from the noise of the upper levels."
    new "No. I am not. This is my workshop. I work here. I find it easier to work underground, away from the noise of the upper levels.\n不，我没有。这是我的工坊。我就在这里工作。我觉得在地下工作更轻松，可以远离上层的喧嚣。"

    old "And I haven't done any more experiments involving live subjects."
    new "And I haven't done any more experiments involving live subjects.\n而且我已经没有再做过涉及活体试验对象的实验了。"

    old "Oh. So you've moved on to torturing dead nagas now? Live nagas aren't enjoyable enough for you anymore?"
    new "Oh. So you've moved on to torturing dead nagas now? Live nagas aren't enjoyable enough for you anymore?\n哦。所以你现在改折磨死掉的naga了？活的naga已经让你提不起兴致了吗？"

    old "I didn't say they were nagas! I was experimenting on the various undead creatures coming from N'Mar in an attempt to try to identify what kind of magic is making them behave like sentient beings."
    new "I didn't say they were nagas! I was experimenting on the various undead creatures coming from N'Mar in an attempt to try to identify what kind of magic is making them behave like sentient beings.\n我没说她们是naga！我是在研究从N'Mar涌来的各种亡灵生物，想弄清楚究竟是哪种魔法让它们表现得像有知觉的活物一样。"

    old "Color me intrigued. Any interesting findings yet?"
    new "Color me intrigued. Any interesting findings yet?\n这倒是勾起了我的兴趣。有什么有趣的发现了吗？"

    old "I'm the Envoy of Grimoire. You can tell us."
    new "I'm the Envoy of Grimoire. You can tell us.\n我是Envoy of Grimoire。你可以告诉我们。"

    old "Sadly, no. The only thing I've been able to determine is that there is some incredibly complex and powerful magic at work here. I've never seen anything like it before."
    new "Sadly, no. The only thing I've been able to determine is that there is some incredibly complex and powerful magic at work here. I've never seen anything like it before.\n很遗憾，没有。我唯一能确定的是，这里有某种极其复杂而强大的魔法在起作用。我以前从没见过这样的东西。"

    old "Escaped? I released her."
    new "Escaped? I released her.\n逃走的？是我放了她。"

    old "Lies!"
    new "Lies!\n胡说！"

    old "I can't lie! I wouldn't risk it after that...mage..."
    new "I can't lie! I wouldn't risk it after that...mage...\n我没法撒谎！在那位……法师……对我做过那些之后，我可不敢冒险。"

    old "'Battlemage extraordinaire' might be the title you're looking for."
    new "'Battlemage extraordinaire' might be the title you're looking for.\n你要找的头衔，也许是“出类拔萃的战斗法师”。"

    old "Yes, whatever. After what he did to me... It's the truth!"
    new "Yes, whatever. After what he did to me... It's the truth!\n是，随便吧。在他对我做了那种事之后……我说的是真的！"

    old "So all of your test subjects were eventually released?"
    new "So all of your test subjects were eventually released?\n所以你的所有试验对象最终都被放走了？"

    old "...No. Not all. Sadly, some didn't make it through all of the experiments."
    new "...No. Not all. Sadly, some didn't make it through all of the experiments.\n……不。不是全部。很遗憾，有些没能挺过所有的实验。"

    old "Argh! You monster!"
    new "Argh! You monster!\n啊——！你这个怪物！"

    old "Sylrissa! We're not done yet!"
    new "Sylrissa! We're not done yet!\nSylrissa！我们还没问完！"

    old "You heard me. You know who I am. Who we are. If we let you live, what will you do?"
    new "You heard me. You know who I am. Who we are. If we let you live, what will you do?\n你听见我说的话了。你知道我是谁。知道我们是谁。如果我们留你一命，你会怎么做？"

    old "N-nothing..."
    new "N-nothing...\n什么……都不会做……"

    old "Think carefully before replying. The first sign of the head explosion is a light headache, but then it rapidly escalates..."
    new "Think carefully before replying. The first sign of the head explosion is a light headache, but then it rapidly escalates...\n回答之前先想清楚。脑袋爆炸的最初征兆是一阵轻微头痛，但接着就会迅速加剧……"

    old "I won't say anything! It's the truth. I'm too scared of you!"
    new "I won't say anything! It's the truth. I'm too scared of you!\n我什么都不会说的！这是实话。我太怕你了！"

    old "Hmm. For once I believe you."
    new "Hmm. For once I believe you.\n嗯。这一次我信你。"

    old "Enough questions! We've heard enough!"
    new "Enough questions! We've heard enough!\n问够了！我们听得够多了！"

    old "Yes. We need to leave now, before they discover us."
    new "Yes. We need to leave now, before they discover us.\n是的。我们得趁他们还没发现，赶紧离开。"

    old "What about Gregorius?"
    new "What about Gregorius?\n那Gregorius怎么办？"

    old "Sylrissa goes quiet and looks Gregorius in the eyes. I can't tell what she's thinking."
    new "Sylrissa goes quiet and looks Gregorius in the eyes. I can't tell what she's thinking.\nSylrissa安静下来，直视着Gregorius的眼睛。我看不出她在想什么。"

    old "As the seconds pass, Gregorius' body begins to shake uncontrollably in fear. He's convinced that he's going to die."
    new "As the seconds pass, Gregorius' body begins to shake uncontrollably in fear. He's convinced that he's going to die.\n随着时间一秒秒过去，Gregorius的身体开始因恐惧而控制不住地发抖。他确信自己必死无疑。"

    old "Please, Sylrissa! Don't you remember?"
    new "Please, Sylrissa! Don't you remember?\n求你了，Sylrissa！你难道不记得了吗？"

    old "Remember what?"
    new "Remember what?\n记得什么？"

    old "I... I risked my career to return you safely to the swamp. A lot of the other mages... They thought that we should terminate you and the others. I argued against it. I'd had enough of death. I didn't want to see you end up like some of the other test subjects."
    new "I... I risked my career to return you safely to the swamp. A lot of the other mages... They thought that we should terminate you and the others. I argued against it. I'd had enough of death. I didn't want to see you end up like some of the other test subjects.\n我……我赌上自己的前程，把你安全送回了沼泽。很多其他法师……他们认为应该把你们这些试验对象都处理掉。是我据理力争反对的。我已经受够了死亡。我不想看到你落得和某些试验对象一样的下场。"

    old "You bastard! You were killing young nagas!"
    new "You bastard! You were killing young nagas!\n你这混蛋！你害死了那么多年轻的naga！"

    old "N-not on purpose! We tried to keep them alive, but some of them were just too weak. They didn't make it through the experiments."
    new "N-not on purpose! We tried to keep them alive, but some of them were just too weak. They didn't make it through the experiments.\n不、不是故意的！我们努力想让她们活着，可有些实在太虚弱了。她们没能熬过实验。"

    old "You think that makes what you did okay? That somehow the fact that you didn't mean to kill us absolves you of your crimes?"
    new "You think that makes what you did okay? That somehow the fact that you didn't mean to kill us absolves you of your crimes?\n你觉得那样就能让你做过的事变得无可指责？就因为你并非存心要杀我们，就能免除你的罪过？"

    old "I... No. It doesn't."
    new "I... No. It doesn't.\n我……不。不能。"

    old "I'm sorry, Sylrissa."
    new "I'm sorry, Sylrissa.\n对不起，Sylrissa。"

    old "Don't do that! Don't say you're sorry! You have no right!"
    new "Don't do that! Don't say you're sorry! You have no right!\n别这样！别说对不起！你没有资格！"

    old "When I started the experiments, I didn't see you and the others as people."
    new "When I started the experiments, I didn't see you and the others as people.\n刚开始做实验的时候，我并没有把你和那些人当人看。"

    old "You were a vicious race of monsters that mercilessly killed my kind without a second thought. I only knew the stories. The stories of your kind attacking our merchants, raiding our villages, and devouring our children."
    new "You were a vicious race of monsters that mercilessly killed my kind without a second thought. I only knew the stories. The stories of your kind attacking our merchants, raiding our villages, and devouring our children.\n在我看来，你们是残暴的怪物种族，会毫不犹豫地杀害我的同胞。我那时只知道那些故事。那些关于你们袭击我们的商人、洗劫我们的村庄、吞噬我们孩子的故事。"

    old "What I was doing... There was nothing to feel guilty about. I was helping my fellow humans and if I killed a few of your kind in the process, who cared? You were evil, unredeemable creatures in my eyes."
    new "What I was doing... There was nothing to feel guilty about. I was helping my fellow humans and if I killed a few of your kind in the process, who cared? You were evil, unredeemable creatures in my eyes.\n我当时做的事……没什么好内疚的。我在帮助自己的人类同胞，如果过程中杀了几个你们这样的人，谁会在乎？在我眼里，你们是邪恶的、无可救药的生物。"

    old "But then I met you, Sylrissa. You changed everything."
    new "But then I met you, Sylrissa. You changed everything.\n但后来我遇到了你，Sylrissa。你改变了一切。"

    old "...?!"
    new "...?!\n……？！"

    old "Of all the test subjects, you were the only one that tried to talk to me."
    new "Of all the test subjects, you were the only one that tried to talk to me.\n在所有试验对象里，你是唯一一个试图跟我说话的人。"

    old "And, with each new question, you showed me that you weren't the souless monster I'd assumed you were. You were someone I could understand. Someone that I could relate to. Someone I could be endeared to."
    new "And, with each new question, you showed me that you weren't the souless monster I'd assumed you were. You were someone I could understand. Someone that I could relate to. Someone I could be endeared to.\n而且，每问一个新问题，你都让我看到，你并不是我想象中那种没有灵魂的怪物。你是我能理解的人。是能让我产生共鸣的人。是能让我生出好感的人。"

    old "I didn't wait for the others to make a decision on what we were going to do with the nagas."
    new "I didn't wait for the others to make a decision on what we were going to do with the nagas.\n我没有等其他人决定该怎么处置那些naga。"

    old "I cast a spell on you to make you appear dead to avoid arousing suspicion and smuggled you out of the guild. I suppose it had the unintended side effect of erasing a part of your memory but, as impossible as it sounds, I was the one who took you back to the swamp."
    new "I cast a spell on you to make you appear dead to avoid arousing suspicion and smuggled you out of the guild. I suppose it had the unintended side effect of erasing a part of your memory but, as impossible as it sounds, I was the one who took you back to the swamp.\n我朝你施了一个咒语，让你看起来像死了一样，以免引起怀疑，然后把你偷偷运出了协会。我想它有一个意想不到的副作用，就是抹去了你的一部分记忆，可是，尽管听上去不可能，确实是我把你带回了沼泽。"

    old "At the very least, I wanted to spare you."
    new "At the very least, I wanted to spare you.\n至少，我想饶你一命。"

    old "I resigned from the project a few months after that. I just... couldn't bear it anymore. You were an exception, but I always saw a bit of you in all of the nagas that came after. That made it hard to continue seeing them as mere test subjects."
    new "I resigned from the project a few months after that. I just... couldn't bear it anymore. You were an exception, but I always saw a bit of you in all of the nagas that came after. That made it hard to continue seeing them as mere test subjects.\n那之后过了几个月，我就退出了这个项目。我只是……再也受不了了。你是个例外，但我在后来那些naga身上，总能看见一点你的影子。这让我很难再把她们仅仅当作试验对象。"

    old "In the end, we did release the remaining nagas but... I don't know. Even with the somewhat successful results of our experiments, I still can't decide if it was all worth it."
    new "In the end, we did release the remaining nagas but... I don't know. Even with the somewhat successful results of our experiments, I still can't decide if it was all worth it.\n最终，我们确实放走了剩下的naga，可是……我不知道。即便实验算是小有成果，我仍然无法断定这一切是否值得。"

    old "Shut up! I don't want to listen anymore!"
    new "Shut up! I don't want to listen anymore!\n闭嘴！我不想再听下去了！"

    old "You weren't... You were supposed to be a monster! I was supposed to kill you and feel good about it!"
    new "You weren't... You were supposed to be a monster! I was supposed to kill you and feel good about it!\n你本该是……你本该是个怪物！我本该杀了你，然后为此感到痛快！"

    old "I'm sorry for taking that from you too then."
    new "I'm sorry for taking that from you too then.\n那我连你这份痛快也一并拿走了，抱歉。"

    old "Sylrissa, we need to hurry."
    new "Sylrissa, we need to hurry.\nSylrissa，我们得抓紧了。"

    old "I hate to rush her, but we've been here awhile now. I can't imagine we have much time left."
    new "I hate to rush her, but we've been here awhile now. I can't imagine we have much time left.\n我不想催她，可我们已经在这里待了好一阵了。我想我们剩下的时间不多了。"

    old "Sylrissa runs a hand through her hair and curses."
    new "Sylrissa runs a hand through her hair and curses.\nSylrissa抬手捋了捋头发，咒骂了一句。"

    old "Shit."
    new "Shit.\n该死。"

    old "Let's... go. I don't want to be here."
    new "Let's... go. I don't want to be here.\n我们……走吧。我不想待在这里。"

    old "You're letting me live?"
    new "You're letting me live?\n你放我一条生路？"

    old "Yeah. You can keep your pathetic life. I don't... want it anymore."
    new "Yeah. You can keep your pathetic life. I don't... want it anymore.\n对。你就留着那条可怜的小命吧。我已经……不想要了。"

    old "Thank you, Sylrissa."
    new "Thank you, Sylrissa.\n谢谢你，Sylrissa。"

    old "Tch."
    new "Tch.\n切。"

    old "I won't tell anyone that the three of you were here, but you need to hurry. I'm sure someone must have noticed the surge of dark magic by now."
    new "I won't tell anyone that the three of you were here, but you need to hurry. I'm sure someone must have noticed the surge of dark magic by now.\n我不会告诉任何人你们三人来过这里，但你们得赶紧。我想现在肯定已经有人注意到那股黑暗魔法的异动了。"

    old "You aren't quite what I thought you were, Gregorius."
    new "You aren't quite what I thought you were, Gregorius.\n你并不完全是我原先以为的那种人，Gregorius。"

    old "Even so..."
    new "Even so...\n即便如此……"

    old "Someone has to pay! I'm sorry, but I just can't let it go!"
    new "Someone has to pay! I'm sorry, but I just can't let it go!\n总得有人付出代价！对不起，但我就是放不下！"

    old "With her usual, ungodly speed, Sylrissa lunges towards Gregorius. I don't even see the cut happen. I just see the aftermath."
    new "With her usual, ungodly speed, Sylrissa lunges towards Gregorius. I don't even see the cut happen. I just see the aftermath.\nSylrissa以她那惯常的、快得不像话的速度扑向Gregorius。我甚至没看见那一刀是怎么挥出的。我只看见了后果。"

    old "Blood spurts from a thin red line on Gregorius' neck. He lifts his hands instinctively to cover the wound, but they never quite make it. His dead body slumps to the floor in a matter of seconds."
    new "Blood spurts from a thin red line on Gregorius' neck. He lifts his hands instinctively to cover the wound, but they never quite make it. His dead body slumps to the floor in a matter of seconds.\n鲜血从Gregorius脖子上一道细红的口子里喷涌而出。他本能地抬手去捂住伤口，却始终没能捂上。几秒钟后，他的尸体瘫倒在地。"

    old "There was no way Enok and I could have stopped her. I'm not sure Enok would've even wanted to."
    new "There was no way Enok and I could have stopped her. I'm not sure Enok would've even wanted to.\n我和Enok根本来不及阻止她。而且我也不能确定，Enok当时是否真的想阻止她。"

    old "We REALLY must go now."
    new "We REALLY must go now.\n我们现在真的必须走了。"

    old "Spurred on by Enok's words, we quickly make our way towards the exit. We don't have to worry about Gregorius talking to anyone, but there's always a chance that we could be noticed by some kind of magic device or a wandering mage."
    new "Spurred on by Enok's words, we quickly make our way towards the exit. We don't have to worry about Gregorius talking to anyone, but there's always a chance that we could be noticed by some kind of magic device or a wandering mage.\n在Enok的催促下，我们迅速朝出口赶去。我们不必担心Gregorius会告发我们，但总有可能被某种魔法装置或某个游荡的法师撞见。"

    old "Luckily, nobody stops us on our way out. For now at least, I think we're okay."
    new "Luckily, nobody stops us on our way out. For now at least, I think we're okay.\n幸运的是，出去的路上没有人拦住我们。至少眼下，我想我们是安全的。"

    old "Not wanting to push our luck, we immediately head back to the swamps. Not a single word is exchanged on the way back. Enok and I seem to have come to a silent agreement to give Sylrissa her space. She has a lot on her mind, after all."
    new "Not wanting to push our luck, we immediately head back to the swamps. Not a single word is exchanged on the way back. Enok and I seem to have come to a silent agreement to give Sylrissa her space. She has a lot on her mind, after all.\n不想再碰运气，我们立刻动身返回沼泽。回去的路上，谁也没有说一句话。Enok和我似乎达成了无声的默契，给Sylrissa留出空间。毕竟，她心里装着太多事。"

    old "It's only when I'm about to depart that I break that silence."
    new "It's only when I'm about to depart that I break that silence.\n直到我准备离开时，才打破了那片沉默。"

    old "Well... That was an unexpected outcome. I guess I'm just glad it's over."
    new "Well... That was an unexpected outcome. I guess I'm just glad it's over.\n嗯……这结局真是出乎意料。我想我只是庆幸这件事总算结束了。"

    old "Sylrissa, before I go... Can I ask one question?"
    new "Sylrissa, before I go... Can I ask one question?\nSylrissa，在我走之前……我能问一个问题吗？"

    old "I suppose I owe you that much."
    new "I suppose I owe you that much.\n我想这点我还是欠你的。"

    old "Did you really have to kill him, Sylrissa?"
    new "Did you really have to kill him, Sylrissa?\n你真的非杀他不可吗，Sylrissa？"

    old "Experimenting on me and my kind? What do you think a human would have done in my place? What would YOU have done?"
    new "Experimenting on me and my kind? What do you think a human would have done in my place? What would YOU have done?\n拿我和我的同类做实验？换作一个人类处在我的位置，他会怎么做？换作你，你会怎么做？"

    old "After everything he did... I just... I couldn't let it go, [protag]."
    new "After everything he did... I just... I couldn't let it go, [protag].\n在他做了那么多之后……我只是……我放不下，[protag]。"

    old "I can't even begin to imagine what you went through. I'm sorry, Sylrissa."
    new "I can't even begin to imagine what you went through. I'm sorry, Sylrissa.\n我甚至无法想象你经历了什么。对不起，Sylrissa。"

    old "To be honest, I thought killing him would feel better."
    new "To be honest, I thought killing him would feel better.\n说实话，我本以为杀了他会让我好受一些。"

    old "Still... I think I can move on now. I feel like a curse I had on me has been removed."
    new "Still... I think I can move on now. I feel like a curse I had on me has been removed.\n不过……我想现在我能向前看了。我感觉压在我身上的诅咒好像被解除了。"

    old "Then at least some good came out of this."
    new "Then at least some good came out of this.\n那至少这件事还有一点好结果。"

    old "Did you get the closure you were looking for?"
    new "Did you get the closure you were looking for?\n你得到了你想要的那个了结吗？"

    old "I... No. But... I think this is better."
    new "I... No. But... I think this is better.\n我……没有。不过……我觉得这样更好。"

    old "I thought Gregorius was a monster, but he wasn't. Not really. I mean, yes, he did terrible things but I might have done similar things in his position."
    new "I thought Gregorius was a monster, but he wasn't. Not really. I mean, yes, he did terrible things but I might have done similar things in his position.\n我本以为Gregorius是个怪物，但他不是。不完全是。我是说，没错，他做过可怕的事，但处在他的位置，我或许也会做出类似的事。"

    old "And now that I've been thinking about it for awhile, there were times when he was actually very considerate."
    new "And now that I've been thinking about it for awhile, there were times when he was actually very considerate.\n而且我翻来覆去想了很久，其实有些时候，他确实非常体贴。"

    old "He snuck me treats sometimes, patiently answered all my dumb questions... And, after he got to know me better, he started using a spell when he cut my tail to make it hurt less."
    new "He snuck me treats sometimes, patiently answered all my dumb questions... And, after he got to know me better, he started using a spell when he cut my tail to make it hurt less.\n他有时会偷偷给我带好吃的，耐心回答我所有蠢问题……而且，等他更了解我之后，他割我尾巴的时候会施一个咒语，让它没那么疼。"

    old "That doesn't make up for everything he did to me, but... Maybe if I focus on those things I'll be able to forgive him."
    new "That doesn't make up for everything he did to me, but... Maybe if I focus on those things I'll be able to forgive him.\n这并不能弥补他对我做过的一切，但是……也许我把心思放在这些事上，就能原谅他。"

    old "It's going to be hard, but it's what I want to do."
    new "It's going to be hard, but it's what I want to do.\n那会很难，但这是我想做的事。"

    old "That's pretty mature of you, Sylrissa."
    new "That's pretty mature of you, Sylrissa.\n你能这么想很成熟，Sylrissa。"

    old "Well, I guess I made the mistake of trying to see things from his perspective."
    new "Well, I guess I made the mistake of trying to see things from his perspective.\n嗯，我想我是犯了个错，试着从他的角度看问题了。"

    old "And it's not like I'm actually any better than him. If I had to experiement and kill someone to save the people I care about, I'm pretty sure I would do it."
    new "And it's not like I'm actually any better than him. If I had to experiement and kill someone to save the people I care about, I'm pretty sure I would do it.\n再说我也并不真的比他好到哪里去。如果我必须做实验、杀人，才能救回我在乎的人，我敢肯定我也会那么做。"

    old "You mean me and Enok?"
    new "You mean me and Enok?\n你是指我和Enok？"

    old "Well, yes. But, um, the others too. We're a team now. I care about all of us."
    new "Well, yes. But, um, the others too. We're a team now. I care about all of us.\n嗯，是的。不过，呃，其他人也算。我们现在是一个团队了。我在乎我们所有人。"

    old "Even Leena?"
    new "Even Leena?\n连Leena也算？"

    old "Ugh. No, maybe not Leena."
    new "Ugh. No, maybe not Leena.\n呃。不，Leena也许不算。"

    old "But of course, only because she's capable of saving herself. There's no other reason in particular, really. No, no. It's not because I actually dislike her or anything. That's absolutely absurd."
    new "But of course, only because she's capable of saving herself. There's no other reason in particular, really. No, no. It's not because I actually dislike her or anything. That's absolutely absurd.\n当然，那只是因为她自己有能力脱身。真的没有别的特别的原因。不不不。绝不是因为我真的讨厌她或别的什么。那简直太荒唐了。"

    old "We all laugh and I'm happy to see Sylrissa getting back to her former self."
    new "We all laugh and I'm happy to see Sylrissa getting back to her former self.\n我们都笑了，我很高兴看到Sylrissa又变回了从前的她。"

    old "I'm sure everyone will think twice before threatening any of us with a protector like you looking after us."
    new "I'm sure everyone will think twice before threatening any of us with a protector like you looking after us.\n我相信，有像你这样强大的保护者照看我们，任何人再想威胁我们，都会三思而后行。"

    old "Thank you, [protag], for helping me. I really owe you for this one."
    new "Thank you, [protag], for helping me. I really owe you for this one.\n谢谢你，[protag]，谢谢你帮了我。这一次我真的欠你。"

    old "I say the phrase half-jokingly, but Sylrissa uses my words as an invitation. In one of her usual, quick movements, she approaches me and wraps her arms around my torso. Then, slowing down, she moves her head closer to mine until our lips meet."
    new "I say the phrase half-jokingly, but Sylrissa uses my words as an invitation. In one of her usual, quick movements, she approaches me and wraps her arms around my torso. Then, slowing down, she moves her head closer to mine until our lips meet.\n我这话是半开玩笑说的，但Sylrissa把我的话当成了邀请。她用她那惯常的利落动作靠近我，双臂环住我的腰。然后，她放缓动作，把脸朝我凑近，直到我们的嘴唇相触。"

    old "This time, she kisses me for real, leaning into it passionately as she slides her hands up my back."
    new "This time, she kisses me for real, leaning into it passionately as she slides her hands up my back.\n这一次，她是真的吻了我，热情地迎上来，双手顺着我的背向上游移。"

    old "I vaguely recall that Enok is still here but, as Sylrissa slips her tongue into my mouth, any embarrassment I feel is overwhelmed by the desire to keep up this momentum."
    new "I vaguely recall that Enok is still here but, as Sylrissa slips her tongue into my mouth, any embarrassment I feel is overwhelmed by the desire to keep up this momentum.\n我模糊地想起Enok还在这里，但随着Sylrissa把舌头探进我口中，我心中的尴尬全被想要继续下去的热望压倒了。"

    old "Sylrissa quickly consumes my every thought."
    new "Sylrissa quickly consumes my every thought.\nSylrissa很快占据了我全部的心思。"

    old "That is, until she breaks the kiss, cruelly sending me back to reality as she slowly moves away from me. Her eyes stay locked on mine, looking for any sign of reaction from me."
    new "That is, until she breaks the kiss, cruelly sending me back to reality as she slowly moves away from me. Her eyes stay locked on mine, looking for any sign of reaction from me.\n直到她放开这个吻，残忍地把我拽回现实，缓缓从我身边退开。她的目光始终锁在我身上，想从我脸上找到任何反应。"

    old "How's that for token of gratitude?"
    new "How's that for token of gratitude?\n这个谢礼怎么样？"

    old "I... Ehm... It's..."
    new "I... Ehm... It's...\n我……呃……这……"

    old "Haha. Yes, Sylrissa does tend to have that effect."
    new "Haha. Yes, Sylrissa does tend to have that effect.\n哈哈。是啊，Sylrissa向来有这种本事。"

    old "Enok thankfully breaks his silence, saving me from having to give Sylrissa a proper response."
    new "Enok thankfully breaks his silence, saving me from having to give Sylrissa a proper response.\n幸好Enok打破了沉默，免得我非得给Sylrissa一个像样的回应不可。"

    old "Sylrissa smiles and some small tears forms on the sides of her beautiful eyes. She slides closer to me and then takes me into a hug."
    new "Sylrissa smiles and some small tears forms on the sides of her beautiful eyes. She slides closer to me and then takes me into a hug.\nSylrissa微笑着，美丽的眼角泛起点点泪光。她朝我凑得更近，然后把我拥进怀里。"

    old "Thanks again, [protag]."
    new "Thanks again, [protag].\n再次谢谢你，[protag]。"

    old "She holds me for several seconds before pulling away and wiping the tears from her eyes. She smiles at me, then looks back to Enok who smiles back at her in return."
    new "She holds me for several seconds before pulling away and wiping the tears from her eyes. She smiles at me, then looks back to Enok who smiles back at her in return.\n她抱了我几秒钟，才松开手，擦去眼角的泪水。她冲我笑了笑，又回头看向Enok，Enok也朝她回以微笑。"

    old "I'm glad that, after everything she's been through in the past, she can still find happiness now."
    new "I'm glad that, after everything she's been through in the past, she can still find happiness now.\n我很高兴，在经历过过去那些磨难之后，她现在依然能找到幸福。"

    old "I need to go. Stay safe, you two."
    new "I need to go. Stay safe, you two.\n我得走了。你们两个注意安全。"

    old "See you around, [protag]."
    new "See you around, [protag].\n回头见，[protag]。"

    old "I find myself once again traveling to the humid swamps to see Sylrissa."
    new "I find myself once again traveling to the humid swamps to see Sylrissa.\n我发现自己又一次前往潮湿的沼泽去见Sylrissa。"

    old "As I approach our usual spot, I start to hear people screaming at each other. Could it be...?"
    new "As I approach our usual spot, I start to hear people screaming at each other. Could it be...?\n快到我们常去的地方时，我听见有人在大声争吵。该不会是……？"

    old "I quicken my step, hoping to reach them before things get out of hand."
    new "I quicken my step, hoping to reach them before things get out of hand.\n我加快脚步，希望能在事情失控之前赶到他们那里。"

    old "When I arrive, I spot Enok leaving with a grumpy look on his face while Sylrissa stays near the river, her tail dipped in the water."
    new "When I arrive, I spot Enok leaving with a grumpy look on his face while Sylrissa stays near the river, her tail dipped in the water.\n我赶到时，看到Enok板着一张脸离开，而Sylrissa则待在河边，尾巴浸在水里。"

    old "...Is this a bad time?"
    new "...Is this a bad time?\n……我是不是来得不是时候？"

    old "Oh, hey, [protag]. And no. It's fine. Come here."
    new "Oh, hey, [protag]. And no. It's fine. Come here.\n哦，嘿，[protag]。没有。没事。过来吧。"

    old "I move closer to Sylrissa, who keeps her gaze fixed on the water flowing around her tail. The sound of the running river has a relaxing effect, almost mesmerizing."
    new "I move closer to Sylrissa, who keeps her gaze fixed on the water flowing around her tail. The sound of the running river has a relaxing effect, almost mesmerizing.\n我走近Sylrissa，她的目光始终停留在绕着尾巴流动的水面上。潺潺河水的声音让人放松，几乎令人沉醉。"

    old "Isn't it beautiful? I could just stay here and watch it all day."
    new "Isn't it beautiful? I could just stay here and watch it all day.\n很美吧？我可以就这么待在这里看上一整天。"

    old "Come on, [protag], I was talking about the river!"
    new "Come on, [protag], I was talking about the river!\n得了，[protag]，我说的是这条河！"

    old "...but I do appreciate what you said. You're such a tease."
    new "...but I do appreciate what you said. You're such a tease.\n……不过你刚才说的话，我还是很受用。你可真会逗人。"

    old "I've learned from the master. Her name is Sylrissa."
    new "I've learned from the master. Her name is Sylrissa.\n我跟大师学的。她的名字叫Sylrissa。"

    old "Hmph. Why don't you sit down next to me?"
    new "Hmph. Why don't you sit down next to me?\n哼。你干嘛不坐到我旁边来？"

    old "Great minds think alike. That's what they say, right?"
    new "Great minds think alike. That's what they say, right?\n英雄所见略同。他们是这么说的，对吧？"

    old "I take a seat next to her and then scoot a little closer."
    new "I take a seat next to her and then scoot a little closer.\n我在她身边坐下，然后又往她那边挪了挪。"

    old "It's just... so relaxing."
    new "It's just... so relaxing.\n只是……太让人放松了。"

    old "I didn't think that you would be someone who appreciated things like this."
    new "I didn't think that you would be someone who appreciated things like this.\n我没想到你会是懂得欣赏这种景致的人。"

    old "Oh? You find it strange that a bloodthirsty naga would take time to appreciate nature's beauty and relax from time to time?"
    new "Oh? You find it strange that a bloodthirsty naga would take time to appreciate nature's beauty and relax from time to time?\n哦？你觉得奇怪吗，一个嗜血的naga居然会抽空欣赏自然之美，时不时放松一下？"

    old "Don't twist my words. You know I didn't mean it like that."
    new "Don't twist my words. You know I didn't mean it like that.\n别曲解我的话。你知道我不是那个意思。"

    old "It's just... Besides elves like me, I don't know a lot of races that take the time to notice how beautiful nature is. They're all so busy going about their daily lives. They forget to appreciate this kind of thing."
    new "It's just... Besides elves like me, I don't know a lot of races that take the time to notice how beautiful nature is. They're all so busy going about their daily lives. They forget to appreciate this kind of thing.\n只是……除了像我这样的elf，我不知道有多少种族会花时间去留意大自然有多美。他们都忙着过自己的日子。他们忘了去欣赏这一类的东西。"

    old "Most races-- humans, dwarves, elves... Well, no. Not elves. They usually make a point of appreciating nature. But it's pretty common for people from other races to be too preoccupied with their busy schedules to enjoy things like this."
    new "Most races-- humans, dwarves, elves... Well, no. Not elves. They usually make a point of appreciating nature. But it's pretty common for people from other races to be too preoccupied with their busy schedules to enjoy things like this.\n大多数种族——人类、dwarf、elf……嗯，不对。elf除外。他们通常都会特意去欣赏自然。不过其他种族的人，常常太专注于忙碌的日程，无暇享受这样的东西，这很常见。"

    old "Ah, I see. I noticed that when you took me to see Grimoire at sunset. There was a non stop activity even after dark."
    new "Ah, I see. I noticed that when you took me to see Grimoire at sunset. There was a non stop activity even after dark.\n啊，我明白了。你带我去看日落时分的Grimoire时，我就注意到了。天都黑了，那里还是忙个不停。"

    old "Yeah, they never stop."
    new "Yeah, they never stop.\n是啊，他们永远停不下来。"

    old "That's a bid sad, isn't it? All those people and none of them have the time to just stop and enjoy the world they live in. I feel lucky compared to them because here I have all the time in the world."
    new "That's a bid sad, isn't it? All those people and none of them have the time to just stop and enjoy the world they live in. I feel lucky compared to them because here I have all the time in the world.\n那有点可悲，不是吗？那么多人，却没有一个有工夫停下脚步，好好享受自己所生活的这个世界。相比之下，我觉得自己很幸运，因为我在这里拥有世上所有的时间。"

    old "Yes and no. I mean... the swamps are my home, in a way. It's all I've known for most of my life, you know?"
    new "Yes and no. I mean... the swamps are my home, in a way. It's all I've known for most of my life, you know?\n算是吧，也算不是。我是说……这片沼泽在某种意义上就是我的家。我这辈子大部分时间都只熟悉这里，你懂吗？"

    old "However, being with you on this mission... It has sort of opened my eyes. You showed me that there was a big world out there. Different races, different cultures. So many things to do. So many interesting places."
    new "However, being with you on this mission... It has sort of opened my eyes. You showed me that there was a big world out there. Different races, different cultures. So many things to do. So many interesting places.\n不过，和你一起执行这个任务……在某种程度上开阔了我的眼界。你让我知道，外面有一个广阔的世界。不同的种族，不同的文化。有那么多事可做。有那么多有趣的地方。"

    old "If you ever want to take another trip to Grimoire, just let me know. I'd be glad to show you more of it."
    new "If you ever want to take another trip to Grimoire, just let me know. I'd be glad to show you more of it.\n如果你哪天想再去Grimoire逛一逛，尽管告诉我。我很乐意带你多看一些。"

    old "If was just me, I'd go with you to Grimoire right now, but..."
    new "If was just me, I'd go with you to Grimoire right now, but...\n如果只有我自己的话，我现在就会跟你去Grimoire，可是……"

    old "I... yes. I would like that. Thank you, [protag]. You're always so nice to me."
    new "I... yes. I would like that. Thank you, [protag]. You're always so nice to me.\n我……好。我很乐意。谢谢你，[protag]。你总是对我这么好。"

    old "You don't need to thank me. I honestly just like spending time with you. You know, if we hurry we might be able to get there in time for me to show you--"
    new "You don't need to thank me. I honestly just like spending time with you. You know, if we hurry we might be able to get there in time for me to show you--\n你不用谢我。我是真的喜欢和你待在一起。你知道吗，如果我们抓紧点，说不定还能赶在日落前到那儿，我就能带你看——"

    old "Wait. You misunderstood. I do want to go, but... Not right now."
    new "Wait. You misunderstood. I do want to go, but... Not right now.\n等等。你误会了。我是想去的，只是……不是现在。"

    old "Ah, let me guess. Enok?"
    new "Ah, let me guess. Enok?\n啊，让我猜猜。是Enok？"

    old "I thought I heard a fight while I was coming here. What happened?"
    new "I thought I heard a fight while I was coming here. What happened?\n我来的时候好像听见了争吵声。发生什么事了？"

    old "Nothing you need to worry about. It isn't anything big."
    new "Nothing you need to worry about. It isn't anything big.\n你不必担心。不是什么大事。"

    old "Even so, if there's something I can help with..."
    new "Even so, if there's something I can help with...\n即便如此，如果有什么我能帮上忙的……"

    old "You're very kind, [protag], but this is something that should stay between him and me. I need to solve it myself."
    new "You're very kind, [protag], but this is something that should stay between him and me. I need to solve it myself.\n你人真好，[protag]，但这件事只能是我和他之间的事。我得自己解决。"

    old "Besides, if you really wanted to help me, you would help me get to Gregorius."
    new "Besides, if you really wanted to help me, you would help me get to Gregorius.\n再说了，如果你真想帮我，你就帮我找到Gregorius。"

    old "She's still thinking about that, huh? I would've hoped she would have dropped it by now."
    new "She's still thinking about that, huh? I would've hoped she would have dropped it by now.\n她还在想着那件事啊。我本来还希望她现在已经放下了。"

    old "I'm not going to do that Sylrissa."
    new "I'm not going to do that Sylrissa.\n我不会那么做的，Sylrissa。"

    old "Yeah. I know."
    new "Yeah. I know.\n嗯。我知道。"

    old "Besides, you have already helped me with a much bigger problem. I'm already going to be in your debt forever as is. I don't need to go adding to it."
    new "Besides, you have already helped me with a much bigger problem. I'm already going to be in your debt forever as is. I don't need to go adding to it.\n再说了，你已经帮过我一个大得多的忙。我早就欠下你还不清的人情了。我不需要再往上加。"

    old "I see. I suppose I should start asking for something in return so you can start paying it off."
    new "I see. I suppose I should start asking for something in return so you can start paying it off.\n我明白了。那我想我该开始要点回报，好让你慢慢还清这笔债。"

    old "Oh? I look forward to seeing what you come up with."
    new "Oh? I look forward to seeing what you come up with.\n哦？我倒是很期待你会想出什么来。"

    old "She says it with a sly grin that sends my thoughts into dangerous territory."
    new "She says it with a sly grin that sends my thoughts into dangerous territory.\n她说这话时带着狡黠的笑，让我的思绪飘进了危险的领域。"

    old "We both stop talking at same time. She turns her attention to the river and I end up doing the same."
    new "We both stop talking at same time. She turns her attention to the river and I end up doing the same.\n我们俩同时停止了说话。她把注意力转向河面，我也照做了。"

    old "In this silence, the sound of running water and birds fluttering from tree to tree nearby becomes more prounounced. We're only there for a few minutes, but it feels like a pleasant eternity."
    new "In this silence, the sound of running water and birds fluttering from tree to tree nearby becomes more prounounced. We're only there for a few minutes, but it feels like a pleasant eternity.\n在这片寂静中，潺潺的水声和鸟儿在树间扑棱飞过的声音显得更加清晰。我们只在那里待了几分钟，却像是一段惬意的永恒。"

    old "Even if we're not talking to each other, spending time enjoying the scenery with Sylrissa like this is something I've grown to love."
    new "Even if we're not talking to each other, spending time enjoying the scenery with Sylrissa like this is something I've grown to love.\n即使彼此不说话，像这样和Sylrissa一起欣赏风景的时光，也已经成了我渐渐喜欢上的事。"

    old "After awhile, Sylrissa cautiously moves her hand closer to mine. When I don't make a move to stop her, she slides her hand over mine and entwines her fingers with mine."
    new "After awhile, Sylrissa cautiously moves her hand closer to mine. When I don't make a move to stop her, she slides her hand over mine and entwines her fingers with mine.\n过了一会儿，Sylrissa小心翼翼地让她的手朝我的手靠近。见我没有躲开，她便把手覆在我的手上，手指与我的交缠在一起。"

    old "She smiles at me and I smile back in turn, but we both remain silent. It's as if neither of us wants to risk ending such a perfect moment."
    new "She smiles at me and I smile back in turn, but we both remain silent. It's as if neither of us wants to risk ending such a perfect moment.\n她对我微笑，我也回以微笑，但我们俩都保持着沉默。仿佛谁都不愿冒险，去打破这样一个完美的时刻。"

    old "We stay like that for a bit longer before Sylrissa finally decides to speak."
    new "We stay like that for a bit longer before Sylrissa finally decides to speak.\n我们就那样又待了一会儿，Sylrissa才终于开口。"

    old "So...Do you ever think about what you'll do after all of this is over?"
    new "So...Do you ever think about what you'll do after all of this is over?\n那么……你有没有想过，这一切结束后你要做什么？"

    old "You? With children? That sounds like a terrible idea. And who says I'd marry you?"
    new "You? With children? That sounds like a terrible idea. And who says I'd marry you?\n你？带着孩子？那听起来可太糟了。而且谁说我一定会嫁给你？"

    old "Ouch. You're breaking my heart here, Sylrissa."
    new "Ouch. You're breaking my heart here, Sylrissa.\n哎哟。你这是在伤我的心啊，Sylrissa。"

    old "She giggles."
    new "She giggles.\n她咯咯地笑了。"

    old "Seriously, though. Considering how much travelling you do? What are you going to do with kids?"
    new "Seriously, though. Considering how much travelling you do? What are you going to do with kids?\n说真的。想想你到处旅行奔波，你要孩子干嘛？"

    old "What? You think I can't run around Aravorn with a gaggle of children in tow? They could carry my equipment for me."
    new "What? You think I can't run around Aravorn with a gaggle of children in tow? They could carry my equipment for me.\n怎么？你觉得我不能带着一窝孩子满Aravorn跑吗？他们还能帮我搬装备呢。"

    old "Maybe. Until they get eaten."
    new "Maybe. Until they get eaten.\n也许吧。直到他们被吃掉为止。"

    old "That's why I plan to have a lot of them."
    new "That's why I plan to have a lot of them.\n所以我打算多生几个。"

    old "That's terrible. And absurd. Almost as absurd as marrying a naga."
    new "That's terrible. And absurd. Almost as absurd as marrying a naga.\n那太可怕了。而且荒谬。几乎和嫁给一个naga一样荒谬。"

    old "I don't really see what's so absurd about that part."
    new "I don't really see what's so absurd about that part.\n我实在看不出这部分有什么荒谬的。"

    old "You wouldn't."
    new "You wouldn't.\n你当然看不出来。"

    old "Still... I was kind of looking for a serious answer, you know?"
    new "Still... I was kind of looking for a serious answer, you know?\n不过……我其实是想听一个认真的答案，你懂吗？"

    old "Yeah, I know. I don't really know what I want to do in the future though, Sylrissa."
    new "Yeah, I know. I don't really know what I want to do in the future though, Sylrissa.\n嗯，我知道。可是Sylrissa，我真的不知道我将来想做什么。"

    old "Sylrissa's hair bounces as she turns her head towards me and flashes me a big smile."
    new "Sylrissa's hair bounces as she turns her head towards me and flashes me a big smile.\nSylrissa转过头朝向我，头发跟着轻轻跳动，冲我绽开一个大大的笑容。"

    old "Yes! I would like that."
    new "Yes! I would like that.\n好！我很乐意。"

    old "I want to keep seeing each other too, no matter what both of us end up doing in the future."
    new "I want to keep seeing each other too, no matter what both of us end up doing in the future.\n我也想继续见到你，不管我们俩将来各自做什么。"

    old "Hearing her earnest reply warms my heart. I smile back and squeeze her hand affectionately."
    new "Hearing her earnest reply warms my heart. I smile back and squeeze her hand affectionately.\n听到她真诚的回答，我心里一暖。我回以微笑，怜爱地握了握她的手。"

    old "I can't seem to stay put in a single place. I guess I would resume my travels around the world."
    new "I can't seem to stay put in a single place. I guess I would resume my travels around the world.\n我似乎没法在一个地方安顿下来。我想我会重新踏上环游世界的旅程。"

    old "...I guess deep down I already knew that was going to be your answer."
    new "...I guess deep down I already knew that was going to be your answer.\n……我想在内心深处，我早就知道你会给出这个答案。"

    old "You know... You could come with me."
    new "You know... You could come with me.\n你知道吗……你可以跟我一起走。"

    old "Oh. This... this is unexpected."
    new "Oh. This... this is unexpected.\n哦。这……这太突然了。"

    old "Think about it. The two of us together, exploring Aravorn. Sounds kind of wonderful, right?"
    new "Think about it. The two of us together, exploring Aravorn. Sounds kind of wonderful, right?\n你想想看。我们俩一起，探索Aravorn。听起来挺美妙的，对吧？"

    old "The idea does have a certain charm to it."
    new "The idea does have a certain charm to it.\n这个想法确实有它迷人的地方。"

    old "Our little moment gets cut short when we hear some rustling coming from the vegetation nearby. Sylrissa stands quickly, ready to unsheathe her swords, when Enok slides out of the bushes and into view."
    new "Our little moment gets cut short when we hear some rustling coming from the vegetation nearby. Sylrissa stands quickly, ready to unsheathe her swords, when Enok slides out of the bushes and into view.\n附近树丛里传来一阵窸窣声，打断了我们的小小时光。Sylrissa迅速站起，准备拔剑，这时Enok从灌木丛中钻了出来，进入我们的视线。"

    old "Sorry, I didn't mean to startle you two."
    new "Sorry, I didn't mean to startle you two.\n抱歉，我不是故意吓你们俩的。"

    old "Don't worry about it. I'm just glad it was you and not some monster we'd have to deal with."
    new "Don't worry about it. I'm just glad it was you and not some monster we'd have to deal with.\n别担心。我只是庆幸来的是你，而不是什么我们还得应付的怪物。"

    old "Now that Enok is back, I should probably take my leave. He and Sylrissa still need to sort out that issue they were having earlier, after all."
    new "Now that Enok is back, I should probably take my leave. He and Sylrissa still need to sort out that issue they were having earlier, after all.\n既然Enok回来了，我想我该告辞了。毕竟，他和Sylrissa还得解决他们早先那个问题。"

    old "Anyway, this is probably a good time for me to get going."
    new "Anyway, this is probably a good time for me to get going.\n不管怎样，现在大概是我离开的好时机。"

    old "So soon?"
    new "So soon?\n这么快？"

    old "Duty calls. It was a pleasure, as always, but I need to get back to Grimoire."
    new "Duty calls. It was a pleasure, as always, but I need to get back to Grimoire.\n职责在身。和往常一样愉快，但我得回Grimoire了。"

    old "Bye, [protag]."
    new "Bye, [protag].\n再见，[protag]。"

    old "As I walk away, I glance back to see the two of them talking together. To my relief, they seem to be doing it in a calm and relaxed manner."
    new "As I walk away, I glance back to see the two of them talking together. To my relief, they seem to be doing it in a calm and relaxed manner.\n我走开时回头看了一眼，只见他俩正在一起交谈。让我安心的是，他们似乎聊得平静而放松。"

    old "I don't know what's going on between them. They've never fought like this before. At least, not as far as I know. I have to wonder if the root of their problem is actually me."
    new "I don't know what's going on between them. They've never fought like this before. At least, not as far as I know. I have to wonder if the root of their problem is actually me.\n我不知道他们之间发生了什么。他们以前从没这样吵过架。至少据我所知没有。我不得不怀疑，他们问题的根源会不会其实是我。"

    old "Maybe I am overthinking things though. It's kind of egotistical to think I'm the source of their issues, isn't it? I doubt I'm important enough to be worth fighting each other over."
    new "Maybe I am overthinking things though. It's kind of egotistical to think I'm the source of their issues, isn't it? I doubt I'm important enough to be worth fighting each other over.\n不过也许是我想太多了。觉得自己是他们问题的源头，未免有点自以为是，不是吗？我怀疑自己是否重要到值得他们为我争执。"

    old "I know there is a lot of pressing matters for me to attend to but, despite that, I find myself once again walking towards that special spot on the south border of the swamps, eager to see Sylrissa again."
    new "I know there is a lot of pressing matters for me to attend to but, despite that, I find myself once again walking towards that special spot on the south border of the swamps, eager to see Sylrissa again.\n我知道还有一大堆紧迫的事等着我去处理，但尽管如此，我发现自己又一次走向沼泽南边那个特别的地方，急切地想再见Syrissa一面。"

    old "Upon seeing me approach, she smiles and moves to meet me halfway."
    new "Upon seeing me approach, she smiles and moves to meet me halfway.\n看见我走近，她微笑着迎上前来，在半路与我相会。"

    old "[protag], I was just thinking about you!"
    new "[protag], I was just thinking about you!\n[protag]，我刚刚还在想你呢！"

    old "Naughty thoughts?"
    new "Naughty thoughts?\n是什么不正经的念头吗？"

    old "Yes!"
    new "Yes!\n是！"

    old "Oh... ehm... I was actually kind of joking-"
    new "Oh... ehm... I was actually kind of joking-\n哦……呃……我其实是在开玩笑——"

    old "I wasn't. Come, there's something you must see."
    new "I wasn't. Come, there's something you must see.\n我没有。来吧，有样东西你一定要看看。"

    old "She grabs my hands, and pulls me south, near the coast."
    new "She grabs my hands, and pulls me south, near the coast.\n她抓住我的手，把我往南边拉，朝海岸的方向去。"

    old "I don't know what exactly she wants from me, but at least this time we aren't going north, towards the lizardmen. That's already progress, I'd say."
    new "I don't know what exactly she wants from me, but at least this time we aren't going north, towards the lizardmen. That's already progress, I'd say.\n我不知道她到底想让我看什么，但至少这次我们不是往北走，不是朝lizardmen那边去。要我说，这已经是进步了。"

    old "I found a wonderful place."
    new "I found a wonderful place.\n我找到了一个很棒的地方。"

    old "Better than your spot near the river?"
    new "Better than your spot near the river?\n比你河边那个地方还好？"

    old "Well, that spot does have a lot of advantages. A good view of the surroundings, plenty of fish in the river to use as a food source, an unlimited reserve of water, dry wood to start fires..."
    new "Well, that spot does have a lot of advantages. A good view of the surroundings, plenty of fish in the river to use as a food source, an unlimited reserve of water, dry wood to start fires...\n嗯，那个地方确实有不少好处。周围视野开阔，河里的鱼多到可以当食物来源，水源取之不尽，还有干柴可以生火……"

    old "You don't have to tell me. I already knew that the river was a great place. I guess my question is, what makes this new place so special?"
    new "You don't have to tell me. I already knew that the river was a great place. I guess my question is, what makes this new place so special?\n你不用告诉我。我早就知道那条河是个好地方。我想问的是，这个新地方到底有什么特别的？"

    old "I... I don't know how to explain but, when I found it a few days ago, I immediately thought of you."
    new "I... I don't know how to explain but, when I found it a few days ago, I immediately thought of you.\n我……我不知道该怎么解释，但是几天前我发现它的时候，我立刻就想到了你。"

    old "Really? Okay, consider me intrigued. I definitely want to see this place. But, Sylrissa?"
    new "Really? Okay, consider me intrigued. I definitely want to see this place. But, Sylrissa?\n真的吗？好吧，那你成功勾起我的兴趣了。我一定得看看这地方。不过，Sylrissa？"

    old "Can you please slow down? I'm not nearly as fast as you. At this rate I'm going to trip over something-- probably my own feet."
    new "Can you please slow down? I'm not nearly as fast as you. At this rate I'm going to trip over something-- probably my own feet.\n你能不能慢一点？我可没你那么快。照这个速度，我早晚会绊到什么东西——很可能是我自己的脚。"

    old "Oh, right. Sorry. I guess I got a little too excited."
    new "Oh, right. Sorry. I guess I got a little too excited.\n哦，对。抱歉。我想我有点太兴奋了。"

    old "That's better. So, what is this place? It's along the coast?"
    new "That's better. So, what is this place? It's along the coast?\n这样好多了。那么，那是什么地方？在海边吗？"

    old "Not quite, close to it but ... a little more south."
    new "Not quite, close to it but ... a little more south.\n不完全是，离海边很近，但是……更靠南一点。"

    old "Sylrissa's grip on my hand tightens. She speaks slowly and with a soft voice."
    new "Sylrissa's grip on my hand tightens. She speaks slowly and with a soft voice.\nSylrissa握着我的手紧了紧。她放慢语速，声音轻柔。"

    old "You know, after the time we spent on that hill near Grimoire..."
    new "You know, after the time we spent on that hill near Grimoire...\n你知道吗，自从我们在Grimoire附近那座山上度过那段时光之后……"

    old "That actually left quite the impression on you, didn't it? You talk about it pretty often."
    new "That actually left quite the impression on you, didn't it? You talk about it pretty often.\n那件事给你留下的印象挺深啊，是不是？你经常提起它。"

    old "Yes, because it was something new for me. But, more importantly, because you were there with me. We both experienced it, together, and that made it even more wonderful."
    new "Yes, because it was something new for me. But, more importantly, because you were there with me. We both experienced it, together, and that made it even more wonderful.\n是的，因为它对我来说是件新鲜事。但更重要的是，因为那时你和我在一起。我们共同经历了它，一起，这让它更加美妙。"

    old "I remember thinking that I'd like to return that favor some day. You know, show you something nice that we could experience side by side."
    new "I remember thinking that I'd like to return that favor some day. You know, show you something nice that we could experience side by side.\n我记得当时我就想，有朝一日要报答你这份心意。你知道吗，带你看一些美好的东西，让我们并肩去体验。"

    old "So, when I saw this new place, I immediately decided that I wanted to share it with you."
    new "So, when I saw this new place, I immediately decided that I wanted to share it with you.\n所以，当我看到这个新地方的时候，我立刻决定要和你分享它。"

    old "I smile to myself. Just the fact that she was thinking about me alone makes me happy."
    new "I smile to myself. Just the fact that she was thinking about me alone makes me happy.\n我不禁微笑。仅仅是她一个人惦记着我，就足以让我高兴。"

    old "Thanks, Sylrissa. I'm happy that you thought of me."
    new "Thanks, Sylrissa. I'm happy that you thought of me.\n谢谢，Sylrissa。我很高兴你想到我。"

    old "I-It's not like I do it on purpose exactly. It's just... I'm always thinking about you for some reason or another."
    new "I-It's not like I do it on purpose exactly. It's just... I'm always thinking about you for some reason or another.\n我、我又不是故意那么做的。只是……不知怎的，我总在想着你。"

    old "Whenever I see something new or interesting the first thoughts I have are 'what would [protag] say about this?' or 'is this something that [heshe] would like?'"
    new "Whenever I see something new or interesting the first thoughts I have are 'what would [protag] say about this?' or 'is this something that [heshe] would like?'\n每当我看到新鲜或有趣的东西，脑子里最先冒出来的念头就是：[protag]会怎么看这个？或者，[heshe]会喜欢这个吗？"

    old "And then I get a little sad because you weren't there to experience it with me."
    new "And then I get a little sad because you weren't there to experience it with me.\n然后我又会有点难过，因为你不在那里，没能和我一起经历。"

    old "Yes. Look at me, [protag]."
    new "Yes. Look at me, [protag].\n是的。看着我，[protag]。"

    old "I'm gone from a ruthless, bloodthirsty, and ferocious naga to a sensitive mess of a person who thinks about nature and friendship all day."
    new "I'm gone from a ruthless, bloodthirsty, and ferocious naga to a sensitive mess of a person who thinks about nature and friendship all day.\n我从一个冷酷、嗜血、凶悍的naga，变成了一个多愁善感的人，整天想着自然和友情。"

    old "I would be a disgrace if I was still with my tribe."
    new "I would be a disgrace if I was still with my tribe.\n如果我还待在我的部落里，一定会被人耻笑。"

    old "In fact, you're one of the strongest people I know."
    new "In fact, you're one of the strongest people I know.\n事实上，你是我认识的最坚强的人之一。"

    old "Just because you've started to appreciate other things in life doesn't mean that you've forgotten how to fight."
    new "Just because you've started to appreciate other things in life doesn't mean that you've forgotten how to fight.\n你开始欣赏生活中其他美好的事物，并不意味着你就忘了怎么战斗。"

    old "I guess I'm not surprised that they'd think that. They're wrong though. That interpretation of strength is shallow at best."
    new "I guess I'm not surprised that they'd think that. They're wrong though. That interpretation of strength is shallow at best.\n我想他们会那么想，我并不意外。不过他们错了。那种对力量的理解，往好里说也太过肤浅。"

    old "True strength isn't about overpowering your enemy. That method can only get you so far."
    new "True strength isn't about overpowering your enemy. That method can only get you so far.\n真正的力量不在于压倒你的敌人。那种方法只能让你走到一定地步。"

    old "If you can understand people-- their culture, their feelings, their emotions-- you can open up new opportunities."
    new "If you can understand people-- their culture, their feelings, their emotions-- you can open up new opportunities.\n如果你能理解别人——他们的文化、他们的感受、他们的情绪——你就能打开新的可能。"

    old "Picking up on those subtleties can potentially help you in a fight, but you can also use that knowledge to find a different solution. Maybe even find a way to resolve things peacefully."
    new "Picking up on those subtleties can potentially help you in a fight, but you can also use that knowledge to find a different solution. Maybe even find a way to resolve things peacefully.\n捕捉到那些细微之处，也许能在战斗中帮到你，但你也可以利用这份认知，找到不同的解决办法。甚至也许能找到和平化解事情的办法。"

    old "Or you could charge mindlessly into battle, swords drawn like you seem to prefer. The point is, you'd have options."
    new "Or you could charge mindlessly into battle, swords drawn like you seem to prefer. The point is, you'd have options.\n或者你也可以像你偏好的那样，拔剑不假思索地冲进战场。关键在于，你会有更多选择。"

    old "Sylrissa laughs."
    new "Sylrissa laughs.\nSylrissa笑了。"

    old "You know me too well."
    new "You know me too well.\n你太了解我了。"

    old "But yeah..."
    new "But yeah...\n不过是啊……"

    old "That's true, [protag]. Thanks for saying it."
    new "That's true, [protag]. Thanks for saying it.\n说得没错，[protag]。谢谢你这么说。"

    old "After several more minutes pass, we reach the spot Sylrissa was talking about. It's main feature is a beautiful pond with waterlilies floating along its surface. I don't think I've ever seen so many of them in one place before."
    new "After several more minutes pass, we reach the spot Sylrissa was talking about. It's main feature is a beautiful pond with waterlilies floating along its surface. I don't think I've ever seen so many of them in one place before.\n又过了几分钟，我们来到了Sylrissa说的那个地方。它最主要的景观是一汪美丽的池塘，水面漂浮着睡莲。我以前好像从没在同一个地方见过这么多睡莲。"

    old "When I take a step closer, a group of colorful fish scatter, darting to different ends of the pond. Once they realize I'm not after them, they start slowly coming back."
    new "When I take a step closer, a group of colorful fish scatter, darting to different ends of the pond. Once they realize I'm not after them, they start slowly coming back.\n我走近一步，一群色彩斑斓的鱼四散游开，蹿向池塘的各个角落。等它们意识到我不是来抓它们的，才又慢慢游了回来。"

    old "This place really is beautiful, Sylrissa."
    new "This place really is beautiful, Sylrissa.\n这地方真的很美，Sylrissa。"

    old "I knew you'd say that!"
    new "I knew you'd say that!\n我就知道你会这么说！"

    old "Sylrissa pauses, looking thoughtful all of a sudden."
    new "Sylrissa pauses, looking thoughtful all of a sudden.\nSylrissa停顿了一下，突然一副若有所思的样子。"

    old "You know... We fight evil every day. All sorts of horrendous creatures and people with twisted hearts. You get kind of lost in it."
    new "You know... We fight evil every day. All sorts of horrendous creatures and people with twisted hearts. You get kind of lost in it.\n你知道吗……我们每天都在与邪恶战斗。各种各样可怕的生物，还有心地扭曲的人。你会有些迷失其中。"

    old "That's why it's important to remember that there are places like these. Wonderful and mysterious places where we can relax and remember that there are still things worth holding onto."
    new "That's why it's important to remember that there are places like these. Wonderful and mysterious places where we can relax and remember that there are still things worth holding onto.\n所以重要的是记住，还有这样的地方存在。美妙而神秘的地方，能让我们放松，提醒我们世上仍有值得守护的东西。"

    old "If the undead win, places like this will become rarer and rarer. They may even vanish completely."
    new "If the undead win, places like this will become rarer and rarer. They may even vanish completely.\n如果亡灵赢了，这样的地方会越来越少。甚至可能彻底消失。"

    old "I don't want that to happen. It's our duty to fight the evil at N'Mar and there are so many reasons to do that, but this is one more of them. We have to preserve the beauty of this world."
    new "I don't want that to happen. It's our duty to fight the evil at N'Mar and there are so many reasons to do that, but this is one more of them. We have to preserve the beauty of this world.\n我不想让那种事发生。与N'Mar的邪恶作战是我们的职责，而这么做的理由有千千万万，这又是其中之一。我们必须守护这个世界的美丽。"

    old "I'm going to fight for places like this so that future generations have the chance to feel the same things I feel right now, here by your side in this place."
    new "I'm going to fight for places like this so that future generations have the chance to feel the same things I feel right now, here by your side in this place.\n我要为这样的地方而战，好让后世的子子孙孙有机会，能像我此刻一样，在你身旁、在这片地方，感受到同样的心情。"

    old "These feelings... The ones that you opened my eyes and heart to... They're something I treasure."
    new "These feelings... The ones that you opened my eyes and heart to... They're something I treasure.\n这些感受……你让我睁开眼、敞开心扉而体会到的这些……是我珍视的东西。"

    old "And that's something worth preserving. Right, [protag]?"
    new "And that's something worth preserving. Right, [protag]?\n而那正是值得守护的。对吧，[protag]？"

    old "Sylrissa speaks with a level of determination and passion I've never seen in her before. I can't help but be moved by her resolve."
    new "Sylrissa speaks with a level of determination and passion I've never seen in her before. I can't help but be moved by her resolve.\nSylrissa说话时带着我从未在她身上见过的坚定与热情。我情不自禁，被她的决心所打动。"

    old "Yes, Sylrissa. That is something worth preserving."
    new "Yes, Sylrissa. That is something worth preserving.\n是的，Sylrissa。那确实值得守护。"

    old "Sylrissa smiles at my response, looking absolutely radiant."
    new "Sylrissa smiles at my response, looking absolutely radiant.\nSylrissa听了我的回答，露出微笑，整个人容光焕发。"

    old "This time, it's my turn to surprise her."
    new "This time, it's my turn to surprise her.\n这一次，轮到我让她惊喜了。"

    old "I close the distance between us and steal a short but passionate kiss from her lips."
    new "I close the distance between us and steal a short but passionate kiss from her lips.\n我拉近我们之间的距离，从她唇上偷走一个短暂而热烈的吻。"

    old "You're getting good at this."
    new "You're getting good at this.\n你越来越会这个了。"

    old "Kissing?"
    new "Kissing?\n接吻？"

    old "No, catching me by surprise. You were always good at kissing."
    new "No, catching me by surprise. You were always good at kissing.\n不，是让我猝不及防。接吻你一直都很擅长。"

    old "I close the distance between us and pull her into a tight hug. She seems a bit surprised at first but, soon enough, she's hugging me back. We stay like that for several minutes with nothing but the surrounding noises to keep us company."
    new "I close the distance between us and pull her into a tight hug. She seems a bit surprised at first but, soon enough, she's hugging me back. We stay like that for several minutes with nothing but the surrounding noises to keep us company.\n我拉近我们之间的距离，把她紧紧搂进怀里。她起初似乎有点意外，但很快也回抱住我。我们就那样相拥了好几分钟，只有四周的声响陪伴着我们。"

    old "Thank you for sharing this with me, Sylrissa."
    new "Thank you for sharing this with me, Sylrissa.\n谢谢你和我分享这些，Sylrissa。"

    old "Of course. It was nothing."
    new "Of course. It was nothing.\n当然。这没什么。"

    old "I let her go and say..."
    new "I let her go and say...\n我松开她，说道……"

    old "We should probably head back now. There's still a lot for me to do if we're going to protect places like this."
    new "We should probably head back now. There's still a lot for me to do if we're going to protect places like this.\n我们现在大概该回去了。要想守护这样的地方，我还有一大堆事要做。"

    old "Oh, right. Sure, I understand."
    new "Oh, right. Sure, I understand.\n哦，对。当然，我理解。"

    old "She looks a little sad. I get the feeling that maybe she had other plans. Still, what's done is done. There's no going back now."
    new "She looks a little sad. I get the feeling that maybe she had other plans. Still, what's done is done. There's no going back now.\n她看上去有点难过。我觉得她也许另有安排。不过，木已成舟。现在没有回头路了。"

    old "As we walk, we continue talking about what she said. I was feeling kind of worn out when I first came to the swamp today, but thanks to Sylrissa's words, I'm motivated again. I've remembered what's at stake and why we're doing this."
    new "As we walk, we continue talking about what she said. I was feeling kind of worn out when I first came to the swamp today, but thanks to Sylrissa's words, I'm motivated again. I've remembered what's at stake and why we're doing this.\n我们一边走，一边继续聊着她说的那些话。今天刚到沼泽时，我本来有些疲惫，但多亏了Sylrissa的话，我又重新燃起了干劲。我想起了什么才是攸关紧要的，想起了我们为什么而战。"

    old "It occurs to me that Sylrissa has really grown as a person since I'd first met her. More than ever, I'm proud to call her my friend."
    new "It occurs to me that Sylrissa has really grown as a person since I'd first met her. More than ever, I'm proud to call her my friend.\n我突然想到，自从我第一次见到Sylrissa以来，她真的成长了很多。比以往任何时候，我都更自豪能称她为我的朋友。"

    old "Now come. I promise the pond water isn't cold."
    new "Now come. I promise the pond water isn't cold.\n现在来吧。我保证池塘里的水不冷。"

    old "Wait? What?"
    new "Wait? What?\n等等？什么？"

    old "Once again, I'm pulled along by Sylrissa. She takes me to the edge of the pond, but I dig in my heels before she drags me into it."
    new "Once again, I'm pulled along by Sylrissa. She takes me to the edge of the pond, but I dig in my heels before she drags me into it.\n我再一次被Sylrissa拉着走。她把我带到池塘边，但就在她把我拖下水之前，我脚跟抵地，停住了。"

    old "What is it? Are you afraid of a little water?"
    new "What is it? Are you afraid of a little water?\n怎么了？你怕这么点水吗？"

    old "Um, no. That's not it. I just don't want to get my clothes wet and--"
    new "Um, no. That's not it. I just don't want to get my clothes wet and--\n呃，不是。不是那样的。我只是不想把衣服弄湿，而且——"

    old "It's safe! Look!"
    new "It's safe! Look!\n很安全的！看！"

    old "Sylrissa jumps into the water, splashing me in the process. She disappears below the surface for a brief second before reemerging. She leans back and starts floating on the water, her pretty figure adorned by the waterlillies all around."
    new "Sylrissa jumps into the water, splashing me in the process. She disappears below the surface for a brief second before reemerging. She leans back and starts floating on the water, her pretty figure adorned by the waterlillies all around.\nSylrissa跳进水里，水花溅了我一身。她沉入水面下短短一瞬，又重新浮了出来。她向后仰去，开始漂浮在水面上，漂亮的身姿被四周的睡莲点缀着。"

    old "See? Everything is fine."
    new "See? Everything is fine.\n看到没？一切安好。"

    old "Now I'm facing an altogether different problem. A part of me wants to jump in and join her immediately, but another part is content just looking. Sylrissa is putting on such a beautiful display that it'd be a shame to ruin it."
    new "Now I'm facing an altogether different problem. A part of me wants to jump in and join her immediately, but another part is content just looking. Sylrissa is putting on such a beautiful display that it'd be a shame to ruin it.\n现在我面对的是另一个完全不同的问题。我有一部分想立刻跳下去加入她，另一部分却只想静静地看着。Sylrissa此刻的画面实在太美，破坏了它实在可惜。"

    old "I want this image preserved in my memories forever."
    new "I want this image preserved in my memories forever.\n我想把这幅画面永远保存在记忆里。"

    old "Do you like what you see?"
    new "Do you like what you see?\n你喜欢你看到的吗？"

    old "I don't have the presence of mind to play it cool so I answer her honestly."
    new "I don't have the presence of mind to play it cool so I answer her honestly.\n我实在没那个镇定劲儿去装酷，于是老实回答了她。"

    old "She chuckles in a pleased manner."
    new "She chuckles in a pleased manner.\n她满意地轻笑起来。"

    old "Then, suddenly, she rolls over and slips under the water. At first I suspect that she wants me to chase after her, but then, as she resurfaces once more, I notice a fairly significant change."
    new "Then, suddenly, she rolls over and slips under the water. At first I suspect that she wants me to chase after her, but then, as she resurfaces once more, I notice a fairly significant change.\n接着，她忽然翻了个身，滑入水中。起初我以为她是想让我去追她，但等她再次浮出水面时，我注意到一个相当明显的变化。"

    old "Oh? You have such a strange look on your face, [protag]. What's the matter?"
    new "Oh? You have such a strange look on your face, [protag]. What's the matter?\n哦？你脸上的表情好奇怪啊，[protag]。怎么了？"

    old "She's faking, right? She has to know that she's missing a rather important article of clothing."
    new "She's faking, right? She has to know that she's missing a rather important article of clothing.\n她在装傻，对吧？她肯定知道自己少了一件挺重要的衣物。"

    old "Y-your top..."
    new "Y-your top...\n你、你的上衣……"

    old "Hm? What about it?"
    new "Hm? What about it?\n嗯？上衣怎么了？"

    old "Okay, the sly grin on her face is giving it away. She definitely knows what she's doing."
    new "Okay, the sly grin on her face is giving it away. She definitely knows what she's doing.\n好吧，她脸上那抹狡黠的笑出卖了她。她绝对清楚自己在做什么。"

    old "You're not wearing your top."
    new "You're not wearing your top.\n你没穿上衣。"

    old "What? That can't be."
    new "What? That can't be.\n什么？不可能吧。"

    old "She places her hands underneath her breasts and lifts them, squeezing them together and driving me absolutely crazy."
    new "She places her hands underneath her breasts and lifts them, squeezing them together and driving me absolutely crazy.\n她把手伸到胸下，托起双乳，把它们挤到一起，把我撩拨得快要发疯。"

    old "Oh. What do you know? I am missing my top."
    new "Oh. What do you know? I am missing my top.\n哦。你猜怎么着？我还真少了上衣。"

    old "You know, it'd be really nice if an attractive [prace] would help me find it. So..."
    new "You know, it'd be really nice if an attractive [prace] would help me find it. So...\n你知道吗，要是一位迷人的[prace]肯帮我找找，那就太好了。所以……"

    old "Are you coming? Or are you going to leave the harmless naga all alone in this big pond? All sorts of evil villains could come by and take advantage of her if you aren't here to protect her. Don't you want to save me?"
    new "Are you coming? Or are you going to leave the harmless naga all alone in this big pond? All sorts of evil villains could come by and take advantage of her if you aren't here to protect her. Don't you want to save me?\n你来吗？还是要把这无害的naga孤零零地留在这个大池塘里？要是你不来保护她，各种坏蛋都可能会路过占她便宜。你不想救我吗？"

    old "Alright, alright. You win. I'm jumping in!"
    new "Alright, alright. You win. I'm jumping in!\n好，好。你赢了。我跳！"

    old "I get my clothes off and then join her in the pond."
    new "I get my clothes off and then join her in the pond.\n我脱掉衣服，然后下到池塘里和她在一起。"

    old "What follows is some of the most intense sex I've ever had in my life. And in a pond, no less! Sylrissa seems completely at home in this sort of environment and, well, let's just say it showed."
    new "What follows is some of the most intense sex I've ever had in my life. And in a pond, no less! Sylrissa seems completely at home in this sort of environment and, well, let's just say it showed.\n接下来，是我这辈子经历过的最激烈的一场欢爱。而且还是在池塘里！Sylrissa在这种环境里简直是如鱼得水，呃，我们就这么说吧，这一点表露无遗。"

    old "Eventually, we both crawl out of the pond and lay on the grass next to it as we try to catch our breath. Thankfully, there's enough sunlight shining through the trees dry ourselves off as we recover. All I have to do is enjoy the view of Sylrissa's naked body."
    new "Eventually, we both crawl out of the pond and lay on the grass next to it as we try to catch our breath. Thankfully, there's enough sunlight shining through the trees dry ourselves off as we recover. All I have to do is enjoy the view of Sylrissa's naked body.\n最后，我们俩都爬出池塘，躺在旁边的草地上喘着气。幸好有足够的阳光穿过树梢，让我们在恢复体力时把身子晒干。我只需要好好欣赏Sylrissa赤裸的身体。"

    old "When we're finally ready, I walk back to the swamp with her before departing for Grimoire on my own. I can't wait until I get to see Sylrissa again."
    new "When we're finally ready, I walk back to the swamp with her before departing for Grimoire on my own. I can't wait until I get to see Sylrissa again.\n等我们终于休息好了，我陪她走回沼泽，然后独自启程前往Grimoire。我已经等不及要再见到Sylrissa了。"

    old "Oh, have you come to visit me, sweetheart?"
    new "Oh, have you come to visit me, sweetheart?\n哦，你是来看我的吗，亲爱的？"

    old "Ah, both of them are here. Should this situation be awkward? It feels awkward. Then again, Sylrissa did call me sweetheart right in front of Enok and he didn't seem to mind."
    new "Ah, both of them are here. Should this situation be awkward? It feels awkward. Then again, Sylrissa did call me sweetheart right in front of Enok and he didn't seem to mind.\n啊，他们俩都在。这场面是不是该很尴尬？感觉是挺尴尬的。不过，Sylrissa可是当着Enok的面叫我亲爱的，而他似乎并不介意。"

    old "Have you told him?"
    new "Have you told him?\n你告诉他了吗？"

    old "No, I am planning to do it now if 'your majesty, Enok,' has nothing against it."
    new "No, I am planning to do it now if 'your majesty, Enok,' has nothing against it.\n还没有，我正打算现在说，只要“Enok陛下”不反对。"

    old "Pfft. I'll leave you to it."
    new "Pfft. I'll leave you to it.\n噗。那我就不打扰你们了。"

    old "Enok leaves, looking rather pissed at Sylrissa. Before disappearing from my sight, he waves his hand and smiles at me though. So, I'm guessing that he's not mad at me. Only her?"
    new "Enok leaves, looking rather pissed at Sylrissa. Before disappearing from my sight, he waves his hand and smiles at me though. So, I'm guessing that he's not mad at me. Only her?\nEnok离开了，看着Sylrissa，一副相当不爽的样子。不过他从我视线中消失前，还朝我挥了挥手，对我笑了笑。所以我猜，他不是在生我的气。只生她的气？"

    old "Do you remember when you overheard us fighting awhile ago?"
    new "Do you remember when you overheard us fighting awhile ago?\n你还记得吗，之前有次你听见我们吵架？"

    old "Yes, and you refused to tell me what was going on."
    new "Yes, and you refused to tell me what was going on.\n记得，而且你当时拒绝告诉我发生了什么。"

    old "True. But I can tell you now. It was about the lily pond."
    new "True. But I can tell you now. It was about the lily pond.\n没错。不过我现在可以告诉你了。是因为那个睡莲池塘。"

    old "Uh? What about it?"
    new "Uh? What about it?\n呃？那个池塘怎么了？"

    old "Well, it wasn't exactly a normal pond. I...I lied to you, sorry. I was with Enok when I saw it for the first time."
    new "Well, it wasn't exactly a normal pond. I...I lied to you, sorry. I was with Enok when I saw it for the first time.\n嗯，那其实不是个普通的池塘。我……我骗了你，抱歉。我第一次看到它的时候，是跟Enok在一起。"

    old "That doesn't seem like anything you need to apologize for. Unless there's more?"
    new "That doesn't seem like anything you need to apologize for. Unless there's more?\n这似乎没什么需要道歉的。除非还有别的？"

    old "Enok was the one who initially found the pond. He said that there was a powerful magic aura around it-- a dark one."
    new "Enok was the one who initially found the pond. He said that there was a powerful magic aura around it-- a dark one.\n最初发现那个池塘的是Enok。他说池塘周围有一股强大的魔法气息——是黑暗的那种。"

    old "What?! But...we bathed in it!"
    new "What?! But...we bathed in it!\n什么？！可是……我们还在里面洗了澡！"

    old "Oh, we did more than bathe in it."
    new "Oh, we did more than bathe in it.\n哦，我们做的可不止是洗澡。"

    old "That's exactly my point! It could have been dangerous!"
    new "That's exactly my point! It could have been dangerous!\n这正是我要说的！那可能很危险！"

    old "Phew. Thank god we didn't decide to take a swim in it."
    new "Phew. Thank god we didn't decide to take a swim in it.\n呼。谢天谢地，我们没决定下水去游个泳。"

    old "Right. Anyway..."
    new "Right. Anyway...\n对。总之……"

    old "That's why Enok was angry. I told him I'd like to show the pond to you, but he didn't want me to. He said that it might have been dangerous."
    new "That's why Enok was angry. I told him I'd like to show the pond to you, but he didn't want me to. He said that it might have been dangerous.\n所以Enok才会生气。我跟他说，我想带你去看那个池塘，但他不想让我去。他说那可能很危险。"

    old "Wait, now I'm the one getting angry! Knowing all that, you still decided to go? And you even lured me into it! How could you do this to me?!"
    new "Wait, now I'm the one getting angry! Knowing all that, you still decided to go? And you even lured me into it! How could you do this to me?!\n等等，现在轮到我生气了！明知道那些，你还是决定去？甚至还把我引诱进去！你怎么能这样对我？！"

    old "Calm down, love. Before I took you there, I carefully tested it myself."
    new "Calm down, love. Before I took you there, I carefully tested it myself.\n冷静点，亲爱的。带你去之前，我自己先仔细测试过了。"

    old "You tested it?"
    new "You tested it?\n你测试过了？"

    old "Yes. I wanted to make sure it was harmless for you, just in case... we decided to do what we did."
    new "Yes. I wanted to make sure it was harmless for you, just in case... we decided to do what we did.\n是的。我想确保它对你无害，以防万一……我们决定去做我们做过的事。"

    old "But that's crazy! You went there on your own to test it when you had no idea what the consequences would be?"
    new "But that's crazy! You went there on your own to test it when you had no idea what the consequences would be?\n但那太疯狂了！你明知道会有什么后果，还一个人跑到那里去测试？"

    old "But...since we didn't touch the water, we're safe, right? We aren't cursed or anything are we?"
    new "But...since we didn't touch the water, we're safe, right? We aren't cursed or anything are we?\n可是……既然我们没碰那水，我们就没事，对吧？我们没被诅咒或怎么样吧？"

    old "First of all, relax. Dark magic is not as dangerous as they'd lead you believe in the 'civilized places'."
    new "First of all, relax. Dark magic is not as dangerous as they'd lead you believe in the 'civilized places'.\n首先，放轻松。黑暗魔法并不像他们在那些“文明地方”里让你相信的那么危险。"

    old "Secondly... I tested it on my own before I took you there."
    new "Secondly... I tested it on my own before I took you there.\n其次……我带你去之前，自己先测试过了。"

    old "What!? You actually went back there on your own when you had no idea what the consequences would be?!"
    new "What!? You actually went back there on your own when you had no idea what the consequences would be?!\n什么？！你居然在不知道会有什么后果的情况下，一个人又跑回去了？！"

    old "Well, yeah. Enok was still in the area so I thought, worst case scenario, I could just run over to him and have him counter the spell. There wasn't any need for that though. I swam in the lake for hours and nothing happened."
    new "Well, yeah. Enok was still in the area so I thought, worst case scenario, I could just run over to him and have him counter the spell. There wasn't any need for that though. I swam in the lake for hours and nothing happened.\n嗯，是啊。Enok当时还在附近，所以我想，最坏的情况下，我可以跑过去找他，让他解除咒语。不过根本用不着。我在湖里游了好几个小时，什么事也没发生。"

    old "Well... As long as nothing happened, I guess--"
    new "Well... As long as nothing happened, I guess--\n嗯……只要没出事，我想——"

    old "At least, that's what we thought until today."
    new "At least, that's what we thought until today.\n至少在今天之前，我们一直是这么想的。"

    old "I'm not going to like this, am I?"
    new "I'm not going to like this, am I?\n接下来不会是什么我爱听的吧？"

    old "It's nothing bad. Rather the opposite, [protag]!"
    new "It's nothing bad. Rather the opposite, [protag]!\n不是什么坏事。恰恰相反，[protag]！"

    old "Enok said that my body ended up absorbing all of the dark magic that was in the pond."
    new "Enok said that my body ended up absorbing all of the dark magic that was in the pond.\nEnok说，我的身体最终把池塘里的黑暗魔法全都吸收了。"

    old "How is that a good thing?!"
    new "How is that a good thing?!\n这算什么好事？！"

    old "Calm down. It all turned out okay, alright? Enok examined me using his magic and said that I could use a catalyst to discharge all of the magic I'd absorbed from the pond into a single item."
    new "Calm down. It all turned out okay, alright? Enok examined me using his magic and said that I could use a catalyst to discharge all of the magic I'd absorbed from the pond into a single item.\n冷静。结果一切都很顺利，好吗？Enok用他的魔法给我做了检查，说我可以借助一种催化剂，把我从池塘里吸收的魔法全部导进一件物品里。"

    old "And thus, the legendary dagger, 'Love Of The Lilies,' was born!"
    new "And thus, the legendary dagger, 'Love Of The Lilies,' was born!\n于是，传说中的匕首“Love Of The Lilies”就诞生了！"

    old "Love Of The Lilies?"
    new "Love Of The Lilies?\nLove Of The Lilies？"

    old "Yes, I named it that because we made love in the lily pond!"
    new "Yes, I named it that because we made love in the lily pond!\n是的，我给它起这个名字，因为我们在睡莲池塘里做了爱！"

    old "Annnd... it's completely safe? It's not a cursed dagger? And you're absolutely sure that you're okay?"
    new "Annnd... it's completely safe? It's not a cursed dagger? And you're absolutely sure that you're okay?\n那……它完全安全吗？不是什么被诅咒的匕首？你绝对确定你没事？"

    old "Man. All that brainwashing concerning dark magic they fed you really worked, didn't it? Everything is fine, [protag]. Besides, as Enok probably told you already, nagas have a natural resistance to dark magic. We're not immune, but we're pretty close."
    new "Man. All that brainwashing concerning dark magic they fed you really worked, didn't it? Everything is fine, [protag]. Besides, as Enok probably told you already, nagas have a natural resistance to dark magic. We're not immune, but we're pretty close.\n天。他们给你灌的那套关于黑暗魔法的洗脑，还真起作用了，是不是？一切都好，[protag]。再说了，Enok大概也跟你说过，naga天生就对黑暗魔法有抵抗力。我们不是免疫，但也差不多了。"

    old "I'm trying to calm down, but I just can't get over how lax Sylrissa is being about this. Something seriously bad could have happened to her."
    new "I'm trying to calm down, but I just can't get over how lax Sylrissa is being about this. Something seriously bad could have happened to her.\n我努力想冷静下来，可就是没法对Sylrissa这种满不在乎的态度释怀。她身上本可能发生很严重的坏事。"

    old "Hm. Maybe I can do something to get you to relax."
    new "Hm. Maybe I can do something to get you to relax.\n嗯。也许我能做点什么，让你放松下来。"

    old "Sylrissa slides around behind me and gently begins massaging my shoulders."
    new "Sylrissa slides around behind me and gently begins massaging my shoulders.\nSylrissa滑到我身后，轻轻地开始按摩我的肩膀。"

    old "Better?"
    new "Better?\n好点了吗？"

    old "I take a deep breath. Her massage does feel pretty good."
    new "I take a deep breath. Her massage does feel pretty good.\n我深深吸了口气。她的按摩确实很舒服。"

    old "...Yeah. I'm getting there, anyway."
    new "...Yeah. I'm getting there, anyway.\n……嗯。总之，我正慢慢放松下来。"

    old "You know what's an even better way to relax?"
    new "You know what's an even better way to relax?\n你知道还有什么更好的放松方式吗？"

    old "The suggestive tone in her voice is unmistakable."
    new "The suggestive tone in her voice is unmistakable.\n她语气里的暗示再明显不过了。"

    old "But... What about Enok?"
    new "But... What about Enok?\n可是……Enok怎么办？"

    old "Don't worry about him. He knows not to disturb us."
    new "Don't worry about him. He knows not to disturb us.\n别担心他。他知道别来打扰我们。"

    old "As insane as she makes me sometimes, there's no way I could say no to Sylrissa-- especially when she makes an offer like this."
    new "As insane as she makes me sometimes, there's no way I could say no to Sylrissa-- especially when she makes an offer like this.\n尽管她有时让我抓狂，可要我拒绝Sylrissa是不可能的——尤其是当她提出这种邀请的时候。"

    old "and thus, the legendary sword 'Loyal Companion' was born!"
    new "and thus, the legendary sword 'Loyal Companion' was born!\n于是，传说中的剑“Loyal Companion”诞生了！"

    old "Loyal Companion?"
    new "Loyal Companion?\nLoyal Companion？"

    old "Yes, it symbolizes me. Your loyal companion. But it's not for you, it's for me. Your loyal companion."
    new "Yes, it symbolizes me. Your loyal companion. But it's not for you, it's for me. Your loyal companion.\n是的，它象征着我自己。你忠诚的伙伴。不过它不是给你的，是给我自己的。你忠诚的伙伴。"

    old "All right, all right, I got it."
    new "All right, all right, I got it.\n好，好，我明白了。"

    old "Seriously though, you've helped me do a lot of growing, [protag]. I've learned so much since I've been with you and... well, you have my full loyalty. With this sword, I'll be able to serve you even better than before."
    new "Seriously though, you've helped me do a lot of growing, [protag]. I've learned so much since I've been with you and... well, you have my full loyalty. With this sword, I'll be able to serve you even better than before.\n说真的，你帮助我成长了很多，[protag]。自从和你在一起，我学到了很多……而且，嗯，你拥有我全部的忠诚。有了这把剑，我能比从前更好地为你效力。"

    old "You mean you'll be able to split undead skulls faster?"
    new "You mean you'll be able to split undead skulls faster?\n你是说，你能更快地劈开亡灵的脑壳？"

    old "Yes, that's exactly what I mean! It'll be so much fun!"
    new "Yes, that's exactly what I mean! It'll be so much fun!\n对，我就是这个意思！一定会非常有趣的！"

    old "As I reach the usual spot by the river, I catch sight of Sylrissa. It seems she's on her own today."
    new "As I reach the usual spot by the river, I catch sight of Sylrissa. It seems she's on her own today.\n我来到河边那个老地方，一眼看见了Sylrissa。看来今天只有她一个人。"

    old "I move a little closer and then stop short when I see the strange smile on her face. There's something very offputting about it. It's definitely not one of the smiles I'm used to seeing from her."
    new "I move a little closer and then stop short when I see the strange smile on her face. There's something very offputting about it. It's definitely not one of the smiles I'm used to seeing from her.\n我走近了一些，看到她脸上那奇怪的笑容时，猛地停下了脚步。那笑容里有种让人很不舒服的东西。那绝不是我看惯了的她的笑容。"

    old "Why are you smiling like that?"
    new "Why are you smiling like that?\n你干嘛那样笑？"

    old "Oh, no reason. I am just happy to see you!"
    new "Oh, no reason. I am just happy to see you!\n哦，没什么。我只是很高兴见到你！"

    old "I'm not buying it. There's something that she's not telling me."
    new "I'm not buying it. There's something that she's not telling me.\n我可不信。她有事瞒着我。"

    old "I open my mouth to ask more questions, but I don't end up getting to that last step. In seconds, Sylrissa closes the distance between us and pulls my face to hers."
    new "I open my mouth to ask more questions, but I don't end up getting to that last step. In seconds, Sylrissa closes the distance between us and pulls my face to hers.\n我张嘴想再问几句，却终究没问出口。几秒钟内，Sylrissa拉近了我们之间的距离，把我的脸拉向她的脸。"

    old "We end up kissing for several minutes before I come to my senses and pull back. She's just too damn good at it."
    new "We end up kissing for several minutes before I come to my senses and pull back. She's just too damn good at it.\n我们就这样吻了好几分钟，我才回过神来，抽身退开。她实在是太擅长这个了。"

    old "Enok told me."
    new "Enok told me.\nEnok告诉我的。"

    old "What did he... Oh."
    new "What did he... Oh.\n他跟你……哦。"

    old "Sylrissa laughs and claps me on the shoulder cheerfully."
    new "Sylrissa laughs and claps me on the shoulder cheerfully.\nSylrissa笑着，欢快地拍了拍我的肩膀。"

    old "Did you really think that he wouldn't tell me?"
    new "Did you really think that he wouldn't tell me?\n你真的以为他不会告诉我？"

    old "Honestly? Yes. I really thought he'd keep quiet about it."
    new "Honestly? Yes. I really thought he'd keep quiet about it.\n说实话？是的。我真以为他会对这件事守口如瓶。"

    old "I mean, taking about that sort of thing with the othes is embarrassing, isn't it? I wouldn't think that would be different for nagas."
    new "I mean, taking about that sort of thing with the othes is embarrassing, isn't it? I wouldn't think that would be different for nagas.\n我是说，跟别人谈论那种事情很尴尬，不是吗？我以为naga也一样。"

    old "Hm. I'm not sure, [protag]. This whole situation is pretty new for both of us. But I'm glad."
    new "Hm. I'm not sure, [protag]. This whole situation is pretty new for both of us. But I'm glad.\n嗯。我不确定，[protag]。这种情况对我们俩来说都挺新鲜的。不过我很高兴。"

    old "You're glad?"
    new "You're glad?\n你高兴？"

    old "Yes. I mean, if it was someone else I'd be pissed, but since it's Enok... He's a naga like me. And he also happens to be my best friend. I can understand why you'd be attracted to him."
    new "Yes. I mean, if it was someone else I'd be pissed, but since it's Enok... He's a naga like me. And he also happens to be my best friend. I can understand why you'd be attracted to him.\n是的。我是说，如果是别人，我会很生气，但既然那是Enok……他和我一样是naga。而且他碰巧还是我最好的朋友。我能理解你为什么会被他吸引。"

    old "I end up focusing on that last sentence. What is that supposed to mean? I guess now isn't exactly the time to bring that up though."
    new "I end up focusing on that last sentence. What is that supposed to mean? I guess now isn't exactly the time to bring that up though.\n我的注意力最后落在了她最后一句话上。那是什么意思？不过，我想现在不是提起这个的时候。"

    old "So... what now?"
    new "So... what now?\n那……现在怎么办？"

    old "I'm not sure. Enok isn't here at the moment and I really feel like he should be a part of this conversation."
    new "I'm not sure. Enok isn't here at the moment and I really feel like he should be a part of this conversation.\n我不确定。Enok现在不在，而且我真的觉得，这场谈话他应该参与。"

    old "Maybe... we should all take some time to think? Then, when you come back and Enok is here, we'll talk."
    new "Maybe... we should all take some time to think? Then, when you come back and Enok is here, we'll talk.\n也许……我们都该花点时间想一想？然后等你下次来、Enok也在的时候，我们再谈。"

    old "Alright. That sounds fair."
    new "Alright. That sounds fair.\n好。这听起来很公平。"

    old "Sylrissa nods. I take my leave shortly after that."
    new "Sylrissa nods. I take my leave shortly after that.\nSylrissa点了点头。那之后不久，我便告辞离开了。"

    old "I feel a strange mix of terror and excitement. A part of me is glad that it's finally out in the open, but another part of me is scared to face the consequences of my actions."
    new "I feel a strange mix of terror and excitement. A part of me is glad that it's finally out in the open, but another part of me is scared to face the consequences of my actions.\n我心里有种恐惧与兴奋交织的奇异感觉。一方面我很高兴事情终于摊开了，另一方面，我又害怕面对自己行为的后果。"

    old "I guess, one way or another, it'll all be sorted out the next time I encounter the two of them."
    new "I guess, one way or another, it'll all be sorted out the next time I encounter the two of them.\n我想，无论怎样，等下次再见到他们俩时，一切都会有个结果。"

    old "Why, [protag]? Is it because nagas don't have legs? Or maybe it's because we don't have a butt? At least, not in the same sense as the other races you associate with."
    new "Why, [protag]? Is it because nagas don't have legs? Or maybe it's because we don't have a butt? At least, not in the same sense as the other races you associate with.\n为什么，[protag]？是因为naga没有腿吗？还是因为我们没有屁股？至少，不是你所接触的其他种族那种意义上的屁股。"

    old "Hold on! What on Aravorn are you talking about?!"
    new "Hold on! What on Aravorn are you talking about?!\n等等！看在Aravorn的份上，你到底在说什么？！"

    old "I am trying to figure out what I'm missing compared to the others. What is it that makes me less appealing to someone like you?"
    new "I am trying to figure out what I'm missing compared to the others. What is it that makes me less appealing to someone like you?\n我在努力弄清楚，跟别人相比，我到底缺了什么。是什么让我对你这样的人少了点吸引力？"

    old "You're not missing anything, Sylrissa. I love the way you look. Shouldn't that be obvious by now?"
    new "You're not missing anything, Sylrissa. I love the way you look. Shouldn't that be obvious by now?\n你什么也不缺，Sylrissa。我喜欢你的样子。到现在这难道还不够明显吗？"

    old "Ah. Then it must be my personality that you dislike."
    new "Ah. Then it must be my personality that you dislike.\n啊。那一定是你讨厌我的性格了。"

    old "Is it that I get carried away too much? Or that I make too many jokes?"
    new "Is it that I get carried away too much? Or that I make too many jokes?\n是我太容易得意忘形吗？还是我玩笑开得太多？"

    old "There's nothing wrong with you. Now, what is this all about? I can't fix the issue if I don't know what it is."
    new "There's nothing wrong with you. Now, what is this all about? I can't fix the issue if I don't know what it is.\n你没有任何问题。好了，这到底是怎么回事？不知道问题出在哪儿，我可没法解决。"

    old "I found out that you slept with one of our other party members and I'm trying to figure out why."
    new "I found out that you slept with one of our other party members and I'm trying to figure out why.\n我发现你和我们另一位队友上了床，我想弄清楚为什么。"

    old "Ah. It makes sense now."
    new "Ah. It makes sense now.\n啊。现在说得通了。"

    old "I guess I should have known I'd have to deal with the consequences of my actions sooner or later. Now's the time to tell her what's on my mind."
    new "I guess I should have known I'd have to deal with the consequences of my actions sooner or later. Now's the time to tell her what's on my mind.\n我想我早该知道，早晚得面对自己行为的后果。现在是时候告诉她我的想法了。"

    old "Sylrissa... Like I said before, there isn't anything wrong with you. You're beautiful and I like you as a person."
    new "Sylrissa... Like I said before, there isn't anything wrong with you. You're beautiful and I like you as a person.\nSylrissa……就像我之前说的，你没有任何问题。你很美，作为一个人，我也很喜欢你。"

    old "I haven't said anything bad."
    new "I haven't said anything bad.\n我还没说什么难听的话呢。"

    old "Not yet. But, in my experience, after a sentence like that, the next one usually starts with: 'BUT'."
    new "Not yet. But, in my experience, after a sentence like that, the next one usually starts with: 'BUT'.\n还没有。不过以我的经验，说完那样一句话之后，下一句通常都会以“但是”开头。"

    old "Sylrissa's expression shifts into an angry one. That's not a good mood to leave her in. I'd better explain myself quickly."
    new "Sylrissa's expression shifts into an angry one. That's not a good mood to leave her in. I'd better explain myself quickly.\nSylrissa的表情变得愤怒起来。让她带着这种情绪可不好。我最好赶紧解释清楚。"

    old "You're right. I'm sorry."
    new "You're right. I'm sorry.\n你说得对。对不起。"

    old "The thing is... I don't love you, Sylrissa. I like you and I did enjoy the time we spent together."
    new "The thing is... I don't love you, Sylrissa. I like you and I did enjoy the time we spent together.\n问题是……我并不爱你，Sylrissa。我喜欢你，也确实很享受我们共度的时光。"

    old "Yeah. It was fun."
    new "Yeah. It was fun.\n是啊。那段日子很快乐。"

    old "It was really fun. But... It wasn't love. At least, not for me. I'm sorry if I misled you."
    new "It was really fun. But... It wasn't love. At least, not for me. I'm sorry if I misled you.\n真的很快乐。可是……那不是爱。至少对我来说不是。如果我让你误会了，我很抱歉。"

    old "I see... At least, it wasn't because of who I am."
    new "I see... At least, it wasn't because of who I am.\n我明白了……至少，不是因为我是谁。"

    old "Absolutely not."
    new "Absolutely not.\n绝对不是。"

    old "She's presenting a strong front, but I feel like she's about to cry. I should probably leave her alone. I'm sure the last thing she wants is to break down in front of me."
    new "She's presenting a strong front, but I feel like she's about to cry. I should probably leave her alone. I'm sure the last thing she wants is to break down in front of me.\n她摆出一副坚强的样子，可我觉得她快要哭了。我大概该让她一个人待着。我相信她最不希望的，就是在我面前崩溃。"

    old "I hate that I hurt her, but I can't lie to her about my feelings and I can't change what I've done in the past. As harsh as it is, this is for the best."
    new "I hate that I hurt her, but I can't lie to her about my feelings and I can't change what I've done in the past. As harsh as it is, this is for the best.\n我痛恨自己伤害了她，但我不能对自己的感情撒谎，也无法改变过去做过的事。尽管这很残酷，但这样才是最好的。"

    old "I'm sorry, Sylrissa. You deserved better."
    new "I'm sorry, Sylrissa. You deserved better.\n对不起，Sylrissa。你值得更好的。"

    old "It's fine. I still have Enok so... I'll be fine."
    new "It's fine. I still have Enok so... I'll be fine.\n没关系。我还有Enok，所以……我会没事的。"

    old "I can be thankful for that much. If anyone can pull her out of this, it's him."
    new "I can be thankful for that much. If anyone can pull her out of this, it's him.\n这一点我还能心存感激。如果有谁能把她拉出来，那就是他了。"

    old "I only want you."
    new "I only want you.\n我只要你。"

    old "She looks a bit skeptical. That's only natural though. I have some serious schmoozing to do after what I've done."
    new "She looks a bit skeptical. That's only natural though. I have some serious schmoozing to do after what I've done.\n她看起来有点半信半疑。不过这也自然。在我做过那些事之后，可得好好哄哄她才行。"

    old "Like I said before, there's nothing wrong with you. In fact, if there is a problem with you, it is that you're too perfect."
    new "Like I said before, there's nothing wrong with you. In fact, if there is a problem with you, it is that you're too perfect.\n就像我之前说的，你没有任何问题。事实上，如果说你有什么问题，那就是你太完美了。"

    old "You're fun. You tell the best jokes. You're beautiful, both inside and out. You can always make me smile. Your positivity is contagious."
    new "You're fun. You tell the best jokes. You're beautiful, both inside and out. You can always make me smile. Your positivity is contagious.\n你很风趣。你讲的笑话最棒。你由内而外都很美。你总能逗我笑。你的乐观会感染人。"

    old "Oh? I like this. Go on."
    new "Oh? I like this. Go on.\n哦？我爱听。继续。"

    old "I love you Sylrissa. And, I shouldn't have slept with-"
    new "I love you Sylrissa. And, I shouldn't have slept with-\n我爱你，Sylrissa。而且，我不该和——"

    old "Stop! I don't need to hear that last part. I'm fine now."
    new "Stop! I don't need to hear that last part. I'm fine now.\n停下！最后那部分我不需要听。我现在没事了。"

    old "I mean, we were never engaged or anything, but that doesn't excuse what I did. I'd understand if you were still mad."
    new "I mean, we were never engaged or anything, but that doesn't excuse what I did. I'd understand if you were still mad.\n我是说，我们从来没订过婚什么的，但那也不能成为我所做之事的借口。如果你还在生气，我也能理解。"

    old "Sylrissa shrugs."
    new "Sylrissa shrugs.\nSylrissa耸了耸肩。"

    old "You did what you did. You can't take it back now. And honestly, if you want to keep doing it, you can. I don't really care."
    new "You did what you did. You can't take it back now. And honestly, if you want to keep doing it, you can. I don't really care.\n你做都做了。现在也收不回来了。而且说实话，如果你想继续那样做，也可以。我不是很在乎。"

    old "...you don't have a problem with me sleeping with other people?"
    new "...you don't have a problem with me sleeping with other people?\n……你不介意我和别人上床？"

    old "Nope. I thought you didn't like me for some reason. But if you didn't like me you wouldn't have been able to point out so many of my finer points."
    new "Nope. I thought you didn't like me for some reason. But if you didn't like me you wouldn't have been able to point out so many of my finer points.\n不介意。我还以为你是因为什么原因不喜欢我呢。但如果你不喜欢我，就不可能说出我这么多优点。"

    old "Sylrissa chuckles happily and then meets my eyes with hers. A light blush creeps into her cheeks as she continues."
    new "Sylrissa chuckles happily and then meets my eyes with hers. A light blush creeps into her cheeks as she continues.\nSylrissa开心地轻笑，然后与我四目相对。她继续说着，脸颊泛起淡淡的红晕。"

    old "And you said you love me."
    new "And you said you love me.\n而且你说你爱我。"

    old "She wraps her arms around my shoulders and presses her body against my chest."
    new "She wraps her arms around my shoulders and presses her body against my chest.\n她双臂环住我的肩膀，把身体贴在我的胸膛上。"

    old "Sex is just sex. It's fun, but it doesn't necessarily mean anything deeper than that."
    new "Sex is just sex. It's fun, but it doesn't necessarily mean anything deeper than that.\n性只是性。它很有趣，但未必有比那更深的含义。"

    old "So I don't care if you have sex with one other person or a hundred as long as you love ONLY ME."
    new "So I don't care if you have sex with one other person or a hundred as long as you love ONLY ME.\n所以我不在乎你和一个人还是和一百个人上床，只要你只爱我就行。"

    old "She smiles and then lightly kisses my lips."
    new "She smiles and then lightly kisses my lips.\n她微笑着，然后轻轻吻上我的唇。"

    old "Sylrissa may have given me her blessing, but something about the way she said only me tells me that I shouldn't push my luck."
    new "Sylrissa may have given me her blessing, but something about the way she said only me tells me that I shouldn't push my luck.\nSylrissa也许给了我她的许可，但她说“只爱我”时的语气，让我明白自己不该得寸进尺。"

    old "If she ever mistook me having sex with someone as having actual affection for them... Well, it'd probably end in a bloodbath. So... I think I'll just behave."
    new "If she ever mistook me having sex with someone as having actual affection for them... Well, it'd probably end in a bloodbath. So... I think I'll just behave.\n要是她哪天误会了，以为我和某个人上床就是对那人动了真情……那八成会落得个血流成河的下场。所以……我想我还是老实一点的好。"

    old "Besides, nobody makes me feel the way Sylrissa does. She takes that exact moment to remind me of that by leaning in for another kiss."
    new "Besides, nobody makes me feel the way Sylrissa does. She takes that exact moment to remind me of that by leaning in for another kiss.\n再说了，没人能给我Sylrissa那样的感觉。而她就趁着这个节骨眼，又凑上来吻了我一下，提醒我这一点。"

    old "We begin taking off clothes as we exchange increasingly passionate kisses."
    new "We begin taking off clothes as we exchange increasingly passionate kisses.\n我们开始脱掉衣服，一边交换着越来越热烈的吻。"

    old "Sleeping with someone else was wrong, but at least now I know without a doubt that her arms are the ones I want to be in."
    new "Sleeping with someone else was wrong, but at least now I know without a doubt that her arms are the ones I want to be in.\n和别人上床是错的，但至少现在我能毫无疑问地确认，我想依偎的正是她的怀抱。"

    old "I travel to the swamp again to pay a visit to my love. As I approach the usual spot, I start to realize that there's nobody there."
    new "I travel to the swamp again to pay a visit to my love. As I approach the usual spot, I start to realize that there's nobody there.\n我再次前往沼泽，去看望我的爱人。快到我们常去的那个地方时，我渐渐意识到那里一个人也没有。"

    old "Before I can worry though, I hear the sound of laughter and splashing water coming from downstream. I smile to myself and move closer to the source of the noise."
    new "Before I can worry though, I hear the sound of laughter and splashing water coming from downstream. I smile to myself and move closer to the source of the noise.\n不过，我还没来得及担心，就听见下游传来欢笑声和拍水声。我微微一笑，朝声音的来源走去。"

    old "I expected to find Sylrissa and Enok playing in the water, but I didn't guess that they'd both be naked."
    new "I expected to find Sylrissa and Enok playing in the water, but I didn't guess that they'd both be naked.\n我本以为会看到Sylrissa和Enok在水里玩，却没想到他们俩都光着身子。"

    old "I end up staring for a moment, mezmerized by the beauty of the two of them."
    new "I end up staring for a moment, mezmerized by the beauty of the two of them.\n我不禁呆看了片刻，被他们两人的美丽迷住了。"

    old "As I suspected, I end up finding Sylrissa and Enok playing in the water. They look like they're having a lot of fun."
    new "As I suspected, I end up finding Sylrissa and Enok playing in the water. They look like they're having a lot of fun.\n果然如我所料，我最终发现Sylrissa和Enok在水里玩耍。他们看起来玩得很开心。"

    old "It's definitely a refreshing sight after all of the grim things we've been through lately."
    new "It's definitely a refreshing sight after all of the grim things we've been through lately.\n在经历了最近那些阴郁的事情之后，这绝对是一幅让人神清气爽的景象。"

    old "Oh! Hey, [protag]. It's you, right?"
    new "Oh! Hey, [protag]. It's you, right?\n哦！嘿，[protag]。是你，对吧？"

    old "Yes, don't worry, it's me."
    new "Yes, don't worry, it's me.\n是的，别担心，是我。"

    old "I step out into the open, trying to cover my eyes and look away to respect their privacy. Then, a sudden, sharp tingle shoots through my body and I feel it lock up. I can't move my legs!"
    new "I step out into the open, trying to cover my eyes and look away to respect their privacy. Then, a sudden, sharp tingle shoots through my body and I feel it lock up. I can't move my legs!\n我走到开阔处，努力遮住眼睛、别开视线，以尊重他们的隐私。突然，一阵尖锐的刺痛窜过全身，我感觉到身体僵住了。我的腿动不了了！"

    old "Ah, sorry! That was one of my traps. I'll go over there and unfreeze you in just a second."
    new "Ah, sorry! That was one of my traps. I'll go over there and unfreeze you in just a second.\n啊，抱歉！那是我的一个陷阱。我这就过去帮你解冻，就一小会儿。"

    old "I see. That's smart."
    new "I see. That's smart.\n我明白了。这招真聪明。"

    old "I was wondering why both of you would risk being so... unprotected. I would have expected one of you to stay ashore to guard the area. Now I know why you were both in the water."
    new "I was wondering why both of you would risk being so... unprotected. I would have expected one of you to stay ashore to guard the area. Now I know why you were both in the water.\n我刚才还在想，你们俩怎么敢这么……毫无防备。我本以为你们中会有一个留在岸上放哨。现在我明白你们为什么都在水里了。"

    old "Both Enok and Sylrissa get out of the water and come over to me. Soon enough, I hear Enok casting the spell to unfreeze me."
    new "Both Enok and Sylrissa get out of the water and come over to me. Soon enough, I hear Enok casting the spell to unfreeze me.\nEnok和Sylrissa都从水里出来，朝我走来。很快，我听见Enok念起咒语为我解冻。"

    old "What is it, [protag]? You don't like what you see?"
    new "What is it, [protag]? You don't like what you see?\n怎么了，[protag]？你不喜欢你看到的吗？"

    old "Ehm, it's not that. I just feel a bit embarrassed. I mean I came here uninvited and caught you..."
    new "Ehm, it's not that. I just feel a bit embarrassed. I mean I came here uninvited and caught you...\n呃，不是那样。我只是有点尴尬。我是说，我不请自来，还撞见你们……"

    old "Caught us playing in the water. What's the big deal?"
    new "Caught us playing in the water. What's the big deal?\n撞见我们在水里玩。有什么大不了的？"

    old "Enok, I think [heshe] is embarrassed because we're both naked."
    new "Enok, I think [heshe] is embarrassed because we're both naked.\nEnok，我想[heshe]是因为我们都光着身子才尴尬。"

    old "Ah. I forgot that not all of the other races are as comfortable with nudity as we are. We'll cover up right away then."
    new "Ah. I forgot that not all of the other races are as comfortable with nudity as we are. We'll cover up right away then.\n啊。我忘了，不是所有其他种族都像我们这样对裸体习以为常。那我们马上遮起来。"

    old "Thanks. And, to answer your question Sylrissa, it's not that I didn't like what I saw. It just would have been hard to have a serious conversation with so many... distractions."
    new "Thanks. And, to answer your question Sylrissa, it's not that I didn't like what I saw. It just would have been hard to have a serious conversation with so many... distractions.\n谢谢。而且，回答你的问题，Sylrissa，我不是不喜欢自己看到的。只是身边有这么多……分散注意力的东西，很难好好谈事情。"

    old "Enok, I think [heshe] believes that [heshe] has interrupted something private."
    new "Enok, I think [heshe] believes that [heshe] has interrupted something private.\nEnok，我想[heshe]以为[heshe]打断了什么私密的事。"

    old "Oh, don't worry [protag]. We were just having fun. Like two children playing in the water. Nothing else was going on."
    new "Oh, don't worry [protag]. We were just having fun. Like two children playing in the water. Nothing else was going on.\n哦，别担心，[protag]。我们只是在玩。就像两个孩子在水里嬉戏。没发生别的什么。"

    old "Yeah. We got all of that sexual tension out of our systems a long time ago. We're just friends now."
    new "Yeah. We got all of that sexual tension out of our systems a long time ago. We're just friends now.\n是啊。我们很久以前就把那种性方面的暧昧清空了。我们现在只是朋友。"

    old "Ah. So they really were lovers in the past? I guess considering how casual nagas are when it comes to sex, it should have been obvious."
    new "Ah. So they really were lovers in the past? I guess considering how casual nagas are when it comes to sex, it should have been obvious.\n啊。所以他们以前真的是恋人？我想，考虑到naga对性的随性态度，这早该是显而易见的。"

    old "Noticing my gaze on them, both Sylrissa and Enok smile mischievously. They watch me closely as they brush up against each other in a suggestive manner to tease me. It's working."
    new "Noticing my gaze on them, both Sylrissa and Enok smile mischievously. They watch me closely as they brush up against each other in a suggestive manner to tease me. It's working.\n注意到我的目光落在他们身上，Sylrissa和Enok都露出促狭的笑容。他们一边用挑逗的方式互相蹭了蹭来逗我，一边紧紧盯着我看。这招奏效了。"

    old "I think I'm melting. It's hot here, right? Has the swamp always been this hot?"
    new "I think I'm melting. It's hot here, right? Has the swamp always been this hot?\n我觉得我要融化了。这里好热，对吧？这片沼泽一直是这么热的吗？"

    old "Haha, we'd better put some clothes on before you have a heart attack or something. Unless you'd be interested in a certain activity I have in mind..."
    new "Haha, we'd better put some clothes on before you have a heart attack or something. Unless you'd be interested in a certain activity I have in mind...\n哈哈，我们最好在你们心脏病发作之前穿上衣服。除非……你对我心里想的某个活动感兴趣……"

    old "The water should help with that. Why don't you join our little game? Of course, we could also play something a little more mature now that you're here..."
    new "The water should help with that. Why don't you join our little game? Of course, we could also play something a little more mature now that you're here...\n水应该能帮你降降温。你干嘛不加入我们的小游戏？当然，既然你来了，我们也可以玩点更成熟的东西……"

    old "I'm sure you'd enjoy it. After all, Enok and I are quite a team... in all situations."
    new "I'm sure you'd enjoy it. After all, Enok and I are quite a team... in all situations.\n我保证你会喜欢的。毕竟，我和Enok可是绝佳的搭档……在任何情况下都是。"

    old "Wh-what?"
    new "Wh-what?\n什、什么？"

    old "Both Sylrissa and Enok laugh loudly."
    new "Both Sylrissa and Enok laugh loudly.\nSylrissa和Enok都放声大笑。"

    old "Forgive her. She just wanted to tease you, as usual."
    new "Forgive her. She just wanted to tease you, as usual.\n原谅她吧。她只是想逗逗你，跟往常一样。"

    old "R-right."
    new "R-right.\n好、好吧。"

    old "Once I calm down a bit, we all head back to our usual spot near the river."
    new "Once I calm down a bit, we all head back to our usual spot near the river.\n等我稍微平静下来，我们就一起回到河边那个老地方。"

    old "[protag], both Sylrissa and I actually wanted to talk with you about something..."
    new "[protag], both Sylrissa and I actually wanted to talk with you about something...\n[protag]，其实我和Sylrissa都想跟你谈谈一件事……"

    old "We noticed that you spend a lot of time with both of us. And we both like your company."
    new "We noticed that you spend a lot of time with both of us. And we both like your company.\n我们注意到，你花了很多时间和我们俩在一起。而且我们都喜欢有你在身边。"

    old "And, don't get us wrong, we'll both follow you anywhere, no matter what you say. Even to Inferno itself! But ... we need to know."
    new "And, don't get us wrong, we'll both follow you anywhere, no matter what you say. Even to Inferno itself! But ... we need to know.\n还有，别误会我们，无论你说什么，我们都会追随你去任何地方。哪怕是Inferno！可是……我们得知道。"

    old "Know what?"
    new "Know what?\n知道什么？"

    old "Who you're in love with? Me, or Enok?"
    new "Who you're in love with? Me, or Enok?\n你爱的是谁？是我，还是Enok？"

    old "The question strikes me by surprise even though I know it shouldn't. I had plenty of time to figure out what my answer would be, but I'd kept putting it off."
    new "The question strikes me by surprise even though I know it shouldn't. I had plenty of time to figure out what my answer would be, but I'd kept putting it off.\n这个问题让我措手不及，尽管我明白它本不该如此。我本来有充足的时间想清楚自己的答案，却一直拖着没去想。"

    old "We both owe you, [protag]. You did so much for us. You helped us, when most people in Aravorn would have killed us on sight or ran away. We'll accept whatever choice you make."
    new "We both owe you, [protag]. You did so much for us. You helped us, when most people in Aravorn would have killed us on sight or ran away. We'll accept whatever choice you make.\n我们俩都欠你的，[protag]。你为我们做了那么多。你帮助了我们，而在Aravorn，大多数人一看见我们就会当场杀掉，或者逃之夭夭。无论你做出什么选择，我们都会接受。"

    old "I take a deep breath and think it over one last time before giving them my answer."
    new "I take a deep breath and think it over one last time before giving them my answer.\n我深吸一口气，在给出答案之前，最后想了一遍。"

    old "I'm sorry Sylrissa, but...I like Enok more."
    new "I'm sorry Sylrissa, but...I like Enok more.\n对不起，Sylrissa，但是……我更喜欢Enok。"

    old "Enok, you're kind and handsome, but..."
    new "Enok, you're kind and handsome, but...\nEnok，你温柔又英俊，但是……"

    old "Sylrissa it is then."
    new "Sylrissa it is then.\n那就是Sylrissa了。"

    old "Enok and Sylrissa exchange a surprised look."
    new "Enok and Sylrissa exchange a surprised look.\nEnok和Sylrissa交换了一个惊讶的眼神。"

    old "Why can't I have you both?"
    new "Why can't I have you both?\n为什么我不能两个都要？"

    old "[protag], for the first time we have the chance to live a normal life..."
    new "[protag], for the first time we have the chance to live a normal life...\n[protag]，这是我们第一次有机会过上正常的生活……"

    old "As far as we know, polygamy is not allowed in Grimoire, right?"
    new "As far as we know, polygamy is not allowed in Grimoire, right?\n据我们所知，Grimoire不允许一夫多妻，对吧？"

    old "Well, I am not sure if there are any specific laws against it, but-"
    new "Well, I am not sure if there are any specific laws against it, but-\n嗯，我不确定有没有专门的法律禁止这个，不过——"

    old "Do you know anyone in a polyamorous relationship?"
    new "Do you know anyone in a polyamorous relationship?\n你认识处于多角关系的人吗？"

    old "No. But that doesn't mean it can't happen! I know that it's not common and that some cultures are explicitly against it, but what matters is what we feel about it."
    new "No. But that doesn't mean it can't happen! I know that it's not common and that some cultures are explicitly against it, but what matters is what we feel about it.\n不认识。但那不代表它不能成真！我知道这并不常见，也知道有些文化明确反对它，可重要的是我们自己的感受。"

    old "So the real question is: are you willing to share me?"
    new "So the real question is: are you willing to share me?\n所以真正的问题是：你们愿意和我分享吗？"

    old "That's a good question. But, I believe we already did?"
    new "That's a good question. But, I believe we already did?\n问得好。不过，我想我们不是已经分享过了吗？"

    old "My dear, I think [heshe] means at the same time..."
    new "My dear, I think [heshe] means at the same time...\n亲爱的，我想[heshe]的意思是同时……"

    old "No. That's not... Well, not unless you want to. But that's not the point! I'm not talking about sharing a bed. I'm talking about being in a relationship together. All three of us."
    new "No. That's not... Well, not unless you want to. But that's not the point! I'm not talking about sharing a bed. I'm talking about being in a relationship together. All three of us.\n不。不是那样……嗯，除非你们想。但重点不是那个！我说的不是同床共枕。我说的是我们三个人一起处在一段关系里。"

    old "I know that it probably won't be easy but, if it's us, I think we could make it work. If you both want to, of course."
    new "I know that it probably won't be easy but, if it's us, I think we could make it work. If you both want to, of course.\n我知道这也许不会容易，但是，如果是我们的话，我想我们能经营好。当然，前提是你们都愿意。"

    old "Sylrissa and Enok look at each other consideringly. It just looks like staring to me, but they must have come to some sort of silent agreement because they both turn back towards me with smiles on their faces."
    new "Sylrissa and Enok look at each other consideringly. It just looks like staring to me, but they must have come to some sort of silent agreement because they both turn back towards me with smiles on their faces.\nSylrissa和Enok互相看着对方，若有所思。在我看来那就像是在对视，但他们一定达成了某种无声的共识，因为他们都面带微笑，转向了我。"

    old "It's an interesting proposal, [protag]. I think we'd like to try."
    new "It's an interesting proposal, [protag]. I think we'd like to try.\n这是个有趣的提议，[protag]。我想我们愿意试一试。"

    old "Why not? Sylrissa and I have always gotten along well. I don't see why it couldn't work."
    new "Why not? Sylrissa and I have always gotten along well. I don't see why it couldn't work.\n为什么不呢？我和Sylrissa一直处得很好。我看不出有什么行不通的。"

    old "We might have even suggested it ourselves if we'd realized that you would be so... 'open' to the idea."
    new "We might have even suggested it ourselves if we'd realized that you would be so... 'open' to the idea.\n要是我们早意识到你对这个想法会这么“开放”，说不定我们自己就先提出来了。"

    old "This is a first for me. Honestly, I'd never thought that I'd be the kind of person who'd propose such a thing, but... this feels right."
    new "This is a first for me. Honestly, I'd never thought that I'd be the kind of person who'd propose such a thing, but... this feels right.\n这对我来说是头一回。老实说，我从没想过自己会成为提出这种建议的人，可是……这感觉是对的。"

    old "I let out a relieved sigh. I'm so glad that they both want this too. I'm not sure what I would have done if they'd rejected the idea. Having to pick just one... I don't think I could've done that."
    new "I let out a relieved sigh. I'm so glad that they both want this too. I'm not sure what I would have done if they'd rejected the idea. Having to pick just one... I don't think I could've done that.\n我如释重负地叹了口气。我很高兴他们也都想要这样。要是他们拒绝了，我还真不知道该怎么办。只能二选一的话……我想我做不到。"

    old "Well, I'm glad everyone is happy. I really wish I could stay, but I have to get back to the mission."
    new "Well, I'm glad everyone is happy. I really wish I could stay, but I have to get back to the mission.\n嗯，很高兴大家都很开心。我真希望我能留下来，但我得回去执行任务了。"

    old "We understand, [protag]. We'll both help you however we can."
    new "We understand, [protag]. We'll both help you however we can.\n我们理解，[protag]。我们会尽全力帮你的。"

    old "I can't wait for this N'Mar threat to be over so we can all start our new life together."
    new "I can't wait for this N'Mar threat to be over so we can all start our new life together.\n我已经等不及N'Mar的威胁早点结束，好让我们开始共同的新生活。"

    old "Me either."
    new "Me either.\n我也是。"

    old "I like both of you, and I had a lot of fun, but... I don't think I'm actually in love with either of you."
    new "I like both of you, and I had a lot of fun, but... I don't think I'm actually in love with either of you.\n我喜欢你们两个，我也玩得很开心，可是……我想我其实没有爱上你们中的任何一个。"

    old "This is... embarrassing."
    new "This is... embarrassing.\n这……真尴尬。"

    old "I consider both of you true friends, and I would do anything to help you, but... Well, you know."
    new "I consider both of you true friends, and I would do anything to help you, but... Well, you know.\n我把你们两个都当成真正的朋友，我什么都愿意为你们做，可是……嗯，你们懂的。"

    old "This is probably our fault."
    new "This is probably our fault.\n这大概是我们的错。"

    old "It's the first time we've had a relationship with... someone outside our naga community. We might have expected too much from you."
    new "It's the first time we've had a relationship with... someone outside our naga community. We might have expected too much from you.\n这是我们第一次和我们naga圈子以外的人建立这样的关系。我们也许对你期望太高了。"

    old "It's not just your fault. I knew that was the case. I should have been more considerate of that."
    new "It's not just your fault. I knew that was the case. I should have been more considerate of that.\n不全是你们的错。我早就知道会是那样。我本该更体谅这一点。"

    old "Well, at least it was fun while it lasted."
    new "Well, at least it was fun while it lasted.\n嗯，至少这段日子过得很开心。"

    old "Very fun."
    new "Very fun.\n非常开心。"

    old "They seem to be taking it better than I thought they would. Still, I'll to be more careful about who I sleep with in future. I don't want to end up disappointing anyone else I care about."
    new "They seem to be taking it better than I thought they would. Still, I'll to be more careful about who I sleep with in future. I don't want to end up disappointing anyone else I care about.\n他们看起来比我想象中更能接受这件事。不过，以后我会更小心地选择同床的对象。我不想再让任何我在乎的人失望。"

    old "I'm sorry-"
    new "I'm sorry-\n对不起——"

    old "[protag], we knew that you had to choose one of us sooner or later."
    new "[protag], we knew that you had to choose one of us sooner or later.\n[protag]，我们知道你迟早得在我们中间选一个。"

    old "That's why we decided to accept whatever you decided. But we needed to know, before things became awkward between the three of us."
    new "That's why we decided to accept whatever you decided. But we needed to know, before things became awkward between the three of us.\n所以我们决定，无论你做什么决定，我们都接受。但我们得趁我们三个之间还没变得尴尬，先弄明白。"

    old "Yeah. I guess you're right."
    new "Yeah. I guess you're right.\n是啊。我想你说得对。"

    old "Anyway, I'd better head back now. Duty calls, unfortunately."
    new "Anyway, I'd better head back now. Duty calls, unfortunately.\n总之，我最好现在回去了。很不巧，职责在身。"

    old "[chosen_romance] comes closer and kisses me on the cheek. The other naga looks away."
    new "[chosen_romance] comes closer and kisses me on the cheek. The other naga looks away.\n[chosen_romance]走上前来，在我的脸颊上亲了一下。另一个naga别开了目光。"

    old "As I walk away from the swamp, I hope that they can still remain friends with each other. They've been there for each other for so long... I'm going to trust in that. I know that they'll come out of this okay."
    new "As I walk away from the swamp, I hope that they can still remain friends with each other. They've been there for each other for so long... I'm going to trust in that. I know that they'll come out of this okay.\n我离开沼泽时，希望他们彼此还能继续做朋友。他们相伴了那么久……我打算相信这一点。我知道他们最终会挺过去的。"

    old "It's late now. I probably should have gone to bed hours ago, but I'd gotten so absorbed in the books on undead that I was reading that I've kept putting it off."
