    new "Suddenly, both Enok and Sylrissa get naked. I shouldn't be surprised since I know that this is only a dream, but... it's really a pleasure to see. I'm starting to feel hot.\n突然，Enok和Sylrissa都脱光了衣服。我不该惊讶，因为我知道这不过是个梦，可是……看着真是种享受。我开始觉得浑身发热。"

    old "They keep up their routines as if on a sort of ritual loop. Still, despite the repetitiveness, it's enough to keep me enthralled. I begin touching myself. After all, it'd be a shame not to take advantage of this dream."
    new "They keep up their routines as if on a sort of ritual loop. Still, despite the repetitiveness, it's enough to keep me enthralled. I begin touching myself. After all, it'd be a shame not to take advantage of this dream.\n他们继续着自己的动作，仿佛陷入某种仪式般的循环。不过，尽管重复，也足以让我着迷。我开始抚摸自己。毕竟，不好好利用这个梦就太可惜了。"

    old "I find Vaeril in the Grimoire marketplace."
    new "I find Vaeril in the Grimoire marketplace.\n我在Grimoire的市场里找到了Vaeril。"

    old "Vaeril, it's good to see you out and about. What business brings you to the market? An errand of some sort?"
    new "Vaeril, it's good to see you out and about. What business brings you to the market? An errand of some sort?\nVaeril，很高兴看到你出来走动。是什么事把你带到市场来的？是来跑腿吗？"

    old "Indeed. I've actually begun working at an infirmary near the edge of town. To my knowledge, it's one of the few places in Grimoire where sick non-humans are welcome."
    new "Indeed. I've actually begun working at an infirmary near the edge of town. To my knowledge, it's one of the few places in Grimoire where sick non-humans are welcome.\n确实。事实上，我已经开始在小镇边缘的一间医务室工作了。据我所知，那是Grimoire里少数欢迎非人类病人的地方之一。"

    old "It's also one of the few places in Grimoire where I feel welcome. I have nothing against human society, but sometimes I feel that society has something against me."
    new "It's also one of the few places in Grimoire where I feel welcome. I have nothing against human society, but sometimes I feel that society has something against me.\n那也是Grimoire里少数让我感到受欢迎的地方之一。我对人类社会没有任何敌意，但有时我觉得，是社会对我有敌意。"

    old "Have you been having trouble with harassment? You haven't gotten into any conflicts, have you?"
    new "Have you been having trouble with harassment? You haven't gotten into any conflicts, have you?\n你一直有受到骚扰吗？你没跟人起什么冲突吧？"

    old "No, nothing of that nature. But simply standing in this marketplace, I tend to draw stares that put me in a state of unease. The city tolerates me, but sometimes I feel that it does only that."
    new "No, nothing of that nature. But simply standing in this marketplace, I tend to draw stares that put me in a state of unease. The city tolerates me, but sometimes I feel that it does only that.\n没有，不是那种事。只是单单站在这个市场里，我就容易招来异样的目光，让我浑身不自在。这座城市容忍我，但有时我觉得，它仅仅是容忍而已。"

    old "Perhaps it's all for the best. After all, you're no ordinary elf to begin with. Druids are rare, and druids of your unique talent are rarer still."
    new "Perhaps it's all for the best. After all, you're no ordinary elf to begin with. Druids are rare, and druids of your unique talent are rarer still.\n也许这样反而最好。毕竟，你从一开始就不是普通的elf。德鲁伊本就稀少，而拥有你这种独特天赋的德鲁伊更是凤毛麟角。"

    old "I don't think you have anything to fear in Grimoire, but I think you're right to avoid drawing attention to yourself."
    new "I don't think you have anything to fear in Grimoire, but I think you're right to avoid drawing attention to yourself.\n我不觉得你在Grimoire需要害怕什么，但我也认为，避免引人注目是明智的。"

    old "Grimoire is the capital of the Empire of Man, and it has a long history as a human city. The cultural attitudes of a city this large take a long time to change. But I say go out and let them see you. If enough non-humans are willing to do the same, the people of Grimoire will have no choice but to regard you as people."
    new "Grimoire is the capital of the Empire of Man, and it has a long history as a human city. The cultural attitudes of a city this large take a long time to change. But I say go out and let them see you. If enough non-humans are willing to do the same, the people of Grimoire will have no choice but to regard you as people.\nGrimoire是Empire of Man的首都，它作为人类城市有着悠久的历史。这么大一座城市的文化观念，需要很长的时间才能改变。但我的建议是，走出去，让他们看到你。如果有足够多的非人类愿意这么做，Grimoire的人民就别无选择，只能把你们当作人来看待。"

    old "Most humans who are wary of elves have that attitude not because of experiences they've had with elves, but because they've had no exposure, leaving them with only stories and tall tales to fill that gap in their own experience. The more you walk around and expose them to the genuine article, the more you can erode away those preconceived notions."
    new "Most humans who are wary of elves have that attitude not because of experiences they've had with elves, but because they've had no exposure, leaving them with only stories and tall tales to fill that gap in their own experience. The more you walk around and expose them to the genuine article, the more you can erode away those preconceived notions.\n大多数对elf心存戒备的人类之所以有那种态度，不是因为他们和elf打过交道，而是因为他们从未接触过，只能靠故事和传闻来填补自己经验里的那片空白。你越是四处走动，让他们接触到真实的你，就越能消磨掉那些先入为主的成见。"

    old "That's what I'd like to think, anyway. But I understand if it's little comfort to hear that coming from a human."
    new "That's what I'd like to think, anyway. But I understand if it's little comfort to hear that coming from a human.\n反正，我是这么想的。不过我也理解，这话出自一个人类之口，恐怕起不了多少安慰作用。"

    old "You get used to it over time. Besides, the only stares and odd looks I get are from people I don't know. Most people in Grimoire will treat you like a person if you take the time to talk to them."
    new "You get used to it over time. Besides, the only stares and odd looks I get are from people I don't know. Most people in Grimoire will treat you like a person if you take the time to talk to them.\n时间久了你就习惯了。再说了，我招来的那些注视和异样的目光，都来自我不认识的人。Grimoire的大多数人，只要你肯花时间跟他们聊聊，就会把你当人看待。"

    old "When people look at you funny, it's probably because they're commoners who have never met an elf before. If it makes you feel better, realize that a lot of them aren't resentful of your presence, they're just curious about something they're not familiar with."
    new "When people look at you funny, it's probably because they're commoners who have never met an elf before. If it makes you feel better, realize that a lot of them aren't resentful of your presence, they're just curious about something they're not familiar with.\n当人们用怪异的眼神看你时，很可能因为他们是从没见过elf的平民。如果这能让你好受些，就想想：他们中的许多人并非反感你的存在，只是对陌生的事物感到好奇罢了。"

    old "Then again, my experiences aren't yours. I can't deny that there are times when I feel like humans have an easier time of things here in Grimoire. But we're not going to change the attitudes of this city overnight, so I think the best we can do is deal with the circumstances we're given."
    new "Then again, my experiences aren't yours. I can't deny that there are times when I feel like humans have an easier time of things here in Grimoire. But we're not going to change the attitudes of this city overnight, so I think the best we can do is deal with the circumstances we're given.\n话又说回来，我的经历终究不是你的经历。我无法否认，有时我会觉得，在Grimoire这里，人类确实要轻松一些。但我们不可能一夜之间改变这座城市的态度，所以我想，我们所能做的最好的事，就是应对我们被给予的处境。"

    old "I hope you don't misunderstand my meaning. I don't feel persecuted in any way. In fact, considering what I am, human society has been vastly more accepting of me than my own native people were."
    new "I hope you don't misunderstand my meaning. I don't feel persecuted in any way. In fact, considering what I am, human society has been vastly more accepting of me than my own native people were.\n希望你不要误解我的意思。我丝毫没有觉得受到迫害。事实上，考虑到我的身份，人类社会对我的接纳程度，已经远远超过了我自己原本的同胞。"

    old "I was a hermit when you met me, remember. But when you live in a city such as Grimoire, it's easy to recognize its imperfections, and with that recognition comes a certain desire to see things made better."
    new "I was a hermit when you met me, remember. But when you live in a city such as Grimoire, it's easy to recognize its imperfections, and with that recognition comes a certain desire to see things made better.\n你遇见我的时候，我是个隐士，记得吗。但当你住在像Grimoire这样的城市里，就很容易看清它的种种不完美，而有了这种认识，就会生出一种想让事情变得更好的渴望。"

    old "That is part of what drove me to seek work at the infirmary. It allows me to do work that has a tangible impact on the lives of others. Oftentimes, the people that I touch most are those that are most troubled."
    new "That is part of what drove me to seek work at the infirmary. It allows me to do work that has a tangible impact on the lives of others. Oftentimes, the people that I touch most are those that are most troubled.\n这正是促使我去医务室找工作的部分原因。它让我能做点对他人生活有切实影响的工作。很多时候，我接触最多的，正是那些最困苦的人。"

    old "You said you were here buying herbs, is that right?"
    new "You said you were here buying herbs, is that right?\n你说你是来买草药的，对吧？"

    old "Yes, I've just finished making my purchases and was on my way back to the infirmary."
    new "Yes, I've just finished making my purchases and was on my way back to the infirmary.\n是的，我刚采购完，正要回医务室。"

    old "Do you mind if I walk with you?"
    new "Do you mind if I walk with you?\n你介意我和你一起走吗？"

    old "Please, be me guest."
    new "Please, be me guest.\n请便，别客气。"

    old "This is where I work."
    new "This is where I work.\n这就是我工作的地方。"

    old "I scan the infirmary. It's one large single room, with beds lining all four walls. Every single one is filled, and based on a cursory glance it seems that most of them are elves or dwarves. I count sixteen beds in total."
    new "I scan the infirmary. It's one large single room, with beds lining all four walls. Every single one is filled, and based on a cursory glance it seems that most of them are elves or dwarves. I count sixteen beds in total.\n我扫视了一下医务室。这是一间很大的单间，四壁都靠墙摆着床。每一张床都住满了，粗略一看，似乎大多是elf或dwarf。我数了数，一共十六张床。"

    old "This isn't quite what I expected."
    new "This isn't quite what I expected.\n这和我预想的不太一样。"

    old "Most of these people have nowhere else to go. We're an infirmary. We lack the resources of a hospital, but we have to do the same job as a hospital with what we have."
    new "Most of these people have nowhere else to go. We're an infirmary. We lack the resources of a hospital, but we have to do the same job as a hospital with what we have.\n这些人大多无处可去。我们只是一间医务室。我们缺少医院那样的资源，却得用现有的条件，做和医院一样的工作。"

    old "My services as a healer are in high demand, but most of the healing that happens in this hospital has to be done by time. I can mend a broken bone, but fixing a bad back is beyond my means."
    new "My services as a healer are in high demand, but most of the healing that happens in this hospital has to be done by time. I can mend a broken bone, but fixing a bad back is beyond my means.\n我作为治疗师的服务需求量很大，但这间医务室里的大部分治疗，都只能靠时间来慢慢完成。我能接好断骨，但要治好一处坏掉的脊背，就超出我的能力了。"

    old "Combat wounds are easy. In combat, you're mostly just shifting around flesh that was recently torn apart. It's much harder to restore flesh that has been eaten away by disease."
    new "Combat wounds are easy. In combat, you're mostly just shifting around flesh that was recently torn apart. It's much harder to restore flesh that has been eaten away by disease.\n战斗造成的伤好治。在战斗中，你大多只是把刚被撕裂的皮肉重新归位。但要恢复被疾病啃噬掉的皮肉，就难多了。"

    old "Do you use your, ah, special talent?"
    new "Do you use your, ah, special talent?\n你会用你那，呃，特殊的天赋吗？"

    old "If the question of whether to use my magic was left up to my own whims, I'd use it never. But my whims must bow to the needs of the patients here. I offer what help I can. Yet I can only do so much. And I sometimes wonder if I could do more."
    new "If the question of whether to use my magic was left up to my own whims, I'd use it never. But my whims must bow to the needs of the patients here. I offer what help I can. Yet I can only do so much. And I sometimes wonder if I could do more.\n要是用不用魔法全凭我自己的心意，那我永远都不会用。但我的心意必须让位于这里病人的需要。我尽我所能提供帮助。可我能做的终究有限。有时我也会想，自己是否能做得更多。"

    old "I think we'd all like to do more, Vaeril. There's more suffering in this world than we could address in a lifetime."
    new "I think we'd all like to do more, Vaeril. There's more suffering in this world than we could address in a lifetime.\n我想我们都想做得更多，Vaeril。这个世界的苦难，比我们穷尽一生能应对的还要多。"

    old "When I said 'I wonder if I could do more,' I wasn't talking about philosophical speculation. There's a very specific case I have in mind. I've been contemplating action steps."
    new "When I said 'I wonder if I could do more,' I wasn't talking about philosophical speculation. There's a very specific case I have in mind. I've been contemplating action steps.\n我说“不知道自己能否做得更多”的时候，并不是在谈什么哲思空想。我心里有个非常具体的病例。我一直在考虑该采取什么行动。"

    old "What exactly are you talking about?"
    new "What exactly are you talking about?\n你到底在说什么？"

    old "This boy."
    new "This boy.\n这个男孩。"

    old "Vaeril gestures to the bed nearest the door. A small elf child rests beneath a thin sheet, his chest rising and falling with every breath."
    new "Vaeril gestures to the bed nearest the door. A small elf child rests beneath a thin sheet, his chest rising and falling with every breath.\nVaeril指了指靠门最近的那张床。一个幼小的elf孩子躺在一张薄薄的被单下，胸口随着每一次呼吸一起一伏。"

    old "For this boy, the simple act of taking a breath is an ordeal. Every morning and every night, I give him a bit of vim and vigor, drained from the plants near here. It keeps him alive. But this boy will never breathe normally unless I find some way to mend his throat."
    new "For this boy, the simple act of taking a breath is an ordeal. Every morning and every night, I give him a bit of vim and vigor, drained from the plants near here. It keeps him alive. But this boy will never breathe normally unless I find some way to mend his throat.\n对这个男孩来说，哪怕只是喘一口气都是一场磨难。每天早晚，我都给他注入一点从附近植物中汲取的活力，好让他活下来。可是除非我能找到办法修复他的喉咙，否则这个男孩永远无法正常呼吸。"

    old "Is it that possible?"
    new "Is it that possible?\n那有可能吗？"

    old "Ordinarily, I would say no. This is an affliction this boy has suffered since birth. As I said, I can fix wounds, but there is a problem with his body's constitution. I can't give him what was never there, or so conventional thinking would suggest."
    new "Ordinarily, I would say no. This is an affliction this boy has suffered since birth. As I said, I can fix wounds, but there is a problem with his body's constitution. I can't give him what was never there, or so conventional thinking would suggest.\n按常理，我会说不可能。这是这个男孩从出生起就患上的顽疾。如我所说，我能治好伤口，但他的身体机能出了问题。我无法给他从未有过的东西——或者说，这是常规思路给出的答案。"

    old "However, he is young. Fewer than three years old, by my estimation. His body is forming new muscle and sinew every day. His body has the capability to create a new throat for him."
    new "However, he is young. Fewer than three years old, by my estimation. His body is forming new muscle and sinew every day. His body has the capability to create a new throat for him.\n然而，他还小。据我估计，还不到三岁。他的身体每天都在生长出新的肌肉和筋腱。他的身体有能力为他造出一副新的喉咙。"

    old "But he is so sickly, that his body drains any bit of vigor that might be used for building new muscle. His body is in crisis mode. Simply staying alive is a struggle. It lacks the strength to repair his throat."
    new "But he is so sickly, that his body drains any bit of vigor that might be used for building new muscle. His body is in crisis mode. Simply staying alive is a struggle. It lacks the strength to repair his throat.\n但他病得太重了，身体会把任何可能用于生长新肌肉的活力都消耗殆尽。他的身体处于危机模式。仅仅是活着就已经是场挣扎。它没有力气去修复他的喉咙。"

    old "But you think there may be a way to help him."
    new "But you think there may be a way to help him.\n但你认为也许有办法能帮到他。"

    old "This wood staff of mine has done well enough to keep him alive, but I've run against its limitations. There is a limit to the amount of vigor I can channel through it. But perhaps..."
    new "This wood staff of mine has done well enough to keep him alive, but I've run against its limitations. There is a limit to the amount of vigor I can channel through it. But perhaps...\n我这根木杖能让他活到现在，已经很不错了，但我已触碰到它的极限。我能通过它传导的活力是有上限的。可是也许……"

    old "Perhaps?"
    new "Perhaps?\n也许？"

    old "Perhap infusing it with some kind of herb might increase its potency."
    new "Perhap infusing it with some kind of herb might increase its potency.\n也许把它注入某种草药，能提升它的效力。"

    old "Just any old herb?"
    new "Just any old herb?\n随便什么普通的草药？"

    old "I've tried many herbs. Mugwort, thyme, burdock, comfrey, I've tried them all, except for one. Jewelwort."
    new "I've tried many herbs. Mugwort, thyme, burdock, comfrey, I've tried them all, except for one. Jewelwort.\n我试过很多草药。艾草、百里香、牛蒡、紫草，我全都试过了，只差一种。Jewelwort。"

    old "Jewelwort? Sounds more like a gem than an herb."
    new "Jewelwort? Sounds more like a gem than an herb.\nJewelwort？听起来更像宝石，而不像草药。"

    old "Jewelwort does have the luminescent properties one might associate with a jewel, hence the name. The same structure that gives it that luminescent properties also makes it a potent as a healing agent. It is a beautiful thing to behold, and a powerful asset to any potential medicine-maker."
    new "Jewelwort does have the luminescent properties one might associate with a jewel, hence the name. The same structure that gives it that luminescent properties also makes it a potent as a healing agent. It is a beautiful thing to behold, and a powerful asset to any potential medicine-maker.\nJewelwort确实拥有人们会联想到宝石的那种发光特性，名字也由此而来。赋予它发光特性的同一种结构，也使它成为强效的治疗药剂。它看起来赏心悦目，对任何潜在的制药者来说都是珍贵的资源。"

    old "So why haven't you tried it yet?"
    new "So why haven't you tried it yet?\n那你为什么还没试过它？"

    old "Jewelwort is exceedingly rare. Every day I go to the market in hopes of finding some merchant who might have some of that legendary herb. Unfortunately, there's none to be found. I think it may be extinct. However, I have heard rumors..."
    new "Jewelwort is exceedingly rare. Every day I go to the market in hopes of finding some merchant who might have some of that legendary herb. Unfortunately, there's none to be found. I think it may be extinct. However, I have heard rumors...\nJewelwort极其稀有。我每天都去市场，希望能找到某个拥有这种传奇草药的商人。不幸的是，一无所获。我想它可能已经灭绝了。不过，我听到过一些传言……"

    old "Go on..."
    new "Go on...\n说下去……"

    old "An elf merchant passing through suggested that jewelwort had once been sighted in the blighted wood near the edge of N'Mar."
    new "An elf merchant passing through suggested that jewelwort had once been sighted in the blighted wood near the edge of N'Mar.\n一个路过的elf商人提到，在N'Mar边缘那片枯萎的树林里，曾有人见过Jewelwort。"

    old "And you'd like to investigate."
    new "And you'd like to investigate.\n而你希望去调查一番。"

    old "It's only a rumor."
    new "It's only a rumor.\n那只是个传言。"

    old "Isn't it worth it to follow every lead? This boy's life is at stake."
    new "Isn't it worth it to follow every lead? This boy's life is at stake.\n难道不该追踪每一条线索吗？这个男孩的命危在旦夕。"

    old "The plains of N'Mar are treacherous enough. Who knows what dangers lurk in the blighted wood? It's certainly more than I could face alone, and I wouldn't wish to foist that danger upon anyone."
    new "The plains of N'Mar are treacherous enough. Who knows what dangers lurk in the blighted wood? It's certainly more than I could face alone, and I wouldn't wish to foist that danger upon anyone.\nN'Mar的平原已经够凶险的了。谁知道那片枯萎树林里潜伏着什么危险？那肯定不是我一个人能应付得了的，而我也不愿把那种危险强加给任何人。"

    old "What if I accept the risk willingly? We can go together."
    new "What if I accept the risk willingly? We can go together.\n如果我自愿承担风险呢？我们可以一起去。"

    old "I feared you might make such an offer. Your mission is more important than any of my personal concerns. I wish you wouldn't jeopardize your own safety for something that has nothing to do with you."
    new "I feared you might make such an offer. Your mission is more important than any of my personal concerns. I wish you wouldn't jeopardize your own safety for something that has nothing to do with you.\n我就怕你会提出这样的建议。你的任务比我任何一桩私事都重要。我希望你别为了一件与你无关的事，拿自己的安全冒险。"

    old "Vaeril, I think you need to understand something here. I'm something of a leader."
    new "Vaeril, I think you need to understand something here. I'm something of a leader.\nVaeril，我想你得明白一件事。我在某种程度上算个领袖。"

    old "That is my point precisely. You can't afford to compromise your safety to chase my own personal dilemmas. There are others besides me who rely on your leadership."
    new "That is my point precisely. You can't afford to compromise your safety to chase my own personal dilemmas. There are others besides me who rely on your leadership.\n这正是我的意思。你不能为了追逐我个人的难题，而拿自己的安全做赌注。除了我，还有别人仰赖你的领导。"

    old "A leader is only as strong as his followers. What a leader needs isn't personal strength, but loyalty. And runs both ways. You need to give it to get it."
    new "A leader is only as strong as his followers. What a leader needs isn't personal strength, but loyalty. And runs both ways. You need to give it to get it.\n一个领袖的强弱，取决于他的追随者。领袖需要的不是个人的强大，而是忠诚。而且忠诚是双向的。你得先付出，才能得到。"

    old "How can I expect you to follow me into battle and put your life on the line for my interests if I'm not willing to do the same for you?"
    new "How can I expect you to follow me into battle and put your life on the line for my interests if I'm not willing to do the same for you?\n如果我不愿为你们做同样的事，我又怎能指望你们随我上战场，为我的利益出生入死？"

    old "Let me join you in your quest, Vaeril. I won't take no for an answer."
    new "Let me join you in your quest, Vaeril. I won't take no for an answer.\n让我加入你的行动吧，Vaeril。我不接受“不”这个回答。"

    old "Vaeril, you need to understand something. Right now I'm in the business of assembling a special task force. And I need that task force to be the strongest that it can be."
    new "Vaeril, you need to understand something. Right now I'm in the business of assembling a special task force. And I need that task force to be the strongest that it can be.\nVaeril，你得明白一件事。眼下我正在着手组建一支特别行动队。我需要这支队伍强大到极致。"

    old "Your use your healing powers here in the infirmary to help the weak. But those are the same powers I expect to have at my side in battle."
    new "Your use your healing powers here in the infirmary to help the weak. But those are the same powers I expect to have at my side in battle.\n你在这里的医务室里，用你的治疗能力帮助弱者。但那些能力，也正是我期望在战斗中能伴随我左右的力量。"

    old "When my healer who supports me in combat tells me there may be a way for him to amplify the impact of his healing powers, it's in my best interest to pursue that lead, even if it may be a dead end. And if we manage to save this boy's life in the process, all the better."
    new "When my healer who supports me in combat tells me there may be a way for him to amplify the impact of his healing powers, it's in my best interest to pursue that lead, even if it may be a dead end. And if we manage to save this boy's life in the process, all the better.\n当我在战斗中倚仗的治疗师告诉我，也许有办法放大他治疗能力的效果时，追寻这条线索最符合我的利益，哪怕它可能是条死路。而如果我们能在这个过程中救下这个男孩的命，那就再好不过了。"

    old "I've made a decision, Vaeril. I want you to be the best healer you can be. I'm traveling with you to the blighted wood."
    new "I've made a decision, Vaeril. I want you to be the best healer you can be. I'm traveling with you to the blighted wood.\n我已经做了决定，Vaeril。我要你成为你能成为的最好的治疗师。我会和你一起去那片枯萎的树林。"

    old "Very well. If your mind is made up, far be it from me to challenge your decision."
    new "Very well. If your mind is made up, far be it from me to challenge your decision.\n好吧。既然你心意已决，那也轮不到我来质疑你的决定。"

    old "I have responsibilities to attend to today. But when you're ready to head to the blighted wood, I'll be here waiting."
    new "I have responsibilities to attend to today. But when you're ready to head to the blighted wood, I'll be here waiting.\n今天我还有些职责要处理。不过等你准备好前往那片枯萎的树林时，我会在这里等你。"

    old "We'll make it happen soon, Vaeril. I promise."
    new "We'll make it happen soon, Vaeril. I promise.\n我们很快就会动身的，Vaeril。我保证。"

    old "I meet Vaeril at the infirmary in Grimoire in the early morning before dawn breaks."
    new "I meet Vaeril at the infirmary in Grimoire in the early morning before dawn breaks.\n天还没破晓，我就在清晨时分赶到Grimoire的医务室与Vaeril会合。"

    old "Vaeril, you're up awfully early."
    new "Vaeril, you're up awfully early.\nVaeril，你起得可真早。"

    old "I always am. Sickness never sleeps."
    new "I always am. Sickness never sleeps.\n我一向如此。病痛从不入睡。"

    old "But do you?"
    new "But do you?\n可你会睡吗？"

    old "I sleep when I can. Sometimes at night, sometimes during daylight."
    new "I sleep when I can. Sometimes at night, sometimes during daylight.\n能睡的时候我就睡。有时在夜里，有时在白天。"

    old "I was thinking we might investigate the blighted woods today. Is now a good time for you?"
    new "I was thinking we might investigate the blighted woods today. Is now a good time for you?\n我在想，我们今天也许可以去调查那片枯萎的树林。现在这个时间对你合适吗？"

    old "Good time or bad, it has to be done. We may as well do it now."
    new "Good time or bad, it has to be done. We may as well do it now.\n合不合适，都非做不可。我们不如现在就动身。"

    old "Well, we should head out before the sun gets too high in the sky."
    new "Well, we should head out before the sun gets too high in the sky.\n嗯，我们该趁太阳还没升得太高就出发。"

    old "Let's go, then."
    new "Let's go, then.\n那走吧。"

    old "We arrive at the edge of N'Mar's plains just as the first rays of sun have barely crested the horizon."
    new "We arrive at the edge of N'Mar's plains just as the first rays of sun have barely crested the horizon.\n就在第一缕阳光刚擦过地平线的时候，我们抵达了N'Mar平原的边缘。"

    old "By my estimation, we have around half an hour to get to the blighted woods before the sun gets high enough in the sky to blind us through the mist."
    new "By my estimation, we have around half an hour to get to the blighted woods before the sun gets high enough in the sky to blind us through the mist.\n据我估计，我们大概有半小时的时间赶到那片枯萎的树林，否则太阳升得够高之后，就会透过雾气晃得我们睁不开眼。"

    old "And when the sun has risen?"
    new "And when the sun has risen?\n等太阳完全升起之后呢？"

    old "By that time, we'll be out of the sunlight and into the woods. No risk of being blinded there."
    new "By that time, we'll be out of the sunlight and into the woods. No risk of being blinded there.\n到那时，我们就已经离开阳光，进入树林了。在那里没有晃眼的危险。"

    old "But we'll be stuck in the woods until nightfall, if we can't cross these plains by daylight."
    new "But we'll be stuck in the woods until nightfall, if we can't cross these plains by daylight.\n但如果我们没法在天黑前穿过这些平原，就会被困在树林里直到入夜。"

    old "Yes. I hope that's not a problem for you."
    new "Yes. I hope that's not a problem for you.\n是的。希望那对你来说不是问题。"

    old "It isn't now. But I'm not sure what we'll encounter in the woods."
    new "It isn't now. But I'm not sure what we'll encounter in the woods.\n现在不是。但我不确定我们会在树林里遇到什么。"

    old "Only one way to find out. You know—watch out!"
    new "Only one way to find out. You know—watch out!\n只有一种方法能知道。你知道的——当心！"

    old "Ah, the plains of N'Mar. The more they surprise us, the more they feel the same."
    new "Ah, the plains of N'Mar. The more they surprise us, the more they feel the same.\n啊，N'Mar的平原。它们越是让我们吃惊，越让我们觉得彼此相似。"

    old "I guess I should know better than to feel surprised at the sight of zombies wandering the fields of N'Mar."
    new "I guess I should know better than to feel surprised at the sight of zombies wandering the fields of N'Mar.\n我想我不该看到僵尸在N'Mar的田野上游荡就感到惊讶的。"

    old "There's the woods. Let's not waste any more time out here."
    new "There's the woods. Let's not waste any more time out here.\n那边就是树林了。我们别再在这里浪费时间了。"

    old "These woods are covered in mist, just like the plains."
    new "These woods are covered in mist, just like the plains.\n这些树林和那些平原一样，被雾气笼罩着。"

    old "Indeed they are. Did you expect any different?"
    new "Indeed they are. Did you expect any different?\n确实如此。你还指望会有什么不同吗？"

    old "I guess not. These mists cover all of N'Mar, and it makes sense that they would cover the woods as well as the plains. But knowing something and seeing it in front of your eyes are two different things."
    new "I guess not. These mists cover all of N'Mar, and it makes sense that they would cover the woods as well as the plains. But knowing something and seeing it in front of your eyes are two different things.\n我想不会。这些雾气覆盖着整个N'Mar，它们既覆盖平原，也覆盖树林，这合情合理。但知道一件事，和亲眼看到它，是两回事。"

    old "We can't see very far in these woods, but I can see the river from here."
    new "We can't see very far in these woods, but I can see the river from here.\n在这片树林里我们看不了多远，不过从这里我能看见那条河。"

    old "And if I'm not mistaken, the river is the only landmark we need. The rumors you heard placed the jewelwort in a lake at the end of this river, is that right?"
    new "And if I'm not mistaken, the river is the only landmark we need. The rumors you heard placed the jewelwort in a lake at the end of this river, is that right?\n而如果我没弄错的话，那条河是我们唯一需要的地标。你听到的传言说，Jewelwort就在这条河尽头的湖里，对吧？"

    old "Then let's follow the river."
    new "Then let's follow the river.\n那我们就沿着河走吧。"

    old "Vaeril and I trudge through the forest, following the path carved out by the winding river. Vaeril leads the way, staying close enough to keep the rushing water in sight, but never venturing too close to the river's bank."
    new "Vaeril and I trudge through the forest, following the path carved out by the winding river. Vaeril leads the way, staying close enough to keep the rushing water in sight, but never venturing too close to the river's bank.\n我和Vaeril穿行在森林里，沿着蜿蜒的河流行出的小路前进。Vaeril在前领路，始终保持着让湍急的河水在视线之内的距离，却从不冒险靠河岸太近。"

    old "Scared of water, Vaeril?"
    new "Scared of water, Vaeril?\n怕水吗，Vaeril？"

    old "Scared of water? No. But I do fear what might be lurking under its surface."
    new "Scared of water? No. But I do fear what might be lurking under its surface.\n怕水？不。但我确实害怕水面之下可能潜藏着的东西。"

    old "I'm glad you're willing to admit fear. Fear is something that some people seem to be ashamed to admit, but I've found that a healthy fear of death is one of the most precious assets an adventurer can have."
    new "I'm glad you're willing to admit fear. Fear is something that some people seem to be ashamed to admit, but I've found that a healthy fear of death is one of the most precious assets an adventurer can have.\n我很高兴你愿意承认恐惧。恐惧是有些人羞于承认的东西，但我发现，对死亡怀有健康的畏惧，是冒险者能拥有的最宝贵的财富之一。"

    old "Don't get too paranoid, Vaeril. This is a cruel world, but if you see specters everywhere you look, you lose the ability to distinguish real danger from imagined. After all, these woods surely hold more dangers beyond the aquatic."
    new "Don't get too paranoid, Vaeril. This is a cruel world, but if you see specters everywhere you look, you lose the ability to distinguish real danger from imagined. After all, these woods surely hold more dangers beyond the aquatic.\n别太疑神疑鬼，Vaeril。这是个残酷的世界，但如果你在每个角落都看到幽灵，就会失去分辨真实危险与想象的能力。毕竟，这些树林里肯定还潜藏着比水中更大的危险。"

    old "Perhaps you are right, [protag]. Being a man of the forest, the 'elf from the glade,' as you once called me, I tend to feel safest around trees, yet I have no idea what terrors might lurk within these blighted woods."
    new "Perhaps you are right, [protag]. Being a man of the forest, the 'elf from the glade,' as you once called me, I tend to feel safest around trees, yet I have no idea what terrors might lurk within these blighted woods.\n也许你是对的，[protag]。身为森林之人，你曾称呼我为“来自林间空地的elf”，我总觉得自己在树旁最安心，然而我却不知道，这片枯萎的树林里可能潜伏着怎样的恐怖。"

    old "Meanwhile, the rapid rush of the river tends to put me in a state of unease even when it doesn't threaten my safety. I'll endeavor to be more mindful of my surroundings, even those which offer a deceptive familiarity."
    new "Meanwhile, the rapid rush of the river tends to put me in a state of unease even when it doesn't threaten my safety. I'll endeavor to be more mindful of my surroundings, even those which offer a deceptive familiarity.\n与此同时，河流湍急的奔涌声，即便并不威胁到我的安全，也往往让我心神不宁。我会努力更留意周围的环境，哪怕是那些带着欺骗性熟悉感的环境。"

    old "We tread through the wood, favoring areas where the trees are thin enough to let the sun through. The light is enough to see by, but not so bright as to blind us when scattered by the fog. As we scan the woods while pushing forward, I find the feeling almost familiar."
    new "We tread through the wood, favoring areas where the trees are thin enough to let the sun through. The light is enough to see by, but not so bright as to blind us when scattered by the fog. As we scan the woods while pushing forward, I find the feeling almost familiar.\n我们穿过树林，偏向那些树冠稀疏、能让阳光透进来的地方。光线足够看清道路，却又不至于被雾气打散时晃得我们眼花。我们一边前行一边扫视树林，我竟觉得这种感觉近乎熟悉。"

    old "This feels just like treading the plains of N'Mar by moonlight."
    new "This feels just like treading the plains of N'Mar by moonlight.\n这感觉就像在月光下穿行N'Mar的平原。"

    old "I was thinking the same thing."
    new "I was thinking the same thing.\n我也正这么想。"

    old "And yet we haven't seen any undead."
    new "And yet we haven't seen any undead.\n可我们还没见到任何亡灵。"

    old "Well, it is the middle of the day. The daylight, scant though it may be, is still daylight."
    new "Well, it is the middle of the day. The daylight, scant though it may be, is still daylight.\n嗯，现在是正午。白昼的光，虽然稀薄，但终究是白昼的光。"

    old "Good point."
    new "Good point.\n说得有理。"

    old "Vaeril and I continue following the river deep into the heart of the woods. The air grows thicker with the fetid odor of rotting corpses, but no threats emerge to challenge us."
    new "Vaeril and I continue following the river deep into the heart of the woods. The air grows thicker with the fetid odor of rotting corpses, but no threats emerge to challenge us.\n我和Vaeril继续沿着河流深入树林腹地。空气里腐尸的恶臭愈发浓重，但没有出现任何威胁来挑战我们。"

    old "We find the end of the river, which empties into a large lake."
    new "We find the end of the river, which empties into a large lake.\n我们找到了河的尽头，它汇入一个大湖。"

    old "Here we are. Do you know how to find this jewelwort?"
    new "Here we are. Do you know how to find this jewelwort?\n我们到了。你知道怎么找到这种Jewelwort吗？"

    old "Jewelwort reacts under light. The sunlight here is scant, but hopefully it should be enough to reveal the herb. Look for a glowing moss."
    new "Jewelwort reacts under light. The sunlight here is scant, but hopefully it should be enough to reveal the herb. Look for a glowing moss.\nJewelwort在光线下会有反应。这里的阳光很稀薄，但希望它足以让这草药显现出来。去找发光的苔藓。"

    old "We circle the lake until we arrive on the other side of the river, opposite where we started, but no glowing plants reveal themselves."
    new "We circle the lake until we arrive on the other side of the river, opposite where we started, but no glowing plants reveal themselves.\n我们绕着湖走，一直走到河的另一边，也就是我们出发地点的对岸，却没有任何发光的植物现身。"

    old "There's plenty of sunlight at the lake's center, but toward the edges, there's still enough tree coverage to make things dark. Do you think we need our own light?"
    new "There's plenty of sunlight at the lake's center, but toward the edges, there's still enough tree coverage to make things dark. Do you think we need our own light?\n湖中央阳光充足，但靠近岸边的地方，树冠的遮蔽仍然足以让光线变暗。你觉得我们需要自己打个光吗？"

    old "I suppose it can't hurt to try."
    new "I suppose it can't hurt to try.\n我想试试也无妨。"

    old "Vaeril takes out a torch and some flint, and ignites the torch without much effort."
    new "Vaeril takes out a torch and some flint, and ignites the torch without much effort.\nVaeril取出一支火把和一些火石，没费什么劲就点燃了火把。"

    old "Vaeril waves the torch out over the water's edge, and I see movement beneath the surface."
    new "Vaeril waves the torch out over the water's edge, and I see movement beneath the surface.\nVaeril把火把挥向水面上方，我看见水面下有什么在动。"

    old "Looks like you spooked the fish."
    new "Looks like you spooked the fish.\n看来你把鱼吓着了。"

    old "If this light is bright enough to frighten fish, then it must be bright enough to reveal any jewelwort that we might find here."
    new "If this light is bright enough to frighten fish, then it must be bright enough to reveal any jewelwort that we might find here.\n如果这光亮到能吓到鱼，那它一定也亮到能照出我们可能在这里找到的任何Jewelwort。"

    old "Vaeril and I begin retracing our steps around the water's edge, circling back around. We're on the side of the lake opposite the river when I hear a low groan."
    new "Vaeril and I begin retracing our steps around the water's edge, circling back around. We're on the side of the lake opposite the river when I hear a low groan.\n我和Vaeril开始沿着水边往回走，绕了回去。我们走到与河流相对的那一侧湖边时，我听见一声低沉的呻吟。"

    old "Did you hear that?"
    new "Did you hear that?\n你听见了吗？"

    old "Yes. It sounds like the ground is shifting."
    new "Yes. It sounds like the ground is shifting.\n听见了。听起来像是地面在移动。"

    old "Where is it coming from?"
    new "Where is it coming from?\n声音是从哪里传来的？"

    old "I see Vaeril's pointed ears twitch about, testing the air, before focusing on a tree behind us."
    new "I see Vaeril's pointed ears twitch about, testing the air, before focusing on a tree behind us.\n我看见Vaeril尖尖的耳朵动了动，像是在探测空气，然后锁定在我们身后的一棵树上。"

    old "It seems to be coming from...this tree."
    new "It seems to be coming from...this tree.\n似乎是来自……这棵树。"

    old "Vaeril raises his torch to illuminate the tree. A moss-like coating on the tree's upper trunk begins sparkling."
    new "Vaeril raises his torch to illuminate the tree. A moss-like coating on the tree's upper trunk begins sparkling.\nVaeril举起火把照亮那棵树。树干上部一层苔藓状的覆盖物开始闪闪发光。"

    old "[protag], do you see that?"
    new "[protag], do you see that?\n[protag]，你看见了吗？"

    old "Yes, I see it. I think I can reach it if I stand on the lower branch. Keep that torch steady."
    new "Yes, I see it. I think I can reach it if I stand on the lower branch. Keep that torch steady.\n看见了，我看见了。我想如果我站到下面那根树枝上，应该能够到它。把火把举稳。"

    old "I leap up and grab hold of the lowest branch. I steady myself and begin lifting myself up, but the branch begins shaking. I lose my grip and fall on my back."
    new "I leap up and grab hold of the lowest branch. I steady myself and begin lifting myself up, but the branch begins shaking. I lose my grip and fall on my back.\n我纵身跃起，抓住最低的那根树枝。我稳住身子，开始往上攀，但树枝开始晃动。我失去了抓握，仰面摔了下来。"

    old "[protag], are you alright?"
    new "[protag], are you alright?\n[protag]，你没事吧？"

    old "I'm fine, I just lost my grip. I guess that branch isn't as strong as I thought it was. I can probably make it to the next branch up if I shimmy my way up the trunk."
    new "I'm fine, I just lost my grip. I guess that branch isn't as strong as I thought it was. I can probably make it to the next branch up if I shimmy my way up the trunk.\n我没事，只是手滑了。我想那根树枝没我想的那么结实。如果我能顺着树干往上蹭，大概能爬到上面那根树枝。"

    old "I wrap my arms around the base of the tree, and hoist my feet off the ground. Then I wrap my legs around, dig my heels into the bark, and use that to anchor myself as I inch up. I repeat this several times before the wood begins vibrating. I lose my footing and fall to the ground, thankfully landing on my feet this time."
    new "I wrap my arms around the base of the tree, and hoist my feet off the ground. Then I wrap my legs around, dig my heels into the bark, and use that to anchor myself as I inch up. I repeat this several times before the wood begins vibrating. I lose my footing and fall to the ground, thankfully landing on my feet this time.\n我双臂环住树干底部，把双脚抬离地面。然后我双腿盘绕上去，脚跟蹬进树皮，借力一点一点往上爬。我重复了几次，木头却开始震动起来。我脚下一滑，摔到了地上，好在这次双脚先着地。"

    old "It's odd. The tree's trunk just started shaking."
    new "It's odd. The tree's trunk just started shaking.\n真奇怪。树干刚刚突然开始晃动。"

    old "I don't think it was bending under my weight. This trunk looks too sturdy for someone like me to bring it down. Could it be the ground? Did you feel a tremor?"
    new "I don't think it was bending under my weight. This trunk looks too sturdy for someone like me to bring it down. Could it be the ground? Did you feel a tremor?\n我不觉得它是在我的体重下弯曲。这树干看着太结实了，凭我这样的人根本压不弯它。会不会是地面？你感觉到震颤了吗？"

    old "I felt no tremor. If the tree is shaking you off...I wonder."
    new "I felt no tremor. If the tree is shaking you off...I wonder.\n我没感觉到任何震颤。如果这棵树是在把你甩下来……我有点好奇了。"

    old "Wonder what?"
    new "Wonder what?\n好奇什么？"

    old "I wonder if the tree might be shaking deliberately."
    new "I wonder if the tree might be shaking deliberately.\n我好奇这棵树会不会是故意在摇晃。"

    old "What do you mean? There's someone hiding in the tree and shaking it?"
    new "What do you mean? There's someone hiding in the tree and shaking it?\n你是什么意思？有人躲在树上摇晃它？"

    old "I mean the tree itself. I've never had occasion to observe them myself, but being a druid, I've heard rumors of druids who use magic to animate trees. I wonder if this tree might actively be repelling your advances."
    new "I mean the tree itself. I've never had occasion to observe them myself, but being a druid, I've heard rumors of druids who use magic to animate trees. I wonder if this tree might actively be repelling your advances.\n我指的是树本身。我从未有机会亲眼观察过这类事，但身为德鲁伊，我听过一些传言，说有些德鲁伊能用魔法让树木活动起来。我在想，这棵树会不会是在主动抵抗你的接近。"

    old "Can you...un-animate it?"
    new "Can you...un-animate it?\n你能……让它别动吗？"

    old "Animating a tree is something that's squarely outside my area of expertise. Reversing that process is something I'm just as incapable of. But...I think I may be able to discern what it may be trying to protect itself from."
    new "Animating a tree is something that's squarely outside my area of expertise. Reversing that process is something I'm just as incapable of. But...I think I may be able to discern what it may be trying to protect itself from.\n让一棵树活动起来，这完全超出了我的专长范围。而要逆转这个过程，我同样无能为力。但是……我想我也许能辨别出，它试图保护自己免受什么威胁。"

    old "Druids have a unique empathy for trees. In most cases, this simply means that druids can feel the pain or health of a tree. But if I concentrate, I think I may be able to communicate with it."
    new "Druids have a unique empathy for trees. In most cases, this simply means that druids can feel the pain or health of a tree. But if I concentrate, I think I may be able to communicate with it.\n德鲁伊对树木有独特的共情能力。在大多数情况下，这只是意味着德鲁伊能感受到一棵树的痛苦或健康状况。但如果我集中精神，我想我也许能与它沟通。"

    old "Let's try, then."
    new "Let's try, then.\n那我们就试试吧。"

    old "Vaeril stands against the tree, leaning back into it as he places both of his hands on the tree's trunk and closes his eyes. He begins muttering some chant I can't quite make out, and enters a trance-like state."
    new "Vaeril stands against the tree, leaning back into it as he places both of his hands on the tree's trunk and closes his eyes. He begins muttering some chant I can't quite make out, and enters a trance-like state.\nVaeril靠在那棵树上，身体向后倚着它，把双手放在树干上，闭上了眼睛。他开始念诵某种我完全听不清的咒语，进入了类似出神的状态。"

    old "Vaeril's lips continue moving in some unfamiliar pattern for several minutes, and I notice a familiar glow emanating from his hands where they touch the tree's bark."
    new "Vaeril's lips continue moving in some unfamiliar pattern for several minutes, and I notice a familiar glow emanating from his hands where they touch the tree's bark.\nVaeril的嘴唇以某种陌生的方式持续翕动了好几分钟，我注意到从他双手触碰树皮的地方，散发出一股熟悉的光芒。"

    old "Suddenly, branches erupt from the base of the trunk and wrap around Vaeril. Before I can react, his chest is completely enveloped in the wood."
    new "Suddenly, branches erupt from the base of the trunk and wrap around Vaeril. Before I can react, his chest is completely enveloped in the wood.\n突然，树枝从树干底部爆裂而出，缠住了Vaeril。我还没来得及反应，他的胸口就整个被木头包裹住了。"

    old "Vaeril! Are you alright?"
    new "Vaeril! Are you alright?\nVaeril！你没事吧？"

    old "Vaeril's eye's snap open, completely white, and he begins speaking in a gravely voice."
    new "Vaeril's eye's snap open, completely white, and he begins speaking in a gravely voice.\nVaeril的眼睛猛地睁开，眼珠一片纯白，他开始用一种沙哑低沉的声音说话。"

    old "Do not venture any further, [prace]."
    new "Do not venture any further, [prace].\n不要再往前走了，[prace]。"

    old "Vaeril? What's wrong?"
    new "Vaeril? What's wrong?\nVaeril？你怎么了？"

    old "My name is Jaya. Is Vaeril the name of the companion you came here with?"
    new "My name is Jaya. Is Vaeril the name of the companion you came here with?\n我叫Jaya。Vaeril是和你一同前来的那个同伴的名字吗？"

    old "Your companion, this 'Vaeril,' attempted to commune with me. However, his mind is a flurry of emotions and disconnected thoughts that I could not comprehend. He chose to lend me the use of his voice so that I might speak directly to you."
    new "Your companion, this 'Vaeril,' attempted to commune with me. However, his mind is a flurry of emotions and disconnected thoughts that I could not comprehend. He chose to lend me the use of his voice so that I might speak directly to you.\n你的同伴，这个叫“Vaeril”的人，试图与我沟通。然而，他的思绪是一片混乱的情感与破碎的念头，我无法理解。于是他选择把他的声音借给我，好让我能直接对你说话。"

    old "I am the oldest tree in this wood. Protecting this wood was my duty. Alas, the woods have fallen into decay, and I have withered along with them."
    new "I am the oldest tree in this wood. Protecting this wood was my duty. Alas, the woods have fallen into decay, and I have withered along with them.\n我是这片树林里最古老的树。守护这片树林曾是我的职责。唉，树林已陷入腐朽，我也随之枯萎了。"

    old "Who are you? What are you?"
    new "Who are you? What are you?\n你是谁？你是什么？"

    old "My name is Jaya. I am the elder tree that watches over these woods."
    new "My name is Jaya. I am the elder tree that watches over these woods.\n我叫Jaya。我是守护着这片树林的长老之树。"

    old "Your companion attempted to commune with me. However, his mind is a flurry of emotions and disconnected thoughts that I could not comprehend. He chose to lend me the use of his voice so that I might speak directly to you."
    new "Your companion attempted to commune with me. However, his mind is a flurry of emotions and disconnected thoughts that I could not comprehend. He chose to lend me the use of his voice so that I might speak directly to you.\n你的同伴试图与我沟通。然而，他的思绪是一片混乱的情感与破碎的念头，我无法理解。于是他选择把他的声音借给我，好让我能直接对你说话。"

    old "Protecting this wood was my duty. Alas, the woods have fallen into decay, and I have withered along with them."
    new "Protecting this wood was my duty. Alas, the woods have fallen into decay, and I have withered along with them.\n守护这片树林曾是我的职责。唉，树林已陷入腐朽，我也随之枯萎了。"

    old "When did this wood begin decaying?"
    new "When did this wood begin decaying?\n这片树林是从什么时候开始腐朽的？"

    old "I cannot tell you exactly when it began. We trees do not see time the same as those such as yourself, [prace]. All I know is that I felt the corruption creep onto this forest when an eerie mist began creeping through it. Those mists brought the stench of decay and rot with them, and every day, the vim that flows through the trees of this forest weakens."
    new "I cannot tell you exactly when it began. We trees do not see time the same as those such as yourself, [prace]. All I know is that I felt the corruption creep onto this forest when an eerie mist began creeping through it. Those mists brought the stench of decay and rot with them, and every day, the vim that flows through the trees of this forest weakens.\n我无法确切告诉你它是何时开始的。我们树木看待时间的方式，与你们这样的生灵不同，[prace]。我所知道的只是，当一股诡异的雾气开始在林间蔓延时，我感觉到腐化悄悄爬上了这片森林。那些雾气带来了腐烂与朽坏的气味，而每一天，流经这片森林树木的活力都在减弱。"

    old "The mist you see is my enemy as well. I am part of a group that is fighting the corruption that is spreading through N'Mar. Many people have been killed in the plains surrounding it as well."
    new "The mist you see is my enemy as well. I am part of a group that is fighting the corruption that is spreading through N'Mar. Many people have been killed in the plains surrounding it as well.\n你所见的雾气，也是我的敌人。我属于一个正在对抗N'Mar蔓延腐化的团体。它周围的平原上，也已有许多人丧命。"

    old "The name 'N'Mar' means nothing to me, and I care not of the woes of your people."
    new "The name 'N'Mar' means nothing to me, and I care not of the woes of your people.\n“N'Mar”这个名字对我毫无意义，我也不关心你族人的苦难。"

    old "The corruption of the plains and the corruption of these woods come from the same source. We are fighting the same enemy."
    new "The corruption of the plains and the corruption of these woods come from the same source. We are fighting the same enemy.\n平原的腐化和这些树林的腐化，出自同一个源头。我们对抗的是同一个敌人。"

    old "Where does this corruption stem from?"
    new "Where does this corruption stem from?\n这种腐化源自何处？"

    old "We do not know, precisely. But we do know that whatever the source of this evil is, it lurks within the castle of N'Mar."
    new "We do not know, precisely. But we do know that whatever the source of this evil is, it lurks within the castle of N'Mar.\n我们并不确切知道。但我们知道，无论这邪恶的源头是什么，它都潜伏在N'Mar的城堡里。"

    old "Castle? This is a word devoid of meaning to me."
    new "Castle? This is a word devoid of meaning to me.\n城堡？这个词对我毫无意义。"

    old "It is a large, man-made structure. It is a fortress, a barrier that protects whatever is spreading the corruption through these lands. We want to terminate that corruption at its source. If we succeed in our mission, your woods will be free of that blight as well."
    new "It is a large, man-made structure. It is a fortress, a barrier that protects whatever is spreading the corruption through these lands. We want to terminate that corruption at its source. If we succeed in our mission, your woods will be free of that blight as well.\n那是一座巨大的人造建筑。那是一座要塞，是一道屏障，保护着那个让腐化遍布这些土地的源头。我们想从根源上终结这种腐化。如果我们任务成功，你的树林也将摆脱那场灾难。"

    old "Very well, [prace]. It would appear that we are not enemies. We may in fact share a common enemy. What brought you to these woods?"
    new "Very well, [prace]. It would appear that we are not enemies. We may in fact share a common enemy. What brought you to these woods?\n很好，[prace]。看来我们并非敌人。事实上，我们或许有共同的敌人。是什么把你们带到这片树林来的？"

    old "We came seeking jewelwort."
    new "We came seeking jewelwort.\n我们是来找Jewelwort的。"

    old "Jewelwort is an herb which stores vim. It has been critical to allowing me to survive as long as I have. What use have you for jewelwort?"
    new "Jewelwort is an herb which stores vim. It has been critical to allowing me to survive as long as I have. What use have you for jewelwort?\nJewelwort是一种储存活力的草药。它对我能活到如今，至关重要。你们要Jewelwort做什么？"

    old "My companion, the one you are speaking through, believes that with jewelwort, he will be able to save the life of an elf child."
    new "My companion, the one you are speaking through, believes that with jewelwort, he will be able to save the life of an elf child.\n我的同伴——也就是你现在借以说话的那一位——相信，有了Jewelwort，他就能挽救一个elf孩子的生命。"

    old "I see. Is the survival of this boy critical to your mission to extinguish the plague that covers these lands?"
    new "I see. Is the survival of this boy critical to your mission to extinguish the plague that covers these lands?\n我明白了。这个男孩的存活，对你们消灭这片土地上瘟疫的使命，至关重要吗？"

    old "Yes, it is."
    new "Yes, it is.\n是的，至关重要。"

    old "A white lie. I've told them before, and now doesn't seem like a good time to stop."
    new "A white lie. I've told them before, and now doesn't seem like a good time to stop.\n一个善意的谎言。我以前也撒过，而现在似乎不是该停手的时候。"

    old "My companion is a healer. We need his powers to defeat the undead. And he needs that jewelwort to use his powers."
    new "My companion is a healer. We need his powers to defeat the undead. And he needs that jewelwort to use his powers.\n我的同伴是个治疗师。我们需要他的力量来打败亡灵。而他也需要那株Jewelwort来施展力量。"

    old "I see. If our interests are truly aligned, then I suppose giving you what remains of this jewelwort would help me as well. However..."
    new "I see. If our interests are truly aligned, then I suppose giving you what remains of this jewelwort would help me as well. However...\n我明白了。如果我们利益确实一致，那么我想，把剩下的Jewelwort交给你们，对我也有好处。然而……"

    old "I cannot live long without it. Recently, the undead have begun crawling through these woods. The power I draw from this jewelwort is all that allows me to repel them."
    new "I cannot live long without it. Recently, the undead have begun crawling through these woods. The power I draw from this jewelwort is all that allows me to repel them.\n没有它，我活不了多久。最近，亡灵开始在这片树林里爬行。我从这株Jewelwort中汲取的力量，是我击退它们的全部依仗。"

    old "Without the jewelwort, I—and the rest of these woods—could be dead within several cycles of the sun."
    new "Without the jewelwort, I—and the rest of these woods—could be dead within several cycles of the sun.\n没有Jewelwort，我——以及这片树林的其余部分——可能在太阳几个轮回之内就会死去。"

    old "I'm sorry. I understand your need of the jewelwort, but my need of it is far more immediate. Even if I lend it to you, your mission may fail. And in either case, my responsibility first and foremost is the protection of these woods."
    new "I'm sorry. I understand your need of the jewelwort, but my need of it is far more immediate. Even if I lend it to you, your mission may fail. And in either case, my responsibility first and foremost is the protection of these woods.\n抱歉。我理解你对Jewelwort的需要，但我对它的需要紧迫得多。即使我把它借给你，你们的任务也可能失败。而且无论如何，我首要的职责，就是守护这片树林。"

    old "You say that you could live for a period of several days without the jewelwort?"
    new "You say that you could live for a period of several days without the jewelwort?\n你是说，没有Jewelwort，你也能活上几天？"

    old "By 'day,' I mean the cycles of the sun. We call the rising and setting of the sun one day."
    new "By 'day,' I mean the cycles of the sun. We call the rising and setting of the sun one day.\n我说的“天”，指的是太阳的轮回。我们把太阳的一次升起与落下，称作一天。"

    old "That is correct. The corruption that seeps through this soil, and the undead that follow that tainted ground, are slow to move. But their creep is as inevitable as it is slow."
    new "That is correct. The corruption that seeps through this soil, and the undead that follow that tainted ground, are slow to move. But their creep is as inevitable as it is slow.\n没错。渗入这片土壤的腐化，以及追随着那片被污染土地的亡灵，行动都很缓慢。但它们的蔓延，既缓慢，又不可避免。"

    old "No. This jewelwort is not essential to our quest to oust the undead menace of N'Mar."
    new "No. This jewelwort is not essential to our quest to oust the undead menace of N'Mar.\n不。这株Jewelwort并不是我们驱逐N'Mar亡灵威胁所必需的。"

    old "If this herb is unrelated to your quest, then why do you seek it?"
    new "If this herb is unrelated to your quest, then why do you seek it?\n如果这草药与你们的任务无关，那你们为何还要寻找它？"

    old "We seek the herb for the same reason that you protect the other trees of these woods. It is in our nature to help those of our own kind. A boy in the city that we protect is sick. Can we truly call ourselves his protectors if we are not willing to take these steps to save his life?"
    new "We seek the herb for the same reason that you protect the other trees of these woods. It is in our nature to help those of our own kind. A boy in the city that we protect is sick. Can we truly call ourselves his protectors if we are not willing to take these steps to save his life?\n我们寻找这草药，和你守护这片树林里其他树木，是出于同样的原因。帮助自己的同类，是我们的天性。我们所守护的城市里，有个男孩病了。如果我们不愿采取这些行动去救他的命，我们又怎能真正自称是他的守护者？"

    old "Death is inevitable. It comes to us all, at one point or another. A hundred years from now, you and everyone you know will be dead. A thousand years from now, every tree in this forest will have perished. What matters is not whether we live or die, but what we leave behind."
    new "Death is inevitable. It comes to us all, at one point or another. A hundred years from now, you and everyone you know will be dead. A thousand years from now, every tree in this forest will have perished. What matters is not whether we live or die, but what we leave behind.\n死亡不可避免。它或早或晚，终会降临到我们每个人头上。一百年后，你和你认识的每个人都将死去。一千年后，这片森林里的每一棵树都将凋亡。重要的不是我们是生是死，而是我们留下了什么。"

    old "I protect these woods not out of any love for the trees that surround us, or any fear for my own life. But if this curse persists, life as you and I know it will cease to exist on these plains."
    new "I protect these woods not out of any love for the trees that surround us, or any fear for my own life. But if this curse persists, life as you and I know it will cease to exist on these plains.\n我守护这些树林，并非出于对周围树木的喜爱，也并非出于对我自己性命的恐惧。但如果这个诅咒持续下去，你我所知的这种生命，将在这些平原上不复存在。"

    old "You say you don't care about your own life, or the life of your contemporaries. Yet it seems you long to see their lineage continue. Why is that?"
    new "You say you don't care about your own life, or the life of your contemporaries. Yet it seems you long to see their lineage continue. Why is that?\n你说你不在乎自己的性命，也不在乎你同时代者的性命。然而你似乎渴望看到他们的血脉延续下去。这是为什么？"

    old "For anyone, be they man or tree, what matters is their legacy. A life lasts for a short while. A legacy can outlast a single life. A fixture of history will last for the ages."
    new "For anyone, be they man or tree, what matters is their legacy. A life lasts for a short while. A legacy can outlast a single life. A fixture of history will last for the ages.\n对任何人而言，无论是人是树，重要的是他们的遗产。生命只延续短短一瞬。而遗产却能比一条生命更长久。历史的印记将长存于世世代代。"

    old "You talk about a legacy as something that exists in the far-off future. But I tell you this: if you are not remembered ten years after your death, there is no way you will be remembered a hundred years after your death. Your memory is carried on by the young ones who know you while you're still alive."
    new "You talk about a legacy as something that exists in the far-off future. But I tell you this: if you are not remembered ten years after your death, there is no way you will be remembered a hundred years after your death. Your memory is carried on by the young ones who know you while you're still alive.\n你把遗产说成是存在于遥远未来的东西。但我告诉你：如果你死后十年无人记得，那么你死后一百年，也绝不会有人记得。你的记忆，是由那些在你生前就认识你的年轻人传承下去的。"

    old "I am also interested in preserving a legacy. And that boy—the one that my companion and I seek to save—is part of that legacy. It is people like him who will tell tales of our deeds long after we have died. And if I'm going to leave a legacy, I can't imagine one I'd like more than being remembered as one who saved the young and the weak."
    new "I am also interested in preserving a legacy. And that boy—the one that my companion and I seek to save—is part of that legacy. It is people like him who will tell tales of our deeds long after we have died. And if I'm going to leave a legacy, I can't imagine one I'd like more than being remembered as one who saved the young and the weak.\n我也关心能否留下遗产。而那个男孩——我和我的同伴想要拯救的那个男孩——就是那份遗产的一部分。正是像他这样的人，会在我们死后很久，仍讲述我们的功绩。而如果我要留下遗产，我想不出比“被人铭记为拯救幼弱之人”更好的了。"

    old "Perhaps you are right, [prace]. But in spite of your rhetoric, I cannot allow you to take this jewelwort. Without it, the curse will continue to encroach, until it has seeped into the soil that surrounds my roots."
    new "Perhaps you are right, [prace]. But in spite of your rhetoric, I cannot allow you to take this jewelwort. Without it, the curse will continue to encroach, until it has seeped into the soil that surrounds my roots.\n也许你是对的，[prace]。但尽管你言辞恳切，我还是不能允许你拿走这株Jewelwort。没有它，诅咒就会继续侵蚀，直到渗入我根系周围的土壤。"

    old "I can fight the encroaching wastes. I can slow it. Delay it. But without this jewelwort, they will eventually overtake me, and these woods. I'm sorry, but I can't allow you to take it."
    new "I can fight the encroaching wastes. I can slow it. Delay it. But without this jewelwort, they will eventually overtake me, and these woods. I'm sorry, but I can't allow you to take it.\n我可以对抗那些侵蚀而来的荒芜。我可以减缓它。拖延它。但没有这株Jewelwort，它们终将压倒我，以及这片树林。抱歉，但我不能让你拿走它。"

    old "What if you lent the jewelwort to us, long enough for us to complete our mission? We could return it to you when we were finished."
    new "What if you lent the jewelwort to us, long enough for us to complete our mission? We could return it to you when we were finished.\n如果你把Jewelwort借给我们，借到我们足以完成任务呢？我们完成后可以把它还给你。"

    old "I do not understand. Jewelwort is an herb. Would your mission not consume it?"
    new "I do not understand. Jewelwort is an herb. Would your mission not consume it?\n我不明白。Jewelwort是草药。你们的任务难道不会把它消耗掉吗？"

    old "My companion has the ability to channel his healing abilities through living plants, perhaps in the same way that you do. I do not fully understand it. What I do know is that he has the capability to use it, and still have it intact afterward."
    new "My companion has the ability to channel his healing abilities through living plants, perhaps in the same way that you do. I do not fully understand it. What I do know is that he has the capability to use it, and still have it intact afterward.\n我的同伴有能力通过活生生的植物传导他的治疗能力，也许和你一样。我并不完全理解这一点。我所知道的是，他有能力使用它，而且用完之后它仍然完好无损。"

    old "Interesting. Although I cannot directly communicate with your companion, I do sense good intentions from him, and it would seem that what you say is true. It would seem that you are a trustworthy party."
    new "Interesting. Although I cannot directly communicate with your companion, I do sense good intentions from him, and it would seem that what you say is true. It would seem that you are a trustworthy party.\n有趣。虽然我无法与你的同伴直接沟通，但我确实从他身上感受到了善意，看来你所说的是真的。看来你们是值得信赖的一方。"

    old "Very well. You may borrow what remains of my jewelwort. Please return it when you are done. I can survive several cycles of the sun without it, but any longer than that and you place the life of these woods in jeopardy. I trust you will not take that responsibility lightly."
    new "Very well. You may borrow what remains of my jewelwort. Please return it when you are done. I can survive several cycles of the sun without it, but any longer than that and you place the life of these woods in jeopardy. I trust you will not take that responsibility lightly.\n很好。你们可以借走我剩下的Jewelwort。完成后请务必归还。没有它，我能熬过太阳的几个轮回，但再久一些，你们就会危及这片树林的生命。我相信你们不会轻率地承担这一责任。"

    old "Of course. Thank you, Jaya."
    new "Of course. Thank you, Jaya.\n当然。谢谢你，Jaya。"

    old "The branches that bind Vaeril's body retract and sink back into the bark of the tree, and the glow fades from his eyes as he stumbles forward."
    new "The branches that bind Vaeril's body retract and sink back into the bark of the tree, and the glow fades from his eyes as he stumbles forward.\n缠住Vaeril身体的树枝缩了回去，重新沉入树皮中，他踉跄着向前一步，眼中的光芒也随之褪去。"

    old "Vaeril, are you alright? Are you...you?"
    new "Vaeril, are you alright? Are you...you?\nVaeril，你没事吧？你还是……你自己吗？"

    old "Vaeril pats his own chest."
    new "Vaeril pats his own chest.\nVaeril拍了拍自己的胸口。"

    old "It's all me in here, don't worry."
    new "It's all me in here, don't worry.\n这里完全是我自己，别担心。"

    old "One of the trees upper branches bends downward, slanting toward the ground until it's level with my eyes. A sparkling herb rests at the edge of the branch."
    new "One of the trees upper branches bends downward, slanting toward the ground until it's level with my eyes. A sparkling herb rests at the edge of the branch.\n那棵树上方的一根树枝向下弯折，斜斜垂向地面，直到与我视线齐平。一株闪闪发光的草药静静躺在树枝边缘。"

    old "It seems we've managed to find what we came for."
    new "It seems we've managed to find what we came for.\n看来我们找到了此行要找的东西。"

    old "It's ours to borrow, not to keep. But that should be all that you need to restore that elf boy's help."
    new "It's ours to borrow, not to keep. But that should be all that you need to restore that elf boy's help.\n它是借给我们的，不是给我们的。不过，那应该足够你用来恢复那个elf男孩的健康了。"

    old "In that case, we'll have to endeavor to be good stewards of this gift we've been given, temporary though it may be."
    new "In that case, we'll have to endeavor to be good stewards of this gift we've been given, temporary though it may be.\n那样的话，我们就得努力当好这份礼物的好管家，尽管它可能只是暂时的。"

    old "Vaeril and I retrace our steps through the forest. The sun is low in the sky by the time we reach its edge, and we cross the plains of N'Mar back to Grimoire under the twilit sky."
    new "Vaeril and I retrace our steps through the forest. The sun is low in the sky by the time we reach its edge, and we cross the plains of N'Mar back to Grimoire under the twilit sky.\n我和Vaeril沿着原路穿过森林。等我们走到树林边缘时，太阳已经低垂，我们穿过N'Mar的平原，在暮色笼罩的天空下回到了Grimoire。"

    old "I meet Vaeril back in the infirmary at the edge of Grimoire."
    new "I meet Vaeril back in the infirmary at the edge of Grimoire.\n我在Grimoire边缘的那间医务室里与Vaeril会合。"

    old "[protag]. How fortuitous for you to arrive just now. Your arrival could not be more timely."
    new "[protag]. How fortuitous for you to arrive just now. Your arrival could not be more timely.\n[protag]。你此刻到来，真是凑巧。你来得再及时不过了。"

    old "What do you mean, Vaeril?"
    new "What do you mean, Vaeril?\n你是什么意思，Vaeril？"

    old "I was about to heal the boy. Or make my best attempt at it, at least."
    new "I was about to heal the boy. Or make my best attempt at it, at least.\n我正要给那男孩治疗。或者至少，尽我最大的努力一试。"

    old "You mean you haven't healed him yet?"
    new "You mean you haven't healed him yet?\n你是说，你还没治好他？"

    old "No. You see, jewelwort is similar to other herbs that I use in my healing, but it is more difficult to channel through. But with practice, I think I have the ability to use it effectively, without damaging the herb—or the boy."
    new "No. You see, jewelwort is similar to other herbs that I use in my healing, but it is more difficult to channel through. But with practice, I think I have the ability to use it effectively, without damaging the herb—or the boy.\n没有。你瞧，Jewelwort和我治疗时用的其他草药类似，但它更难传导。不过通过练习，我想我有能力有效地使用它，既不损伤草药——也不伤到男孩。"

    old "Is there a big ceremony you have planned? Some healing ritual?"
    new "Is there a big ceremony you have planned? Some healing ritual?\n你安排了什么盛大的仪式吗？某种治疗仪式？"

    old "No, nothing so grandiose as that. Healing him here is no different from healing someone in battle. I'm even using one of the same staves that I use in combat."
    new "No, nothing so grandiose as that. Healing him here is no different from healing someone in battle. I'm even using one of the same staves that I use in combat.\n不，没什么那么隆重。在这里给他治疗，和在战斗中治疗某个人没什么区别。我用的甚至还是我在战斗中使用的那几根手杖之一。"

    old "Well, if you're going to heal him, I don't mean to hold you up. Let's end this boy's suffering."
    new "Well, if you're going to heal him, I don't mean to hold you up. Let's end this boy's suffering.\n嗯，如果你要给他治疗，我可不想耽搁你。让我们结束这个男孩的痛苦吧。"

    old "Vaeril nods and turns to the bed beside us. He holds one hand over the boy's chest while the other grips the staff, and a pulsing energy erupts from his hands. The energy disspates as it touches the boy, and Vaeril collapses to the floor."
    new "Vaeril nods and turns to the bed beside us. He holds one hand over the boy's chest while the other grips the staff, and a pulsing energy erupts from his hands. The energy disspates as it touches the boy, and Vaeril collapses to the floor.\nVaeril点点头，转向我们旁边的床。他一只手悬在男孩胸口上方，另一只手紧握着手杖，一股脉动的能量从他手中迸发出来。能量一碰到男孩便消散开去，Vaeril瘫倒在地上。"

    old "Vaeril, are you alright?"
    new "Vaeril, are you alright?\nVaeril，你没事吧？"

    old "I just overextended myself a bit. I'm fine. The question is, is he?"
    new "I just overextended myself a bit. I'm fine. The question is, is he?\n我只是有点用力过猛。我没事。问题是，他怎么样？"

    old "Vaeril leans in speaks softly into the boy's ear."
    new "Vaeril leans in speaks softly into the boy's ear.\nVaeril俯下身，凑到男孩耳边轻声说话。"

    old "Anton, can you hear me?"
    new "Anton, can you hear me?\nAnton，你能听见我吗？"

    old "Suddenly, the boy begins coughing and sputtering, and a thick black liquid comes out of his mouth. Vaeril quickly tilts the boy's head to the side, allowing the fluid to flow from the boy's mouth and nose onto the floor."
    new "Suddenly, the boy begins coughing and sputtering, and a thick black liquid comes out of his mouth. Vaeril quickly tilts the boy's head to the side, allowing the fluid to flow from the boy's mouth and nose onto the floor.\n突然，男孩开始咳嗽、喷溅，一股浓稠的黑色液体从他嘴里涌出。Vaeril迅速把男孩的头侧向一边，让液体从男孩的嘴和鼻子里流到地上。"

    old "If you're worrying if it's some diseased foulness or plague, it's nothing of the sort. It's simply all of the dust that has accumulated in this boy's lungs over so many months. He should be able to breathe properly now."
    new "If you're worrying if it's some diseased foulness or plague, it's nothing of the sort. It's simply all of the dust that has accumulated in this boy's lungs over so many months. He should be able to breathe properly now.\n如果你是在担心那是什么疾病、秽物或瘟疫，根本不是那么回事。那不过是这个男孩肺里积攒了这么多个月的灰尘。现在他应该能正常呼吸了。"

    old "The boy blinks and nods, and wipes a trail of dribbling fluid from the corner of his mouth. Vaeril picks up a cloth and hands it to him."
    new "The boy blinks and nods, and wipes a trail of dribbling fluid from the corner of his mouth. Vaeril picks up a cloth and hands it to him.\n男孩眨了眨眼，点点头，从嘴角擦去一道流下的口水。Vaeril 拿起一块布递给他。"

    old "Blow your nose into this."
    new "Blow your nose into this.\n把鼻子擤进这块布里。"

    old "The boy blows into the cloth, and Vaeril takes it back. As he crumbles it into a wad, I notice that the cloth is now almost completely black."
    new "The boy blows into the cloth, and Vaeril takes it back. As he crumbles it into a wad, I notice that the cloth is now almost completely black.\n男孩往布里擤了擤，Vaeril 把布拿了回去。就在他把布揉成一团时，我注意到那块布现在几乎完全变黑了。"

    old "Anton, listen to me carefully. I want you to pick up a cloth from that table and blow your nose into it once before you go to bed, and once again when you wake up in the morning. You'll do this every day until I tell you otherwise. Do you understand?"
    new "Anton, listen to me carefully. I want you to pick up a cloth from that table and blow your nose into it once before you go to bed, and once again when you wake up in the morning. You'll do this every day until I tell you otherwise. Do you understand?\nAnton，仔细听我说。我要你从那张桌子上拿一块布，睡觉前把鼻子擤进去一次，早上醒来再擤一次。你要每天这样做，直到我让你停下为止。明白吗？"

    old "The boy nods, then looks up at me and cocks his head."
    new "The boy nods, then looks up at me and cocks his head.\n男孩点点头，然后抬头看着我，歪了歪脑袋。"

    old "Who is [heshe]?"
    new "Who is [heshe]?\n[heshe]是谁？"

    old "This is [protag]. [HeShe]'s the one who helped me find the thing that cured you."
    new "This is [protag]. [HeShe]'s the one who helped me find the thing that cured you.\n这是[protag]。[HeShe]就是帮我找到治好你的东西的人。"

    old "I don't feel cured. I feel sick. My head hurts."
    new "I don't feel cured. I feel sick. My head hurts.\n我没觉得自己好了。我还是难受，头很疼。"

    old "But you're talking now. Does your chest hurt when you talk?"
    new "But you're talking now. Does your chest hurt when you talk?\n但你现在能说话了。你说话的时候胸口疼吗？"

    old "No, but my head still hurts."
    new "No, but my head still hurts.\n不疼，但我的头还是疼。"

    old "Everything in time, child. Everything in time."
    new "Everything in time, child. Everything in time.\n都要慢慢来，孩子。都要慢慢来。"

    old "Now what?"
    new "Now what?\n现在怎么办？"

    old "The boy's path to recovery will not be a rapid or an easy one. But I think we've past the worst of it."
    new "The boy's path to recovery will not be a rapid or an easy one. But I think we've past the worst of it.\n这孩子的康复之路不会快，也不会轻松。但我想最糟的阶段已经过去了。"

    old "Vaeril, can we step outside for a moment? I'd like to speak to you privately."
    new "Vaeril, can we step outside for a moment? I'd like to speak to you privately.\nVaeril，我们能出去一下吗？我想私下跟你谈谈。"

    old "I don't imagine that the outdoors will offer us any privacy. This setting seems as close and intimate as any. Even if the patients do overhear us, what harm can they do. You wouldn't tell anyone what you heard here, right Anton?"
    new "I don't imagine that the outdoors will offer us any privacy. This setting seems as close and intimate as any. Even if the patients do overhear us, what harm can they do. You wouldn't tell anyone what you heard here, right Anton?\n我不觉得去外面就能有多少隐私。这里的环境跟别处一样私密亲密。就算被病人听到了，他们又能怎样。你不会把在这里听到的说出去吧，对吧，Anton？"

    old "The boy perked up at hearing his own name."
    new "The boy perked up at hearing his own name.\n听到自己的名字，男孩一下子打起了精神。"

    old "See? He wasn't even listening until I said his name."
    new "See? He wasn't even listening until I said his name.\n看到了吧？在我叫出他的名字之前，他压根没在听。"

    old "Fine, we can talk here."
    new "Fine, we can talk here.\n好吧，我们就在这里谈。"

    old "Vaeril escorts me to a table—it's more of a desk, actually—that sits near the door."
    new "Vaeril escorts me to a table—it's more of a desk, actually—that sits near the door.\nVaeril 领我走到一张桌子前——其实更像是一张书桌——就摆在门边。"

    old "So what is it that we need to discuss?"
    new "So what is it that we need to discuss?\n那么，我们需要谈些什么呢？"

    old "I'd like to talk about the jewelwort."
    new "I'd like to talk about the jewelwort.\n我想谈谈 jewelwort 的事。"

    old "It worked just fine. That little collapse I had before, that was entirely my fault. The lack of practice. If I did it again, I wouldn't make the same mistake again."
    new "It worked just fine. That little collapse I had before, that was entirely my fault. The lack of practice. If I did it again, I wouldn't make the same mistake again.\n它的效果很好。我之前那点小失误，完全是我自己的错，是练习不够。如果再让我做一次，我不会再犯同样的错误了。"

    old "Could you use it in combat?"
    new "Could you use it in combat?\n你能在战斗中使用它吗？"

    old "Certainly. The jewelwort increased my healing powers immensely. Its effects should be the same in combat as they would be out of it. It's unfortunate that it's only on loan. It would be a great boon if we had the ability to keep it. But we did make a promise in good faith to return it."
    new "Certainly. The jewelwort increased my healing powers immensely. Its effects should be the same in combat as they would be out of it. It's unfortunate that it's only on loan. It would be a great boon if we had the ability to keep it. But we did make a promise in good faith to return it.\n当然可以。jewelwort 极大地增强了我的治疗能力。它在战斗中的效果应该和在战斗外一样。可惜它只是借来的。如果我们能把它留下，那会是极大的助益。不过我们确实诚心诚意许下了归还的承诺。"

    old "Yes, of course. A promise is a promise. Jaya did us a favor by lending us the jewelwort. The least we can do to repay his kindness is to return what we borrowed."
    new "Yes, of course. A promise is a promise. Jaya did us a favor by lending us the jewelwort. The least we can do to repay his kindness is to return what we borrowed.\n是的，当然。承诺就是承诺。Jaya 把 jewelwort 借给我们，是帮了我们一个大忙。要报答他的恩情，我们至少该把借来的东西还回去。"

    old "Vaeril, I need you to understand something. There are things in this world more important than promises."
    new "Vaeril, I need you to understand something. There are things in this world more important than promises.\nVaeril，我需要你明白一件事。这个世界上有比承诺更重要的东西。"

    old "My job is to defeat the undead menace at N'Mar. If we fail in that mission, the evil that lurks within that castle will continue to spread across the lands. This is bigger than either of us. Bigger than the blighted wood on N'Mar."
    new "My job is to defeat the undead menace at N'Mar. If we fail in that mission, the evil that lurks within that castle will continue to spread across the lands. This is bigger than either of us. Bigger than the blighted wood on N'Mar.\n我的职责是消灭 N'Mar 的不死威胁。如果我们任务失败，潜伏在那座城堡里的邪恶就会继续蔓延到各地。这比我们两个人都重要，比 N'Mar 那片枯萎的树林更重要。"

    old "And certainly bigger than our promise to Jaya."
    new "And certainly bigger than our promise to Jaya.\n当然也比我们对 Jaya 的承诺更重要。"

    old "If we fail to stamp out the source of that undead nightmare, it could spread spread all across the lands. There's too much at stake here. Our mission is too important than the promise we made to Jaya."
    new "If we fail to stamp out the source of that undead nightmare, it could spread spread all across the lands. There's too much at stake here. Our mission is too important than the promise we made to Jaya.\n如果我们不能铲除那场不死噩梦的源头，它可能会蔓延到所有地方。这里牵涉太多了。我们的使命比我们对 Jaya 许下的承诺重要得多。"

    old "If we don't return this jewelwort, Jaya will die."
    new "If we don't return this jewelwort, Jaya will die.\n如果我们不归还这株 jewelwort，Jaya 会死。"

    old "And if we fail in our mission, thousands may perish, Jaya among them. It feels terrible to condemn someone to death. But if I can sacrifice the life of a tree and his friends to strengthen my army, I'll make that trade. Perhaps you feel differently, as a man of the forest. But by ceding the blighted woods of N'Mar, we may save the entire Great Forest."
    new "And if we fail in our mission, thousands may perish, Jaya among them. It feels terrible to condemn someone to death. But if I can sacrifice the life of a tree and his friends to strengthen my army, I'll make that trade. Perhaps you feel differently, as a man of the forest. But by ceding the blighted woods of N'Mar, we may save the entire Great Forest.\n可如果我们任务失败，死去的可能是成千上万的人，Jaya 也在其中。把人推向死亡的感觉很糟。但如果牺牲一棵树和他朋友们的生命就能壮大我的军队，我愿意做这笔交易。或许你作为森林中人，会有不同的感受。但放弃 N'Mar 那片枯萎的树林，我们也许就能拯救整座 Great Forest。"

    old "So you agree with me?"
    new "So you agree with me?\n所以你同意我的看法？"

    old "What you say is true. The outcome of our mission is of tantamount importance. And keeping the jewelwort increases our chances of success."
    new "What you say is true. The outcome of our mission is of tantamount importance. And keeping the jewelwort increases our chances of success.\n你说得对。我们任务的成败至关重要。而留下 jewelwort 会增加我们成功的机会。"

    old "You've come to a perfectly defensible conclusion. Who am I to disagree?"
    new "You've come to a perfectly defensible conclusion. Who am I to disagree?\n你得出的是一个完全站得住脚的结论。我又凭什么反对呢？"

    old "You're on my team, Vaeril. I expect your loyalty, but I understand that devotion has its limits. You're within your rights to disagree."
    new "You're on my team, Vaeril. I expect your loyalty, but I understand that devotion has its limits. You're within your rights to disagree.\n你是我的队友，Vaeril。我期望你的忠诚，但我也明白奉献是有限度的。你有权不同意。"

    old "And I choose not to."
    new "And I choose not to.\n而我选择不反对。"

    old "Then it's settled. We'll keep the jewelwort."
    new "Then it's settled. We'll keep the jewelwort.\n那就这么定了。我们留下 jewelwort。"

    old "And I can assure you I'll make good use of it."
    new "And I can assure you I'll make good use of it.\n我可以向你保证，我会好好利用它。"

    old "I think it may be best to fashion the jewelwort into some sort of more permanent talisman that I can affix to my staff."
    new "I think it may be best to fashion the jewelwort into some sort of more permanent talisman that I can affix to my staff.\n我想最好是把 jewelwort 做成某种更持久的护符，好固定在我的法杖上。"

    old "How long will that take?"
    new "How long will that take?\n那要花多长时间？"

    old "Several days. I'll start right away."
    new "Several days. I'll start right away.\n几天。我马上就开始。"

    old "We return to the blighted woods of N'Mar the same way we came. We locate Jaya in the woods without incident."
    new "We return to the blighted woods of N'Mar the same way we came. We locate Jaya in the woods without incident.\n我们顺着来时的路返回 N'Mar 那片枯萎的树林，一路无事，在林中找到了 Jaya。"

    old "So what comes now?"
    new "So what comes now?\n那现在呢？"

    old "Perhaps it's best for me to commune with Jaya, in case he has anything further to say to us."
    new "Perhaps it's best for me to commune with Jaya, in case he has anything further to say to us.\n或许最好让我和 Jaya 沟通一下，说不定他还有话要对我们说。"

    old "Vaeril stands with his back to the tree, and places his hands on it. He mumbles for a few moments before the tree extends branchs that wrap around him."
    new "Vaeril stands with his back to the tree, and places his hands on it. He mumbles for a few moments before the tree extends branchs that wrap around him.\nVaeril 背对着树站好，把双手放在树上。他低语了片刻，随后树伸出枝条，把他缠绕起来。"

    old "Vaeril's body perks up, and his eyes begin glowing as the color drains from his face."
    new "Vaeril's body perks up, and his eyes begin glowing as the color drains from his face.\nVaeril 的身体挺了起来，他的眼睛开始发光，脸上的血色随之褪去。"

    old "Hello [prace]."
    new "Hello [prace].\n你好，[prace]。"

    old "Hello, Jaya. We've come back to return what we borrowed."
    new "Hello, Jaya. We've come back to return what we borrowed.\n你好，Jaya。我们回来归还借走的东西了。"

    old "I hold the jewelwort aloft, and a branch sweeps down and plucks the herb from my grasp."
    new "I hold the jewelwort aloft, and a branch sweeps down and plucks the herb from my grasp.\n我把 jewelwort 高高举起，一根树枝扫下来，从我手中取走了这株草药。"

    old "It is a relief to finally have the jewelwort back."
    new "It is a relief to finally have the jewelwort back.\n终于拿回了 jewelwort，真是如释重负。"

    old "What exactly is it that the jewelwort allows you to do? What is special about it?"
    new "What exactly is it that the jewelwort allows you to do? What is special about it?\njewelwort 究竟能让你做什么？它到底有什么特别之处？"

    old "The jewelwort is what allows me to drink the life out of this pool. In return, I keep the forest alive. It is cyclical. Without the jewelwort, my ability to draw life force from the water is greatly weakened."
    new "The jewelwort is what allows me to drink the life out of this pool. In return, I keep the forest alive. It is cyclical. Without the jewelwort, my ability to draw life force from the water is greatly weakened.\njewelwort 让我能够汲取这片水塘中的生命。作为回报，我让森林保持生机。这是循环的。没有了 jewelwort，我从水中汲取生命力的能力就会大大减弱。"

    old "In your absence, I have had time to ruminate on the dilema you shared with me. The business related to what you called a castle."
    new "In your absence, I have had time to ruminate on the dilema you shared with me. The business related to what you called a castle.\n你不在的这段时间，我有空仔细思考了你告诉我的那个难题，就是你所说的那座城堡的事。"

    old "I cannot give you custody of this jewelwort. It's far too precious to me. But I can offer you some of its fruits."
    new "I cannot give you custody of this jewelwort. It's far too precious to me. But I can offer you some of its fruits.\n我不能把这株 jewelwort 交给你保管。它对我来说太珍贵了。但我可以给你一些它的果实。"

    old "Fruits?"
    new "Fruits?\n果实？"

    old "I drink vim with the jewelwort. It's within my power to excrete some of it in a form that may be useful to you."
    new "I drink vim with the jewelwort. It's within my power to excrete some of it in a form that may be useful to you.\n我靠 jewelwort 汲取活力。我有能力把其中一些排出来，变成对你有用的形态。"

    old "Look at my trunk. Next to your friend."
    new "Look at my trunk. Next to your friend.\n看看我的树干，就在你朋友旁边。"

    old "It looks shiny."
    new "It looks shiny.\n看起来亮晶晶的。"

    old "It's yours to take."
    new "It's yours to take.\n你拿去吧。"

    old "I take a closer look at Jaya's trunk, and see a hardened bit of sap. I grip it, and the hardened sap snaps off."
    new "I take a closer look at Jaya's trunk, and see a hardened bit of sap. I grip it, and the hardened sap snaps off.\n我凑近细看 Jaya 的树干，看到一块凝固的树液。我抓住它，那块凝固的树液咔的一声断了下来。"

    old "If one of your companions falls in battle, feed them this sap. They will enter battle with renewed vigor."
    new "If one of your companions falls in battle, feed them this sap. They will enter battle with renewed vigor.\n如果你的同伴中有人在战斗中倒下，就把这树液喂给他们。他们会带着重新焕发的活力重返战场。"

    old "Thank you, Jaya."
    new "Thank you, Jaya.\n谢谢你，Jaya。"

    old "Producing the sap is not an easy process for me. It takes time and precious resources. This is all I can give you. Please don't ask for more."
    new "Producing the sap is not an easy process for me. It takes time and precious resources. This is all I can give you. Please don't ask for more.\n产出这种树液对我来说并不容易，它需要时间和宝贵的资源。这是我所能给你的全部。请不要再多要了。"

    old "You're too generous, Jaya."
    new "You're too generous, Jaya.\n你太慷慨了，Jaya。"

    old "Perhaps I am generous. Or perhaps I am simply concerned with assisting you in defeating our shared enemy. Rid the woods of this blight, [prace]. Help save my fellow trees."
    new "Perhaps I am generous. Or perhaps I am simply concerned with assisting you in defeating our shared enemy. Rid the woods of this blight, [prace]. Help save my fellow trees.\n也许我是慷慨。又或许，我只是想协助你击败我们共同的敌人。请除掉这片树林的枯萎之害吧，[prace]。帮我救救我的树木同胞。"

    old "We will, Jaya. I promise it."
    new "We will, Jaya. I promise it.\n我们会的，Jaya。我保证。"

    old "I take notice of Vaeril's staff."
    new "I take notice of Vaeril's staff.\n我注意到了 Vaeril 的法杖。"

    old "Is that the jewelwort talisman?"
    new "Is that the jewelwort talisman?\n那就是 jewelwort 护符吗？"

    old "Indeed it is. It's ready to take into battle the moment that duty calls."
    new "Indeed it is. It's ready to take into battle the moment that duty calls.\n正是。只要职责召唤，它随时可以带进战场。"

    old "I can equip it on any staff. This will be a great help in battles."
    new "I can equip it on any staff. This will be a great help in battles.\n我可以把它装在任何法杖上。这在战斗中会是极大的助力。"

    old "I'm glad to hear it. Vaeril, is this your home?"
    new "I'm glad to hear it. Vaeril, is this your home?\n听你这么说我很高兴。Vaeril，这里就是你的家吗？"

    old "It feels odd to call this inn my home. I have slept here every night since coming to Grimoire. And yet it seems that all I do here is sleep. Most of my waking hours are spent in the infirmary. I've never had occasion to entertain guests, and even when I have, it's been at the infirmary."
    new "It feels odd to call this inn my home. I have slept here every night since coming to Grimoire. And yet it seems that all I do here is sleep. Most of my waking hours are spent in the infirmary. I've never had occasion to entertain guests, and even when I have, it's been at the infirmary.\n把这家客栈称作我的家，感觉有点奇怪。自从来到 Grimoire，我每晚都睡在这里。可似乎我在这里做的只有睡觉。我醒着的大部分时间都在医务室度过。我从没有机会招待客人，就算有，也都是在医务室。"

    old "Did my visiting you at work bother you?"
    new "Did my visiting you at work bother you?\n我去你工作的地方找你，会打扰到你吗？"

    old "Not at all. In fact, your presence fills me with a sense of excitement and expectation."
    new "Not at all. In fact, your presence fills me with a sense of excitement and expectation.\n完全不会。事实上，你的到来让我满心兴奋和期待。"

    old "Maybe it's all the time we've spent fighting zombies together. You've come to associate that feeling of fear and excitement with me as a person."
    new "Maybe it's all the time we've spent fighting zombies together. You've come to associate that feeling of fear and excitement with me as a person.\n也许是因为我们一起打僵尸的时间太久了。你把那种恐惧和兴奋的感觉，跟作为人的我联系在了一起。"

    old "That may be the case, but you're a very unique person, [protag]. I've never met anyone quite like you."
    new "That may be the case, but you're a very unique person, [protag]. I've never met anyone quite like you.\n也许是这样，但你是一个非常特别的人，[protag]。我从没见过像你这样的人。"

    old "[protag]...you're really quite ruthless."
    new "[protag]...you're really quite ruthless.\n[protag]……你真的相当冷酷无情。"

    old "I'm not sure I like that description."
    new "I'm not sure I like that description.\n我不太确定自己喜欢这个评价。"

    old "Most people don't. Most people would actively try to avoid that kind of label. But you, you're different. You're more concerned with getting the best outcome than leaving everyone feeling good. And when it comes to a mission like ours, that's exactly what's required."
    new "Most people don't. Most people would actively try to avoid that kind of label. But you, you're different. You're more concerned with getting the best outcome than leaving everyone feeling good. And when it comes to a mission like ours, that's exactly what's required.\n大多数人都不喜欢。大多数人都会刻意避开这种标签。可你不一样。你更在意取得最好的结果，而不是让每个人都感觉良好。而对我们这样的任务来说，这恰恰是所需要的。"

    old "At first, I wasn't sure what to make of you. But as we've spent more time together, you've shown me more and more of who you are. And I like what I see."
    new "At first, I wasn't sure what to make of you. But as we've spent more time together, you've shown me more and more of who you are. And I like what I see.\n起初，我不知道该怎么看待你。但随着我们相处的时间越来越长，你让我看到了越来越多真实的你。而我喜欢的，正是我看到的这一切。"

    old "I don't see why that's a bad thing. Sometimes, ruthlessness is what's called for. The best outcome isn't always the one that leaves everyone feeling good."
    new "I don't see why that's a bad thing. Sometimes, ruthlessness is what's called for. The best outcome isn't always the one that leaves everyone feeling good.\n我不明白这有什么不好。有时候，冷酷无情正是所需要的。最好的结果并不总是让每个人都感觉良好。"

    old "You aren't even ashamed to admit it in front of me. And I think that's what I like so much about you."
    new "You aren't even ashamed to admit it in front of me. And I think that's what I like so much about you.\n你甚至毫不羞愧地在我面前承认这一点。我想这正是我如此喜欢你的原因。"

    old "[protag], my life has not been an easy one. Others struggle with the circumstances that surround them. But in my case, the very thing that I am, my very existence, has been a trial to be coped with."
    new "[protag], my life has not been an easy one. Others struggle with the circumstances that surround them. But in my case, the very thing that I am, my very existence, has been a trial to be coped with.\n[protag]，我这一生过得并不轻松。别人挣扎于周遭的境遇。可对我来说，我本身是什么，我自身的存在，就是一场需要去应对的考验。"

    old "I am an elf, but I have been hated by elves my entire life. When people found out what I was, they thought the world would be better with me dead. And at many points in my life, I questioned whether they were right."
    new "I am an elf, but I have been hated by elves my entire life. When people found out what I was, they thought the world would be better with me dead. And at many points in my life, I questioned whether they were right.\n我是个 Elf，却一生都被 Elves 所憎恨。当人们得知我的身份，他们都觉得我死了对这个世界更好。在我人生的许多时刻，我都怀疑过他们是否说对了。"

    old "For many reasons, I told myself that the reason I lived in exile was to protect myself from the world. But as time wore on, I realized the truth: I was really trying to protect the world from myself."
    new "For many reasons, I told myself that the reason I lived in exile was to protect myself from the world. But as time wore on, I realized the truth: I was really trying to protect the world from myself.\n出于种种原因，我告诉自己，我流亡是为了保护自己免受世界的伤害。但随着时间的推移，我认清了真相：我其实是在努力保护世界，免受我自己的伤害。"

    old "I was planning to live the rest of my life alone in that forest until the day I died. But you can into my life. You disrupted it. Rather than condemn me for my...abilities, you encouraged me. I wondered what could possess someone to behave as you did."
    new "I was planning to live the rest of my life alone in that forest until the day I died. But you can into my life. You disrupted it. Rather than condemn me for my...abilities, you encouraged me. I wondered what could possess someone to behave as you did.\n我本打算在那片森林里独自度过余生，直到死去的那一天。可你走进了我的生活，把它打乱了。你没有因为我的……能力而指责我，反而鼓励了我。我一直在想，究竟是什么能让一个人像你这样对待我。"

    old "But as time has gone on, and I've seen the way you act, I've realized something. We're birds of a feather, you and I."
    new "But as time has gone on, and I've seen the way you act, I've realized something. We're birds of a feather, you and I.\n但随着时间的推移，看到你做事的方式，我意识到了一件事。你我是同一类人。"

    old "Birds of a feather?"
    new "Birds of a feather?\n同一类人？"

    old "You possess a unique gift, [protag]. It's a bit different from mine in that there's no magic to it. And yet it's just as much a part of you as my special talent is a part of me."
    new "You possess a unique gift, [protag]. It's a bit different from mine in that there's no magic to it. And yet it's just as much a part of you as my special talent is a part of me.\n你拥有一份独特的天赋，[protag]。它和我的略有不同，因为它不含魔法。然而它就像我的特殊才能之于我一样，是你不可分割的一部分。"

    old "You're fierce in a way that other people aren't. It's a trait that the world is quick to condemn when they see it. But much like my life-draining powers, your ruthlessness is something that can be harnessed for good. "
    new "You're fierce in a way that other people aren't. It's a trait that the world is quick to condemn when they see it. But much like my life-draining powers, your ruthlessness is something that can be harnessed for good. \n你身上有一种他人没有的凶猛。世人一见到这种特质，就急于加以谴责。但就像我汲取生命的能力一样，你的冷酷无情是可以被用于善途的。"

    old "Your gift doesn't make you a bad person. You can use it to achieve good things. But you achieve it in a way that other people may find despicable. And yet you still do it."
    new "Your gift doesn't make you a bad person. You can use it to achieve good things. But you achieve it in a way that other people may find despicable. And yet you still do it.\n你的天赋并不会让你变成坏人。你可以用它成就好事。只是你达成目标的方式，在别人看来也许可鄙。可你依然会去做。"

    old "You showed me my unique gift, and then you showed me yours. At first, I was afraid of it. But now, I'm awed by it."
    new "You showed me my unique gift, and then you showed me yours. At first, I was afraid of it. But now, I'm awed by it.\n你让我看到了我自己独特的天赋，接着又让我看到了你的。起初我很害怕，但现在，我对它满怀敬畏。"

    old "You don't wait for the world to hand you want you want. You reach out and take it."
    new "You don't wait for the world to hand you want you want. You reach out and take it.\n你不会等着世界把你想要的东西送到你手上。你会伸手去把它夺过来。"

    old "And yet, for as long as I've known you, you've had a single-minded devotion to your objective. You put the mission first, and that makes you a force to be reckoned with. But what about your wants and needs? You've never been one to express them."
    new "And yet, for as long as I've known you, you've had a single-minded devotion to your objective. You put the mission first, and that makes you a force to be reckoned with. But what about your wants and needs? You've never been one to express them.\n然而，在我认识你的这段时间里，你对目标始终一心一意。你把任务放在第一位，这让你成为一股不容小觑的力量。可你自己的愿望和需求呢？你从来都不是个会表达它们的人。"

    old "So now I have to ask...what is it that you want?"
    new "So now I have to ask...what is it that you want?\n所以现在我不得不问……你究竟想要什么？"

    old "You're right, Vaeril. I have been focused on the mission. I've prioritized it ahead of my own personal needs and the needs of others."
    new "You're right, Vaeril. I have been focused on the mission. I've prioritized it ahead of my own personal needs and the needs of others.\n你说得对，Vaeril。我一直专注于任务。我把任务排在个人需求，甚至他人的需求之前。"

    old "This isn't out of any sense of duty or obligation, although I am bound by those as well. To me, the mission is what matters most. The mission is where I get my personal fulfillment. The mission is what gives meaning to my life."
    new "This isn't out of any sense of duty or obligation, although I am bound by those as well. To me, the mission is what matters most. The mission is where I get my personal fulfillment. The mission is what gives meaning to my life.\n这并非出于任何职责或义务感，尽管我也受这些束缚。对我来说，任务才是最重要的。任务是我获得个人满足的地方，任务赋予了我生命的意义。"

    old "Do you know what I want? I want to see the evil of N'Mar banished. And to achieve that, I want people like you, who are willing to follow me into battle, knowing that their life may be in jeopardy. People who are willing to devote themselves to something that is bigger and more important than they are."
    new "Do you know what I want? I want to see the evil of N'Mar banished. And to achieve that, I want people like you, who are willing to follow me into battle, knowing that their life may be in jeopardy. People who are willing to devote themselves to something that is bigger and more important than they are.\n你知道我想要什么吗？我想看到 N'Mar 的邪恶被驱逐。为了实现这一点，我需要像你这样的人，愿意追随我上战场，明知自己的生命可能身处险境。愿意把自己奉献给比他们自身更伟大、更重要的事业的人。"

    old "Working alongside you has been a privilege. And I hope to continue doing just that."
    new "Working alongside you has been a privilege. And I hope to continue doing just that.\n与你并肩作战一直是我的荣幸。我希望能够继续下去。"

    old "I see, [protag]. It has been a privilege and honor for me as well."
    new "I see, [protag]. It has been a privilege and honor for me as well.\n我明白了，[protag]。这对我来说同样是荣幸与荣耀。"

    old "See you soon, Vaeril."
    new "See you soon, Vaeril.\n回头见，Vaeril。"

    old "As I leave Vaeril alone, I wonder if perhaps he was hoping for a different answer from me."
    new "As I leave Vaeril alone, I wonder if perhaps he was hoping for a different answer from me.\n我独自离开 Vaeril，心里琢磨着他是不是原本希望从我这里得到不同的答复。"

    old "He seemed slightly disappointed by my reply."
    new "He seemed slightly disappointed by my reply.\n他似乎对我的回答略感失望。"

    old "Well, no time to think about this. I have more urgent tasks I must attend to."
    new "Well, no time to think about this. I have more urgent tasks I must attend to.\n算了，没时间想这些。我还有更紧迫的任务要处理。"

    old "I want you, Vaeril."
    new "I want you, Vaeril.\n我想要你，Vaeril。"

    old "I take a step forward and place a hand on his chest, running it up and down the fabric of his tunic, feeling the shape of his body. I grab a handful of the fabric, and pull him toward me."
    new "I take a step forward and place a hand on his chest, running it up and down the fabric of his tunic, feeling the shape of his body. I grab a handful of the fabric, and pull him toward me.\n我向前一步，把手放到他的胸口，隔着他的短袍布料上下摩挲，感受着他身体的轮廓。我抓住一把衣料，把他拉向我。"

    old "I stare into his face, and he stares back, with large, longing eyes."
    new "I stare into his face, and he stares back, with large, longing eyes.\n我凝视着他的脸，他也凝视着我，一双大眼睛里满是渴望。"

    old "You've wanted this too."
    new "You've wanted this too.\n你也一直想要这样。"

    old "I place a hand on his cheek, and he closes his eyes as I place a kiss on his lips."
    new "I place a hand on his cheek, and he closes his eyes as I place a kiss on his lips.\n我把手放到他的脸颊上，当我在他唇上落下一吻时，他闭上了眼睛。"

    old "Take off your clothes and get on the bed."
    new "Take off your clothes and get on the bed.\n脱掉衣服，到床上去。"

    old "Vaeril disrobes and lies on the bed. He looks at me with a eager, beckoning look."
    new "Vaeril disrobes and lies on the bed. He looks at me with a eager, beckoning look.\nVaeril 脱去衣服，躺到床上。他用一种热切、勾人的目光看着我。"

    old "The day that I met you, I knew that one day, we would do great things together."
    new "The day that I met you, I knew that one day, we would do great things together.\n遇见你的那一天，我就知道，总有一天我们会一起成就一番大事业。"

    old "In fact, 'great' might be understating it. Vaeril, you and I are going to do wonderful things. Amazing things."
    new "In fact, 'great' might be understating it. Vaeril, you and I are going to do wonderful things. Amazing things.\n事实上，'大事业'这个词可能都说轻了。Vaeril，你和我将一起做出美妙的事，令人惊叹的事。"

    old "I jump on top of Vaeril, straddling him, and push his face into my chest. I feel the warmth of his breath on my skin."
    new "I jump on top of Vaeril, straddling him, and push his face into my chest. I feel the warmth of his breath on my skin.\n我跳到 Vaeril 身上，跨坐在他身上，把他的脸按进我的胸口。我感受到他呼吸的温热拂在我的皮肤上。"

    old "Incredible things. Things like this."
    new "Incredible things. Things like this.\n不可思议的事。就像这样的事。"

    old "You and I are going to have one hell of a night."
    new "You and I are going to have one hell of a night.\n你和我将要度过一个无比销魂的夜晚。"

    old "Vaeril, is this your home?"
    new "Vaeril, is this your home?\nVaeril，这里就是你的家吗？"

    old "Not at all. The infirmary keeps me busy, but it's a dark place. Perhaps that's why I was drawn to it-the darkness seems to suit me better than the light. When you come to visit, you're a like a light from the darkness. Seeing you brightens my day."
    new "Not at all. The infirmary keeps me busy, but it's a dark place. Perhaps that's why I was drawn to it-the darkness seems to suit me better than the light. When you come to visit, you're a like a light from the darkness. Seeing you brightens my day.\n完全不是。医务室让我很忙，但那里是个阴暗的地方。也许这正是我被它吸引的原因——黑暗似乎比光明更适合我。当你来看我时，你就像黑暗中的一束光。见到你，我的日子都明亮了起来。"

    old "I take you out at night to fight undead monsters, and together we trekked into a blighted and decaying wood. I'm not sure that I deserved to be called a light from the darkness."
    new "I take you out at night to fight undead monsters, and together we trekked into a blighted and decaying wood. I'm not sure that I deserved to be called a light from the darkness.\n我夜里带你出去打不死怪物，还和你一起跋涉进了那片枯萎腐烂的树林。我不太确定自己配得上'黑暗中的一束光'这个称呼。"

    old "You walk through darkness, and yet you project light everywhere you go. And I've willingly followed that beacon everywhere she's taken me."
    new "You walk through darkness, and yet you project light everywhere you go. And I've willingly followed that beacon everywhere she's taken me.\n你穿行于黑暗，却每到一处都投射出光明。而我心甘情愿地跟随那束光，随她走到任何地方。"

    old "I lived alone for many years. When I heard you making a ruckus in the forest, I wasn't sure what I would feel when I saw you. I think I was apprehensive. I was fearful. I didn't know what kind of trouble you might be bringing with you."
    new "I lived alone for many years. When I heard you making a ruckus in the forest, I wasn't sure what I would feel when I saw you. I think I was apprehensive. I was fearful. I didn't know what kind of trouble you might be bringing with you.\n我独自生活了很多年。当我听到你在森林里弄出动静时，我不确定见到你时会是什么感觉。我想我是忐忑的，是害怕的。我不知道你可能会带来什么样的麻烦。"

    old "But when I laid eyes on you, I felt no fear. I felt an incredible calm. I sensed a kindness about you. In spite of myself, I founding myself trusting you. And I've been so happy that my trust has proven to be so well-placed."
    new "But when I laid eyes on you, I felt no fear. I felt an incredible calm. I sensed a kindness about you. In spite of myself, I founding myself trusting you. And I've been so happy that my trust has proven to be so well-placed.\n但当我看到你的那一刻，我没有感到恐惧。我感到一种不可思议的平静。我感受到了你身上的善良。我不由自主地开始信任你。而我的信任被证明没有错付，这让我无比高兴。"

    old "My entire life, people have looked at me and seen only the worst of me. I was an elf who was a pariah among elves. But somehow, you looked at me, and decided somehow that you wanted to make a companion out of me. And I can't thank you enough."
    new "My entire life, people have looked at me and seen only the worst of me. I was an elf who was a pariah among elves. But somehow, you looked at me, and decided somehow that you wanted to make a companion out of me. And I can't thank you enough.\n我这一生，人们看着我，只看到我最糟糕的一面。我是一个在 Elves 中被排斥的弃儿。可不知为何，你看着我，却决定要与我结伴同行。我怎样感谢你都不为过。"

    old "You've already done more than enough to thank me, Vaeril. Every time you follow me into battle, I can feel confident that you'll have my back. That's something I'll never take for granted."
    new "You've already done more than enough to thank me, Vaeril. Every time you follow me into battle, I can feel confident that you'll have my back. That's something I'll never take for granted.\n你已经报答我太多了，Vaeril。每次你随我上战场，我都能安心地相信你会护着我。这一点我永远不会视为理所当然。"

    old "Not at all. The infirmary keeps me busy, but it's a dark place. Perhaps that's why I was drawn to it—the darkness seems to suit me better than the light. When you come to visit, you're a like a light from the darkness. Seeing you brightens my day."
    new "Not at all. The infirmary keeps me busy, but it's a dark place. Perhaps that's why I was drawn to it—the darkness seems to suit me better than the light. When you come to visit, you're a like a light from the darkness. Seeing you brightens my day.\n完全不是。医务室让我很忙，但那里是个阴暗的地方。也许这正是我被它吸引的原因——黑暗似乎比光明更适合我。当你来看我时，你就像黑暗中的一束光。见到你，我的日子都明亮了起来。"

    old "You walk through darkness, and yet you project light everywhere you go. And I've willingly followed that beacon everywhere [heshe]'s taken me."
    new "You walk through darkness, and yet you project light everywhere you go. And I've willingly followed that beacon everywhere [heshe]'s taken me.\n你穿行于黑暗，却每到一处都投射出光明。而我心甘情愿地跟随那束光，随[heshe]走到任何地方。"

    old "But when I laid eyes on you, I felt no fear. I felt an incredible calm. You looked just like an angel, fallen from heaven."
    new "But when I laid eyes on you, I felt no fear. I felt an incredible calm. You looked just like an angel, fallen from heaven.\n但当我看到你的那一刻，我没有感到恐惧。我感到一种不可思议的平静。你看起来就像一位从天而降的天使。"

    old "I'm not sure I deserve to be compared to an angel. Even on a good day, I don't look very divine, and especially not when I'm covered in bruises and cuts from falling out of a tree."
    new "I'm not sure I deserve to be compared to an angel. Even on a good day, I don't look very divine, and especially not when I'm covered in bruises and cuts from falling out of a tree.\n我不太确定自己配得上被比作天使。就算状态最好的时候，我看起来也不怎么超凡脱俗，尤其是当我从树上摔下来、浑身是淤青和伤口的时候。"

    old "Please don't misunderstand me, [protag]. I serve at your beck and call. You need people who are willing to follow you into battle, to lay down their life if need be, and I am just one of those people. While our relationship is certainly nothing trivial, I also understand that it's also nothing special."
    new "Please don't misunderstand me, [protag]. I serve at your beck and call. You need people who are willing to follow you into battle, to lay down their life if need be, and I am just one of those people. While our relationship is certainly nothing trivial, I also understand that it's also nothing special.\n请别误解我，[protag]。我随时听候你的差遣。你需要愿意追随你上战场、必要时不惜牺牲性命的人，而我不过是其中之一。我们的关系固然不浅，可我也明白，它同样算不上什么特别。"

    old "I must confess...when we met in the forest, and I shouldered your weight and felt your grip around me, I did feel something in that moment. I saw you as someone that I wanted to protect, to guard, to shield from all harm."
    new "I must confess...when we met in the forest, and I shouldered your weight and felt your grip around me, I did feel something in that moment. I saw you as someone that I wanted to protect, to guard, to shield from all harm.\n我必须承认……我们在森林相遇时，当我扛起你的重量、感受到你紧紧抓住我时，那一刻我的确心有所动。我把你看作一个我想要保护、想要守护、想要替其挡开一切伤害的人。"

    old "I imagined that perhaps you and I might be two souls destined to be together. I...I let my mind get away from me."
    new "I imagined that perhaps you and I might be two souls destined to be together. I...I let my mind get away from me.\n我想象过，也许你我是注定要在一起的两个灵魂。我……是我自己想得太远了。"

    old "Forgive me, [protag]. I felt something for you then, but I've buried those feelings. It would be improper for someone who is your follower to think such things."
    new "Forgive me, [protag]. I felt something for you then, but I've buried those feelings. It would be improper for someone who is your follower to think such things.\n原谅我，[protag]。当时我对你动了心，但我已经埋葬了那份感情。身为你的追随者，有这种念头是不合适的。"

    old "Vaeril, I feel the loyalty you offer me exceeds what I deserve as a leader. You're always giving up part of yourself to serve others. I feel blessed to be on the receiving end of that giving, and I hope that you divine some purpose and meaning from our mission. I hope that, in all of this, you don't forget to take care of yourself."
    new "Vaeril, I feel the loyalty you offer me exceeds what I deserve as a leader. You're always giving up part of yourself to serve others. I feel blessed to be on the receiving end of that giving, and I hope that you divine some purpose and meaning from our mission. I hope that, in all of this, you don't forget to take care of yourself.\nVaeril，我觉得你给我的忠诚，超出了我作为领袖应得的。你总是牺牲自己的一部分去服务他人。能成为这份付出的受惠者，我深感幸运。我希望你能从我们的使命中寻得某种意义与目标，也希望在这一切之中，你不要忘了照顾好自己。"

    old "Thank you for your service."
    new "Thank you for your service.\n感谢你的效劳。"

    old "Vaeril. He said he buried those feelings. But he didn't fool me. He was still interested in me more than a loyal follower. I felt a bit bad to be so blunt with him. However, I only see him as a friend, and nothing more."
    new "Vaeril. He said he buried those feelings. But he didn't fool me. He was still interested in me more than a loyal follower. I felt a bit bad to be so blunt with him. However, I only see him as a friend, and nothing more.\nVaeril。他说他埋葬了那些感情，但他骗不过我。他对我的在意，仍超过一个忠诚的追随者。对他如此直白，我有点过意不去。不过，我只把他当作朋友，仅此而已。"

    old "I think it was the right choice to tell him how I truly feel."
    new "I think it was the right choice to tell him how I truly feel.\n我觉得把真实想法告诉他，是正确的选择。"

    old "Vaeril..."
    new "Vaeril...\nVaeril……"

    old "That day when we met in the forest, I felt a connection to you, just as you felt for me. As you lifted me from the ground, I felt the warmth of your embrace, and I felt safe. In my mind, I entertained thoughts that you might whisk me away from all harm, that you would take me to a place where we would be together."
    new "That day when we met in the forest, I felt a connection to you, just as you felt for me. As you lifted me from the ground, I felt the warmth of your embrace, and I felt safe. In my mind, I entertained thoughts that you might whisk me away from all harm, that you would take me to a place where we would be together.\n那天我们在森林里相遇，我对你产生了一种联结，正如你对我一样。当你把我从地上扶起时，我感受到你怀抱的温暖，我感到安心。在我脑海中，我曾幻想你会把我带离一切伤害，带我去一个我们能在一起的地方。"

    old "My responsibilities don't allow for such fantasies to be realized. I have obligations I must fulfill, as do you. But would it be so wrong for us to forget those obligations for just one night, to be together and think of nothing but each other?"
    new "My responsibilities don't allow for such fantasies to be realized. I have obligations I must fulfill, as do you. But would it be so wrong for us to forget those obligations for just one night, to be together and think of nothing but each other?\n我的责任不允许这样的幻想成真。我有必须履行的义务，你也一样。可是，就一个晚上，让我们暂时忘掉那些义务，待在一起，心里只想着彼此，这真的就那么错吗？"

    old "Vaeril opens his arms wide, and I collapse forward into his embrace. I feel strong, warm arms wrap around me, and I place my hands on his chest, gazing into his deep, soulful eyes."
    new "Vaeril opens his arms wide, and I collapse forward into his embrace. I feel strong, warm arms wrap around me, and I place my hands on his chest, gazing into his deep, soulful eyes.\nVaeril 张开双臂，我向前倒进他的怀抱。我感到强壮而温暖的手臂环住我，我把双手放在他的胸口，凝视着他深邃而深情的眼睛。"

    old "Vaeril, I..."
    new "Vaeril, I...\nVaeril，我……"

    old "Vaeril lowers his head next to mine, and I feel the warmth of his breath tickle my ear as he whispers into it."
    new "Vaeril lowers his head next to mine, and I feel the warmth of his breath tickle my ear as he whispers into it.\nVaeril 把头低到我耳边，我感到他呼吸的温热搔得我耳朵发痒，他正对着我的耳朵低语。"

    old "[protag]...you don't have to say anything."
    new "[protag]...you don't have to say anything.\n[protag]……你什么都不必说。"

    old "I grab hold of his robe and slide it off his shoulders."
    new "I grab hold of his robe and slide it off his shoulders.\n我抓住他的长袍，从他肩上褪下来。"

    old "I grab his belt and tug at it, struggling with the buckle for a few moments."
    new "I grab his belt and tug at it, struggling with the buckle for a few moments.\n我抓住他的腰带拽了拽，和带扣较了一会儿劲。"

    old "Allow me."
    new "Allow me.\n让我来。"

    old "Vaeril places his hands over mine, grasping them firmly but gently. He places my hands on my own belt, and I begin undoing it as he undoes his."
    new "Vaeril places his hands over mine, grasping them firmly but gently. He places my hands on my own belt, and I begin undoing it as he undoes his.\nVaeril 把他的手覆在我的手上，牢牢却又轻柔地握住。他把我的手放到我自己的腰带上，我开始解自己的，他则解他的。"

    old "We undress, and Vaeril leads me to the bed. We spend a moment, eyes locked."
    new "We undress, and Vaeril leads me to the bed. We spend a moment, eyes locked.\n我们脱去衣服，Vaeril 引我走向床边。有那么一刻，我们四目相对。"

    old "You're beautiful, [protag]. Every part of you is beautiful. The way you smile, the way that you move, the way that you always push forward with steadfast determination. Every day I've known you, I've gotten to see more of who you are. And every step of the way, I like what I see."
    new "You're beautiful, [protag]. Every part of you is beautiful. The way you smile, the way that you move, the way that you always push forward with steadfast determination. Every day I've known you, I've gotten to see more of who you are. And every step of the way, I like what I see.\n你真美，[protag]。你的一切都很美。你微笑的样子，你动作的样子，你总是带着坚定决心向前奋进的样子。认识你的每一天，我都能更多地看到真实的你。而一路走来，我喜欢的正是我看到的这一切。"

    old "I want to know you, [protag]. I want to know all of you."
    new "I want to know you, [protag]. I want to know all of you.\n我想了解你，[protag]。我想了解你的全部。"

    old "I slide into bed beside Vaeril, and feel his arms hold me close."
    new "I slide into bed beside Vaeril, and feel his arms hold me close.\n我滑进 Vaeril 身边的被窝，感受到他的双臂紧紧抱住我。"

    old "As I lie in bed in Vaeril's embrace, I feel warm and safe. I wish that this could last forever. But one night will do for now."
    new "As I lie in bed in Vaeril's embrace, I feel warm and safe. I wish that this could last forever. But one night will do for now.\n躺在 Vaeril 的怀抱里，我感到温暖而安心。我多希望这一切能永远持续下去。不过就现在而言，一夜也就足够了。"

    old "I find Vaeril at the inn in Grimoire."
    new "I find Vaeril at the inn in Grimoire.\n我在 Grimoire 的客栈找到了 Vaeril。"

    old "Hello [protag]."
    new "Hello [protag].\n你好，[protag]。"

    old "Vaeril. How have you been? Any troubles?"
    new "Vaeril. How have you been? Any troubles?\nVaeril。最近怎么样？有什么麻烦吗？"

    old "No. Here nobody knows me. I am only an elf, like many others."
    new "No. Here nobody knows me. I am only an elf, like many others.\n没有。这里没人认识我。我和其他许多人一样，只是个 Elf。"

    old "I wanted to ask you something. Regarding the dark elves."
    new "I wanted to ask you something. Regarding the dark elves.\n我想问你件事。关于 Dark Elves。"

    old "The ones who attacked us at the edge of the great forest?"
    new "The ones who attacked us at the edge of the great forest?\n在 Great Forest 边缘袭击我们的那些吗？"

    old "Yes. What's the story behind them? I know they're exiled from Grandtree. But apart this, I know not much else."
    new "Yes. What's the story behind them? I know they're exiled from Grandtree. But apart this, I know not much else.\n是的。他们背后有什么故事？我知道他们是被从 Grandtree 放逐的。但除此之外，我了解得不多。"

    old "It's complicated. It is said that the dark elves were born when an elf mixed his blood with that of a demon."
    new "It's complicated. It is said that the dark elves were born when an elf mixed his blood with that of a demon.\n说来复杂。据说 Dark Elves 是在一个 Elf 把自己的血和恶魔的血混合时诞生的。"

    old "Is that true, or just a story people tell?"
    new "Is that true, or just a story people tell?\n这是真的，还是只是人们口口相传的故事？"

    old "Who can say? The stories are so old at this point that it's nearly impossible to separate fact from fiction."
    new "Who can say? The stories are so old at this point that it's nearly impossible to separate fact from fiction.\n谁能说得准呢？这些故事如今已太过古老，几乎不可能把事实和虚构区分开来。"

    old "But their origin matters less than the fact that many druids, even elder druids, believe the dark elves spreads corruption in the great forest. Their mere presence can harm the trees and other plants."
    new "But their origin matters less than the fact that many druids, even elder druids, believe the dark elves spreads corruption in the great forest. Their mere presence can harm the trees and other plants.\n但比起他们的起源，更重要的是一个事实：许多德鲁伊，甚至长老德鲁伊，都相信 Dark Elves 在 Great Forest 里散布腐化。他们仅仅在场，就可能伤害树木和其他植物。"

    old "Vaeril seems to have a lot in common with the dark elves. I should be careful about what I'm about to say."
    new "Vaeril seems to have a lot in common with the dark elves. I should be careful about what I'm about to say.\nVaeril 似乎和 Dark Elves 有很多共同点。我接下来要说的话，得小心些。"

    old "I find it hard to believe. I mean, the ones who attacked us were clearly evil. But not more than any other human, dwarf or nomad bandit."
    new "I find it hard to believe. I mean, the ones who attacked us were clearly evil. But not more than any other human, dwarf or nomad bandit.\n我很难相信。我的意思是，袭击我们的那些家伙显然是邪恶的。但也未必比任何人类、Dwarf 或 Nomad 强盗更邪恶。"

    old "What are you trying to say, [protag]?"
    new "What are you trying to say, [protag]?\n你想说什么，[protag]？"

    old "You can't conclude from the misdeeds of some dark elves that all dark elves must be evil. That the thing that matters are people's actions. There can be evil as much as there can be any good in any race."
    new "You can't conclude from the misdeeds of some dark elves that all dark elves must be evil. That the thing that matters are people's actions. There can be evil as much as there can be any good in any race.\n你不能因为一些 Dark Elves 的恶行，就断定所有 Dark Elves 都必然是邪恶的。重要的是人的行为。任何种族里，都既可能有恶，也可能有善。"

    old "Your words are like caresses to me."
    new "Your words are like caresses to me.\n你的话对我来说就像爱抚。"

    old "Why stupid? They're only trying to protect the great forest."
    new "Why stupid? They're only trying to protect the great forest.\n为什么说蠢？他们只是想保护 Great Forest。"

    old "Yes, by exiling a whole race? Many people, even children and the elderly or infirm, pushed at the edge of the forest, just because of the blood they were born with?"
    new "Yes, by exiling a whole race? Many people, even children and the elderly or infirm, pushed at the edge of the forest, just because of the blood they were born with?\n是啊，靠放逐整个种族？许多人，甚至孩子、老人和体弱者，都被赶到森林边缘，仅仅因为他们与生俱来的血脉？"

    old "This is wrong. They should be working together to find a solution."
    new "This is wrong. They should be working together to find a solution.\n这是错的。他们应该携手寻找解决之道。"

    old "I know, but better live in exile, than be dead. After all, that's the same choice I made."
    new "I know, but better live in exile, than be dead. After all, that's the same choice I made.\n我知道，但流亡总比死去强。毕竟，那也正是我做出的选择。"

    old "I'm sorry, Vaeril."
    new "I'm sorry, Vaeril.\n对不起，Vaeril。"

    old "I imagined that you could identify yourself in all this..."
    new "I imagined that you could identify yourself in all this...\n我原以为你能在这整件事里看到自己的影子……"

    old "I am. But the reasons that elves have for treating me differently are not imaginary. You've seen what I do. I do really hurt the trees of the great forest."
    new "I am. But the reasons that elves have for treating me differently are not imaginary. You've seen what I do. I do really hurt the trees of the great forest.\n我确实看到了。但 Elves 区别对待我，那些理由并不是凭空想象的。你已经见过我做的事。我确实会伤害 Great Forest 的树木。"

    old "Yes, however you also give something in exchange. You take life, to give life."
    new "Yes, however you also give something in exchange. You take life, to give life.\n是的，不过你也会给出相应的回报。你汲取生命，是为了赋予生命。"

    old "How is this different from a man who cuts a tree to have woodfire and keep his family warm during Hibernia?"
    new "How is this different from a man who cuts a tree to have woodfire and keep his family warm during Hibernia?\n这和一个在 Hibernia 期间砍树取柴火、让家人取暖的人有什么不同？"

    old "There is a cost to everything. Some people choose to ignore that simple reality. But you don't have to."
    new "There is a cost to everything. Some people choose to ignore that simple reality. But you don't have to.\n凡事都有代价。有些人选择无视这个简单的现实。但你不必这样。"

    old "Thanks, [protag]. You gave me much to think about. I should try to use my talents to help the others more."
    new "Thanks, [protag]. You gave me much to think about. I should try to use my talents to help the others more.\n谢谢，[protag]。你让我想了很多。我应该试着用自己的才能去更多地帮助别人。"

    old "You're welcome, Vaeril."
    new "You're welcome, Vaeril.\n不客气，Vaeril。"

    old "Ah, [protag], I'm glad that you came so quickly."
    new "Ah, [protag], I'm glad that you came so quickly.\n啊，[protag]，很高兴你来得这么快。"

    old "Hello, Vaeril. Your request sounded urgent. What happened?"
    new "Hello, Vaeril. Your request sounded urgent. What happened?\n你好，Vaeril。你的请求听上去很紧急。出什么事了？"

    old "I'm sorry for distracting you from your duties. I do understand how crucial they are, but... please understand, this is important to me."
    new "I'm sorry for distracting you from your duties. I do understand how crucial they are, but... please understand, this is important to me.\n抱歉让你从职责中分心。我明白那些职责有多关键，但是……请理解，这件事对我很重要。"

    old "Alright. What's troubling you, my dear Vaeril?"
    new "Alright. What's troubling you, my dear Vaeril?\n好吧。什么事让你烦心，我亲爱的 Vaeril？"

    old "I was talking with some of the others a few days ago..."
    new "I was talking with some of the others a few days ago...\n几天前，我和其他一些人聊了聊……"

    old "Who in particular?"
    new "Who in particular?\n具体是谁？"

    old "Vaeril's expression darkens for a brief moment before he's able to return it to a more neutral one."
    new "Vaeril's expression darkens for a brief moment before he's able to return it to a more neutral one.\nVaeril 的表情短暂地一沉，随后才勉强恢复成比较中性的样子。"

    old "You know who I'm talking about. I heard that you spent time with other people..."
    new "You know who I'm talking about. I heard that you spent time with other people...\n你知道我说的是谁。我听说你和别人待在一起……"

    old "That's only natural, isn't it? I'm a leader. Getting to know my team better is essential. Why-"
    new "That's only natural, isn't it? I'm a leader. Getting to know my team better is essential. Why-\n这不是很自然吗？我是个领袖。更好地了解我的团队是必要的。为什么——"

    old "And this includes sleeping with them?"
    new "And this includes sleeping with them?\n这也包括和他们上床吗？"

    old "What? I didn't-"
    new "What? I didn't-\n什么？我没有——"

    old "[protag], don't lie to me. Please. I know everything. Asking this of you might seem like a bit too much, but..."
    new "[protag], don't lie to me. Please. I know everything. Asking this of you might seem like a bit too much, but...\n[protag]，别对我撒谎。求你了。我全都知道了。这样问你也许有点过分，但是……"

    old "I am not ready to share you with others and I never will be. I don't WANT to."
    new "I am not ready to share you with others and I never will be. I don't WANT to.\n我还没准备好和别人分享你，而且我永远不会。我也不想。"

    old "I want you to be mine. Only mine."
    new "I want you to be mine. Only mine.\n我想要你属于我。只属于我。"

    old "Do you feel the same? And don't worry, your answer won't have any impact on our mission. I will still follow you as before. I just... I need to know one way or the other to put my mind at ease."
    new "Do you feel the same? And don't worry, your answer won't have any impact on our mission. I will still follow you as before. I just... I need to know one way or the other to put my mind at ease.\n你也有同样的感觉吗？别担心，你的回答不会对我们的任务有任何影响。我仍会像从前一样追随你。我只是……我需要知道答案，无论哪一种，好让我安心。"

    old "With everything going on right now... I'm sorry, Vaeril. I don't feel cofident making a decision like that right now."
    new "With everything going on right now... I'm sorry, Vaeril. I don't feel cofident making a decision like that right now.\n眼下发生了这么多事……对不起，Vaeril。我现在没有信心做出这样的决定。"

    old "Vaeril's gaze drops to the floor."
    new "Vaeril's gaze drops to the floor.\nVaeril 的目光垂落到地板上。"

    old "I have more important things in my mind, and-"
    new "I have more important things in my mind, and-\n我脑子里有更重要的事，而且——"

    old "There's no need to explain, [protag]. I got my answer."
    new "There's no need to explain, [protag]. I got my answer.\n不必解释了，[protag]。我得到答案了。"

    old "Wait! It wasn't a 'no'."
    new "Wait! It wasn't a 'no'.\n等等！那不是'不'。"

    old "It wasn't a yes. That's what matters, [protag]."
    new "It wasn't a yes. That's what matters, [protag].\n可也不是'是'。那才是重点，[protag]。"

    old "After what you told me that night at the inn... After what happened after... How could you just say that you don't know?"
    new "After what you told me that night at the inn... After what happened after... How could you just say that you don't know?\n那晚在客栈你对我说过那些话之后……在那之后发生了那些事之后……你怎么能只说一句你不知道？"

    old "...Perhaps, you're right."
    new "...Perhaps, you're right.\n……也许，你是对的。"

    old "I hope that whoever ends up with you will treat you well. As for me, I need some time alone now."
    new "I hope that whoever ends up with you will treat you well. As for me, I need some time alone now.\n我希望最终和你在一起的人，能好好待你。至于我，现在需要一个人静一静。"

    old "I leave the inn, feeling bad for Vaeril."
    new "I leave the inn, feeling bad for Vaeril.\n我离开客栈，为 Vaeril 感到难过。"

    old "I don't doubt that he'll continue fighting at my side until the N'Mar crisis is over. But after that? I'm not sure. He may not want to see me ever again after this."
    new "I don't doubt that he'll continue fighting at my side until the N'Mar crisis is over. But after that? I'm not sure. He may not want to see me ever again after this.\n我不怀疑他会继续在我身边战斗，直到 N'Mar 危机结束。但那之后呢？我不确定。也许这之后，他再也不想见到我了。"

    old "Vaeril, I owe you an apology."
    new "Vaeril, I owe you an apology.\nVaeril，我欠你一个道歉。"

    old "I take Vaeril's hands in mine and squeeze them affectionately as I stare into his blue eyes and hope that my sincerity gets through to him."
    new "I take Vaeril's hands in mine and squeeze them affectionately as I stare into his blue eyes and hope that my sincerity gets through to him.\n我握住 Vaeril 的双手，深情地握了握，同时凝视着他蓝色的眼睛，希望我的真诚能传达到他心里。"

    old "We hadn't defined our relationship and I used that to justify what I did at the time but... I was wrong to do that to you."
    new "We hadn't defined our relationship and I used that to justify what I did at the time but... I was wrong to do that to you.\n我们当初没有明确我们的关系，而我利用这一点为自己当时的行为开脱，但是……那样对你是我的错。"

    old "I should have been more honest with you. I should have told you that I was seeing other people."
    new "I should have been more honest with you. I should have told you that I was seeing other people.\n我本该对你更坦诚。我本该告诉你，我还在和别人交往。"

    old "Vaeril lets out a sigh, and then shows me a feeble smile."
    new "Vaeril lets out a sigh, and then shows me a feeble smile.\nVaeril 叹了口气，然后对我挤出一个勉强的微笑。"

    old "Yes, you should have."
    new "Yes, you should have.\n是的，你本该如此。"

    old "But I promise you this: from today on, you'll be the only one. I'll still need to meet with the others, of course, but it'll only be to talk."
    new "But I promise you this: from today on, you'll be the only one. I'll still need to meet with the others, of course, but it'll only be to talk.\n但我向你保证：从今天起，你会是唯一的一个。当然，我仍需要和其他人见面，但那只是谈事而已。"

    old "That's all I ask, [protag]."
    new "That's all I ask, [protag].\n这就是我全部所求，[protag]。"

    old "I decide to stay with Vaeril at the inn. I feel a bit guilty at how I behaved. Vaeril is such a sweet person. I'll be loyal to him in future."
    new "I decide to stay with Vaeril at the inn. I feel a bit guilty at how I behaved. Vaeril is such a sweet person. I'll be loyal to him in future.\n我决定留在客栈陪 Vaeril。我对自己的行为感到有点内疚。Vaeril 是那么温柔的人。今后我会忠于他。"

    old "I meet up with Vaeril near the great forest border."
    new "I meet up with Vaeril near the great forest border.\n我在 Great Forest 边界附近与 Vaeril 会合。"

    old "Hello, Vaeril."
    new "Hello, Vaeril.\n你好，Vaeril。"

    old "My dear [protag]. Come here."
    new "My dear [protag]. Come here.\n亲爱的[protag]。过来。"

    old "He wraps me in a strong embrace. We kiss, and then he speaks."
    new "He wraps me in a strong embrace. We kiss, and then he speaks.\n他把我拥入有力的怀抱。我们亲吻，然后他开口说话。"

    old "Thank you for joining me."
    new "Thank you for joining me.\n谢谢你愿意来陪我。"

    old "It's my pleasure, Vaeril."
    new "It's my pleasure, Vaeril.\n这是我的荣幸，Vaeril。"

    old "Can you tell me what this is about though? The message I got was a bit cryptic. Are you in trouble or something?"
    new "Can you tell me what this is about though? The message I got was a bit cryptic. Are you in trouble or something?\n不过你能告诉我这是怎么回事吗？我收到的消息有点隐晦。你是遇到什么麻烦了吗？"

    old "Oh, it's nothing like that. I'm sorry if I worried you. It's just..."
    new "Oh, it's nothing like that. I'm sorry if I worried you. It's just...\n哦，不是那种事。抱歉让你担心了。只是……"

    old "I like Grimoire. However, I am an elf. A druid even. I miss the forest."
    new "I like Grimoire. However, I am an elf. A druid even. I miss the forest.\n我喜欢 Grimoire。不过，我是个 Elf。甚至还是个德鲁伊。我想念森林。"

    old "Yes, I know what you're talking about. I like Grimoire, but staying away from the forest for days... it hurts."
    new "Yes, I know what you're talking about. I like Grimoire, but staying away from the forest for days... it hurts.\n是的，我明白你的意思。我喜欢 Grimoire，但一连几天远离森林……很难受。"

    old "I don't know what the future has in store for us. Some of us might never come back from our final assault-"
    new "I don't know what the future has in store for us. Some of us might never come back from our final assault-\n我不知道未来有什么在等着我们。我们中有些人可能再也不会从最后的进攻中回来了——"

    old "Don't say that!"
    new "Don't say that!\n别这么说！"

    old "[protag], you know that this is true. I hope that we will all come back safely, of course, but there is always a chance that won't happen."
    new "[protag], you know that this is true. I hope that we will all come back safely, of course, but there is always a chance that won't happen.\n[protag]，你知道这是真的。我当然希望我们都能平安归来，但总有可能事与愿违。"

    old "Knowing that, I want to spend as much of my time in nature as possible before we head to N'Mar. Of course, I can't just come here alone."
    new "Knowing that, I want to spend as much of my time in nature as possible before we head to N'Mar. Of course, I can't just come here alone.\n正因知道这一点，我想在前往 N'Mar 之前，尽可能多地在自然中度过。当然，我不能独自来这里。"

    old "You fear the great forest elves might still be hunting you?"
    new "You fear the great forest elves might still be hunting you?\n你担心 Great Forest 的 Elves 可能还在追捕你？"

    old "I don't know. Kusho has sort of forgiven me, but the Elder Druids of Grandtree? I don't think so."
    new "I don't know. Kusho has sort of forgiven me, but the Elder Druids of Grandtree? I don't think so.\n我不知道。Kusho 算是原谅我了，但 Grandtree 的长老德鲁伊呢？我觉得不会。"

    old "Traveling with you should be safe though. They should recognize you and I doubt that they'd risk attacking the Envoy of Grimoire."
    new "Traveling with you should be safe though. They should recognize you and I doubt that they'd risk attacking the Envoy of Grimoire.\n不过与你同行应该安全。他们应该认得你，我怀疑他们不敢冒险袭击 Grimoire 特使。"

    old "Is that so? You're making me feel important."
    new "Is that so? You're making me feel important.\n是吗？你让我觉得自己很重要。"

    old "You are important to me. You always were."
    new "You are important to me. You always were.\n你对我很重要。一直都是。"

    old "I take his hand in mine and then the two of us start walking deeper into the forest together."
    new "I take his hand in mine and then the two of us start walking deeper into the forest together.\n我握住他的手，然后我们两人一起向森林深处走去。"

    old "However, the area Vaeril guides me to is full of brambles and spikes, more so than anywhere else I've been."
    new "However, the area Vaeril guides me to is full of brambles and spikes, more so than anywhere else I've been.\n然而，Vaeril 领我去的这片地方满是荆棘和尖刺，比我去过的任何地方都多。"

    old "I apologize, my love. I picked this place because it's so impervious that most people wouldn't bother passing through, but perhaps it wasn't such a great idea."
    new "I apologize, my love. I picked this place because it's so impervious that most people wouldn't bother passing through, but perhaps it wasn't such a great idea.\n抱歉，我的爱人。我选这里是因为它太难穿行，大多数人都不愿经过，但也许这不是个好主意。"

    old "<Scratch>"
    new "<Scratch>\n<Scratch>"

    old "I hear a ripping sound and turn back towards Vaeril. Luckily, he seems to be okay. I can't say the same for his outfit, however. The brambles have torn open the chest part of his robe!"
    new "I hear a ripping sound and turn back towards Vaeril. Luckily, he seems to be okay. I can't say the same for his outfit, however. The brambles have torn open the chest part of his robe!\n我听到一声撕裂声，转身看向 Vaeril。幸运的是，他似乎没事。不过他的衣服就不好说了。荆棘把他长袍的胸口部分撕开了！"

    old "Are you all right?"
    new "Are you all right?\n你没事吧？"

    old "Vaeril manages to keep his expression serious. I try to respectfully do the same, but the situation is becoming almost comical."
    new "Vaeril manages to keep his expression serious. I try to respectfully do the same, but the situation is becoming almost comical.\nVaeril 勉强保持着严肃的表情。我也尽量郑重其事，但眼下这情形几乎变得有些滑稽。"

    old "Yes, yes! I'm fine. Don't worry, let's just keep going!"
    new "Yes, yes! I'm fine. Don't worry, let's just keep going!\n没事，没事！我很好。别担心，我们继续走吧！"

    old "I don't know, Vaeril. You're already covered in scratches and your outfit... Well, it's getting more revealing by the minute."
    new "I don't know, Vaeril. You're already covered in scratches and your outfit... Well, it's getting more revealing by the minute.\n我说不准，Vaeril。你已经满身刮痕，你的衣服……嗯，它正一刻比一刻更暴露。"

    old "The scratches aren't an issue. As for my clothes..."
    new "The scratches aren't an issue. As for my clothes...\n刮痕不是问题。至于我的衣服……"

    old "Come on. We're elves. Don't act like it's something strange for us."
    new "Come on. We're elves. Don't act like it's something strange for us.\n别这样。我们是 Elves。别表现得这好像对我们来说是件奇怪的事。"

    old "You always say that elves are one with nature and that it's not uncommon for them to be naked in middle of it."
    new "You always say that elves are one with nature and that it's not uncommon for them to be naked in middle of it.\n你总说 Elves 与自然融为一体，说他们在大自然中赤身裸体并不罕见。"

    old "I know, but..."
    new "I know, but...\n我知道，不过……"

    old "Are you worried that someone might come? Here, in this forsaken nest of brambles and thorns?"
    new "Are you worried that someone might come? Here, in this forsaken nest of brambles and thorns?\n你是担心会有人来吗？在这种被遗忘的荆棘和尖刺窝里？"

    old "I... suppose that you are right. Someone would have to be crazy to venture all the way out here."
    new "I... suppose that you are right. Someone would have to be crazy to venture all the way out here.\n我……想来你是对的。得有多疯狂才会一路冒险跑到这里来。"

    old "They'd have to be more than crazy. They'd have to be absolutely insane-- in a charming and endearing sort of way, of course."
    new "They'd have to be more than crazy. They'd have to be absolutely insane-- in a charming and endearing sort of way, of course.\n岂止是疯狂。他们得彻底疯掉——当然，是那种迷人又讨喜的疯法。"

    old "Vaeril chuckles and then begins to slowly undress. I follow his lead, taking in the details of Vaeril's body as we go. He's more muscular than I'd expect a magic user to be."
    new "Vaeril chuckles and then begins to slowly undress. I follow his lead, taking in the details of Vaeril's body as we go. He's more muscular than I'd expect a magic user to be.\nVaeril 轻笑起来，然后开始慢慢脱衣。我跟着他照做，一边打量 Vaeril 身体的细节。他的肌肉比我预想中一个施法者该有的更强健。"

    old "It doesn't get any better up ahead. Going through this will take hours."
    new "It doesn't get any better up ahead. Going through this will take hours.\n前面也好不到哪去。穿过去要花上好几个小时。"

    old "Damn. If only I could use a little bit of my magic... to open a passage."
    new "Damn. If only I could use a little bit of my magic... to open a passage.\n该死。要是能用一点我的魔法……开出一条通道就好了。"

    old "That'd just make the great forest elves even angrier at you."
    new "That'd just make the great forest elves even angrier at you.\n那只会让 Great Forest 的 Elves 对你更恼火。"

    old "Vaeril sighs, finally admitting defeat."
    new "Vaeril sighs, finally admitting defeat.\nVaeril 叹了口气，终于承认了失败。"

    old "You're right, [protag]. I'm sorry. That was a stupid thought."
    new "You're right, [protag]. I'm sorry. That was a stupid thought.\n你说得对，[protag]。抱歉。那是个愚蠢的想法。"

    old "What? But we just started going into the forest!"
    new "What? But we just started going into the forest!\n什么？可我们才刚刚开始进森林啊！"

    old "First of all, unless you're planning on walking back to Grimoire completely naked, moving forward is not a good idea."
    new "First of all, unless you're planning on walking back to Grimoire completely naked, moving forward is not a good idea.\n首先，除非你打算一丝不挂地走回 Grimoire，否则继续前进可不是个好主意。"

    old "...I suppose I can't exactly argue with that."
    new "...I suppose I can't exactly argue with that.\n……我想这一点我确实没法反驳。"

    old "Second, while I enjoy spending time with you, my time is not unlimited. I don't want to spend the little bit of it that I actually have with you walking through a dense forest and getting my clothes torn."
    new "Second, while I enjoy spending time with you, my time is not unlimited. I don't want to spend the little bit of it that I actually have with you walking through a dense forest and getting my clothes torn.\n其次，虽然我很享受和你共度时光，但我的时间并不宽裕。我不想把真正属于我的那一点点时间，花在穿过密林、把衣服扯破上。"

    old "I see. You're right, of course. Let's go back."
    new "I see. You're right, of course. Let's go back.\n明白了。你说得当然对。我们回去吧。"

    old "He seems sad but, honestly, I think that this is the best solution. Continuing along this path would be foolish to say the least."
    new "He seems sad but, honestly, I think that this is the best solution. Continuing along this path would be foolish to say the least.\n他看起来有些难过，但老实说，我认为这是最好的解决办法。继续沿着这条路走，至少可以说是愚蠢的。"

    old "Once we're back in Grimoire, I''ll see what I can do to fix your outfit."
    new "Once we're back in Grimoire, I''ll see what I can do to fix your outfit.\n等我们回到 Grimoire，我会看看能怎么修补你的衣服。"

    old "Hm? I didn't know that you knew how to sew."
    new "Hm? I didn't know that you knew how to sew.\n嗯？我不知道你还会缝纫。"

    old "It's one of my many hidden talents!"
    new "It's one of my many hidden talents!\n这是我众多隐藏才能之一！"

    old "We head back to Grimoire's inn where Vaeril is staying. Once we're there, he strips down so I can take a look at his clothes."
    new "We head back to Grimoire's inn where Vaeril is staying. Once we're there, he strips down so I can take a look at his clothes.\n我们回到 Grimoire 的客栈，Vaeril 就住在那儿。一到那里，他便脱去衣服，好让我看看他的衣服。"

    old "However, it's not Vaeril's clothes that I end up taking a closer look at that night."
    new "However, it's not Vaeril's clothes that I end up taking a closer look at that night.\n然而，那一夜我最终细细打量的，并不是 Vaeril 的衣服。"

    old "Let's just say that we quickly forgot about the problem at hand and started doing other, more interesting, activities..."
    new "Let's just say that we quickly forgot about the problem at hand and started doing other, more interesting, activities...\n这么说吧，我们很快就忘了手头的问题，开始做些别的、更有趣的活动……"

    old "Let's try to find a spot where we can lie down and relax."
    new "Let's try to find a spot where we can lie down and relax.\n我们找个能躺下来放松的地方吧。"

    old "Relax. Now that's something I'd like to."
    new "Relax. Now that's something I'd like to.\n放松。这正是我想做的事。"

    old "After a few minutes, we find the perfect spot. The only noises are the birds and the wind blowing through the trees. It's really wonderful."
    new "After a few minutes, we find the perfect spot. The only noises are the birds and the wind blowing through the trees. It's really wonderful.\n几分钟后，我们找到了完美的地点。四周只有鸟鸣和吹过树间的风声。实在太美妙了。"

    old "We spend a few hours there, doing... other things. When we get back to Grimoire, I feel fully energized and ready to take on any challenge that the undead can throw at us."
    new "We spend a few hours there, doing... other things. When we get back to Grimoire, I feel fully energized and ready to take on any challenge that the undead can throw at us.\n我们在那里待了几个小时，做些……别的事。等回到 Grimoire 时，我浑身充满了干劲，准备好迎接亡灵可能抛给我们的任何挑战。"

    old "I meet with Vaeril at Grimoire's inn just before sunset."
    new "I meet with Vaeril at Grimoire's inn just before sunset.\n我在日落前来到 Grimoire 的客栈与 Vaeril 会面。"

    old "I have a surprise for you."
    new "I have a surprise for you.\n我有个惊喜给你。"

    old "You know I don't like surprises..."
    new "You know I don't like surprises...\n你知道我不喜欢惊喜……"

    old "This surprise is one you'll like. Trust me."
    new "This surprise is one you'll like. Trust me.\n这个惊喜你会喜欢的。相信我。"

    old "Hm. Alright..."
    new "Hm. Alright...\n嗯。好吧……"

    old "Good. Now, come on. Follow me."
    new "Good. Now, come on. Follow me.\n很好。那么，走吧，跟我来。"

    old "It's not too far."
    new "It's not too far.\n不算太远。"

    old "This is Grimoire's central garden."
    new "This is Grimoire's central garden.\n这里是 Grimoire 的中央花园。"

    old "Indeed, it is."
    new "Indeed, it is.\n的确如此。"

    old "We pass by two guards who hail me in front of the garden's gates."
    new "We pass by two guards who hail me in front of the garden's gates.\n我们经过两名守卫，他们在花园大门前向我致意。"

    old "Why are there guards at the entrance? I've never seen them before."
    new "Why are there guards at the entrance? I've never seen them before.\n入口处为什么会有守卫？我以前从没见过。"

    old "Let's just say that they have orders to block all citizens from accessing the garden until further notice."
    new "Let's just say that they have orders to block all citizens from accessing the garden until further notice.\n这么说吧，他们奉命在另行通知之前，阻止所有市民进入花园。"

    old "Why? What did you tell them?"
    new "Why? What did you tell them?\n为什么？你跟他们说了什么？"

    old "Oh, nothing much. Just that we're going to perform a powerful nature ritual and that we need to be left alone and undisturbed in order for it to work."
    new "Oh, nothing much. Just that we're going to perform a powerful nature ritual and that we need to be left alone and undisturbed in order for it to work.\n哦，没什么。只是说我们要举行一场强大的自然仪式，为了仪式生效，需要独处、不受打扰。"

    old "What!? You lied to the Council!?"
    new "What!? You lied to the Council!?\n什么！？你骗了议会！？"

    old "It's fine, Vaeril. The council won't ask any questions. As long as I get results, they have nothing to complain about. And considering all the work we've all done up until now... Well, I think they can forgive this one small abuse of power."
    new "It's fine, Vaeril. The council won't ask any questions. As long as I get results, they have nothing to complain about. And considering all the work we've all done up until now... Well, I think they can forgive this one small abuse of power.\n没关系，Vaeril。议会什么都不会问。只要我能拿出成果，他们就没话可说。再想想我们迄今为止所做的一切……嗯，我想这点小小的以权谋私，他们是可以原谅的。"

    old "I can't believe it."
    new "I can't believe it.\n真不敢相信。"

    old "Come, let's lie down on the grass."
    new "Come, let's lie down on the grass.\n来吧，我们躺到草地上。"

    old "Vaeril is still a bit unsure at first but, after lying down with me for awhile, he eventually relaxes and starts to enjoy himself. We watch as the sun sets, its rays filtering magnificently through the trees. It's absolutely perfect. Even better than I hoped it'd be."
    new "Vaeril is still a bit unsure at first but, after lying down with me for awhile, he eventually relaxes and starts to enjoy himself. We watch as the sun sets, its rays filtering magnificently through the trees. It's absolutely perfect. Even better than I hoped it'd be.\nVaeril 起初还有点犹豫，但和我一起躺了一会儿后，他终于放松下来，开始享受。我们看着夕阳西沉，阳光穿过树木，洒下绝美的光。这一切完美极了，甚至比我期望的还要好。"

    old "This is beautiful."
    new "This is beautiful.\n这太美了。"

    old "It is. It's not as beautiful as you though."
    new "It is. It's not as beautiful as you though.\n是啊。不过没有你美。"

    old "What you did for me today. It's... Damn! I can't even begin to describe it in words."
    new "What you did for me today. It's... Damn! I can't even begin to describe it in words.\n你今天为我做的这一切。这……该死！我甚至无法用言语开始形容。"

    old "Then don't."
    new "Then don't.\n那就别形容。"

    old "I close my eyes for a moment. It's not as quiet as the forest, but it's still a nice atmosphere overall. Here in the garden with Vaeril at my side, it's easy to forget that we're in the middle of a city."
    new "I close my eyes for a moment. It's not as quiet as the forest, but it's still a nice atmosphere overall. Here in the garden with Vaeril at my side, it's easy to forget that we're in the middle of a city.\n我闭了一会儿眼睛。这里没有森林那么安静，但整体氛围依然很好。在这花园里，有 Vaeril 陪在我身边，很容易让人忘记我们正身处一座城市的中央。"

    old "When I open my eyes again, I turn my head to look at Vaeril. I have to do a double take to make sure I'm not imagining things because Vaeril is suddenly naked."
    new "When I open my eyes again, I turn my head to look at Vaeril. I have to do a double take to make sure I'm not imagining things because Vaeril is suddenly naked.\n当我再次睁开眼，转头看向 Vaeril。我不得不再看上一眼，好确认自己不是眼花——因为 Vaeril 突然就赤身裸体了。"

    old "Wh-when did that happen?"
    new "Wh-when did that happen?\n什、什么时候的事？"

    old "I have gotten rather skilled at undressing quickly thanks to you."
    new "I have gotten rather skilled at undressing quickly thanks to you.\n多亏了你，我如今脱衣服的速度已经相当娴熟。"

    old "We both laugh."
    new "We both laugh.\n我们俩都笑了。"

    old "When I open my eyes again, I see Vaeril next to me. His eyes are closed. On his face a calm, relaxed expression."
    new "When I open my eyes again, I see Vaeril next to me. His eyes are closed. On his face a calm, relaxed expression.\n当我再次睁开眼，看到 Vaeril 就在我身旁。他的眼睛闭着，脸上是一副平静而放松的神情。"

    old "For a moment I thought you were sleeping."
    new "For a moment I thought you were sleeping.\n有一瞬间我还以为你睡着了。"

    old "No, don't worry. I was only listening to the distant city noises. Normally, I don't like them. But now... together with you in this place, in this moment? It's relaxing, almost hypnotizing."
    new "No, don't worry. I was only listening to the distant city noises. Normally, I don't like them. But now... together with you in this place, in this moment? It's relaxing, almost hypnotizing.\n没有，别担心。我只是在听远处城市的声音。平时我并不喜欢这些声音。但现在……和你一起，在这里，在这一刻？很放松，几乎让人着迷。"

    old "I could stay here, looking at you like this for the rest of the day."
    new "I could stay here, looking at you like this for the rest of the day.\n我可以就这样看着你，在这里待上一整天。"

    old "But, unfortunately, we don't have that much time, right?"
    new "But, unfortunately, we don't have that much time, right?\n可惜，我们没有那么多时间，对吧？"

    old "I sigh. He's right, of course."
    new "I sigh. He's right, of course.\n我叹了口气。他说得当然没错。"

    old "No, unfortunately."
    new "No, unfortunately.\n没有，真可惜。"

    old "Then we'd better get started."
    new "Then we'd better get started.\n那我们最好开始吧。"

    old "Started? On what, exactly?"
    new "Started? On what, exactly?\n开始？具体开始什么？"

    old "The magic ritual, of course!"
    new "The magic ritual, of course!\n当然是魔法仪式！"

    old "He takes my hand and pulls me so that I land on top of him. I laugh and he responds with a mirthful laugh of his own."
    new "He takes my hand and pulls me so that I land on top of him. I laugh and he responds with a mirthful laugh of his own.\n他抓住我的手一拉，让我落在他身上。我笑了，他也报以一阵欢快的笑。"

    old "Then, I lean over and kiss him. One of his hands runs up the back of my neck while the other one paws blindly at my clothes as our kiss intensifies."
    new "Then, I lean over and kiss him. One of his hands runs up the back of my neck while the other one paws blindly at my clothes as our kiss intensifies.\n随后，我俯身吻他。他的一只手沿着我颈后往上摸，另一只手则在我们热吻渐深时，盲目地撕扯着我的衣服。"

    old "I think this is going to be an unforgettable magic ritual."
    new "I think this is going to be an unforgettable magic ritual.\n我想这会是一场令人难忘的魔法仪式。"

    old "Hmm? It appears as though we have an interloper."
    new "Hmm? It appears as though we have an interloper.\n嗯？看来我们这里来了个不速之客。"

    old "I tense up, and assume a combat stance. Whether my next move is to run or fight, I intend to be ready for it."
    new "I tense up, and assume a combat stance. Whether my next move is to run or fight, I intend to be ready for it.\n我绷紧身体，摆出战斗姿态。无论下一步是逃还是战，我都要做好准备。"

    old "Please, [prace]. Whatever weapons you may have, let them remain hidden. We have no quarrel with you."
    new "Please, [prace]. Whatever weapons you may have, let them remain hidden. We have no quarrel with you.\n请别这样，[prace]。不管你带着什么武器，都让它继续藏着吧。我们与你并无过节。"

    old "Who are you, and what are you doing here?"
    new "Who are you, and what are you doing here?\n你们是谁，在这里做什么？"

    old "Ah, where are my manners? I'm Zachary, and this here is my Valery."
    new "Ah, where are my manners? I'm Zachary, and this here is my Valery.\n啊，是我失礼了。我是 Zachary，这位是我的 Valery。"

    old "Will you do us the courtesy of telling us your name?"
    new "Will you do us the courtesy of telling us your name?\n能否赏脸告诉我们你的名字？"

    old "A pleasure, [protag]. Valery and I are simply come here to investigate an...anomaly."
    new "A pleasure, [protag]. Valery and I are simply come here to investigate an...anomaly.\n幸会，[protag]。Valery 和我只是来这里调查一处……异常。"

    old "Funny, I came here for the exact same reason."
    new "Funny, I came here for the exact same reason.\n有意思，我来这里也是出于同样的原因。"

    old "Ah, then it would appear we share a mission. Perhaps we can work together."
    new "Ah, then it would appear we share a mission. Perhaps we can work together.\n啊，那我们似乎有着共同的任务。也许我们可以合作。"

    old "I came here hoping to find the source of a blight that has been plaguing these lands. I thought that it might be caused by N'Mar's vampires, and here I find two vampires. Quite a coincidence."
    new "I came here hoping to find the source of a blight that has been plaguing these lands. I thought that it might be caused by N'Mar's vampires, and here I find two vampires. Quite a coincidence.\n我来这里，本想找到一直困扰这片土地的枯萎之害的源头。我原以为它可能是由 N'Mar 的 Vampires 引起的，结果就在这里撞见两个 Vampires。真是巧了。"

    old "One vampire, actually. Valery, you see, hasn't fully turned. Right now, she is but a lowly thrall."
    new "One vampire, actually. Valery, you see, hasn't fully turned. Right now, she is but a lowly thrall.\n实际上是一个 Vampire。你瞧，Valery 还没有完全转化。眼下她不过是个低微的血仆。"

    old "Valery pulls back her collar to reveal a pair of bite marks on her neck, which I can only assume Zachary is responsible for."
    new "Valery pulls back her collar to reveal a pair of bite marks on her neck, which I can only assume Zachary is responsible for.\nValery 拉开她的领口，露出脖子上的一对咬痕，我只能推测那是 Zachary 所为。"

    old "She's a loyal one, but still no vampire. Time will see to that, however."
    new "She's a loyal one, but still no vampire. Time will see to that, however.\n她是个忠心的仆从，不过还算不上 Vampire。然而时间会促成这一切。"

    old "As for your insinuation that my companion and I are in some way responsible for the corruption on these lands, I must vehemently deny any responsibility. I can see your line of thinking, and the truth is that you are correct in assuming that the vampires of N'Mar are in some way responsible. But those vampires are not my people. Not any more, at least."
    new "As for your insinuation that my companion and I are in some way responsible for the corruption on these lands, I must vehemently deny any responsibility. I can see your line of thinking, and the truth is that you are correct in assuming that the vampires of N'Mar are in some way responsible. But those vampires are not my people. Not any more, at least.\n至于你暗示我和我的同伴与这片土地的腐化多少有关，我必须坚决否认任何责任。我能看出你的思路，而事实是，你推测 N'Mar 的 Vampires 与此多少有关，这没错。但那些 Vampires 不是我的人。至少现在不再是了。"

    old "It sounds like you are involved with them."
    new "It sounds like you are involved with them.\n听起来你和他们打过交道。"

    old "Yes. I had dreams of one day ascending to the throne of that castle. I got quite good at climbing the ranks, you know."
    new "Yes. I had dreams of one day ascending to the throne of that castle. I got quite good at climbing the ranks, you know.\n是的。我曾经梦想有朝一日登上那座城堡的王座。要知道，我很擅长一路往上爬。"

    old "But climbing the ranks makes you more enemies than friends, and the problem with having vampires as enemies is that they tend to hold grudges, and they live quite a long time. Eventually I realized that I was surrounded by enemies, and found myself unwanted within the walls of that castle."
    new "But climbing the ranks makes you more enemies than friends, and the problem with having vampires as enemies is that they tend to hold grudges, and they live quite a long time. Eventually I realized that I was surrounded by enemies, and found myself unwanted within the walls of that castle.\n但往上爬会让你树敌多过交友，而把 Vampires 当成敌人的麻烦在于，他们记仇，而且寿命极长。最终我意识到自己已四面受敌，在那座城堡的城墙内成了不受欢迎的人。"

    old "They banished you?"
    new "They banished you?\n他们放逐了你？"

    old "In a manner of speaking. I suppose that would make the vampires that currently inhabit the castle of N'Mar my enemies. I presume the same is true of you as well."
    new "In a manner of speaking. I suppose that would make the vampires that currently inhabit the castle of N'Mar my enemies. I presume the same is true of you as well.\n算是吧。我想这样一来，眼下盘踞在 N'Mar 城堡里的那些 Vampires 就成了我的敌人。我猜你也同样如此。"

    old "Yes, I am currently opposing the corruption of N'Mar."
    new "Yes, I am currently opposing the corruption of N'Mar.\n是的，我目前正在对抗 N'Mar 的腐化。"

    old "Well then, being that we share a common enemy, I suppose that would make us friends, would it not?"
    new "Well then, being that we share a common enemy, I suppose that would make us friends, would it not?\n那么，既然我们有共同的敌人，我想这就让我们成了朋友，不是吗？"

    old "I guess that would make us friends. At the very least, we share a common interest."
    new "I guess that would make us friends. At the very least, we share a common interest.\n我想那确实让我们成了朋友。至少，我们有共同的利益。"

    old "Isn't that wonderful, Valery? I wasn't expecting to make a friend today."
    new "Isn't that wonderful, Valery? I wasn't expecting to make a friend today.\n这不是很好吗，Valery？我今天本没指望能交到朋友。"

    old "Yes, it is quite lovely to have made a new friend."
    new "Yes, it is quite lovely to have made a new friend.\n是啊，能交到新朋友，实在令人愉快。"

    old "Valery and I don't have much in the way of friends, you see. Ever since I was...evicted from the castle, I've found it hard to find companions. Vampires are not well-liked, you see."
    new "Valery and I don't have much in the way of friends, you see. Ever since I was...evicted from the castle, I've found it hard to find companions. Vampires are not well-liked, you see.\nValery 和我没什么朋友，你明白的。自从我被……逐出城堡之后，就很难找到同伴。要知道，Vampires 并不招人喜欢。"

    old "To consumate our new friendship, I'd like to offer you a gift."
    new "To consumate our new friendship, I'd like to offer you a gift.\n为了成全我们这份新友谊，我想送你一份礼物。"

    old "I'm sorry, Zachary. I hope you'll forgive me if I find myself a bit hesitant to call a vampire 'friend,' especially one that I just met."
    new "I'm sorry, Zachary. I hope you'll forgive me if I find myself a bit hesitant to call a vampire 'friend,' especially one that I just met.\n抱歉，Zachary。如果我发现自己有点犹豫，不愿把一个 Vampire 称作'朋友'——尤其是一个刚刚认识的——还请你见谅。"

    old "Of course, I understand. The world has little fondness for vampires, and knowing the exploits of my...friends at N'Mar, I can't say that I blame them. I'm no saint either, of course."
    new "Of course, I understand. The world has little fondness for vampires, and knowing the exploits of my...friends at N'Mar, I can't say that I blame them. I'm no saint either, of course.\n当然，我理解。这世界对 Vampires 本就没多少好感，再想想我在 N'Mar 的那些……朋友的所作所为，我也不能怪世人。我当然也不是什么圣人。"

    old "Still, I hope that for the time being we can at least be friendly acquaintences. As a gesture of goodwill, I'd like to offer you a small gift."
    new "Still, I hope that for the time being we can at least be friendly acquaintences. As a gesture of goodwill, I'd like to offer you a small gift.\n不过，我希望眼下我们至少能友好相处。作为善意的表示，我想送你一份小礼物。"

    old "Zachary reaches into his breast pocket and pulls out a small vial. He tosses it to me, and I snatch it from the air."
    new "Zachary reaches into his breast pocket and pulls out a small vial. He tosses it to me, and I snatch it from the air.\nZachary 把手伸进胸前的口袋，掏出一个小瓶。他把瓶子抛给我，我一把从空中接住。"

    old "I study the vial. It's a thick, dark-colored liquid, but it's hard to make out its exact color in the dim light."
    new "I study the vial. It's a thick, dark-colored liquid, but it's hard to make out its exact color in the dim light.\n我端详着瓶子。里面是一种浓稠的深色液体，但在昏暗的光线下很难看清它确切的颜色。"

    old "It's blood, of course. Taken from Valery, while she's still in a position to give blood."
    new "It's blood, of course. Taken from Valery, while she's still in a position to give blood.\n当然是血。是从 Valery 身上取的，趁她还能供血的时候。"

    old "Please, enjoy it."
    new "Please, enjoy it.\n请享用吧。"

    old "I don't see what use someone like me has for this."
    new "I don't see what use someone like me has for this.\n我看不出像我这样的人要这东西有什么用。"

    old "You said you have a quarrel with the beasts of N'Mar, yes? Vampires, of course, but also ghouls and other sorts. The undead thirst for blood. And now you have a vial of something they desire. Perhaps it will come in handy if you ever need to parley with them, yes?"
    new "You said you have a quarrel with the beasts of N'Mar, yes? Vampires, of course, but also ghouls and other sorts. The undead thirst for blood. And now you have a vial of something they desire. Perhaps it will come in handy if you ever need to parley with them, yes?\n你说过你和 N'Mar 的野兽们有过节，对吧？当然是 Vampires，但还有食尸鬼和其他种类。亡灵都渴望鲜血。现在你手上就有一小瓶它们渴求的东西。将来若需要与它们谈判，说不定能派上用场，是吧？"

    old "It's very pure."
    new "It's very pure.\n它非常纯净。"

    old "Of course it is, dear Valery. Directly from your neck into that glass vial. You won't find anything fresher. I hope it proves useful in your future endeavors."
    new "Of course it is, dear Valery. Directly from your neck into that glass vial. You won't find anything fresher. I hope it proves useful in your future endeavors.\n当然了，亲爱的 Valery。直接从你的脖子流进那玻璃瓶里。你再也找不到比这更新鲜的了。希望它在你将来的行动中能证明有用。"

    old "Thank...you?"
    new "Thank...you?\n谢……谢？"

    old "Well, I think we've spent enough time looking about. I believe it is time for me and Valery to bid you adieu."
    new "Well, I think we've spent enough time looking about. I believe it is time for me and Valery to bid you adieu.\n好了，我想我们四处看得也够久了。我和 Valery 该向你道别了。"

    old "Wait. I came here to investigate the blight."
    new "Wait. I came here to investigate the blight.\n等等。我是来调查枯萎之害的。"

    old "Yes, as did we. As I told you, I suspected that N'Mar might be somehow responsible for odd phenomena in this area, and my suspicions were confirmed."
    new "Yes, as did we. As I told you, I suspected that N'Mar might be somehow responsible for odd phenomena in this area, and my suspicions were confirmed.\n是啊，我们也是。如我所说，我怀疑 N'Mar 或许与这地区的怪异现象有关，而我的怀疑得到了证实。"

    old "How do I know? A vampire just knows these things."
    new "How do I know? A vampire just knows these things.\n我怎么知道？Vampire 就是知道这些事。"

    old "How do we stop it?"
    new "How do we stop it?\n我们怎么阻止它？"

    old "Oh, Valery and I just performed a little ritual of sorts. You just missed it, actually. A blood ritual, of course, as vampires do. That little vial of blood is just a bit of what's leftover from the ritual."
    new "Oh, Valery and I just performed a little ritual of sorts. You just missed it, actually. A blood ritual, of course, as vampires do. That little vial of blood is just a bit of what's leftover from the ritual.\n哦，Valery 和我刚刚做了一场小小的仪式。你其实正好错过了。当然是血祭，Vampires 一贯如此。那小小一瓶血，只是仪式剩下的一点点。"

    old "So the corruption around this area..."
    new "So the corruption around this area...\n所以这一带周围的腐化……"

    old "For now? It's stalled, halted. Not eliminated. For that, you'll need to go to the source."
    new "For now? It's stalled, halted. Not eliminated. For that, you'll need to go to the source.\n眼下？它被遏制住了，暂时停滞了。但并没有被根除。要根除，你得去源头。"

    old "And what is the source?"
    new "And what is the source?\n那源头是什么？"

    old "N'Mar, of course. But you already knew that, didn't you?"
    new "N'Mar, of course. But you already knew that, didn't you?\n当然是 N'Mar。不过你早就知道了，不是吗？"

    old "I think we've said all there is to say for now. Valery is quite exhausted from the ritual and all, so we should be on our way."
    new "I think we've said all there is to say for now. Valery is quite exhausted from the ritual and all, so we should be on our way.\n我想眼下该说的都说完了。Valery 因为这场仪式之类的事已经很疲惫，我们该上路了。"

    old "Goodbye."
    new "Goodbye.\n再见。"

    old "Wait—"
    new "Wait—\n等等——"

    old "I call out, but Zachary and Valery seem to vanish from sight, as though they melted into the darkness itself. It seems they have no interest in revealing themselves."
    new "I call out, but Zachary and Valery seem to vanish from sight, as though they melted into the darkness itself. It seems they have no interest in revealing themselves.\n我喊出声，但 Zachary 和 Valery 似乎从视野中消失了，仿佛融入了黑暗本身。看来他们无意现身。"

    old "Ah well. If Zachary is telling me the truth, it means that the small issue plaguing this area is dealt with. For now, at least."
    new "Ah well. If Zachary is telling me the truth, it means that the small issue plaguing this area is dealt with. For now, at least.\n算了。如果 Zachary 说的是实话，那就意味着困扰这一带的小麻烦已经解决了。至少眼下如此。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. We meet again."
    new "Ah, [protag]. We meet again.\n啊，[protag]。我们又见面了。"

    old "Zachary, what a surprise to see you here. And you too, Valery."
    new "Zachary, what a surprise to see you here. And you too, Valery.\nZachary，在这里见到你真意外。还有你，Valery。"

    old "I presume you're here for the same reason we are."
    new "I presume you're here for the same reason we are.\n我猜你来这里，和我们出于同样的原因。"

    old "If you're assuming I came here to investigate the corruption running through this area, then you'd be correct."
    new "If you're assuming I came here to investigate the corruption running through this area, then you'd be correct.\n如果你是在假设我前来调查贯穿这一带的腐化，那你猜对了。"

    old "Yes. Your arrival is actually quite...fortuitous."
    new "Yes. Your arrival is actually quite...fortuitous.\n是的。你的到来其实相当……凑巧。"

    old "You see, I came here with Valery, hoping to end the corruption with the same blood ritual we performed last time. Unfortunately, we hit a bit of a complication."
    new "You see, I came here with Valery, hoping to end the corruption with the same blood ritual we performed last time. Unfortunately, we hit a bit of a complication.\n你瞧，我带着 Valery 来到这里，本希望用我们上次施展的那种血祭来终结腐化。不幸的是，我们遇到了点麻烦。"

    old "Valery smiles, bearing fangs at me."
    new "Valery smiles, bearing fangs at me.\nValery 微笑着，朝我露出尖牙。"

    old "You see, Valery has fully turned. And while I am quite happy to have her now as a vampire companion, it does mean that I no longer have a thrall to draw blood from. Very unfortunate."
    new "You see, Valery has fully turned. And while I am quite happy to have her now as a vampire companion, it does mean that I no longer have a thrall to draw blood from. Very unfortunate.\n你瞧，Valery 已经完全转化了。虽然我很高兴她现在成了我的 Vampire 同伴，但这确实意味着我再也没有可供取血的血仆了。实在遗憾。"

    old "Very unfortunate."
    new "Very unfortunate.\n实在遗憾。"

    old "But now that you've arrived, I think we have a solution to that problem. That is, of course, presuming that you are willing to be a blood donor."
    new "But now that you've arrived, I think we have a solution to that problem. That is, of course, presuming that you are willing to be a blood donor.\n但既然你到了，我想我们有了解决那个问题的办法。当然，前提是你愿意做个献血者。"

    old "What exactly are you asking me?"
    new "What exactly are you asking me?\n你到底在问我什么？"

    old "Oh, please understand. I'm not asking you to be my thrall. The ritual won't turn you into a vampire like Valery here. Her vampirication had to do with something else entirely. I just need to draw a bit of blood from your neck. Enough to fill a small glass or two."
    new "Oh, please understand. I'm not asking you to be my thrall. The ritual won't turn you into a vampire like Valery here. Her vampirication had to do with something else entirely. I just need to draw a bit of blood from your neck. Enough to fill a small glass or two.\n哦，请理解。我不是要你做我的血仆。这场仪式不会把你变成像 Valery 那样的 Vampire。她之所以变成 Vampire，完全是另一回事。我只需从你的脖子上取一点血，够装满一两小杯就行。"

    old "And why should I consent to this?"
    new "And why should I consent to this?\n那我为什么要同意？"

    old "You want to end the corruption here, don't you? This area was tainted with a blood ritual, and the corruption can only be halted with a blood ritual. It's by no means a permanent solution, but it will at least halt the corruption for now, until we can find a more permanent solution."
    new "You want to end the corruption here, don't you? This area was tainted with a blood ritual, and the corruption can only be halted with a blood ritual. It's by no means a permanent solution, but it will at least halt the corruption for now, until we can find a more permanent solution.\n你想终结这里的腐化，不是吗？这片地区是被一场血祭污染的，而腐化也只能用血祭来遏制。这绝不是永久的解决办法，但至少能暂时止住腐化，直到我们找到更彻底的方案。"

    old "Why are you doing this? Why do you have such an interest in 'saving' these lands?"
    new "Why are you doing this? Why do you have such an interest in 'saving' these lands?\n你为什么要这么做？你为什么对'拯救'这些土地如此上心？"

    old "What can I say? The vampires of N'Mar don't like me, and I don't like them. If I had the chance to throw a wrench into their plans, I'll take it. I like getting on their nerves."
    new "What can I say? The vampires of N'Mar don't like me, and I don't like them. If I had the chance to throw a wrench into their plans, I'll take it. I like getting on their nerves.\n我能说什么呢？N'Mar 的 Vampires 不喜欢我，我也不喜欢他们。若有机会搅乱他们的计划，我会抓住。我喜欢给他们添堵。"

    old "So what do you say, [protag]? Will you offer me some of your blood? I just need a little bit, is all. We're in this together, aren't we?"
    new "So what do you say, [protag]? Will you offer me some of your blood? I just need a little bit, is all. We're in this together, aren't we?\n那么，你怎么说，[protag]？愿意给我一些你的血吗？我只需要一点点，仅此而已。我们是同一阵线的，不是吗？"

    old "I consider Zachary's offer. The last time we met, he did seem sincere in his efforts to stem the blight, and whatever ritual he performed, it did seem like the odd occurrences around that area stopped after he did his deed. It might be coincidence, but it seems like he knows what he's doing."
    new "I consider Zachary's offer. The last time we met, he did seem sincere in his efforts to stem the blight, and whatever ritual he performed, it did seem like the odd occurrences around that area stopped after he did his deed. It might be coincidence, but it seems like he knows what he's doing.\n我斟酌着 Zachary 的提议。上次见面时，他努力遏制枯萎之害的诚意似乎是真的，而且无论他施展的是什么仪式，那一带的怪异现象在他动手之后似乎确实停止了。也许是巧合，但看起来他知道自己在做什么。"

    old "I'm sorry, Zachary, but I don't think I'm ready to readily offer a vampire my blood."
    new "I'm sorry, Zachary, but I don't think I'm ready to readily offer a vampire my blood.\n抱歉，Zachary，但我觉得自己还没准备好轻易把血献给一个 Vampire。"

    old "That's fair enough. I suppose we'll have to find some alternate solution."
    new "That's fair enough. I suppose we'll have to find some alternate solution.\n合情合理。我想我们得另找别的办法了。"

    old "Are you going to..."
    new "Are you going to...\n你打算……"

    old "Oh, please don't worry, [protag]. I have no intention of kidnapping someone and taking their blood. We were fortunate enough to chance upon several wild beasts, which we did draw blood from in case it was necessary for an event such as this."
    new "Oh, please don't worry, [protag]. I have no intention of kidnapping someone and taking their blood. We were fortunate enough to chance upon several wild beasts, which we did draw blood from in case it was necessary for an event such as this.\n哦，请别担心，[protag]。我没有绑架人取血的打算。我们很幸运地碰上了几头野兽，也确实从它们身上取了血，以备遇上现在这种情况时之需。"

    old "It's not an ideal solution, as beast blood always is unreliable. There's a chance the ritual will fail, but the worst that can happen is that we'll be back where we started."
    new "It's not an ideal solution, as beast blood always is unreliable. There's a chance the ritual will fail, but the worst that can happen is that we'll be back where we started.\n这不是理想的解决办法，因为野兽的血总是不太可靠。仪式有失败的可能，但最坏的结果也不过是我们回到原点。"

    old "We'll be back where we started."
    new "We'll be back where we started.\n我们回到原点。"

    old "Anyway, I'll respect your wishes and leave you be. We'll proceed with the ritual without you. Goodbye, [protag]."
    new "Anyway, I'll respect your wishes and leave you be. We'll proceed with the ritual without you. Goodbye, [protag].\n总之，我会尊重你的意愿，不再打扰你。我们会自行继续仪式。再会，[protag]。"

    old "Alright, Zachary. I'll volunteer for your ritual."
    new "Alright, Zachary. I'll volunteer for your ritual.\n好吧，Zachary。我自愿为你的仪式献血。"

    old "Delightful."
    new "Delightful.\n太好了。"

    old "Valery, since you now also have the ability to draw blood, should you do it or should I?"
    new "Valery, since you now also have the ability to draw blood, should you do it or should I?\nValery，既然你现在也有取血的能力，是你来还是我来？"

    old "Ooh, [hisher] neck does look quite soft. I wouldn't mind a nibble."
    new "Ooh, [hisher] neck does look quite soft. I wouldn't mind a nibble.\n哦，[hisher]脖子看起来确实很柔软。我不介意咬上一小口。"

    old "Don't I have a say in this?"
    new "Don't I have a say in this?\n这事我就没有发言权吗？"

    old "Fair enough, fair enough. Let's leave it up to [protag] to decide."
    new "Fair enough, fair enough. Let's leave it up to [protag] to decide.\n也是，也是。那就由[protag]来决定吧。"

    old "Zachary, you can do the deed."
    new "Zachary, you can do the deed.\nZachary，你来吧。"

    old "I'm flattered that you chose me, [protag]. No hard feelings, I hope."
    new "I'm flattered that you chose me, [protag]. No hard feelings, I hope.\n你选了我，我受宠若惊，[protag]。希望没有伤到你的感情。"

    old "No hard feelings."
    new "No hard feelings.\n没有。"

    old "Come here."
    new "Come here.\n过来。"

    old "Zachary wraps his arm around me."
    new "Zachary wraps his arm around me.\nZachary 用胳膊环住我。"

    old "It helps if you close your eyes and relax."
    new "It helps if you close your eyes and relax.\n闭上眼睛、放轻松会好一些。"

    old "I close my eyes and make myself limp in Zachary's arms."
    new "I close my eyes and make myself limp in Zachary's arms.\n我闭上眼睛，让自己瘫软在 Zachary 的怀里。"

    old "I feel the touch of Zachary's cold finger against my cheek, and he traces a line from my ear to the base of my nick, running his finger along the surface of the skin."
    new "I feel the touch of Zachary's cold finger against my cheek, and he traces a line from my ear to the base of my nick, running his finger along the surface of the skin.\n我感觉到 Zachary 冰冷的手指触上我的脸颊，他从我的耳朵一路描画到脖根，指尖沿着皮肤表面滑过。"

    old "Zachary presses on the base of my neck with one of his fingers, and I shiver under his touch. He leans in and whispers into my ear."
    new "Zachary presses on the base of my neck with one of his fingers, and I shiver under his touch. He leans in and whispers into my ear.\nZachary 用一根手指按住我的脖根，我在他的触碰下一颤。他凑过来，对着我的耳朵低语。"

    old "You will feel a momentary pain. But I'm not going to hurt you."
    new "You will feel a momentary pain. But I'm not going to hurt you.\n你会感到一阵短暂的疼痛。但我不会伤害你。"

    old "I feel the touch of two sharp points on the skin of my neck, and feel the sensation of Zachary's fangs sinking into my flesh. I feel pain for a moment—but soon the pain is replaced by the warm, wet feeling of blood being drawn out of me."
    new "I feel the touch of two sharp points on the skin of my neck, and feel the sensation of Zachary's fangs sinking into my flesh. I feel pain for a moment—but soon the pain is replaced by the warm, wet feeling of blood being drawn out of me.\n我感到两个尖锐的点贴上我脖子的皮肤，感觉到 Zachary 的尖牙陷入我的皮肉。有那么一瞬间我感到疼痛——但很快，痛感就被血液从我体内被抽出的那种温热、湿润的感觉所取代。"

    old "Zachary cradles my body gently in his arms as the blood continues to flow, and I feel a tingling sensation, spreading throughout my body."
    new "Zachary cradles my body gently in his arms as the blood continues to flow, and I feel a tingling sensation, spreading throughout my body.\nZachary 轻轻把我的身体搂在怀里，血液持续流淌，我感到一阵酥麻感蔓延全身。"

    old "Eventually, the flow of blood stops, and I feel Zachary's tongue lap at the holes in my neck. There's a slight stinging sensation as he licks over the wounds and his licking leaves my skin feeling dry. Dry and intact."
    new "Eventually, the flow of blood stops, and I feel Zachary's tongue lap at the holes in my neck. There's a slight stinging sensation as he licks over the wounds and his licking leaves my skin feeling dry. Dry and intact.\n终于，血流停了，我感觉到 Zachary 的舌头舔舐着我脖子上的伤口。当他舔过伤口时，有一丝刺痛感，而他的舔舐让我的皮肤感到干燥。干燥而完好。"

    old "I open my eyes and stand up. I reach a hand to my neck to feel where his teeth went in, and surprisingly I can't find the holes."
    new "I open my eyes and stand up. I reach a hand to my neck to feel where his teeth went in, and surprisingly I can't find the holes.\n我睁开眼睛站起身。我伸手摸向脖子，想找到他的牙齿咬入的位置，可奇怪的是，我找不到那些伤口。"

    old "No scars, yes? I specialize in ceremonial blood-letting. And I'm very good at what I do."
    new "No scars, yes? I specialize in ceremonial blood-letting. And I'm very good at what I do.\n没有疤痕，对吧？我专精于仪式性的放血。而我在这一行干得相当出色。"

    old "Now, stand back."
    new "Now, stand back.\n现在，退后。"

    old "I move to the edge of the chamber, and Zachary pulls a small vial from his pocket. The vial is filled with some sort of white powder."
    new "I move to the edge of the chamber, and Zachary pulls a small vial from his pocket. The vial is filled with some sort of white powder.\n我退到房间的边缘，Zachary 从口袋里掏出一个小瓶。瓶子里装着某种白色粉末。"

    old "Zachary takes the powder and sprinkles it around himself, enclosing himself in a white powder circle. Then, he pulls out a candle and flicks at the wick."
    new "Zachary takes the powder and sprinkles it around himself, enclosing himself in a white powder circle. Then, he pulls out a candle and flicks at the wick.\nZachary 拿起粉末撒在自己周围，用白色粉末圈把自己围住。接着，他掏出一根蜡烛，弹了弹烛芯。"

    old "[protag], you might want to close your eyes for this."
    new "[protag], you might want to close your eyes for this.\n[protag]，这一步你或许想闭上眼睛。"

    old "I close my eyes. I feel my skin grow warm, and a wave of heat washes over me. A moment later, my skin grows cold, and I open my eyes to see Zachary standing in the middle of a pile of ash."
    new "I close my eyes. I feel my skin grow warm, and a wave of heat washes over me. A moment later, my skin grows cold, and I open my eyes to see Zachary standing in the middle of a pile of ash.\n我闭上眼睛。我感到皮肤变暖，一股热浪掠过全身。片刻后，我的皮肤变冷，我睁开眼，看到 Zachary 站在一堆灰烬中间。"

    old "I'll watch."
    new "I'll watch.\n我会看着。"

    old "Very well."
    new "Very well.\n很好。"

    old "Zachary takes a deep breath, and blows over the wick of the unlit candle, it erupts into a red flame. Suddenly, the white powder circle around him bursts into flame, and the fire creeps up and around him until Zachary is completely enveloped in the blaze."
    new "Zachary takes a deep breath, and blows over the wick of the unlit candle, it erupts into a red flame. Suddenly, the white powder circle around him bursts into flame, and the fire creeps up and around him until Zachary is completely enveloped in the blaze.\nZachary 深吸一口气，朝未点燃的蜡烛芯吹去，烛火腾地燃起红色火焰。突然间，他周围的白色粉末圈燃起火来，火焰向上蔓延、将他环绕，直到 Zachary 完全被烈焰吞没。"

    old "I feel the chamber grow hot, but suddenly the fire completely disappears. Zachary appears to be completely unharmed, with a pile of ash around him."
    new "I feel the chamber grow hot, but suddenly the fire completely disappears. Zachary appears to be completely unharmed, with a pile of ash around him.\n我感到房间变得灼热，但突然间火焰完全消失了。Zachary 看起来毫发无损，身边堆着一圈灰烬。"

    old "How did that not burn you to a crisp?"
    new "How did that not burn you to a crisp?\n那怎么没把你烧成焦炭？"

    old "Quite simple. The fire burned around me. I was surrounded by the flames, but I was never on fire."
    new "Quite simple. The fire burned around me. I was surrounded by the flames, but I was never on fire.\n很简单。火是绕着我烧的。我被火焰包围，但我自己从未着火。"

    old "Then where did the ash come from? What was burning?"
    new "Then where did the ash come from? What was burning?\n那灰烬是从哪来的？是什么在燃烧？"

    old "Your blood, of course."
    new "Your blood, of course.\n当然是你的血。"

    old "Zachary takes the vial that held the white powder, which is now empty. He raises the vial to his lips and spits into it, filling it with a foul-smelling dark red sludge."
    new "Zachary takes the vial that held the white powder, which is now empty. He raises the vial to his lips and spits into it, filling it with a foul-smelling dark red sludge.\nZachary 拿起那个曾装着白色粉末、如今已空的小瓶。他把瓶子举到唇边，朝里面吐了一口，将瓶中注满一种散发着恶臭的暗红色黏浆。"

    old "Valery, you seemed eager. I wouldn't mind letting you nibble at my neck."
    new "Valery, you seemed eager. I wouldn't mind letting you nibble at my neck.\nValery，你看起来很急切。我不介意让你咬一咬我的脖子。"

    old "Valery grins, bearing her fangs, and licks her lips as her eyes study my neck."
    new "Valery grins, bearing her fangs, and licks her lips as her eyes study my neck.\nValery 咧嘴一笑，露出尖牙，一边舔着嘴唇，一边用眼睛打量着我的脖子。"

    old "She places a hand on each of my shoulders and leans in, playfully licking my nose before pulling back."
    new "She places a hand on each of my shoulders and leans in, playfully licking my nose before pulling back.\n她把两只手各放在我一边肩膀上，凑上前来，调皮地舔了舔我的鼻子，然后又退了回去。"

    old "Is that part necessary for the blood ritual?"
    new "Is that part necessary for the blood ritual?\n那是血祭的必要环节吗？"

    old "Just having some fun."
    new "Just having some fun.\n只是逗逗趣。"

    old "Valery lowers her head to the base of my neck, and I feel her tongue press against my skin. She licks my neck, tracing a line with her tongue upwards until she stops just short of my ear."
    new "Valery lowers her head to the base of my neck, and I feel her tongue press against my skin. She licks my neck, tracing a line with her tongue upwards until she stops just short of my ear.\nValery 把头低到我脖根，我感到她的舌头贴上我的皮肤。她舔着我的脖子，用舌头向上描画出一条线，直到在离我耳朵只差一点的地方停下。"

    old "She giggles softly into my ear."
    new "She giggles softly into my ear.\n她对着我的耳朵轻轻咯咯笑。"

    old "My, what tender skin you have."
    new "My, what tender skin you have.\n哎呀，你的皮肤真是娇嫩。"

    old "I feel a pressure on my neck, and suddenly a sharp pain as her fangs dig into my skin—but the pain soon vanishes and is replaced by the warm, wet feeling of blood flowing from the holes in my neck."
    new "I feel a pressure on my neck, and suddenly a sharp pain as her fangs dig into my skin—but the pain soon vanishes and is replaced by the warm, wet feeling of blood flowing from the holes in my neck.\n我感到脖子上一阵压力，随后她的尖牙刺入皮肤，传来一阵锐痛——但疼痛很快消失，取而代之的是血液从我脖子上的伤口汩汩流出的那种温热、湿润的感觉。"

    old "I hear the sound of Valery lapping at my blood, and her tongue tickles my neck until the flow of blood stops. She draws her tongue across my neck once more before pulling away."
    new "I hear the sound of Valery lapping at my blood, and her tongue tickles my neck until the flow of blood stops. She draws her tongue across my neck once more before pulling away.\n我听见 Valery 舔舐我血液的声音，她的舌头在我脖子上轻挠，直到血流停止。她又用舌头从我脖子上一遍划过，然后才退开。"

    old "I feel the warm sensation of a trail of blood dribbling down my neck, and Valery reaches in, wiping up the blood with her finger. She winks at me and licks the blood off her finger."
    new "I feel the warm sensation of a trail of blood dribbling down my neck, and Valery reaches in, wiping up the blood with her finger. She winks at me and licks the blood off her finger.\n我感到一股温热的血沿着脖子往下淌，Valery 伸手过来，用手指把血抹掉。她朝我眨了眨眼，把手指上的血舔干净。"

    old "Wouldn't want that last little bit to go to waste."
    new "Wouldn't want that last little bit to go to waste.\n可不能让那最后一小滴浪费掉。"

    old "Lovely. Now, [protag], if you wouldn't mind standing back..."
    new "Lovely. Now, [protag], if you wouldn't mind standing back...\n好极了。那么，[protag]，如果你不介意退后……"

    old "I stand at the edge of the clearing, and Zachary pulls a small vial from his pocket. A white powder is inside."
    new "I stand at the edge of the clearing, and Zachary pulls a small vial from his pocket. A white powder is inside.\n我站到空地的边缘，Zachary 从口袋里掏出一个小瓶。里面装着白色粉末。"

    old "Zachary takes the powder and sprinkles it around Valery, drawing a circle around her. Then, he takes out a candle and hands it to Valery."
    new "Zachary takes the powder and sprinkles it around Valery, drawing a circle around her. Then, he takes out a candle and hands it to Valery.\nZachary 拿起粉末撒在 Valery 周围，绕着她画出一个圈。接着，他取出一根蜡烛，递给 Valery。"

    old "Valery holds the candle with both hands, then closes her eyes and takes a deep breath."
    new "Valery holds the candle with both hands, then closes her eyes and takes a deep breath.\nValery 双手握住蜡烛，然后闭上眼睛，深吸一口气。"

    old "I close my eyes. I feel my skin grow warm, and a wave of heat washes over me. A moment later, my skin grows cold, and I open my eyes to see Valery standing in the middle of a pile of ash."
    new "I close my eyes. I feel my skin grow warm, and a wave of heat washes over me. A moment later, my skin grows cold, and I open my eyes to see Valery standing in the middle of a pile of ash.\n我闭上眼睛。我感到皮肤变暖，一股热浪掠过全身。片刻后，我的皮肤变冷，我睁开眼，看到 Valery 站在一堆灰烬中间。"

    old "Valery breaths out, and as her breath passes over the wick of the unlit candle, it erupts into a red flame. Suddenly, the white powder circle around Valery bursts into flame, and the fire creeps up and around Valery until she is completely enveloped in the blaze."
    new "Valery breaths out, and as her breath passes over the wick of the unlit candle, it erupts into a red flame. Suddenly, the white powder circle around Valery bursts into flame, and the fire creeps up and around Valery until she is completely enveloped in the blaze.\nValery 呼出一口气，当她的气息拂过未点燃的蜡烛芯时，烛火腾地燃起红色火焰。突然间，Valery 周围的白色粉末圈燃起火来，火焰向上蔓延、将她环绕，直到她完全被烈焰吞没。"

    old "I feel the area grow hot, but suddenly the fire completely disappears. Valery appears completely unharmed, with a pile of ash around her."
    new "I feel the area grow hot, but suddenly the fire completely disappears. Valery appears completely unharmed, with a pile of ash around her.\n我感到这片地方变得灼热，但突然间火焰完全消失了。Valery 看起来毫发无损，身边堆着一圈灰烬。"

    old "Quite simple. The fire burned around her, not on her. Valery was never on fire."
    new "Quite simple. The fire burned around her, not on her. Valery was never on fire.\n很简单。火是绕着她烧的，而不是烧在她身上。Valery 从未着火。"

    old "The ritual is complete."
    new "The ritual is complete.\n仪式完成了。"

    old "Zachary takes the empty vial that previously held the white powder and hands it to Valery."
    new "Zachary takes the empty vial that previously held the white powder and hands it to Valery.\nZachary 拿起那个先前装着白色粉末的空瓶，递给 Valery。"

    old "Cough into this."
    new "Cough into this.\n咳到这里面。"

    old "Valery coughs and hacks, until a disgusting-looking sludge comes out of her mouth. She spits it into the vial, and Zachary seals it."
    new "Valery coughs and hacks, until a disgusting-looking sludge comes out of her mouth. She spits it into the vial, and Zachary seals it.\nValery 一阵咳嗽、干呕，直到一股恶心的黏浆从她嘴里冒出来。她把它吐进瓶子里，Zachary 把瓶子封好。"

    old "Since you've been so kind to assist us with this ritual, I'd like to offer you this as a token of appreciation."
    new "Since you've been so kind to assist us with this ritual, I'd like to offer you this as a token of appreciation.\n既然你如此好心协助我们完成这场仪式，我想把这个作为谢礼献给你。"

    old "Zachary presents the vial to me. It looks like a sickening mixture of red and black."
    new "Zachary presents the vial to me. It looks like a sickening mixture of red and black.\nZachary 把瓶子呈到我面前。它看上去像一种令人作呕的红黑混合物。"

    old "What...is it?"
    new "What...is it?\n这……是什么？"

    old "Your blood. It's tainted with ash, but that won't stop vampires, ghouls, and their ilk from lusting after it. And the fact that its tainted has the benefit of doing them quite a bit of harm."
    new "Your blood. It's tainted with ash, but that won't stop vampires, ghouls, and their ilk from lusting after it. And the fact that its tainted has the benefit of doing them quite a bit of harm.\n是你的血。它掺入了灰烬，但这并不妨碍 Vampires、食尸鬼及其同类对它垂涎欲滴。而它被污染这一点，反倒有个好处——能给他们造成不小的伤害。"

    old "Harm them how?"
    new "Harm them how?\n怎么伤害他们？"

    old "Oh, not enough harm to incapacitate them. But let's just say that their health will suffer quite a bit if they decide to ingest it. And they will ingest it, if given the opportunity. It is blood, after all. There are fewer impulses stronger in the undead than bloodlust."
    new "Oh, not enough harm to incapacitate them. But let's just say that their health will suffer quite a bit if they decide to ingest it. And they will ingest it, if given the opportunity. It is blood, after all. There are fewer impulses stronger in the undead than bloodlust.\n哦，还不至于伤到让他们无法行动。但这么说吧，如果他们决定吞下它，健康会受相当大的影响。而且只要有机会，他们一定会吞。毕竟是血啊。在亡灵身上，很少有比嗜血更强的冲动。"

    old "So, I can feed this blood to undead beasts?"
    new "So, I can feed this blood to undead beasts?\n所以，我可以把这血喂给亡灵野兽？"

    old "Or vampires, if you'd like. Though, do bear in mind what they say. A beast is once bitten, twice shy. If you try to parley with tainted blood, it will fool them the first time. But after that, you can count out any chance of amiable negotiation. Poisoning people tends to make them angry, in my experience."
    new "Or vampires, if you'd like. Though, do bear in mind what they say. A beast is once bitten, twice shy. If you try to parley with tainted blood, it will fool them the first time. But after that, you can count out any chance of amiable negotiation. Poisoning people tends to make them angry, in my experience.\n或者 Vampires，如果你愿意的话。不过请记住那句老话：一朝被咬，十年怕草绳。你若试图用被污染的血去谈判，第一次能骗过他们。但那次之后，就别指望还有什么友好谈判的可能了。依我的经验，给人下毒往往会让对方恼火。"

    old "...thank you, Zachary. I'm sure I'll have use for this in the future."
    new "...thank you, Zachary. I'm sure I'll have use for this in the future.\n……谢谢你，Zachary。我相信将来会用得上这个。"

    old "Thank you again for your time."
    new "Thank you again for your time.\n再次感谢你抽出时间。"

    old "Now, if you'll excuse me and Valery, we must be off."
    new "Now, if you'll excuse me and Valery, we must be off.\n那么，恕我和 Valery 失陪，我们得走了。"

    old "We must be off."
    new "We must be off.\n我们得走了。"

    old "The two vampires draw their capes around them, then unfurl them in a flash of color. The flashing of the capes kicks up dust, and I cover my eyes to shield them. When I open my eyes, Zachary and Valery are nowhere to be seen."
    new "The two vampires draw their capes around them, then unfurl them in a flash of color. The flashing of the capes kicks up dust, and I cover my eyes to shield them. When I open my eyes, Zachary and Valery are nowhere to be seen.\n两个 Vampires 把斗篷裹到身上，然后在一片色彩中抖开。斗篷抖开的动作扬起灰尘，我抬手遮住眼睛。等我睁开眼时，Zachary 和 Valery 已不见踪影。"

    old "I'm back in the desert, walking the dunes. The first time I came here, I assumed that it would be my only visit. Now, I'm here for...the third time? And still haven't accomplished what I originally came here for. It's time to change that."
    new "I'm back in the desert, walking the dunes. The first time I came here, I assumed that it would be my only visit. Now, I'm here for...the third time? And still haven't accomplished what I originally came here for. It's time to change that.\n我回到沙漠，走在沙丘上。第一次来这里时，我以为这会是唯一一次。如今，这已经是……第三次了？而我还没完成最初来这里的初衷。是时候改变这一切了。"

    old "The sands that once seemed treacherous to navigate are now easy for me to amble over, thanks to the legwear I received from the Dunemarchers. These greaves really are a marvel of craftsmanship."
    new "The sands that once seemed treacherous to navigate are now easy for me to amble over, thanks to the legwear I received from the Dunemarchers. These greaves really are a marvel of craftsmanship.\n曾经看似凶险难行的沙地，如今我都能轻松漫步其上，这多亏了 Dunemarchers 送给我的腿部护具。这双护胫真是工艺的奇迹。"

    old "I spot a familiar figure on the horizon, and the figure approaches me until I can make out the familiar form of Nuala."
    new "I spot a familiar figure on the horizon, and the figure approaches me until I can make out the familiar form of Nuala.\n我在地平线上看到一个熟悉的身影，那人影朝我走近，直到我能辨认出 Nuala 熟悉的身形。"

    old "[protag], welcome back."
    new "[protag], welcome back.\n[protag]，欢迎回来。"

    old "Hello, Nuala. You know, every time I come to these dunes, you seem to find me. I'm beginning to wonder if all of your time is spent just watching the horizon, awaiting my return."
    new "Hello, Nuala. You know, every time I come to these dunes, you seem to find me. I'm beginning to wonder if all of your time is spent just watching the horizon, awaiting my return.\n你好，Nuala。你知道吗，每次我来这些沙丘，你似乎都能找到我。我都在怀疑你是不是把所有时间都花在眺望地平线、等我回来了。"

    old "I'm eager to meet anyone who ventures into the desert. But you're definitely my favorite visitor."
    new "I'm eager to meet anyone who ventures into the desert. But you're definitely my favorite visitor.\n我很想见见任何闯进沙漠的人。但你绝对是我最中意的访客。"

    old "My, Nuala, I'm flattered. Is it my charming personality, or my lovely face?"
    new "My, Nuala, I'm flattered. Is it my charming personality, or my lovely face?\n哎呀，Nuala，我受宠若惊。是我迷人的性格，还是我可爱的脸蛋？"

    old "That's kind of you to say, Nuala. I didn't realize you were so fond of me."
    new "That's kind of you to say, Nuala. I didn't realize you were so fond of me.\n你这么说真好，Nuala。我不知道你这么喜欢我。"

    old "I think the thing I like most about you is that, of all the visitors we get, you are the least likely among them to try to shoot me with an arrow or stab me with a spear."
    new "I think the thing I like most about you is that, of all the visitors we get, you are the least likely among them to try to shoot me with an arrow or stab me with a spear.\n我想我最喜欢你的一点是，在所有来访者当中，你是最不可能用箭射我、或用矛捅我的那一个。"

    old "Ah. So it's a matter of survival."
    new "Ah. So it's a matter of survival.\n啊。原来是事关生存。"

    old "Patrolling the border to the desert is my responsibility to my tribe. The fact that sometimes I see you...that is not the reason I patrol. But it is a nice to see you."
    new "Patrolling the border to the desert is my responsibility to my tribe. The fact that sometimes I see you...that is not the reason I patrol. But it is a nice to see you.\n巡逻沙漠边境，是我对部落的职责。偶尔能见到你……那不是我巡逻的原因。但能见到你真好。"

    old "The expression on your face says that you are not just here to talk and enjoy my company."
    new "The expression on your face says that you are not just here to talk and enjoy my company.\n你脸上的表情说明，你来这里不只是为了聊天、享受我的陪伴。"

    old "I'm afraid not. You see, the last time I came here, I gained an ally, and quite a valuable one as well. But that is not why I came here."
    new "I'm afraid not. You see, the last time I came here, I gained an ally, and quite a valuable one as well. But that is not why I came here.\n恐怕不是。你瞧，我上次来这里，得到了一位盟友，而且相当有价值。但那不是我这次来的原因。"

    old "It's about tomb of Urd."
    new "It's about tomb of Urd.\n是关于 Urd 的坟墓。"

    old "So you haven't forgotten."
    new "So you haven't forgotten.\n看来你还没忘。"

    old "Of course not. Larik can't stop talking about it."
    new "Of course not. Larik can't stop talking about it.\n当然没忘。Larik 总是不停地谈起它。"

    old "What has Larik been saying?"
    new "What has Larik been saying?\nLarik 都说了些什么？"

    old "He never talks to me about it. Apparently it is something that he only discusses with the tribe elders. But they talk about it so often, and so loudly, that I can't help but hear their constant references to the tomb, and the curse of the desert."
    new "He never talks to me about it. Apparently it is something that he only discusses with the tribe elders. But they talk about it so often, and so loudly, that I can't help but hear their constant references to the tomb, and the curse of the desert.\n他从不对我谈这件事。显然，这是只和部落长老们讨论的事。但他们谈起得那么频繁、那么大声，我难免会不断听到他们提到那座坟墓，还有沙漠的诅咒。"

    old "'The curse of the desert?'"
    new "'The curse of the desert?'\n'沙漠的诅咒？'"

    old "I think you should talk to Larik yourself. He can explain it to you."
    new "I think you should talk to Larik yourself. He can explain it to you.\n我想你应该亲自和 Larik 谈谈。他能跟你解释。"

    old "I thought you said it was only between Larik and the tribe elders."
    new "I thought you said it was only between Larik and the tribe elders.\n你不是说这只是 Larik 和部落长老之间的事吗？"

    old "You are already involved. It wasn't until you came around that Larik took such a fevered interest in the tomb of Urd."
    new "You are already involved. It wasn't until you came around that Larik took such a fevered interest in the tomb of Urd.\n你已经卷进来了。直到你出现，Larik 才对 Urd 的坟墓产生了那么强烈的兴趣。"

    old "Let's go, then. Take me to Larik."
    new "Let's go, then. Take me to Larik.\n那我们走吧。带我去见 Larik。"

    old "Ah, [protag]. I was wondering when you'd be back."
    new "Ah, [protag]. I was wondering when you'd be back.\n啊，[protag]。我正想着你什么时候回来。"

    old "You were expecting me?"
    new "You were expecting me?\n你在等我？"

    old "Of course. I haven't forgotten why you originally came here. You were searching for the tomb of Urd."
    new "Of course. I haven't forgotten why you originally came here. You were searching for the tomb of Urd.\n当然。我没忘记你最初为什么来这里。你在寻找 Urd 的坟墓。"

    old "It seems you've taken an interest in it as well."
    new "It seems you've taken an interest in it as well.\n看来你也对它产生了兴趣。"

    old "Ah, so Nuala told you? Well, I guess I can't stop her from overhearing. She always did have sharp ears."
    new "Ah, so Nuala told you? Well, I guess I can't stop her from overhearing. She always did have sharp ears.\n啊，是 Nuala 告诉你的？算了，我也没法阻止她偷听。她向来耳朵尖。"

    old "What is it about the tomb that has gotten your interest? Nuala said something about a curse."
    new "What is it about the tomb that has gotten your interest? Nuala said something about a curse.\n这座坟墓的什么引起了你的兴趣？Nuala 提到了什么诅咒。"

    old "You've seen the desert's corruption for yourself. Those scorpions, they seem to exude some kind of dark power, almost as if they were drawing their energy from another realm."
    new "You've seen the desert's corruption for yourself. Those scorpions, they seem to exude some kind of dark power, almost as if they were drawing their energy from another realm.\n你已经亲眼见过沙漠的腐化了。那些蝎子，它们似乎散发着某种黑暗的力量，几乎就像是从另一个界域汲取能量。"

    old "You suggested that the blight covering the lands of N'Mar might be related to the desert's corruption. If that were the case, we would expect the desert infestation to be worst on its northern border, the part closest to N'Mar."
    new "You suggested that the blight covering the lands of N'Mar might be related to the desert's corruption. If that were the case, we would expect the desert infestation to be worst on its northern border, the part closest to N'Mar.\n你曾提出，覆盖 N'Mar 土地的枯萎之害可能与沙漠的腐化有关。如果是那样，我们本应预期沙漠的侵扰在其北部边境、最靠近 N'Mar 的部分最严重。"

    old "But it's the opposite. The places where the desert is thickest with the creatures of darkness are south of us. And coincidentally, that happens to be where the tomb of Urd is located."
    new "But it's the opposite. The places where the desert is thickest with the creatures of darkness are south of us. And coincidentally, that happens to be where the tomb of Urd is located.\n但情况恰恰相反。沙漠中黑暗生物最密集的地方在我们南边。而巧合的是，那里正是 Urd 坟墓的所在。"

    old "Interesting."
    new "Interesting.\n有意思。"

    old "[protag], I didn't ask you before, but what is your business with the tomb? I feel compelled to ask."
    new "[protag], I didn't ask you before, but what is your business with the tomb? I feel compelled to ask.\n[protag]，我之前没问过你，但你和这座坟墓有什么关系？我觉得有必要问一问。"

    old "According to rumor, Urd was buried with his weapons."
    new "According to rumor, Urd was buried with his weapons.\n据传闻，Urd 下葬时带着他的武器。"

    old "You speak of Baneslayer and Benediction. Urd's legendary silver axe and rod."
    new "You speak of Baneslayer and Benediction. Urd's legendary silver axe and rod.\n你说的是 Baneslayer 和 Benediction。Urd 传奇的银斧和法杖。"

    old "You know of them?"
    new "You know of them?\n你知道它们？"

    old "Of course I do. No one knows the legend of Urd better than the people of the desert. Some members of our tribe are directly descended from him. His stories have been passed down from generation to generation."
    new "Of course I do. No one knows the legend of Urd better than the people of the desert. Some members of our tribe are directly descended from him. His stories have been passed down from generation to generation.\n当然知道。没有人比沙漠的子民更了解 Urd 的传说。我们部落的一些成员就是他的直系后裔。他的故事代代相传。"

    old "Stories can be exaggerated, however. Over the course of hundreds of years, it can be hard to separate fact from fiction. What we do know is that there once lived a great warrior named Urd, who was memorialized in a stone tomb that now rests within the sands of this desert. Any more than that may be pure falsehood."
    new "Stories can be exaggerated, however. Over the course of hundreds of years, it can be hard to separate fact from fiction. What we do know is that there once lived a great warrior named Urd, who was memorialized in a stone tomb that now rests within the sands of this desert. Any more than that may be pure falsehood.\n然而故事也可能被夸大。历经数百年，很难把事实和虚构区分开。我们所确知的是，曾经有一位名叫 Urd 的伟大战士，被安葬在一座石墓中，如今静卧于这片沙漠的沙土里。除此之外，更多的可能纯属虚构。"

    old "Legend has it that Urd's Baneslayer and Benediction felled three giant beasts. The first was a fire-breathing dragon. The creature was thought to be invincible, covered with a scaled hide that blunted the impact of any blade or arrow."
    new "Legend has it that Urd's Baneslayer and Benediction felled three giant beasts. The first was a fire-breathing dragon. The creature was thought to be invincible, covered with a scaled hide that blunted the impact of any blade or arrow.\n传说 Urd 的 Baneslayer 和 Benediction 击倒过三头巨兽。第一头是喷火的巨龙。那生物曾被认为不可战胜，浑身覆盖着鳞甲，任何刀剑或箭矢的威力都会被它钝化。"

    old "Urd charged the beast, head-on. The dragon opened its mouth and loosed its immolating flames, but Urd held Benediction aloft, and his rod protected him from the searing flames. Then, as the beast stood before him with its mouth agape, Urd charged in with Baneslayer, slicing its tongue out."
    new "Urd charged the beast, head-on. The dragon opened its mouth and loosed its immolating flames, but Urd held Benediction aloft, and his rod protected him from the searing flames. Then, as the beast stood before him with its mouth agape, Urd charged in with Baneslayer, slicing its tongue out.\nUrd 正面冲向那头巨兽。巨龙张开嘴，喷出灼热的火焰，但 Urd 高举 Benediction，他的法杖护住了他，使他免受烈焰灼烧。接着，当巨兽张着大口立在他面前时，Urd 挥着 Baneslayer 冲上前去，割下了它的舌头。"

    old "The dragon flew away, and Urd stalked the beast for ten days, until at last it succumbed to its wound and completely bled out from the wound in its mouth."
    new "The dragon flew away, and Urd stalked the beast for ten days, until at last it succumbed to its wound and completely bled out from the wound in its mouth.\n巨龙飞走了，Urd 追猎了它十天，直到它最终因伤势不支，从嘴里的伤口彻底流血而死。"

    old "Do you believe the tales?"
    new "Do you believe the tales?\n你相信这些故事吗？"

    old "Ha! A good question, [protag]. And I'm afraid I don't have a good answer for it. You see, regardless of whether his stories are true, Urd is a hero to our people."
    new "Ha! A good question, [protag]. And I'm afraid I don't have a good answer for it. You see, regardless of whether his stories are true, Urd is a hero to our people.\n哈！问得好，[protag]。恐怕我给不出一个好答案。你看，无论他的故事是真是假，Urd 都是我们人民的英雄。"

    old "Urd the battlemage, wielder of the axe and rod. The warriors who pride themselves on their toughness aspire to match Urd's strength. The shamans who pride themselves in the practice of magic aspire to match Urd's prowess with magic. And every member of the tribe aspires to match Urd's courage."
    new "Urd the battlemage, wielder of the axe and rod. The warriors who pride themselves on their toughness aspire to match Urd's strength. The shamans who pride themselves in the practice of magic aspire to match Urd's prowess with magic. And every member of the tribe aspires to match Urd's courage.\nUrd 是战斗法师，斧与法杖的执掌者。以坚韧自傲的战士渴望比肩 Urd 的力量。以修行魔法自傲的萨满渴望比肩 Urd 的魔法造诣。而部落的每个成员都渴望比肩 Urd 的勇气。"

    old "You seek his tomb. Perhaps there you will find his legendary weapons, Baneslayer and Benediction. Perhaps you will find nothing. Regardless, I'd like to accompany you. Your reasons for seeking the tomb are practical. Mine are more...personal."
    new "You seek his tomb. Perhaps there you will find his legendary weapons, Baneslayer and Benediction. Perhaps you will find nothing. Regardless, I'd like to accompany you. Your reasons for seeking the tomb are practical. Mine are more...personal.\n你在寻找他的坟墓。也许在那里，你会找到他传奇的武器 Baneslayer 和 Benediction。也许你什么都找不到。无论如何，我都想陪你同去。你寻找坟墓的理由很实际。我的则更……私人。"

    old "Didn't I just tell you? Urd is a hero to our people. Many people of the desert make pilgrimage to his burial site. It is a rite of passage. Every one of our people, myself included, has a very...sentimental attachment to that location."
    new "Didn't I just tell you? Urd is a hero to our people. Many people of the desert make pilgrimage to his burial site. It is a rite of passage. Every one of our people, myself included, has a very...sentimental attachment to that location.\n我不是刚说过吗？Urd 是我们人民的英雄。许多沙漠子民都会到他的安葬之地朝圣。这是一种成年礼。我们每个人，包括我自己，都对那个地方怀着很深的……情感。"

    old "And that besides, if you are intending to enter his tomb, I feel it is my duty to ensure that you, as an outsider, do not do anything to defile or desecrate the site."
    new "And that besides, if you are intending to enter his tomb, I feel it is my duty to ensure that you, as an outsider, do not do anything to defile or desecrate the site.\n除此之外，如果你打算进入他的坟墓，我觉得自己有责任确保你作为一个外人，不会做出任何玷污或亵渎此地的事。"

    old "That is not to say that I mistrust you, or object to your plan to take any relics you may find there. I think that Urd would be proud to know that Baneslayer and Benediction might once again serve the purpose of fighting creatures of darkness."
    new "That is not to say that I mistrust you, or object to your plan to take any relics you may find there. I think that Urd would be proud to know that Baneslayer and Benediction might once again serve the purpose of fighting creatures of darkness.\n这倒不是说我不信任你，或者反对你带走你在那里可能找到的任何遗物。我想 Urd 若得知 Baneslayer 和 Benediction 能再次用于对抗黑暗生物，一定会感到骄傲。"

    old "But there are certain things which you may not know. I would want to be there simply to protect you from your own ignorance."
    new "But there are certain things which you may not know. I would want to be there simply to protect you from your own ignorance.\n但有些事你也许并不知情。我想待在那里，只是想保护你免受自己无知的伤害。"

    old "You're coming with me? What about your people?"
    new "You're coming with me? What about your people?\n你要跟我一起去？那你的人民怎么办？"

    old "Larik chuckles to himself."
    new "Larik chuckles to himself.\nLarik 自顾自地轻笑起来。"

    old "[protag], I am their leader, not their caretaker. In the past, I have left them for days at a time. Surely they can spare a few hours without me. The elders still preside over the tribe, and they know what to do, even in case of trouble."
    new "[protag], I am their leader, not their caretaker. In the past, I have left them for days at a time. Surely they can spare a few hours without me. The elders still preside over the tribe, and they know what to do, even in case of trouble.\n[protag]，我是他们的领袖，不是他们的保姆。过去我也曾一次离开好几天。他们肯定能省出几个小时不用我。长老们仍在主持部落，就算遇到麻烦，他们也知道该怎么做。"

    old "Besides, Nuala will be here. With a shaman like her watching over them, what have they to fear?"
    new "Besides, Nuala will be here. With a shaman like her watching over them, what have they to fear?\n再说了，Nuala 会在这里。有像她这样的萨满看护着他们，他们还有什么好怕的？"

    old "You've been waiting a long time to visit the tomb of Urd. So have I. Let's stop talking about it and start doing it."
    new "You've been waiting a long time to visit the tomb of Urd. So have I. Let's stop talking about it and start doing it.\n你等了好久才来探访 Urd 的坟墓。我也是。别光说了，动手吧。"

    old "Larik leads me across the dunes, away from the tribe and deeper into the desert sands. His pace is quick—not so quick that I can't keep up, but quick enough that I find myself short of breath."
    new "Larik leads me across the dunes, away from the tribe and deeper into the desert sands. His pace is quick—not so quick that I can't keep up, but quick enough that I find myself short of breath.\nLarik 领着我穿过沙丘，远离部落，深入沙漠腹地。他的步伐很快——快得还不至于让我跟不上，但也快得让我有些上气不接下气。"

    old "You move faster than Nuala did."
    new "You move faster than Nuala did.\n你走得比 Nuala 快。"

    old "Nuala is a scout. She watches for threats, and stalks prey. I'm not so passive."
    new "Nuala is a scout. She watches for threats, and stalks prey. I'm not so passive.\nNuala 是个斥候。她警戒威胁，追踪猎物。我可没那么被动。"

    old "Aren't you worried about attracting the attention of jackals?"
    new "Aren't you worried about attracting the attention of jackals?\n你不担心引来豺狼的注意吗？"

    old "In these sands? No. The jackals tend to favor the areas of the dunes that border on the desert's flatlands. Here, there is no prey, and hence, there are no predators. This is a place of death."
    new "In these sands? No. The jackals tend to favor the areas of the dunes that border on the desert's flatlands. Here, there is no prey, and hence, there are no predators. This is a place of death.\n在这片沙地里？不会。豺狼更喜欢沙丘中靠近沙漠平地的区域。这里没有猎物，因而也没有掠食者。这是一片死亡之地。"

    old "Because of the tomb of Urd?"
    new "Because of the tomb of Urd?\n是因为 Urd 的坟墓吗？"

    old "It's the other way around. This was chosen as Urd's burial site because it is devoid of life. Here, there will be none to defile his grave, be they beast or man."
    new "It's the other way around. This was chosen as Urd's burial site because it is devoid of life. Here, there will be none to defile his grave, be they beast or man.\n恰恰相反。这里之所以被选作 Urd 的安葬地，正是因为它没有生命。在这里，无论是兽是人，都没有谁能亵渎他的坟墓。"

    old "But we're here."
    new "But we're here.\n但我们到了。"

    old "Yes, we are. But visiting the tomb is a privilege that we have earned through generations of craftsmanship and charting this lifeless desert."
    new "Yes, we are. But visiting the tomb is a privilege that we have earned through generations of craftsmanship and charting this lifeless desert.\n是的，到了。但探访这座坟墓，是我们凭借世代相传的技艺、并绘制这片死寂沙漠的地图才赢得的特权。"

    old "Do you think it is an accident that I know the fastest route to get us here? An outsider would get completely lost in these sands before they got anywhere near the tomb. And any intruders would find themselves sinking into the sands before they got even this far."
    new "Do you think it is an accident that I know the fastest route to get us here? An outsider would get completely lost in these sands before they got anywhere near the tomb. And any intruders would find themselves sinking into the sands before they got even this far.\n你以为我知道来这里最快的路线是偶然吗？外人会在这些沙地里彻底迷路，根本走不到坟墓附近。任何闯入者，还没走到这么远，就会发现自己正陷入流沙。"

    old "The Dunemarchers have won the right to visit the tomb of Urd. There is a reason that what you knew about the tomb came entirely from old texts, and not from personal accounts. This is our place."
    new "The Dunemarchers have won the right to visit the tomb of Urd. There is a reason that what you knew about the tomb came entirely from old texts, and not from personal accounts. This is our place.\nDunemarchers 赢得了探访 Urd 坟墓的权利。你之所以对这座坟墓的了解全都来自古籍，而非亲历者的叙述，是有原因的。这是属于我们的地方。"

    old "And soon, it will be your place."
    new "And soon, it will be your place.\n而很快，它也会成为你的地方。"

    old "It is part of the tradition of our people. None of us are born knowing how to make it to the tomb. It is something that is taught, passed from the older generation to the younger, from teacher to student."
    new "It is part of the tradition of our people. None of us are born knowing how to make it to the tomb. It is something that is taught, passed from the older generation to the younger, from teacher to student.\n这是我们人民传统的一部分。没有人天生就知道怎么抵达那座坟墓。这是被教会的，从长辈传给晚辈，从老师传给学生。"

    old "Once, I was a lad making it here for the first time, with the guidance of an older tribe member. And several times since then, I have led young ones here, so that they may know the route. And now, I do the same for you."
    new "Once, I was a lad making it here for the first time, with the guidance of an older tribe member. And several times since then, I have led young ones here, so that they may know the route. And now, I do the same for you.\n曾经，我也是第一次来到这里的小伙子，由一位年长的部落成员带领。从那以后，我又多次领着年轻人来这里，好让他们认路。而现在，我也为你做着同样的事。"

    old "In a way, you have become one of us, [protag]."
    new "In a way, you have become one of us, [protag].\n从某种意义上说，你已经成了我们中的一员，[protag]。"

    old "I am honored, Larik. I understand that your willingness to share this trip with me is not something that I should take lightly."
    new "I am honored, Larik. I understand that your willingness to share this trip with me is not something that I should take lightly.\n我很荣幸，Larik。我明白，你愿意与我分享这趟旅程，这不是我该等闲视之的事。"

    old "To be a Dunemarcher is to follow the path of Urd."
    new "To be a Dunemarcher is to follow the path of Urd.\n成为 Dunemarcher，就是追随 Urd 的道路。"

    old "I appreciate the sentiment, Larik. But I am not sure that I deserve to be called one of your people."
    new "I appreciate the sentiment, Larik. But I am not sure that I deserve to be called one of your people.\n我感激你的这份心意，Larik。但我不确定自己配得上被称作你们的一员。"

    old "You and your people have spent years, decades in this desert. I have been here for days. I can't hope to compare."
    new "You and your people have spent years, decades in this desert. I have been here for days. I can't hope to compare.\n你和你的族人在沙漠里度过了数年、数十年。我才来了几天。我无法与你们相比。"

    old "[protag]. We call ourselves 'Dunemarchers.' Those who walk the dunes. Look at yourself. Here you are, amongst the dunes, walking along them without faltering and without fear."
    new "[protag]. We call ourselves 'Dunemarchers.' Those who walk the dunes. Look at yourself. Here you are, amongst the dunes, walking along them without faltering and without fear.\n[protag]。我们自称'Dunemarchers'——行走沙丘的人。看看你自己。此刻你就置身沙丘之间，踏着它们前行，既不退缩，也不畏惧。"

    old "I'm only able to walk here because of the gift of these greaves."
    new "I'm only able to walk here because of the gift of these greaves.\n我之所以能在这里行走，全靠这双护胫的馈赠。"

    old "Greaves that you earned through trial. And make no mistake, the person wearing the greaves is just as instrumental. It's not just what you are wearing that allows you to navigate the sands with such ease, it is the way that you move your feet."
    new "Greaves that you earned through trial. And make no mistake, the person wearing the greaves is just as instrumental. It's not just what you are wearing that allows you to navigate the sands with such ease, it is the way that you move your feet.\n那是你历经考验赢来的护胫。而且别搞错了，穿着护胫的人同样关键。让你如此轻松穿行沙地的，不只是你穿戴的东西，还有你迈步的方式。"

    old "You say that I'm one of your people, but I'm not sure that I am one. In fact, I'm not sure that I'd want to be called one."
    new "You say that I'm one of your people, but I'm not sure that I am one. In fact, I'm not sure that I'd want to be called one.\n你说我是你们的一员，但我不确定自己是。事实上，我不确定自己是否愿意被这样称呼。"

    old "Oh?"
    new "Oh?\n哦？"

    old "Larik, you and your people are devoted to this desert. You share a symbiotic relationship with it. You give to the desert, and the desert gives back. It is something that requires dedication."
    new "Larik, you and your people are devoted to this desert. You share a symbiotic relationship with it. You give to the desert, and the desert gives back. It is something that requires dedication.\nLarik，你和你的族人都献身于这片沙漠。你们与它共生。你们给予沙漠，沙漠也回报你们。这需要献身精神。"

    old "I can look at your relationship with the desert and admire it from a distance. But when I consider the amount of dedication that it would take for me to do the same...it seems more than I can muster."
    new "I can look at your relationship with the desert and admire it from a distance. But when I consider the amount of dedication that it would take for me to do the same...it seems more than I can muster.\n我能看待你们与沙漠的关系，并远远地欣赏它。但当我想到，要让我也做到同样的事需要付出多少献身……那似乎超出了我的能力。"

    old "Perhaps you will see it differently some day. But [protag], know this. You're already walking these dunes and tread to places where few others would be capable of reaching."
    new "Perhaps you will see it differently some day. But [protag], know this. You're already walking these dunes and tread to places where few others would be capable of reaching.\n也许有一天你会另有一番看法。但[protag]，你要知道。你已经走在这片沙丘上，踏入了鲜有人能抵达的地方。"

    old "Yes, and I've done it with greaves that were woven by your people."
    new "Yes, and I've done it with greaves that were woven by your people.\n是的，而我是靠着你们族人编织的护胫做到的。"

    old "But you know how to walk in them. And that is no trivial skill."
    new "But you know how to walk in them. And that is no trivial skill.\n但你知道怎么穿着它行走。那可不是微不足道的本事。"

    old "Urd's tale teaches us that it is not merely enough to have the correct tools at your disposal. You must have the cunning and skill to employ them effectively."
    new "Urd's tale teaches us that it is not merely enough to have the correct tools at your disposal. You must have the cunning and skill to employ them effectively.\nUrd 的故事告诉我们，仅仅拥有趁手的工具是不够的。你还必须拥有将其有效运用的机敏与技艺。"

    old "Among the tales of Urd, perhaps my favorite is the one of slaying the hydra."
    new "Among the tales of Urd, perhaps my favorite is the one of slaying the hydra.\n在 Urd 的故事中，也许我最喜欢的是斩杀九头蛇的那一个。"

    old "The beast of many heads."
    new "The beast of many heads.\n那多头之兽。"

    old "Yes. Whenever the hydra lost a head, two more heads would spring from the womb. A seemingly invincible beast."
    new "Yes. Whenever the hydra lost a head, two more heads would spring from the womb. A seemingly invincible beast.\n是的。九头蛇每失去一个头，断口处就会再生出两个头。一头看似不可战胜的野兽。"

    old "How did Urd slay the hydra?"
    new "How did Urd slay the hydra?\nUrd 是怎么斩杀九头蛇的？"

    old "With Baneslayer, he removed one of the hydra's heads. And with the healing powers of Benediction, he sealed the hydra's wounds."
    new "With Baneslayer, he removed one of the hydra's heads. And with the healing powers of Benediction, he sealed the hydra's wounds.\n他用 Baneslayer 斩下九头蛇的一个头，又用 Benediction 的治愈之力封住九头蛇的伤口。"

    old "He defeated his enemy by healing it?"
    new "He defeated his enemy by healing it?\n他靠治愈敌人来打败它？"

    old "Clever, no? The hydra uses injuries to its advantage. Take away its injuries...and its advantage is gone."
    new "Clever, no? The hydra uses injuries to its advantage. Take away its injuries...and its advantage is gone.\n很聪明，不是吗？九头蛇利用伤势为自己牟利。夺走它的伤势……它的优势也就消失了。"

    old "One by one, Baneslayer removed the hydra's heads. And one by one, Benediction sealed the hydra's wounds, preventing it from regenerating. Eventually, the last head was removed, and the hydra was slain."
    new "One by one, Baneslayer removed the hydra's heads. And one by one, Benediction sealed the hydra's wounds, preventing it from regenerating. Eventually, the last head was removed, and the hydra was slain.\n一个接一个，Baneslayer 斩下九头蛇的头；一个接一个，Benediction 封住九头蛇的伤口，使它无法再生。最终，最后一个头被斩下，九头蛇被击杀。"

    old "That's quite a story."
    new "That's quite a story.\n真是个了不起的故事。"

    old "Indeed it is. I've been known to repeat it, so if you catch me telling that same story again, please interrupt me."
    new "Indeed it is. I've been known to repeat it, so if you catch me telling that same story again, please interrupt me.\n确实如此。我出了名的爱重复讲它，所以如果你发现我又在讲同一个故事，请打断我。"

    old "I believe we've arrived."
    new "I believe we've arrived.\n我想我们到了。"

    old "Larik and I stand at the crest of a dune overlooking a large basin. At the bottom of the basin is a black rock formation."
    new "Larik and I stand at the crest of a dune overlooking a large basin. At the bottom of the basin is a black rock formation.\nLarik 和我站在一座沙丘的顶端，俯瞰着一个大盆地。盆地底部是一处黑色的岩石构造。"

    old "That rock formation looks artificial. Is that the tomb?"
    new "That rock formation looks artificial. Is that the tomb?\n那岩石构造看起来像是人工的。那就是坟墓吗？"

    old "You have a good eye, [protag]. Yes, that is where Urd rests. However, something is wrong."
    new "You have a good eye, [protag]. Yes, that is where Urd rests. However, something is wrong.\n你眼光不错，[protag]。没错，那就是 Urd 安息的地方。不过，有些不对劲。"

    old "What's the problem?"
    new "What's the problem?\n什么问题？"

    old "I am not certain. We should investigate."
    new "I am not certain. We should investigate.\n我不确定。我们该去查看一下。"

    old "Larik and I approach the rock formation. As we draw nearer, I can see that there are several small stones surrounding a larger hoodoo, which seems to have several patterns carved into it around the base."
    new "Larik and I approach the rock formation. As we draw nearer, I can see that there are several small stones surrounding a larger hoodoo, which seems to have several patterns carved into it around the base.\nLarik 和我朝那岩石构造走去。走近后，我看到几块小石头围着一根更大的石柱，那石柱底部似乎刻着几圈花纹。"

    old "Look at the sand."
    new "Look at the sand.\n看看这些沙。"

    old "I study the stone and suddenly realize what is wrong."
    new "I study the stone and suddenly realize what is wrong.\n我端详着石头，突然意识到哪里不对劲。"

    old "The rocks aren't black. It's the sand that's covering them."
    new "The rocks aren't black. It's the sand that's covering them.\n石头不是黑色的。是覆盖在它们上面的沙是黑的。"

    old "Where is the black sand coming from?"
    new "Where is the black sand coming from?\n这黑沙是从哪来的？"

    old "That is the question."
    new "That is the question.\n这正是问题所在。"

    old "Larik places his hand against the black sand, and wipes it off of the stone. Immediately, the surrounding sand begins to flow to re-cover the bit that he wiped away."
    new "Larik places his hand against the black sand, and wipes it off of the stone. Immediately, the surrounding sand begins to flow to re-cover the bit that he wiped away.\nLarik 把手按在黑沙上，把它从石头上抹掉。周围的沙立刻开始流动，重新盖住他抹去的那一块。"

    old "The sand seems to have a life of its own."
    new "The sand seems to have a life of its own.\n这些沙似乎有自己的生命。"

    old "Speaking of which... what is that!?"
    new "Speaking of which... what is that!?\n说到这个……那是什么！？"

    old "The black sand is taking the shape of some kind of monster, coming towards us."
    new "The black sand is taking the shape of some kind of monster, coming towards us.\n黑沙正聚成某种怪物的形状，朝我们扑来。"

    old "I don't know what it is, but it doesn't look friendly. Get ready to fight, [protag]!"
    new "I don't know what it is, but it doesn't look friendly. Get ready to fight, [protag]!\n我不知道那是什么，但它看起来不怀好意。准备战斗，[protag]！"

    old "Have you ever seen anything like this? This isn't normal, right?"
    new "Have you ever seen anything like this? This isn't normal, right?\n你见过这样的东西吗？这不正常，对吧？"

    old "No. The sand seems...possessed, somehow. As if something were controlling it."
    new "No. The sand seems...possessed, somehow. As if something were controlling it.\n没有。这沙似乎……被附身了似的，仿佛有什么东西在操控它。"

    old "And look there, on the ground. There was something...'inside' that thing made of sand. Perhaps what remains of some unfortunate traveler."
    new "And look there, on the ground. There was something...'inside' that thing made of sand. Perhaps what remains of some unfortunate traveler.\n再看那边，地上。那个沙做的怪物里有……什么东西。也许是某个不幸旅人的遗骸。"

    old "We're taking it, at least we can use it to avenge whoever this was."
    new "We're taking it, at least we can use it to avenge whoever this was.\n我们把它拿走，至少可以用它来为这死者复仇。"

    old "I have many questions about what is happening here, and no answers. However, the black sand, it seems to be all concentrated here, at Urd's tomb. And I suspect that whatever answers we seek will be found within."
    new "I have many questions about what is happening here, and no answers. However, the black sand, it seems to be all concentrated here, at Urd's tomb. And I suspect that whatever answers we seek will be found within.\n关于这里发生的事，我有很多疑问，却没有答案。然而，黑沙似乎全都集中在这里，集中在 Urd 的坟墓。我猜想，我们所寻求的答案，就在坟墓之内。"

    old "How do we get inside?"
    new "How do we get inside?\n我们怎么进去？"

    old "Here."
    new "Here.\n这里。"

    old "Larik points to a flat section of the rock."
    new "Larik points to a flat section of the rock.\nLarik 指向岩石上一处平坦的地方。"

    old "This circular stone covers the entrance."
    new "This circular stone covers the entrance.\n这块圆形的石板盖着入口。"

    old "Larik grips the stone slab from one end and pushes it away, exposing a cavity in the rock. Almost immediately, the black sands begin to shift, and the stone rolls back into place."
    new "Larik grips the stone slab from one end and pushes it away, exposing a cavity in the rock. Almost immediately, the black sands begin to shift, and the stone rolls back into place.\nLarik 从一端抓住石板，把它推开，露出岩石里的一个洞口。几乎立刻，黑沙开始移动，石板又滚回了原位。"

    old "Incredible. The sands have this kind of power."
    new "Incredible. The sands have this kind of power.\n难以置信。这些沙竟有这种力量。"

    old "Sands that can move rock are probably strong enough to choke a man. And yet the sands don't seem to react to us at all."
    new "Sands that can move rock are probably strong enough to choke a man. And yet the sands don't seem to react to us at all.\n能移动岩石的沙，恐怕强到足以把人活活扼死。然而这些沙对我们似乎毫无反应。"

    old "Indeed. The sands only reacted when I disturbed them, or disturbed the rock. It seems almost as if whatever dark force is here has only taken control over the sand itself."
    new "Indeed. The sands only reacted when I disturbed them, or disturbed the rock. It seems almost as if whatever dark force is here has only taken control over the sand itself.\n确实。只有在我惊扰了沙、或惊扰了岩石时，沙才有反应。看起来，这里的某种黑暗力量似乎只控制了沙本身。"

    old "What about the scorpions that I saw earlier with Nuala? Those seem to have sprung from the same corruption."
    new "What about the scorpions that I saw earlier with Nuala? Those seem to have sprung from the same corruption.\n那我早前和 Nuala 一起看到的那些蝎子呢？它们似乎也源自同样的腐化。"

    old "And yet scorpions are beasts of the sand. If a sand-dweller like an ant lion or sand king were to lay its eggs inside of this black sand, who knows what would happen?"
    new "And yet scorpions are beasts of the sand. If a sand-dweller like an ant lion or sand king were to lay its eggs inside of this black sand, who knows what would happen?\n然而蝎子本就是沙地之兽。如果像蚁狮或沙王这样的沙栖生物在黑沙中产卵，谁知道会发生什么？"

    old "So you think we're not at risk of being attacked?"
    new "So you think we're not at risk of being attacked?\n所以你认为我们没有受到攻击的危险？"

    old "Not directly. However, the sand does have power over the land itself. And that poses a problem, because if we enter the tomb, it will seal us inside. I can roll the tomb from the outside, but once inside, it is much more formidable."
    new "Not directly. However, the sand does have power over the land itself. And that poses a problem, because if we enter the tomb, it will seal us inside. I can roll the tomb from the outside, but once inside, it is much more formidable.\n不是直接的。不过，这些沙确实对土地本身有掌控力。这就带来一个问题，因为如果我们进入坟墓，它会把我们封在里面。我能在外面推动石板，但一旦进去，就要棘手得多。"

    old "You should stay outside, then. I'll go in to investigate."
    new "You should stay outside, then. I'll go in to investigate.\n那你应该待在外面。我进去查看。"

    old "I can't hold the stone against the force of the sands. I don't have the strength to hold the entrance open for that long."
    new "I can't hold the stone against the force of the sands. I don't have the strength to hold the entrance open for that long.\n我无法顶着沙的力量顶住石板。我没有力气把入口撑开那么久。"

    old "Then let the stone roll back into place. I'll beckon you from within when I'm ready for you to open the entrance and release me. Will you be able to hear me from outside if I yell for you?"
    new "Then let the stone roll back into place. I'll beckon you from within when I'm ready for you to open the entrance and release me. Will you be able to hear me from outside if I yell for you?\n那就让石板滚回原位吧。等我准备好让你打开入口、放我出来时，我会从里面叫你。如果我朝你喊，你在外面能听到吗？"

    old "Yes, I can do that."
    new "Yes, I can do that.\n能，我可以。"

    old "Then let's do it."
    new "Then let's do it.\n那就动手吧。"

    old "Larik nods and pushes the stone aside, exposing the tomb's entrance. I step through, and a moment later, the stone rolls back into place, trapping me inside."
    new "Larik nods and pushes the stone aside, exposing the tomb's entrance. I step through, and a moment later, the stone rolls back into place, trapping me inside.\nLarik 点点头，把石板推开，露出坟墓的入口。我走了进去，片刻后，石板滚回原位，把我困在了里面。"

    old "Larik, can you hear me?"
    new "Larik, can you hear me?\nLarik，你能听到我吗？"

    old "I hear Larik's muffled voice from the other side."
    new "I hear Larik's muffled voice from the other side.\n我听到 Larik 从另一边传来的闷闷的声音。"

    old "Yes. Are you alright?"
    new "Yes. Are you alright?\n能。你没事吧？"

    old "I'm okay. I'll call if I need help."
    new "I'm okay. I'll call if I need help.\n我没事。需要帮忙我会喊。"

    old "I can hear Larik well enough when I'm standing directly beside the entrance. If I venture too far in, he probably won't be able to hear me. I should proceed with caution."
    new "I can hear Larik well enough when I'm standing directly beside the entrance. If I venture too far in, he probably won't be able to hear me. I should proceed with caution.\n当我直接站在入口旁时，能清楚地听到 Larik 的声音。如果我走得太深，他大概就听不到我了。我应该谨慎前行。"

    old "The stone that covers the entrance isn't a perfect seal. A scant amount of sunlight pokes through the cracks at the edges of the entrance, and by that dim light I'm able to survey the tomb's chamber."
    new "The stone that covers the entrance isn't a perfect seal. A scant amount of sunlight pokes through the cracks at the edges of the entrance, and by that dim light I'm able to survey the tomb's chamber.\n盖着入口的石板并不完全密封。少量阳光从入口边缘的缝隙透进来，借着这昏暗的光，我得以查看墓室。"

    old "I return to the entrance and call out."
    new "I return to the entrance and call out.\n我回到入口处，喊出声来。"

    old "Larik! Are you still out there?"
    new "Larik! Are you still out there?\nLarik！你还在外面吗？"

    old "I'm still here! You want out?"
    new "I'm still here! You want out?\n我还在！你想出来吗？"

    old "Yes, I think I'm done in here."
    new "Yes, I think I'm done in here.\n是的，我想我在这里面看完了。"

    old "The stone rolls away from the entrance, and I step out into the light."
    new "The stone rolls away from the entrance, and I step out into the light.\n石板从入口处滚开，我迈步走进光亮中。"

    old "[protag], what happened in there?"
    new "[protag], what happened in there?\n[protag]，里面发生了什么？"

    old "I saw...vampires. Vampires from N'Mar."
    new "I saw...vampires. Vampires from N'Mar.\n我看到了……Vampires。来自 N'Mar 的 Vampires。"

    old "Are they the ones that were spawning the magic that blackened the sands?"
    new "Are they the ones that were spawning the magic that blackened the sands?\n是他们在制造使沙变黑的魔法吗？"

    old "No, I think it's the opposite. Rather than propogating the dark magic, they seemed to be trying to dispel it."
    new "No, I think it's the opposite. Rather than propogating the dark magic, they seemed to be trying to dispel it.\n不，我想恰恰相反。他们非但没有散播黑暗魔法，反而像是在设法驱散它。"

    old "How could that be?"
    new "How could that be?\n怎么会这样？"

    old "Not all vampires are on friendly terms. Perhaps they're fighting the same enemy that I am."
    new "Not all vampires are on friendly terms. Perhaps they're fighting the same enemy that I am.\n并非所有 Vampires 都彼此交好。也许他们正和我对抗着同一个敌人。"

    old "I think I may have discovered the source of the corruption that springs from this tomb."
    new "I think I may have discovered the source of the corruption that springs from this tomb.\n我想我可能发现了这坟墓中腐化的源头。"

    old "[protag], look at the stone."
    new "[protag], look at the stone.\n[protag]，看那块石头。"

    old "I turn back and look at the stone that covered the tomb's entrance."
    new "I turn back and look at the stone that covered the tomb's entrance.\n我转过身，看向盖着坟墓入口的那块石板。"

    old "It hasn't resealed the tomb."
    new "It hasn't resealed the tomb.\n它没有再封住坟墓。"

    old "I look at the stone, and slowly the blackness that covers it begins to dissipate. The sand lightens in color, then begins sliding down the rock face until it hits the ground, mixing indistinctly with the sand of the desert's dunes."
    new "I look at the stone, and slowly the blackness that covers it begins to dissipate. The sand lightens in color, then begins sliding down the rock face until it hits the ground, mixing indistinctly with the sand of the desert's dunes.\n我看着那块石头，覆盖其上的黑色缓缓消散。沙的颜色变浅，随后开始顺着岩面滑落，直到落到地面，与沙漠沙丘的沙混为一体，难分彼此。"

    old "I wouldn't believe it if I didn't see it. Apparently, whatever you did inside of that tomb worked. If the corruption is really gone, then we should be able to enter the tomb and explore."
    new "I wouldn't believe it if I didn't see it. Apparently, whatever you did inside of that tomb worked. If the corruption is really gone, then we should be able to enter the tomb and explore.\n若不是亲眼所见，我是不会信的。看来，你在坟墓里所做的无论是什么，都奏效了。如果腐化真的消失了，那我们就能进入坟墓一探究竟了。"

    old "Explore?"
    new "Explore?\n一探究竟？"

    old "[protag], I haven't forgotten why you came here in the first place. You came here looking for Urd's legendary axe and rod. You've helped me and my people with our problem. Now it is my duty to help you with yours. Let's go inside."
    new "[protag], I haven't forgotten why you came here in the first place. You came here looking for Urd's legendary axe and rod. You've helped me and my people with our problem. Now it is my duty to help you with yours. Let's go inside.\n[protag]，我没忘记你最初为什么来这里。你是来找 Urd 传奇的斧与法杖的。你帮我和我的族人解决了我们的难题。现在轮到我帮你解决你的了。我们进去吧。"

    old "Larik and I step into the tomb. With the entrance open behind us, I can now see the interior more clearly, and I spot a passageway leading further into the tombs."
    new "Larik and I step into the tomb. With the entrance open behind us, I can now see the interior more clearly, and I spot a passageway leading further into the tombs.\nLarik 和我走进坟墓。入口在身后敞开着，如今我能更清楚地看到内部，还发现了一条通往更深处的墓道。"

    old "Do you want to lead the way?"
    new "Do you want to lead the way?\n你想带路吗？"

    old "If you're asking for me to be your guide inside this tomb, be warned that I am no more familiar with its interior than you are."
    new "If you're asking for me to be your guide inside this tomb, be warned that I am no more familiar with its interior than you are.\n如果你是想让我在这坟墓里做你的向导，那我得提醒你，我对它的内部并不比你熟悉。"

    old "You've never been in here?"
    new "You've never been in here?\n你从没进来过？"

    old "No one has entered the tomb's inner catacombs for many decades. Stories say that the innermost catacombs are sealed by magic."
    new "No one has entered the tomb's inner catacombs for many decades. Stories say that the innermost catacombs are sealed by magic.\n数十年来，没有人进入过坟墓内部的地穴。据说最深处的地穴被魔法封印着。"

    old "That sounds believable."
    new "That sounds believable.\n听起来可信。"

    old "Yes, I think so too. The tomb of Urd has always had a certain mystic quality to it, even before the corruption began stemming from it. Perhaps the desert corruption was pulling from some kind of latent magic that rests here."
    new "Yes, I think so too. The tomb of Urd has always had a certain mystic quality to it, even before the corruption began stemming from it. Perhaps the desert corruption was pulling from some kind of latent magic that rests here.\n是的，我也这么想。Urd 的坟墓一直带有某种神秘的特质，甚至在腐化开始从中滋生之前就是如此。也许沙漠的腐化，正是从沉睡于此的某种潜藏魔法中汲取力量。"

    old "You think that might be possible?"
    new "You think that might be possible?\n你觉得那有可能吗？"

    old "Anything is possible. But our eyes will tell us soon enough whether the stories are true. Let's see what really lies inside this tomb."
    new "Anything is possible. But our eyes will tell us soon enough whether the stories are true. Let's see what really lies inside this tomb.\n凡事皆有可能。不过这些故事是真是假，我们的眼睛很快就会告诉我们。让我们看看这坟墓里究竟藏着什么。"

    old "I'm inclined to doubt such stories."
    new "I'm inclined to doubt such stories.\n我倾向于怀疑这类故事。"

    old "Oh? For what reason?"
    new "Oh? For what reason?\n哦？什么理由？"

    old "Any time I hear stories of events long ago that involve magic, my instinct is to be skeptical."
    new "Any time I hear stories of events long ago that involve magic, my instinct is to be skeptical.\n每当听到久远过去里涉及魔法的故事，我的本能就是怀疑。"

    old "And yet you're in the tomb of a centuries-passed warrior, hoping to find his legendary weapons."
    new "And yet you're in the tomb of a centuries-passed warrior, hoping to find his legendary weapons.\n而你此刻却身处一位已逝数世纪之久的战士的坟墓，指望找到他传奇的武器。"

    old "I'm here because of credible scholarly authorities, not the tall tales of common people."
    new "I'm here because of credible scholarly authorities, not the tall tales of common people.\n我来这里，是因为可靠的学术权威，而不是普通人的夸张传说。"

    old "Oral tradition is still a form of record keeping, [protag]. But doubt what you will, and let your eyes tell you what truly is. Let's see what really is inside this tomb."
    new "Oral tradition is still a form of record keeping, [protag]. But doubt what you will, and let your eyes tell you what truly is. Let's see what really is inside this tomb.\n口述传统仍是一种记录方式，[protag]。但你想怀疑什么就怀疑吧，让你的眼睛告诉你真相。让我们看看这坟墓里究竟有什么。"

    old "Larik turns his attention to the walls of the chamber. He touches a section of the wall and begins running his hand along it."
    new "Larik turns his attention to the walls of the chamber. He touches a section of the wall and begins running his hand along it.\nLarik 把注意力转向墓室的墙壁。他触到墙上的一处，开始用手沿着它摸索。"

    old "Looking for etchings."
    new "Looking for etchings.\n在找刻痕。"

    old "What about the catacombs?"
    new "What about the catacombs?\n那地穴怎么办？"

    old "If we're going to search this tomb, we should search it. I have a feeling that patience will reward us. Destiny has a way of punishing the foolhardy."
    new "If we're going to search this tomb, we should search it. I have a feeling that patience will reward us. Destiny has a way of punishing the foolhardy.\n既然要搜查这座坟墓，那就该好好搜。我有种感觉，耐心会有回报。命运自有办法惩罚鲁莽之人。"

    old "Speaking from personal experience?"
    new "Speaking from personal experience?\n这是亲身体会？"

    old "Heh. What young boy hasn't experienced a bit of pain as a result of poor choices? It's how we learn. But sometimes, we can learn without painful mistakes."
    new "Heh. What young boy hasn't experienced a bit of pain as a result of poor choices? It's how we learn. But sometimes, we can learn without painful mistakes.\n嘿。哪个小男孩没有因为糟糕的选择吃过点苦头？我们就是这样学习的。但有时，不必经历痛苦的错误，我们也能学到东西。"

    old "Larik's hand stops over a section of the wall, and he taps it gently with the head of his axe. Several loose pebbles are dislodged by the impact. The small stones fall to the floor, leaving a groove in the wall."
    new "Larik's hand stops over a section of the wall, and he taps it gently with the head of his axe. Several loose pebbles are dislodged by the impact. The small stones fall to the floor, leaving a groove in the wall.\nLarik 的手停在墙上的一处，他用斧头轻轻敲了敲。几下敲击震落了几块松动的碎石。小石子掉到地上，墙上露出了一道凹槽。"

    old "I think I've found it."
    new "I think I've found it.\n我想我找到了。"

    old "Larik points the handle of his axe at the wall, and gives it several more gentle taps. With each tap, sand is dislodged from small grooves, and what's left seems to be a series of symbols."
    new "Larik points the handle of his axe at the wall, and gives it several more gentle taps. With each tap, sand is dislodged from small grooves, and what's left seems to be a series of symbols.\nLarik 把斧柄指向墙面，又轻轻敲了几下。每敲一下，就有沙从细小的凹槽里震落，剩下的似乎是一串符号。"

    old "What do these symbols mean?"
    new "What do these symbols mean?\n这些符号是什么意思？"

    old "It's writing."
    new "It's writing.\n是文字。"

    old "Can you read it?"
    new "Can you read it?\n你能读懂吗？"

    old "It's an older language, but one that is still taught by the village elders. And the tribe's future elders, which includes me. Yes, I can read it. However, the meaning does not translate cleanly. These symbols express ideas, rather than complete sentences."
    new "It's an older language, but one that is still taught by the village elders. And the tribe's future elders, which includes me. Yes, I can read it. However, the meaning does not translate cleanly. These symbols express ideas, rather than complete sentences.\n这是一种更古老的语言，但村中长老仍在教授。部落未来的长老，包括我在内，也都要学。是的，我能读懂。不过，它的含义没法直截了当地翻译出来。这些符号表达的是概念，而不是完整的句子。"

    old "This passage. It says, 'mystic seal, mystic break. Sunrise, sunset.'"
    new "This passage. It says, 'mystic seal, mystic break. Sunrise, sunset.'\n这一段。它写着：'神秘的封印，神秘的破封。日出，日落。'"

    old "What is that supposed to mean? Something about the time of day?"
    new "What is that supposed to mean? Something about the time of day?\n那是什么意思？跟一天中的时辰有关？"

    old "Perhaps. But there are many symbols that express sunrise and sunset. Some symbols were used in recordkeeping, to report the time of day. Other symbols are intended to express more...romantic notions of sunrise and sunset."
    new "Perhaps. But there are many symbols that express sunrise and sunset. Some symbols were used in recordkeeping, to report the time of day. Other symbols are intended to express more...romantic notions of sunrise and sunset.\n也许。但表达日出和日落的符号有很多种。有些符号用于记事，用来记录一天中的时辰。另一些符号则意在表达关于日出与日落的更……浪漫的意涵。"

    old "I think whoever wrote 'sunrise, sunset' intended these symbols to indicate ideas. Two opposite concepts."
    new "I think whoever wrote 'sunrise, sunset' intended these symbols to indicate ideas. Two opposite concepts.\n我想写'日出、日落'的人，是打算用这些符号来表示概念。两个相反的概念。"

    old "Similar to the first part. 'Mystic seal, mystic break.' In a way, the sunset is the 'undoing' of the sunrise. And a 'mystic break' might be the opposite of a 'mystic seal.' Breaking the seal?"
    new "Similar to the first part. 'Mystic seal, mystic break.' In a way, the sunset is the 'undoing' of the sunrise. And a 'mystic break' might be the opposite of a 'mystic seal.' Breaking the seal?\n和前半部分类似。'神秘的封印，神秘的破封。'从某种意义上说，日落是日出的'消解'。而'神秘的破封'或许是'神秘的封印'的反面。破开封印？"

    old "This seems to be consistent with the ideas that there is some kind of magic seal on the this tomb's inner catacombs."
    new "This seems to be consistent with the ideas that there is some kind of magic seal on the this tomb's inner catacombs.\n这似乎与'这坟墓内部地穴上有某种魔法封印'的想法吻合。"

    old "But the seal can be broken. Mystic break...breaking the magical seal with magic?"
    new "But the seal can be broken. Mystic break...breaking the magical seal with magic?\n但封印可以被破开。神秘的破封……用魔法破开魔法封印？"

    old "That makes sense. I don't know how else you would undo a magical seal."
    new "That makes sense. I don't know how else you would undo a magical seal.\n这说得通。我不知道除此之外还能怎样解除魔法封印。"

    old "[protag], there's another thing. There's a symbol, here. I believe it says 'danger.'"
    new "[protag], there's another thing. There's a symbol, here. I believe it says 'danger.'\n[protag]，还有一件事。这里有个符号。我想它写的是'危险'。"

    old "Danger within?"
    new "Danger within?\n内部的危险？"

    old "Perhaps it means, 'danger if the seal is broken.' Or maybe it is part of a separate idea, not related to the magic seal."
    new "Perhaps it means, 'danger if the seal is broken.' Or maybe it is part of a separate idea, not related to the magic seal.\n也许它的意思是'封印若破，必有危险'。又或许它是另一个独立概念的一部分，与魔法封印无关。"

    old "Danger. Some kind of deterrent? To scare people away?"
    new "Danger. Some kind of deterrent? To scare people away?\n危险。某种威慑？用来把人吓跑？"

    old "It may be more of a caution. A warning. Proceed with caution."
    new "It may be more of a caution. A warning. Proceed with caution.\n也许更是一种告诫。一种警告。谨慎行事。"

    old "I believe we may be best to heed its advice. What do you think?"
    new "I believe we may be best to heed its advice. What do you think?\n我认为我们最好听从它的劝告。你觉得呢？"

    old "I am sure that whoever wrote this warning knew a lot more about what dangers lurk inside this tomb than we do. I think we'd do well to take their advice."
    new "I am sure that whoever wrote this warning knew a lot more about what dangers lurk inside this tomb than we do. I think we'd do well to take their advice.\n我确信，写下这警告的人，比我们更了解这坟墓里潜伏着何种危险。我想我们最好接受他们的建议。"

    old "What do you suggest?"
    new "What do you suggest?\n你有什么建议？"

    old "I think that we should leave. With just the two of us here, it seems dangerous to go any further."
    new "I think that we should leave. With just the two of us here, it seems dangerous to go any further.\n我想我们应该离开。只有我们两个在这里，再往前走似乎太危险了。"

    old "Perhaps we can return once we've had a chance to reconsider things and prepare for what trials might wait ahead."
    new "Perhaps we can return once we've had a chance to reconsider things and prepare for what trials might wait ahead.\n也许等我们有机会重新考虑、并为前方可能等待的考验做好准备之后，可以再回来。"

    old "I want to keep going."
    new "I want to keep going.\n我想继续往前走。"

    old "So do I, [protag]. But I wonder if that is possible."
    new "So do I, [protag]. But I wonder if that is possible.\n我也是，[protag]。但我怀疑这是否可行。"

    old "This writing seems to suggest that magic is an essential tool on proceeding forward. I believe it would be foolish for us to continue without a practiced shaman."
    new "This writing seems to suggest that magic is an essential tool on proceeding forward. I believe it would be foolish for us to continue without a practiced shaman.\n这些文字似乎在暗示，魔法是继续前进必不可少的工具。我认为，没有一位经验丰富的萨满，我们就贸然继续，是愚蠢的。"

    old "Someone like Nuala, then?"
    new "Someone like Nuala, then?\n那么，像 Nuala 那样的人？"

    old "That is exactly what I was thinking."
    new "That is exactly what I was thinking.\n这正是我所想的。"

    old "[protag], there are mysteries in this tomb, mysteries that I would like to see unraveled. More than that, if there are artifacts within this tomb that might aid you on your quest, I believe I owe it to you to aid in their pursuit."
    new "[protag], there are mysteries in this tomb, mysteries that I would like to see unraveled. More than that, if there are artifacts within this tomb that might aid you on your quest, I believe I owe it to you to aid in their pursuit.\n[protag]，这坟墓里有谜团，有我希望解开的谜团。不仅如此，如果这坟墓里有能助你完成使命的遗物，我想我理应帮你寻得它们。"

    old "But this is not an endeavor to be made halfheartedly. Let us go back to camp, have a chance to rest. We can return to this problem with fresh eyes, as well as a shaman to help us should magic essential in surviving whatever trials might lie ahead."
    new "But this is not an endeavor to be made halfheartedly. Let us go back to camp, have a chance to rest. We can return to this problem with fresh eyes, as well as a shaman to help us should magic essential in surviving whatever trials might lie ahead.\n但这不该是一件半心半意去做的事。让我们回营地，休息一下。我们可以带着崭新的眼光回来处理这个问题，同时带上一位萨满，以便在前方无论何种考验中，若需魔法方能活命，有人相助。"

    old "Very well. Let's head back to camp."
    new "Very well. Let's head back to camp.\n很好。我们回营地去。"

    old "I step out of the tomb, and Larik follows me into the sunlight."
    new "I step out of the tomb, and Larik follows me into the sunlight.\n我走出坟墓，Larik 跟着我走进阳光里。"

    old "[protag], it has become clear to me that the fate of my people is deeply connected with your mission."
    new "[protag], it has become clear to me that the fate of my people is deeply connected with your mission.\n[protag]，我越来越清楚，我人民的命运与你的使命息息相关。"

    old "It seems odd, but the darkness itself seems to heed your beck and call."
    new "It seems odd, but the darkness itself seems to heed your beck and call.\n说来奇怪，但黑暗本身似乎都听从你的召唤。"

    old "Oh, I wouldn't go that far."
    new "Oh, I wouldn't go that far.\n哦，我可没到那种地步。"

    old "Is it so outlandish for me to say? You disappear into Urd's tomb, and moments after you emerge, the corruption that was infesting it subsides. One might even call you a light-bringer."
    new "Is it so outlandish for me to say? You disappear into Urd's tomb, and moments after you emerge, the corruption that was infesting it subsides. One might even call you a light-bringer.\n我这么说很离谱吗？你消失在 Urd 的坟墓里，出来之后没过多久，侵扰那里的腐化就消退了。人们甚至可以说你是位光明使者。"

    old "'Light-bringer,' eh? If that's my new title, I like it."
    new "'Light-bringer,' eh? If that's my new title, I like it.\n'光明使者'，嗯？如果这是我的新头衔，我喜欢。"

    old "I'm not sure that I can live up to the title. I'm not a light-bringer."
    new "I'm not sure that I can live up to the title. I'm not a light-bringer.\n我不确定自己配得上这个头衔。我不是什么光明使者。"

    old "You chased away the darkness. That sounds like a light-bringer to me."
    new "You chased away the darkness. That sounds like a light-bringer to me.\n你驱散了黑暗。在我看来，这就像一位光明使者。"

    old "I cannot help but think that my people would benefit from seeing you succeed in your mission. I think that I now have a personal interest in your affairs."
    new "I cannot help but think that my people would benefit from seeing you succeed in your mission. I think that I now have a personal interest in your affairs.\n我不禁觉得，看到你成功完成使命，我的人民将从中受益。我想，如今我对你的事务有了私人的关切。"

    old "I'd like to lend you my own personal aid, if you would have it. I preside over my people by day, but I could be called upon to lend my axe to your fight."
    new "I'd like to lend you my own personal aid, if you would have it. I preside over my people by day, but I could be called upon to lend my axe to your fight.\n如果你愿意接受，我想亲自助你一臂之力。我白天主持部落事务，但也可以应召把我的斧头借给你的战斗。"

    old "If you're ready to cleave skulls on my behalf, I feel I'd be a fool to refuse the offer."
    new "If you're ready to cleave skulls on my behalf, I feel I'd be a fool to refuse the offer.\n如果你愿意为我劈开头骨，我觉得自己要是拒绝，就太蠢了。"

    old "Excellent. It will be a pleasure to fight alongside you."
    new "Excellent. It will be a pleasure to fight alongside you.\n太好了。能与你并肩作战，将是我的荣幸。"

    old "[protag]. Do you have a moment?"
    new "[protag]. Do you have a moment?\n[protag]。你有空吗？"

    old "If it's something that you care about, then it's probably something I should care about. What is it, Kusho?"
    new "If it's something that you care about, then it's probably something I should care about. What is it, Kusho?\n如果是你在意的事，那大概也是我该在意的事。什么事，Kusho？"

    old "I may be long overdue in saying this, but I owe you my thanks in assisting me with the arrest of Vaeril."
    new "I may be long overdue in saying this, but I owe you my thanks in assisting me with the arrest of Vaeril.\n这话我可能早就该说了，但我得感谢你协助我逮捕 Vaeril。"

    old "Your service to me is thanks enough, Vaeril. Words are cheap. Actions say far more."
    new "Your service to me is thanks enough, Vaeril. Words are cheap. Actions say far more.\n你为我效力，就已是足够的感谢了，Vaeril。言语是廉价的。行动才有分量。"

    old "Well, I've given you my thanks, and I may now owe you an apology."
    new "Well, I've given you my thanks, and I may now owe you an apology.\n好了，我谢过你了，而现在我可能还欠你一个道歉。"

    old "I presumed that Vaeril's dark magic was the source of the odd happenings around the Great Forest. I hunted him down with the intention of ending the blight. However..."
    new "I presumed that Vaeril's dark magic was the source of the odd happenings around the Great Forest. I hunted him down with the intention of ending the blight. However...\n我曾推断 Vaeril 的黑暗魔法是 Great Forest 周围那些怪事的源头。我追捕他，本是为了终结那场枯萎之害。然而……"

    old "Vaeril has been incarcerated, and yet still the woodcrashers continue to roam and decimate the forest. The man that we put in jain may not be responsible for the blight after all."
    new "Vaeril has been incarcerated, and yet still the woodcrashers continue to roam and decimate the forest. The man that we put in jain may not be responsible for the blight after all.\nVaeril 已被收监，可 woodcrashers 仍在森林里游荡、肆意破坏。我们关进牢里的那个人，也许根本不该为那场枯萎之害负责。"

    old "Are you saying we put an innocent man in jail?"
    new "Are you saying we put an innocent man in jail?\n你是说我们把一个无辜的人关进了监狱？"

    old "No, no. Please don't misunderstand. Vaeril's foul sorceries are, in and of themselves, a crime deserving of punishment. While Vaeril lived in exile, the truth is that it would have been fair in the eyes of the law to imprison him at any time."
    new "No, no. Please don't misunderstand. Vaeril's foul sorceries are, in and of themselves, a crime deserving of punishment. While Vaeril lived in exile, the truth is that it would have been fair in the eyes of the law to imprison him at any time.\n不，不。请别误会。Vaeril 的邪恶巫术本身，就是该受惩罚的罪行。在 Vaeril 流亡期间，事实上，从法律角度看，任何时候监禁他都算合情合理。"

    old "However, at the time, Vaeril was not seen as a threat to be imprisoned. That changed when the woodcrashers showed up."
    new "However, at the time, Vaeril was not seen as a threat to be imprisoned. That changed when the woodcrashers showed up.\n然而，在当时，Vaeril 并不被视为需要监禁的威胁。直到 woodcrashers 出现，情况才改变。"

    old "Vaeril deserves his fate. But it is clear now that imprisoning him has done nothing to end the corruption in the Great Forest. Though I succeeded in achieving my objective to apprehend Vaeril, I failed in my mission to save the forest."
    new "Vaeril deserves his fate. But it is clear now that imprisoning him has done nothing to end the corruption in the Great Forest. Though I succeeded in achieving my objective to apprehend Vaeril, I failed in my mission to save the forest.\nVaeril 该当此命。但如今已很清楚，监禁他丝毫无助于终结 Great Forest 的腐化。尽管我达成了逮捕 Vaeril 的目标，却在拯救森林的使命上失败了。"

    old "I've given you my thanks, and I've given you my apology. Now I'd like to submit a request. Of course, I'm not so presumptuous as to think you'll be ready to accept it so readily."
    new "I've given you my thanks, and I've given you my apology. Now I'd like to submit a request. Of course, I'm not so presumptuous as to think you'll be ready to accept it so readily.\n我已向你道过谢，也向你道过歉。现在我想提出一个请求。当然，我不会自以为你会那么容易就接受。"

    old "I'm not going to refuse your request before I've had a chance to hear it, Kusho."
    new "I'm not going to refuse your request before I've had a chance to hear it, Kusho.\n在我有机会听到你的请求之前，我是不会拒绝的，Kusho。"

    old "Very well. Some new information has come to light. I have spent some time stalking the woodcrashers of the Great Forest."
    new "Very well. Some new information has come to light. I have spent some time stalking the woodcrashers of the Great Forest.\n很好。有了一些新线索。我花了一段时间追踪 Great Forest 的 woodcrashers。"

    old "Stalking them?"
    new "Stalking them?\n追踪它们？"

    old "As a hunter stalks prey. I am a slayer of beasts as well as a slayer of men."
    new "As a hunter stalks prey. I am a slayer of beasts as well as a slayer of men.\n就像猎人追踪猎物那样。我既是野兽的屠戮者，也是人的屠戮者。"

    old "So you've been hunting the woodcrashers."
    new "So you've been hunting the woodcrashers.\n所以你一直在猎杀那些 woodcrashers。"

    old "Not exactly, no. The woodcrashers are too numerous to be hunted out. The forest is vast, and their numbers increase every day. I could kill ten woodcrashers every day, and yet still more would continue to spawn. No, it is not enough to kill individual woodcrashers."
    new "Not exactly, no. The woodcrashers are too numerous to be hunted out. The forest is vast, and their numbers increase every day. I could kill ten woodcrashers every day, and yet still more would continue to spawn. No, it is not enough to kill individual woodcrashers.\n也不完全是。woodcrashers 数量太多，猎杀不尽。森林广阔，它们的数目每天都在增加。我可以每天杀死十头 woodcrashers，可仍会有更多不断滋生。不，杀死单独的 woodcrashers 是不够的。"

    old "That is why I have been stalking them. Studying them. Following them. And by tracking their behavior and movements, I believe I have identified where it is that they spawn from."
    new "That is why I have been stalking them. Studying them. Following them. And by tracking their behavior and movements, I believe I have identified where it is that they spawn from.\n正因如此，我一直在追踪它们。研究它们。跟踪它们。通过记录它们的行为和动向，我相信我已经确定了它们是从哪里滋生的。"

    old "Is this where I enter the equation?"
    new "Is this where I enter the equation?\n这就是我出场的地方？"

    old "In a manner of speaking. You see, though I consider the Great Forest my home, it is impossible for one elf to know it in its entirety."
    new "In a manner of speaking. You see, though I consider the Great Forest my home, it is impossible for one elf to know it in its entirety.\n从某种意义上说。你看，虽然我把 Great Forest 视为家园，但一个 Elf 不可能完全了解它。"

    old "Additionally, due to the nature of my profession, I have tended to favor the areas of the forest which are near settlements—the portions of the forest where one would be most likely to encounter other elves."
    new "Additionally, due to the nature of my profession, I have tended to favor the areas of the forest which are near settlements—the portions of the forest where one would be most likely to encounter other elves.\n此外，由于我职业的性质，我往往偏爱靠近聚落的林区——也就是最可能遇到其他 Elves 的森林地带。"

    old "However, the woodcrashers tend to favor the portions of the forest which are least inhabited."
    new "However, the woodcrashers tend to favor the portions of the forest which are least inhabited.\n然而，woodcrashers 往往偏爱森林中最荒无人烟的地带。"

    old "I have given it some thought. I think that I would benefit greatly from having a guide. Specifically, a guide that is familiar with the portions of the forest where I may be out of my element."
    new "I have given it some thought. I think that I would benefit greatly from having a guide. Specifically, a guide that is familiar with the portions of the forest where I may be out of my element.\n我对此作了一番思考。我想，若有一位向导，我将受益匪浅。具体来说，是一位熟悉那些我可能力不从心的林区的向导。"

    old "The sort of elf who has spent many years living in the forest, sticking to the areas which are least likely to be inhabited by other elves."
    new "The sort of elf who has spent many years living in the forest, sticking to the areas which are least likely to be inhabited by other elves.\n那种在森林里生活多年、专待在少有其他 Elves 出没之地的 Elf。"

    old "I am, of course, speaking of Vaeril."
    new "I am, of course, speaking of Vaeril.\n当然，我说的是 Vaeril。"

    old "What are you suggesting?"
    new "What are you suggesting?\n你是什么意思？"

    old "The passage of time has shown us that Vaeril is not linked to the woodcrasher infestation in the forest. He is not part of the problem. What if he could be part of the solution?"
    new "The passage of time has shown us that Vaeril is not linked to the woodcrasher infestation in the forest. He is not part of the problem. What if he could be part of the solution?\n时间的流逝已经向我们表明，Vaeril 与森林里的 woodcrasher 侵扰并无关联。他不是问题的一部分。如果他能成为解决办法的一部分呢？"

    old "Vaeril was imprisoned with your authorization. I'm sure that he could be released with your authorization, at least on a provisional basis."
    new "Vaeril was imprisoned with your authorization. I'm sure that he could be released with your authorization, at least on a provisional basis.\nVaeril 是经你授权才被监禁的。我相信，经你授权他也能获释，至少是临时性的。"

    old "Have you asked Vaeril himself?"
    new "Have you asked Vaeril himself?\n你问过 Vaeril 本人吗？"

    old "No. I haven't bothered making a visit. I figured that would be best left in your hands."
    new "No. I haven't bothered making a visit. I figured that would be best left in your hands.\n没有。我一直没费心去探望。我想这事最好还是交给你。"

    old "Anyway, this doesn't need to happen today. In fact, I think you should give this some thought. Releasing a man from jail—even if it's only a temporary release—isn't something that should be done on an impulse."
    new "Anyway, this doesn't need to happen today. In fact, I think you should give this some thought. Releasing a man from jail—even if it's only a temporary release—isn't something that should be done on an impulse.\n总之，这事不必今天办。事实上，我认为你应该好好想想。把一个人放出牢房——即便只是暂时释放——也不该凭一时冲动去做。"

    old "I'll give it some thought, Kusho."
    new "I'll give it some thought, Kusho.\n我会考虑的，Kusho。"

    old "[protag], one last thing. When we were escorting Vaeril from the Great Forest to Grimoire, I noticed something. He seems to trust you. He's more relaxed around you."
    new "[protag], one last thing. When we were escorting Vaeril from the Great Forest to Grimoire, I noticed something. He seems to trust you. He's more relaxed around you.\n[protag]，最后一件事。当我们护送 Vaeril 从 Great Forest 前往 Grimoire 时，我注意到一些事。他似乎信任你。他在你身边更放松。"

    old "In the event that you do decide to release Vaeril, I think it would be best for us to travel to the forest as a party of three. Me, you, and him."
    new "In the event that you do decide to release Vaeril, I think it would be best for us to travel to the forest as a party of three. Me, you, and him.\n如果你确实决定释放 Vaeril，我想我们最好三人同行前往森林。我、你，还有他。"

    old "Were it just me and Vaeril, I might have...concerns. I don't think that Vaeril trusts me in the same way that I trust you."
    new "Were it just me and Vaeril, I might have...concerns. I don't think that Vaeril trusts me in the same way that I trust you.\n如果只有我和 Vaeril，我可能会……有些顾虑。我觉得 Vaeril 不像我信任你那样信任我。"

    old "I understand, Kusho. Let me see what I can do."
    new "I understand, Kusho. Let me see what I can do.\n我明白了，Kusho。让我看看我能做些什么。"

    old "Yes [protag]?"
    new "Yes [protag]?\n怎么了，[protag]？"

    old "I've made my mind about your request. I'm going to ask for Vaeril's release today."
    new "I've made my mind about your request. I'm going to ask for Vaeril's release today.\n关于你的请求，我已拿定主意。我今天就去申请释放 Vaeril。"

    old "Good. I'll be here waiting for you two then."
    new "Good. I'll be here waiting for you two then.\n好。那我就在这里等你们俩。"

    old "Apolimesho, would it be possible for me to arrange the temporary release of a prisoner?"
    new "Apolimesho, would it be possible for me to arrange the temporary release of a prisoner?\nApolimesho，我有可能安排暂时释放一名囚犯吗？"

    old "That depends on the conditions of the arrest. We'd likely need to involve the arresting officer."
    new "That depends on the conditions of the arrest. We'd likely need to involve the arresting officer.\n那得看逮捕时的情形。我们很可能需要让负责逮捕的官员参与进来。"

    old "In this case, I'm the arresting officer."
    new "In this case, I'm the arresting officer.\n在这件事上，我就是负责逮捕的官员。"

    old "Ah. The matter of that elf, was it?"
    new "Ah. The matter of that elf, was it?\n啊。是那个 Elf 的事，对吧？"

    old "That can be arranged. I presume that the prisoner will be released directly into your custody? As long as you're there, I don't think we'll have a problem."
    new "That can be arranged. I presume that the prisoner will be released directly into your custody? As long as you're there, I don't think we'll have a problem.\n那可以安排。我想那名囚犯会直接交到你看管之下？只要有你在，我想不会有问题。"

    old "How soon can you make it happen?"
    new "How soon can you make it happen?\n最快什么时候能办成？"

    old "As soon as noon today, if you're ready. Can you be ready and waiting at the city gates? He'll need to be escorted there."
    new "As soon as noon today, if you're ready. Can you be ready and waiting at the city gates? He'll need to be escorted there.\n如果你准备好了，最快今天中午。你能在城门口准备好等候吗？他需要被押送到那里。"

    old "Then I'll meet you there."
    new "Then I'll meet you there.\n那我会去那里与你碰面。"

    old "Before noon, I track down Kusho and let him know that I've secured Vaeril's release. Kusho follows me back to the city gate to await Vaeril's release."
    new "Before noon, I track down Kusho and let him know that I've secured Vaeril's release. Kusho follows me back to the city gate to await Vaeril's release.\n中午前，我找到 Kusho，告诉他我已办妥 Vaeril 的释放。Kusho 随我回到城门，等待 Vaeril 获释。"

    old "Two city guards arrive, each gripping Vaeril by one of his arms. His hands and legs are in chains."
    new "Two city guards arrive, each gripping Vaeril by one of his arms. His hands and legs are in chains.\n两名城卫兵到了，各自抓住 Vaeril 的一只胳膊。他的手脚都戴着镣铐。"

    old "Are you the one taking this man into custody?"
    new "Are you the one taking this man into custody?\n你就是接管这名囚犯的人吗？"

    old "Yes, I'm [protag]."
    new "Yes, I'm [protag].\n是的，我是[protag]。"

    old "We'll need you to sign this."
    new "We'll need you to sign this.\n我们需要你签一下这个。"

    old "The soldier hands me an official-looking document, and I look it over before putting my signature at the bottom."
    new "The soldier hands me an official-looking document, and I look it over before putting my signature at the bottom.\n士兵递给我一份看起来是官方的文件，我查看了一遍，然后在底部签上名字。"

    old "I gesture to the irons binding Vaeril's hands and feet."
    new "I gesture to the irons binding Vaeril's hands and feet.\n我朝锁着 Vaeril 手脚的镣铐比了比。"

    old "Are those really necessary?"
    new "Are those really necessary?\n那些真的有必要吗？"

    old "This man is pretty tame, remarkably well-behaved as prisoners go. I don't think you have to worry about him running off. But, you know. The irons are kind of necessary for appearances."
    new "This man is pretty tame, remarkably well-behaved as prisoners go. I don't think you have to worry about him running off. But, you know. The irons are kind of necessary for appearances.\n这个人挺温顺，在囚犯里算异常老实的。我觉得你不必担心他会逃跑。不过，你知道的。为了做做样子，镣铐多少还是得有的。"

    old "This isn't a good place to unbind him. Townspeople are milling about, and it might put some people in a state of unease. But you can release him once you're beyond the city limits."
    new "This isn't a good place to unbind him. Townspeople are milling about, and it might put some people in a state of unease. But you can release him once you're beyond the city limits.\n这里不是给他解开镣铐的好地方。镇民来来往往，可能会让一些人不安。不过一旦你出了城界，就可以放了他。"

    old "The soldier hands me a key and salutes me before marching off."
    new "The soldier hands me a key and salutes me before marching off.\n士兵递给我一把钥匙，向我行了个礼，然后迈步离开。"

    old "Sorry about the irons, Vaeril."
    new "Sorry about the irons, Vaeril.\n镣铐的事，抱歉了，Vaeril。"

    old "No apology needed. I consented to be arrested, and this is standard procedure as far as prisoner handling is concerned."
    new "No apology needed. I consented to be arrested, and this is standard procedure as far as prisoner handling is concerned.\n不必道歉。是我同意被捕的，就囚犯处置而言，这是标准程序。"

    old "In fact, I've been treated quite well. I think they've figured out that the best way to encourage good behavior from prisoners is to reward it. I'm still eating prison food, but I haven't gone hungry. There's even a collection of books on Grimoire history available for me to read."
    new "In fact, I've been treated quite well. I think they've figured out that the best way to encourage good behavior from prisoners is to reward it. I'm still eating prison food, but I haven't gone hungry. There's even a collection of books on Grimoire history available for me to read.\n事实上，我受到的待遇相当好。我想他们已想明白，鼓励囚犯好好表现的最好方式，就是给予奖励。我仍吃着牢饭，但没饿过肚子。甚至还有一套关于 Grimoire 历史的书供我阅读。"

    old "I suppose you've been doing a lot of reading, then."
    new "I suppose you've been doing a lot of reading, then.\n我想那你读了不少书。"

    old "It's kept me from getting bored."
    new "It's kept me from getting bored.\n这让我不至于无聊。"

    old "Vaeril gives Kusho a respectful nod."
    new "Vaeril gives Kusho a respectful nod.\nVaeril 恭敬地向 Kusho 点了点头。"

    old "I suppose you had some involvement in my release."
    new "I suppose you had some involvement in my release.\n我想我的获释，你也出了份力。"

    old "You assume correctly."
    new "You assume correctly.\n你猜得没错。"

    old "And I presume you want something from me. You don't strike me as the kind to offer mercy purely out of the goodness of your heart. No offense."
    new "And I presume you want something from me. You don't strike me as the kind to offer mercy purely out of the goodness of your heart. No offense.\n而我想，你是想从我这里得到些什么。你看起来不像那种纯粹出于善心而施以仁慈的人。无意冒犯。"

    old "No offense taken. You're right, 'mercy' isn't what motivates most of my actions. I'm here for a selfish reason."
    new "No offense taken. You're right, 'mercy' isn't what motivates most of my actions. I'm here for a selfish reason.\n没有冒犯。你说得对，'仁慈'并非我大多数行为的动机。我来这里是出于自私的理由。"

    old "And what reason would that be?"
    new "And what reason would that be?\n那是什么理由呢？"

    old "We want you to help us hunt down the source of the blight in the Great Forest."
    new "We want you to help us hunt down the source of the blight in the Great Forest.\n我们想让你帮我们追查出 Great Forest 枯萎之害的源头。"

    old "That doesn't sound so selfish to me. That sounds like something being done for the benefit of all elves."
    new "That doesn't sound so selfish to me. That sounds like something being done for the benefit of all elves.\n这听起来可不算自私。这听起来像是一件造福所有 Elves 的事。"

    old "That may be the case, but the main reason I am concerned with saving the Great Forest is that it is my home. I wouldn't have the same interest in stopping the blight if it were wracking the lands of dwarves or Amazons. An elf puts elf interests first."
    new "That may be the case, but the main reason I am concerned with saving the Great Forest is that it is my home. I wouldn't have the same interest in stopping the blight if it were wracking the lands of dwarves or Amazons. An elf puts elf interests first.\n也许是这样，但我关心拯救 Great Forest 的主要原因，是它是我的家。如果这场枯萎之害正在摧残的是 Dwarves 或 Amazons 的土地，我可不会有同样的兴致去阻止。Elf 把 Elf 的利益放在首位。"

    old "Very well, I'll assist you on your mission. After all, I also have an interest in saving the forest as well."
    new "Very well, I'll assist you on your mission. After all, I also have an interest in saving the forest as well.\n很好，我会协助你的任务。毕竟，我同样也有拯救这片森林的意愿。"

    old "Kusho raises a questioning eyebrow."
    new "Kusho raises a questioning eyebrow.\nKusho 扬起一道质疑的眉毛。"

    old "Are you surprised? I may have chosen to live my life apart from other elves, but the forest was still my home even when I was in exile. I still consider it my home."
    new "Are you surprised? I may have chosen to live my life apart from other elves, but the forest was still my home even when I was in exile. I still consider it my home.\n你很惊讶？我或许选择远离其他 Elves 生活，但即使流亡期间，森林仍是我的家。我至今仍视它为家。"

    old "What do you think I spent my time doing in that prison cell when I wasn't reading? I would close my eyes and dream of the forest. Even from these many miles away, I can see the individual paths and streams in my mind's eye."
    new "What do you think I spent my time doing in that prison cell when I wasn't reading? I would close my eyes and dream of the forest. Even from these many miles away, I can see the individual paths and streams in my mind's eye.\n你以为我不读书时，在那间牢房里都做些什么？我会闭上眼睛，梦见森林。即便隔着这许多里路，我仍能在心眼中看见一条条小径和溪流。"

    old "That's what I'm counting on. I want you to take a look at this map."
    new "That's what I'm counting on. I want you to take a look at this map.\n这正是我所指望的。我想让你看看这张地图。"

    old "Kusho removes a folded parchment from his pocket and lays it out in front of Vaeril. He begins pointing at specific points in the map."
    new "Kusho removes a folded parchment from his pocket and lays it out in front of Vaeril. He begins pointing at specific points in the map.\nKusho 从口袋里取出一张折好的羊皮纸，在 Vaeril 面前展开。他开始指向地图上的几个特定地点。"

    old "Right here, this is where I've determined the source of the blight to be. Or at the very least, that's where the woodcrashers are spawning. The difficulty is, I've never been there myself."
    new "Right here, this is where I've determined the source of the blight to be. Or at the very least, that's where the woodcrashers are spawning. The difficulty is, I've never been there myself.\n就在这里，这是我判定的枯萎之害源头所在。或者至少，那里是 woodcrashers 滋生的地方。困难在于，我自己从没到过那里。"

    old "I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse. I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf to penetrate."
    new "I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse. I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf to penetrate.\n我试过这里、这里和这里，但每次都遇到密得无法穿行的荆棘。我从树梢之上的高处侦察过，但那些灌木太茂密，任何 Elf 都钻不进去。"

    old "I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse. I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf—or [prace]—to penetrate."
    new "I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse. I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf—or [prace]—to penetrate.\n我试过这里、这里和这里，但每次都遇到密得无法穿行的荆棘。我从树梢之上的高处侦察过，但那些灌木太茂密，任何 Elf——或[prace]——都钻不进去。"

    old "You are right when you say that the brush is too dense for us to penetrate."
    new "You are right when you say that the brush is too dense for us to penetrate.\n你说得对，那些灌木太茂密，我们确实穿不过去。"

    old "If you can't actually take us there, then what good are you to us?"
    new "If you can't actually take us there, then what good are you to us?\n如果你不能真正把我们带到那里，那你对我们有什么用？"

    old "Please, understand my meaning. There is no way for any of us to penetrate that brush. However, there is another beast that can penetrate it. After all, if the woodcrashers spawn there, how do you think it is that they make their way to the other parts of the forest?"
    new "Please, understand my meaning. There is no way for any of us to penetrate that brush. However, there is another beast that can penetrate it. After all, if the woodcrashers spawn there, how do you think it is that they make their way to the other parts of the forest?\n请理解我的意思。我们谁都穿不过那片灌木。然而，有另一种野兽能穿过去。毕竟，如果 woodcrashers 在那里滋生，你觉得它们是怎么跑到森林其他地方的？"

    old "Simple. We look for the places where woodcrashers have already torn through the bramble."
    new "Simple. We look for the places where woodcrashers have already torn through the bramble.\n很简单。我们去找 woodcrashers 已经撕开荆棘的地方。"

    old "That sounds...dangerous."
    new "That sounds...dangerous.\n听起来……很危险。"

    old "I'm not denying that. But [protag], I don't believe you are the type to shirk from danger."
    new "I'm not denying that. But [protag], I don't believe you are the type to shirk from danger.\n我不否认。但[protag]，我不认为你是那种会回避危险的人。"

    old "I'm prepared to fight if we have to fight. And I know that killing is Kusho's speciality. But what about you, Vaeril? Are you prepared to fight the woodcrashers, if it comes to that?"
    new "I'm prepared to fight if we have to fight. And I know that killing is Kusho's speciality. But what about you, Vaeril? Are you prepared to fight the woodcrashers, if it comes to that?\n如果不得不打，我随时准备战斗。我也知道杀伐是 Kusho 的专长。可你呢，Vaeril？如果真到那一步，你准备好和 woodcrashers 战斗了吗？"

    old "I think my talents are better suited to healing than fighting. Though, when working as a team, healing powers can have applications in combat. But I'm not sure how kindly Kusho would take to my use of...certain magics."
    new "I think my talents are better suited to healing than fighting. Though, when working as a team, healing powers can have applications in combat. But I'm not sure how kindly Kusho would take to my use of...certain magics.\n我想我的才能更适合治疗而非战斗。不过，作为团队协作，治愈之力在战斗中也能派上用场。但我不确定 Kusho 会怎么看待我使用……某些魔法。"

    old "Would it be hypocritical for me to draw the life force from the forest, as we fought to save it?"
    new "Would it be hypocritical for me to draw the life force from the forest, as we fought to save it?\n在我们为拯救森林而战时，我却从森林汲取生命力，这会不会太虚伪？"

    old "The forest wants to be saved. I'm sure that, if asked, she would willingly lend you the life force you need to sustain us through combat against the woodcrashers. After all, those beasts are doing far more damage than a single lone druid ever could."
    new "The forest wants to be saved. I'm sure that, if asked, she would willingly lend you the life force you need to sustain us through combat against the woodcrashers. After all, those beasts are doing far more damage than a single lone druid ever could.\n森林想要被拯救。我相信，若被请求，她会愿意借给你所需的生命力，支撑我们与 woodcrashers 的战斗。毕竟，那些野兽造成的破坏，远非一个孤身德鲁伊可比。"

    old "If you're prepared to work together, then let's get going."
    new "If you're prepared to work together, then let's get going.\n如果你们都准备好携手合作，那就出发吧。"

    old "As soon as we get beyond the city limits of Grimoire, I remove the irons binding Vaeril, and we hurry to the forest."
    new "As soon as we get beyond the city limits of Grimoire, I remove the irons binding Vaeril, and we hurry to the forest.\n我们一出了 Grimoire 的城界，我就解下锁着 Vaeril 的镣铐，然后我们匆匆赶往森林。"

    old "[protag], thank you for coming to see me."
    new "[protag], thank you for coming to see me.\n[protag]，谢谢你来看我。"

    old "No thanks needed, Vaeril. What did you want to talk about?"
    new "No thanks needed, Vaeril. What did you want to talk about?\n不用谢，Vaeril。你想谈什么？"

    old "Lately I've been receiving troubling news about the Great Forest."
    new "Lately I've been receiving troubling news about the Great Forest.\n最近，我一直收到关于 Great Forest 的令人不安的消息。"

    old "Receiving news how?"
    new "Receiving news how?\n怎么收到消息的？"

    old "Grimoire is a large city, [protag]. It's a stopping point for many well-traveled people visiting the human empire. Some of those visitors happen to be elves, or those who have passed through the Great Forest."
    new "Grimoire is a large city, [protag]. It's a stopping point for many well-traveled people visiting the human empire. Some of those visitors happen to be elves, or those who have passed through the Great Forest.\nGrimoire 是个大城市，[protag]。它是许多走南闯北的人造访人类帝国时的歇脚点。其中一些访客恰好是 Elves，或是曾途经 Great Forest 的人。"

    old "So what's the news?"
    new "So what's the news?\n那消息是什么？"

    old "If you recall, at the time that we left the forest, I was being hunted by a man who suspected I was connected with many strange goings-on in the forest. The business with the woodcrashers, for example."
    new "If you recall, at the time that we left the forest, I was being hunted by a man who suspected I was connected with many strange goings-on in the forest. The business with the woodcrashers, for example.\n如果你还记得，我们离开森林时，我正被一个人追捕，他怀疑我与森林里许多怪事有关。比如 woodcrashers 那档子事。"

    old "Yes, I recall. I had a close encounter with one of them myself."
    new "Yes, I recall. I had a close encounter with one of them myself.\n是的，我记得。我自己还和其中一人近距离打过交道。"

    old "Since I've left, apparently the strange forces have continued to eat through the forest."
    new "Since I've left, apparently the strange forces have continued to eat through the forest.\n自我离开后，那些奇怪的力量显然仍在不断侵蚀森林。"

    old "These magics have manifested themselves in the form of the woodcrashers, which grow more numerous, and in the form of thick bramble, a massive network of thorns and vines that is eating through the forest. They are plants, and yet...they seem to be driven by some sort of dark energy."
    new "These magics have manifested themselves in the form of the woodcrashers, which grow more numerous, and in the form of thick bramble, a massive network of thorns and vines that is eating through the forest. They are plants, and yet...they seem to be driven by some sort of dark energy.\n这些魔法以 woodcrashers 的形式显现，数目日益增多；也以茂密荆棘的形式显现，那是一张正吞噬森林的、由尖刺与藤蔓织成的庞大网络。它们是植物，然而……它们似乎被某种黑暗能量所驱使。"

    old "I wonder if this could be related to the business around N'Mar. For the forest and the plains to be afflicted at the same time, that doesn't feel like coincidence."
    new "I wonder if this could be related to the business around N'Mar. For the forest and the plains to be afflicted at the same time, that doesn't feel like coincidence.\n我在想，这是否与 N'Mar 一带的事有关。森林和平原同时遭难，这感觉不像是巧合。"

    old "I think there may be a connection as well. I'd investigate it if I could. However..."
    new "I think there may be a connection as well. I'd investigate it if I could. However...\n我也觉得可能有联系。若有可能，我会去调查。然而……"

    old "You're still a wanted man."
    new "You're still a wanted man.\n你仍是个通缉犯。"

    old "Yes. As it is, I can't go back to the forest."
    new "Yes. As it is, I can't go back to the forest.\n是的。就目前而言，我回不了森林。"

    old "You may not be able to go to the forest, but I can. This seems like it's worth investigating further."
    new "You may not be able to go to the forest, but I can. This seems like it's worth investigating further.\n你也许去不了森林，但我能去。这事似乎值得进一步调查。"

    old "Perhaps this map may help."
    new "Perhaps this map may help.\n也许这张地图能帮上忙。"

    old "Vaeril hands me a parchment with several markings on it."
    new "Vaeril hands me a parchment with several markings on it.\nVaeril 递给我一张羊皮纸，上面有几处标记。"

    old "Hopefully you can read this better than I can. I must confess, while I am quite adept at navigating the forest on foot, when it comes to taking a bird's eye view, I am somewhat inexperienced."
    new "Hopefully you can read this better than I can. I must confess, while I am quite adept at navigating the forest on foot, when it comes to taking a bird's eye view, I am somewhat inexperienced.\n希望你能比我读得更明白。我必须承认，虽然我徒步穿行森林很在行，但说到从鸟瞰视角来看，我就有些生疏了。"

    old "The markings indicate places where people have reported sightings of youngling woodcrashers. It is my belief that as they mature, the younglings stray further and further from where they've spawned. If you trace the woodcrasher sightings back to where the smallest ones are, you'll be likely to find wherever it is that they spawn."
    new "The markings indicate places where people have reported sightings of youngling woodcrashers. It is my belief that as they mature, the younglings stray further and further from where they've spawned. If you trace the woodcrasher sightings back to where the smallest ones are, you'll be likely to find wherever it is that they spawn.\n这些标记标出了人们报告见过 woodcrasher 幼体的地方。我相信，随着幼体成熟，它们会离滋生地越来越远。如果你沿着 woodcrasher 目击报告往回追溯，找到最小幼体出没的地方，就很可能会找到它们的滋生地。"

    old "Coincidentally, those markings also happen to line up with places where people have spotted the thick bramble."
    new "Coincidentally, those markings also happen to line up with places where people have spotted the thick bramble.\n巧合的是，这些标记恰好也与人们发现茂密荆棘的地方吻合。"

    old "Something tells me that's not a coincidence."
    new "Something tells me that's not a coincidence.\n我的直觉告诉我，那不是巧合。"

    old "Intuition says they're related. But I hesitate to jump to conclusions."
    new "Intuition says they're related. But I hesitate to jump to conclusions.\n直觉说它们彼此相关。但我还不愿贸然下结论。"

    old "I'll see what I can find, Vaeril. It's unfortunate that I can't bring you with me, but this map is already a great help. Thank you."
    new "I'll see what I can find, Vaeril. It's unfortunate that I can't bring you with me, but this map is already a great help. Thank you.\n我会看看能找到什么，Vaeril。很遗憾不能带你同行，但这张地图已经是极大的帮助。谢谢。"

    old "I have more urgent things to attend to right now, but I plan to pay a visit to the Great Forest after out first incursion on Castle N'Mar."
    new "I have more urgent things to attend to right now, but I plan to pay a visit to the Great Forest after out first incursion on Castle N'Mar.\n眼下我还有更紧迫的事要处理，但我计划在我们对 Castle N'Mar 的首次进攻之后，去一趟 Great Forest。"

    old "I follow Vaeril's map. As I approach the marked spots that are nearest the edge of the forest, I quickly discover the 'bramble' that Vaeril spoke of. It's a dense cluster of thorns and vines, nearly twice as tall as I am. It's impossible to see over."
    new "I follow Vaeril's map. As I approach the marked spots that are nearest the edge of the forest, I quickly discover the 'bramble' that Vaeril spoke of. It's a dense cluster of thorns and vines, nearly twice as tall as I am. It's impossible to see over.\n我循着 Vaeril 的地图前进。当我接近靠近森林边缘的标记点时，很快发现了 Vaeril 所说的'荆棘'。那是一丛密实的尖刺与藤蔓，几乎有我两倍高，根本无法越过它看过去。"

    old "I look to the trees above, hoping to find a way to climb over the bramble, but I quickly realize that there are none to be found."
    new "I look to the trees above, hoping to find a way to climb over the bramble, but I quickly realize that there are none to be found.\n我抬头望向那些树，希望能找到翻越荆棘的办法，但很快就意识到根本无路可寻。"

    old "The ground that the bramble covers is completely devoid of trees. It must have choked all of them out. This bramble is overtaking the forest. Around its base, the ground is dry and tepid, nothing like the rich and moist life-giving soil that covers the rest of the forest."
    new "The ground that the bramble covers is completely devoid of trees. It must have choked all of them out. This bramble is overtaking the forest. Around its base, the ground is dry and tepid, nothing like the rich and moist life-giving soil that covers the rest of the forest.\n荆棘覆盖的地面上，树木已荡然无存。它一定是把那些树全都扼死了。这荆棘正吞没森林。在它根部周围，地面干燥而贫瘠，与覆盖森林其余部分那肥沃湿润、孕育生命的土壤截然不同。"

    old "I hear a voice from behind, and I turn to face it."
    new "I hear a voice from behind, and I turn to face it.\n我听到身后传来一个声音，于是转身面对它。"

    old "Things have gotten worse, haven't they?"
    new "Things have gotten worse, haven't they?\n情况变得更糟了，不是吗？"

    old "Kusho. Fancy seeing you here."
    new "Kusho. Fancy seeing you here.\nKusho。真巧，在这里见到你。"

    old "I would say the same thing. I'm an elf of the forest. My presence here shouldn't be unexpected. You, on the other hand...what brings you back?"
    new "I would say the same thing. I'm an elf of the forest. My presence here shouldn't be unexpected. You, on the other hand...what brings you back?\n我也正想这么说。我是森林的 Elf。我出现在这里不该让人意外。倒是你……什么风把你吹回来了？"

    old "It's like you said. Things have gotten worse."
    new "It's like you said. Things have gotten worse.\n正如你所说。情况更糟了。"

    old "This is troubling. The forest continues to decay, overrun by woodcrashers and now this bramble. Who would have thought a plant could be so fierce? And yet, here it is."
    new "This is troubling. The forest continues to decay, overrun by woodcrashers and now this bramble. Who would have thought a plant could be so fierce? And yet, here it is.\n这令人不安。森林持续衰败，先是被 woodcrashers 侵占，如今又加上这些荆棘。谁能想到一株植物会如此凶猛？然而，它就在眼前。"

    old "My personal mission hasn't advanced any since we last spoke, either. Try as I might, my target continues to elude me. In fact, any trace of him seems to be gone."
    new "My personal mission hasn't advanced any since we last spoke, either. Try as I might, my target continues to elude me. In fact, any trace of him seems to be gone.\n自从我们上次谈话以来，我的个人任务也毫无进展。我尽力而为，可目标仍在躲避我。事实上，他的任何踪迹似乎都已消失。"

    old "Months ago, I would hear rumors here and there of a lone druid, an elf wandering the forest. I couldn't catch him, but at least I would hear of his presence. But since we've last met, I've turned up no new leads."
    new "Months ago, I would hear rumors here and there of a lone druid, an elf wandering the forest. I couldn't catch him, but at least I would hear of his presence. But since we've last met, I've turned up no new leads.\n数月前，我还能时不时听到传言，说有个孤身的德鲁伊、一个 Elf 在森林里游荡。我抓不到他，但至少能听到他的消息。可自我们上次见面以来，我没再找到任何新线索。"

    old "I can't help but think that Vaeril himself may be responsible for the bramble. There is a possibility that within this mass of thorns, there is an elf, drawing power from the forest and channeling it into this foul infestation."
    new "I can't help but think that Vaeril himself may be responsible for the bramble. There is a possibility that within this mass of thorns, there is an elf, drawing power from the forest and channeling it into this foul infestation.\n我忍不住想，这荆棘或许是 Vaeril 本人所为。有可能在这团尖刺之中，藏着一个 Elf，正从森林汲取力量，并将其注入这场邪恶的侵扰。"

    old "What if he's left the forest entirely?"
    new "What if he's left the forest entirely?\n如果他已彻底离开森林了呢？"

    old "I suppose that is also a possibility. But as I said, I've heard no news of him lurking about, either in the forest or outside of it."
    new "I suppose that is also a possibility. But as I said, I've heard no news of him lurking about, either in the forest or outside of it.\n我想那也是一种可能。但如我所说，无论森林内外，我都没听说他出没的消息。"

    old "What if I told you that Vaeril had left the forest?"
    new "What if I told you that Vaeril had left the forest?\n如果我告诉你，Vaeril 已经离开了森林呢？"

    old "Are you speaking hypothetically?"
    new "Are you speaking hypothetically?\n你是在假设吗？"

    old "No sense in hiding the truth now."
    new "No sense in hiding the truth now.\n现在再隐瞒真相没有意义。"

    old "I was just asking. What if?"
    new "I was just asking. What if?\n我只是问问。假如呢？"

    old "Well, if I did find out that Vaeril had left the forest, then it would make my attempt to hunt him down seem like quite the wild goose chase, wouldn't it? I suppose I would feel quite foolish."
    new "Well, if I did find out that Vaeril had left the forest, then it would make my attempt to hunt him down seem like quite the wild goose chase, wouldn't it? I suppose I would feel quite foolish.\n那么，如果我真发现 Vaeril 已离开森林，那我对他的追捕，就成了一场徒劳的追逐，不是吗？我想我会觉得自己相当愚蠢。"

    old "But part of me wishes that I could be assured that Vaeril had nothing to do with this infestation. The more I see of it, the more I find myself doubting that it could be the work of a single individual."
    new "But part of me wishes that I could be assured that Vaeril had nothing to do with this infestation. The more I see of it, the more I find myself doubting that it could be the work of a single individual.\n但我内心有一部分，希望自己能确信 Vaeril 与这场侵扰无关。我见得越多，就越怀疑这不可能是一人之力所为。"

    old "Until I discover what has become of Vaeril, I must suspect him. But if I could eliminate him as a suspect, I think it would help me get to the root of discovering what is blighting the forest."
    new "Until I discover what has become of Vaeril, I must suspect him. But if I could eliminate him as a suspect, I think it would help me get to the root of discovering what is blighting the forest.\n在我查明 Vaeril 的下落之前，我必须怀疑他。但如果能排除他的嫌疑，我想那会有助于我追查到底是什么在祸害森林。"

    old "You see, [protag], while I am an assassin, my killing is always goal-driven. I've hunted Vaeril because I believed that doing so would stem the blight. And he is already guilty of numerous other crimes; it's documented that he's practiced foul magics."
    new "You see, [protag], while I am an assassin, my killing is always goal-driven. I've hunted Vaeril because I believed that doing so would stem the blight. And he is already guilty of numerous other crimes; it's documented that he's practiced foul magics.\n你看，[protag]，我虽是个刺客，但我的杀戮总是有目标的。我追捕 Vaeril，是因为我相信这样做能遏制枯萎之害。而且他本就犯下众多其他罪行；有记录表明他施展过邪恶魔法。"

    old "However, hunting Vaeril was merely a means to an end. My ultimate purpose is and has always been to preserve these forests. Unfortunately, as you can see, I seem to have failed in my mission."
    new "However, hunting Vaeril was merely a means to an end. My ultimate purpose is and has always been to preserve these forests. Unfortunately, as you can see, I seem to have failed in my mission.\n然而，追捕 Vaeril 不过是达成目的的手段。我最终的目的，一直是守护这些森林。不幸的是，如你所见，我的使命似乎失败了。"

    old "Do you have an obligation to these forests as a protector?"
    new "Do you have an obligation to these forests as a protector?\n你作为守护者，对这些森林负有义务吗？"

    old "Obligation? Not formally. But I am an elf. Grant Tree is my home and heritage. I can't sit idly by while it continues to decay."
    new "Obligation? Not formally. But I am an elf. Grant Tree is my home and heritage. I can't sit idly by while it continues to decay.\n义务？并非正式的。但我是一个 Elf。Grant Tree 是我的家园和传承。我不能坐视它继续衰败。"

    old "Kusho, I need to be straight with you. The truth is, I know what happened to Vaeril."
    new "Kusho, I need to be straight with you. The truth is, I know what happened to Vaeril.\nKusho，我得跟你直说。真相是，我知道 Vaeril 的下落。"

    old "What, exactly, did you discover about Vaeril?"
    new "What, exactly, did you discover about Vaeril?\n关于 Vaeril，你到底发现了什么？"

    old "He left this forest some time ago. Around the time that I left."
    new "He left this forest some time ago. Around the time that I left.\n他前一阵子离开了这片森林。大约就是我离开的时候。"

    old "Ah. Say no more. I'm not so foolish as to assume that Vaeril's departure coinciding with your arrival is a coincidence."
    new "Ah. Say no more. I'm not so foolish as to assume that Vaeril's departure coinciding with your arrival is a coincidence.\n啊。不用再说了。我还不至于蠢到认为 Vaeril 的离开与你的到来恰好同时是巧合。"

    old "Still. You say that Vaeril has left the forest?"
    new "Still. You say that Vaeril has left the forest?\n不过。你说 Vaeril 已经离开了森林？"

    old "He's been nowhere near here."
    new "He's been nowhere near here.\n他根本不在这一带附近。"

    old "Interesting. That confirms my suspicions, then. My hunt for Vaeril was nothing more than a red herring. The true culprit must be some other manner of dark magic."
    new "Interesting. That confirms my suspicions, then. My hunt for Vaeril was nothing more than a red herring. The true culprit must be some other manner of dark magic.\n有意思。那么这就证实了我的猜疑。我对 Vaeril 的追捕不过是个障眼法。真正的元凶，必定是某种其他的黑暗魔法。"

    old "When we first met, you told me that there were strange mists covering N'Mar. Perhaps the two blights stem from the same source."
    new "When we first met, you told me that there were strange mists covering N'Mar. Perhaps the two blights stem from the same source.\n我们初次见面时，你告诉我 N'Mar 笼罩着奇怪的迷雾。也许这两场祸害源自同一个源头。"

    old "Perhaps so."
    new "Perhaps so.\n也许吧。"

    old "Something tells me that the way this blight spreads through the forest is deliberate. You see, this corruption covers the most remote corners of the forest. It seems to deliberately avoid the places where elvish settlements lie."
    new "Something tells me that the way this blight spreads through the forest is deliberate. You see, this corruption covers the most remote corners of the forest. It seems to deliberately avoid the places where elvish settlements lie.\n我有种感觉，这场祸害在森林中的蔓延是刻意的。你看，这腐化覆盖的是森林最偏远的角落，似乎有意避开 Elf 聚居地所在之处。"

    old "That is a small blessing. It means that there haven't been any elves displaced by the creeping corruption, even if the forest is dying around them. However, it has also left me in the frustrating position of having very little information to go on. The places where the corruption spreads are the least charted parts of the forest."
    new "That is a small blessing. It means that there haven't been any elves displaced by the creeping corruption, even if the forest is dying around them. However, it has also left me in the frustrating position of having very little information to go on. The places where the corruption spreads are the least charted parts of the forest.\n这是小小的幸事。这意味着没有 Elves 因腐化的蔓延而流离失所，即使森林正在他们周围死去。然而，这也让我陷入沮丧的境地：几乎没有什么信息可循。腐化蔓延的地方，正是森林里最无地图可查的部分。"

    old "I've tried to learn these parts of the woods. But it occurs to me that there is an elf who has spent most of his life precisely in the parts of the forest that I know the least about."
    new "I've tried to learn these parts of the woods. But it occurs to me that there is an elf who has spent most of his life precisely in the parts of the forest that I know the least about.\n我试图了解这些林区。但我忽然想到，有一个 Elf，他大半生恰恰就生活在我最不了解的那些森林地带。"

    old "After all, Vaeril lived his life avoiding other elves, just as the bramble seems to do. The irony of Vaeril's absence is that he would actually be a great help in my investigation, if I could find him."
    new "After all, Vaeril lived his life avoiding other elves, just as the bramble seems to do. The irony of Vaeril's absence is that he would actually be a great help in my investigation, if I could find him.\n毕竟，Vaeril 一生都在躲避其他 Elves，正如那荆棘似乎所做的那样。Vaeril 缺席的讽刺之处在于，如果能找到他，他其实会对我的调查大有帮助。"

    old "What if I could find him?"
    new "What if I could find him?\n如果我能找到他呢？"

    old "As I said, that would be a great help. But do you know where he is?"
    new "As I said, that would be a great help. But do you know where he is?\n如我所说，那会是极大的帮助。但你知道他在哪里吗？"

    old "I do, but I think he'd be reluctant to return to these woods."
    new "I do, but I think he'd be reluctant to return to these woods.\n知道，但我想他不愿回到这片树林。"

    old "I understand. From the sound of things, he left because he knew that I was hunting him. But [protag], if you are in contact with him, you can give him my assurance that he'll receive no hostility from me. Quite the contrary, I'm willing to bury the hatchet, provided he's willing to assist in locating the source of the forest's plague."
    new "I understand. From the sound of things, he left because he knew that I was hunting him. But [protag], if you are in contact with him, you can give him my assurance that he'll receive no hostility from me. Quite the contrary, I'm willing to bury the hatchet, provided he's willing to assist in locating the source of the forest's plague.\n我理解。从情形来看，他离开是因为知道我在追捕他。但[protag]，如果你和他有联系，你可以向他保证，他不会受到我的敌意。恰恰相反，只要他愿意协助找出森林瘟疫的源头，我乐意冰释前嫌。"

    old "I'll let him know that."
    new "I'll let him know that.\n我会转告他的。"

    old "If you find him, bring him back here. Please, I need any potential lead I can get."
    new "If you find him, bring him back here. Please, I need any potential lead I can get.\n如果你找到他，把他带回这里。拜托了，任何潜在的线索我都要。"

    old "Vaeril, I went back to the forest and I discovered the bramble. It's even worse than you described."
    new "Vaeril, I went back to the forest and I discovered the bramble. It's even worse than you described.\nVaeril，我回了趟森林，发现了那荆棘。情况比你描述的还糟。"

    old "I was afraid you'd come back with news like that."
    new "I was afraid you'd come back with news like that.\n我就怕你带回来这样的消息。"

    old "I also happened to meet someone else who was investigating the bramble. Kusho."
    new "I also happened to meet someone else who was investigating the bramble. Kusho.\n我还碰巧遇到了另一个在调查那荆棘的人。Kusho。"

    old "Is that so? I suppose it's a good thing I didn't go along, then."
    new "Is that so? I suppose it's a good thing I didn't go along, then.\n是吗？那我想，我没跟着去是件好事。"

    old "Actually, I think Kusho may have changed his opinion on you, Vaeril. He no longer believes that you're responsible for whatever corruption has been spawning the woodcrashers and brambles. He's willing to let bygones be bygones. In fact, he indicated that he'd like your help."
    new "Actually, I think Kusho may have changed his opinion on you, Vaeril. He no longer believes that you're responsible for whatever corruption has been spawning the woodcrashers and brambles. He's willing to let bygones be bygones. In fact, he indicated that he'd like your help.\n实际上，我想 Kusho 对你的看法可能已经改变，Vaeril。他不再认为你该为滋生 woodcrashers 和荆棘的那场腐化负责。他愿意让过去的事过去。事实上，他暗示过希望得到你的帮助。"

    old "Uh? My help?"
    new "Uh? My help?\n呃？我的帮助？"

    old "Of course, there's the possibility that it might be a trap. But Kusho seemed very sincere to me. His original reason for hunting you was that he suspected you were responsible for the foulness that had covered the forest."
    new "Of course, there's the possibility that it might be a trap. But Kusho seemed very sincere to me. His original reason for hunting you was that he suspected you were responsible for the foulness that had covered the forest.\n当然，不排除那可能是个陷阱。但 Kusho 在我眼里显得非常真诚。他当初追捕你的理由，是怀疑你该为覆盖森林的那片污秽负责。"

    old "But he's taken the fact that the blight has worsened in your absence as evidence of your innocent. He wants to find the true source of the corruption. And he thinks that you can help."
    new "But he's taken the fact that the blight has worsened in your absence as evidence of your innocent. He wants to find the true source of the corruption. And he thinks that you can help.\n但他已把你缺席期间祸害加剧这一事实，当作你无罪的证据。他想找到腐化的真正源头。而且他认为你能帮忙。"

    old "It would seem that Kusho and I share a goal, then. If he's willing to trust me, then I'm willing to trust him. Besides, if he truly wants me dead, he'd probably catch wind of my location sooner or later."
    new "It would seem that Kusho and I share a goal, then. If he's willing to trust me, then I'm willing to trust him. Besides, if he truly wants me dead, he'd probably catch wind of my location sooner or later.\n那么，Kusho 和我似乎有着共同的目标。如果他愿意信任我，那我也愿意信任他。何况，如果他真想要我死，迟早也会打探到我的下落。"

    old "Even if Kusho does mean me harm, I think it's better to face him now than to spend the rest of my life awaiting the day when I'll discover someone has planted an arrow in my back."
    new "Even if Kusho does mean me harm, I think it's better to face him now than to spend the rest of my life awaiting the day when I'll discover someone has planted an arrow in my back.\n即便 Kusho 真想害我，我想现在面对他，也好过用余生去等待某一天发现有人把箭射进我的后背。"

    old "Should we go to meet with Kusho now?"
    new "Should we go to meet with Kusho now?\n我们现在该去见 Kusho 吗？"

    old "I think he'd rather see us sooner than later. The corruption spreads with every passing day."
    new "I think he'd rather see us sooner than later. The corruption spreads with every passing day.\n我想他宁愿早点见到我们。腐化正随着每一天过去而蔓延。"

    old "Then we should waste no time in discovering its cause. Let's go, [protag]."
    new "Then we should waste no time in discovering its cause. Let's go, [protag].\n那我们就别再浪费时间，尽快查明它的成因。走吧，[protag]。"

    old "We head to the forest, and return to where I met Kusho before. After a bit of wandering around the bramble, we find him crouched down, studying the ground."
    new "We head to the forest, and return to where I met Kusho before. After a bit of wandering around the bramble, we find him crouched down, studying the ground.\n我们前往森林，回到我之前遇到 Kusho 的地方。在荆棘附近转了一会儿后，我们发现他正蹲在地上研究着什么。"

    old "Vaeril. It's quite a surprise to see you. I hope you don't hold any ill will toward me."
    new "Vaeril. It's quite a surprise to see you. I hope you don't hold any ill will toward me.\nVaeril。见到你真意外。希望你对我不抱任何敌意。"

    old "None at all. You were doing your job."
    new "None at all. You were doing your job.\n完全没有。你只是在尽你的本分。"

    old "I thought I was protecting the forest by hunting you. But there is a much darker magic that threatens the forest. I'm hoping that, with your help, we can discover its source."
    new "I thought I was protecting the forest by hunting you. But there is a much darker magic that threatens the forest. I'm hoping that, with your help, we can discover its source.\n我原以为追捕你就是在保护森林。但威胁森林的，是一种远比这黑暗的魔法。我希望，在你的帮助下，我们能找到它的源头。"

    old "How can I be of assistance?"
    new "How can I be of assistance?\n我能帮上什么忙？"

    old "Right here, this is where I've determined the source of the blight to be. Or at the very least, that's where the woodcrashers are spawning. The difficulty is, I've never been there myself. I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse."
    new "Right here, this is where I've determined the source of the blight to be. Or at the very least, that's where the woodcrashers are spawning. The difficulty is, I've never been there myself. I tried here, here, and here, but every time I encountered bramble too thick for me to traverse.\n就在这里，这是我判定的枯萎之害源头所在。或者至少，那里是 woodcrashers 滋生的地方。困难在于，我自己从没到过那里。我试过这里、这里和这里，但每次都遇到密得无法穿行的荆棘。"

    old "I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf to penetrate."
    new "I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf to penetrate.\n我从树梢之上的高处侦察过，但那些灌木太茂密，任何 Elf 都钻不进去。"

    old "I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf—or [prace]—to penetrate."
    new "I scouted it out from a high position above the treetops, but the brush is too dense for any elf—or [prace]—to penetrate.\n我从树梢之上的高处侦察过，但那些灌木太茂密，任何 Elf——或[prace]——都钻不进去。"

    old "I was hoping that you might be able to help us with that. How, exactly, are we supposed to cut through that bramble?"
    new "I was hoping that you might be able to help us with that. How, exactly, are we supposed to cut through that bramble?\n我希望你或许能帮我们解决这个。我们究竟该怎么穿过那片荆棘？"

    old "I think I know how. You said that the bramble covers the area where the woodcrashers spawn."
    new "I think I know how. You said that the bramble covers the area where the woodcrashers spawn.\n我想我知道该怎么办。你说过，荆棘覆盖着 woodcrashers 滋生的区域。"

    old "Yes. They seem to stem from the same source."
    new "Yes. They seem to stem from the same source.\n是的。它们似乎源自同一个源头。"

    old "And yet somehow, the woodcrashers escape the bramble and are free to ravage the other parts of the forest."
    new "And yet somehow, the woodcrashers escape the bramble and are free to ravage the other parts of the forest.\n然而不知为何，woodcrashers 却能逃出荆棘，肆意蹂躏森林的其他地方。"

    old "Yes. It's quite a puzzle."
    new "Yes. It's quite a puzzle.\n是的。这真是个难解的谜。"

    old "It seems obvious to me. The woodcrashers simple charge through the bramble, the same way that they charge through trees."
    new "It seems obvious to me. The woodcrashers simple charge through the bramble, the same way that they charge through trees.\n在我看来这很明显。woodcrashers 只是径直冲过荆棘，就像它们冲过树木一样。"

    old "And just as they leave destruction on their wake when they charge through the trees, they must do the same thing to the bramble as they charge through."
    new "And just as they leave destruction on their wake when they charge through the trees, they must do the same thing to the bramble as they charge through.\n而正如它们冲过树木时会在身后留下破坏，它们冲过荆棘时必然也会对荆棘做同样的事。"

    old "If we look hard enough, we may find the parts where they have penetrated. There may very well be a number of woodcrasher-sized tunnels carved into the bramble where it is most dense."
    new "If we look hard enough, we may find the parts where they have penetrated. There may very well be a number of woodcrasher-sized tunnels carved into the bramble where it is most dense.\n如果我们仔细找，或许能找到它们穿过的缺口。在最茂密的荆棘里，很可能有不少 woodcrasher 大小的通道被凿了出来。"

    old "That's an interesting idea. We'll go in the same way that they come out. I think it's worth trying. Come on, I'll bring you to where the bramble is most dense. That's where we should find the center of all this."
    new "That's an interesting idea. We'll go in the same way that they come out. I think it's worth trying. Come on, I'll bring you to where the bramble is most dense. That's where we should find the center of all this.\n这是个有趣的想法。我们就走它们出来的路进去。我觉得值得一试。来吧，我带你去荆棘最茂密的地方。那里应该就是这一切的中心。"

    old "Kusho's map leads us to the right area of the forest, and Vaeril's keen sense for where things are leads us to the edge of the bramble Kusho described."
    new "Kusho's map leads us to the right area of the forest, and Vaeril's keen sense for where things are leads us to the edge of the bramble Kusho described.\nKusho 的地图把我们带到森林中正确的区域，而 Vaeril 对事物方位敏锐的直觉，把我们领到了 Kusho 所描述的那片荆棘边缘。"

    old "Why do you suppose this mass of vines and thorns came here?"
    new "Why do you suppose this mass of vines and thorns came here?\n你觉得这团藤蔓和尖刺为什么会长到这里来？"

    old "This bramble is a perversion of the forest. Just as the woodcrashers represent a manner of beast that preys on the forest by tearing down its trees, the bramble is a plant that covers and chokes out the trees of a forest. It is like a weed, stifling the growth of trees, and sucking the moisture from their roots, making it impossible for them to grow."
    new "This bramble is a perversion of the forest. Just as the woodcrashers represent a manner of beast that preys on the forest by tearing down its trees, the bramble is a plant that covers and chokes out the trees of a forest. It is like a weed, stifling the growth of trees, and sucking the moisture from their roots, making it impossible for them to grow.\n这荆棘是对森林的扭曲。正如 woodcrashers 代表一种靠推倒树木来猎食森林的野兽，荆棘则是一种覆盖森林、扼杀树木的植物。它就像野草，压制树木的生长，从树根吸走水分，让它们无法生长。"

    old "It grows like a weed. Every other creature in the forest shares a symbiotic relationship with the life around it."
    new "It grows like a weed. Every other creature in the forest shares a symbiotic relationship with the life around it.\n它像野草一样疯长。森林里其他每种生物，都与周围的生灵保持着共生关系。"

    old "The forests draw water from the ground, but they offer a place for small woodland animals to live, and their shade keeps the streams that feed them from drying up. That supplication—the give and take—is what has allowed this forest to persevere for millennia."
    new "The forests draw water from the ground, but they offer a place for small woodland animals to live, and their shade keeps the streams that feed them from drying up. That supplication—the give and take—is what has allowed this forest to persevere for millennia.\n森林从地下汲取水分，却也为小林地的动物提供了栖身之所，它们的荫蔽又让滋养它们的溪流不致干涸。那份祈求——那种付出与索取——正是这座森林能延续千年的原因。"

    old "The bramble and the woodcrashers thrive by stealing the life from the creatures and plants around them. There is no giving, only taking. Because of that, their numbers grow exponentially—but eventually, they will run out of other living things to suck the life from. They will eventually hunt their prey to the point of extinction."
    new "The bramble and the woodcrashers thrive by stealing the life from the creatures and plants around them. There is no giving, only taking. Because of that, their numbers grow exponentially—but eventually, they will run out of other living things to suck the life from. They will eventually hunt their prey to the point of extinction.\n荆棘和 woodcrashers 靠从周围的动植物身上窃取生命而繁盛。它们只索取，不给予。正因如此，它们的数量呈指数级增长——但终有一天，它们会耗尽可吸取生命的其他生灵。它们最终会把猎物逼到灭绝。"

    old "Not if we have anything to say about it."
    new "Not if we have anything to say about it.\n只要有我们在，就不会那样。"

    old "Yes, that is why we're here. And I think we've come to the right place. This is where the woodcrashers tear through the bramble."
    new "Yes, that is why we're here. And I think we've come to the right place. This is where the woodcrashers tear through the bramble.\n是的，这正是我们来此的原因。而且我想我们来对了地方。这里就是 woodcrashers 撕开荆棘之处。"

    old "Vaeril points to a large gap in the bramble. Sure enough, it looks like a tunnel, formed from some beast tearing through. All that remains is a path of scattered twigs."
    new "Vaeril points to a large gap in the bramble. Sure enough, it looks like a tunnel, formed from some beast tearing through. All that remains is a path of scattered twigs.\nVaeril 指向荆棘中一个宽大的缺口。果然，它看起来像条隧道，由某种野兽撕开而成。剩下的只是一条散落着断枝的小径。"

    old "And look, there's another break in the bramble over there, even larger than this one."
    new "And look, there's another break in the bramble over there, even larger than this one.\n再看，那边荆棘还有另一处缺口，比这个还大。"

    old "Kusho points, and I follow his gaze. Several feet away, there is indeed another tunnel through the bramble."
    new "Kusho points, and I follow his gaze. Several feet away, there is indeed another tunnel through the bramble.\nKusho 指过去，我顺着他的目光看去。几英尺外，荆棘中确实还有另一条隧道。"

    old "Which path should we take?"
    new "Which path should we take?\n我们该走哪条路？"

    old "Even if there is a tunnel carved out for us, it's still a thorny mess. If we tried squeezing through this small gap, I'd worry about the thorns pricking and bleeding us. We should take the larger gap."
    new "Even if there is a tunnel carved out for us, it's still a thorny mess. If we tried squeezing through this small gap, I'd worry about the thorns pricking and bleeding us. We should take the larger gap.\n即便有条为我们凿出的隧道，那里仍是一团带刺的乱麻。如果我们硬挤进这个狭窄的缺口，我担心荆棘会扎伤我们、让我们流血。我们该走那个更大的缺口。"

    old "Kusho. Think about what the gap means. These so-called tunnels are carved out by the indiscriminate rampaging beasts. What kind of beast makes a big tunnel?"
    new "Kusho. Think about what the gap means. These so-called tunnels are carved out by the indiscriminate rampaging beasts. What kind of beast makes a big tunnel?\nKusho。想想这个缺口意味着什么。这些所谓的隧道，是不分青红皂白横冲直撞的野兽凿出来的。什么样的野兽会凿出大隧道？"

    old "I see your point. A bigger tunnel means a bigger beast."
    new "I see your point. A bigger tunnel means a bigger beast.\n我明白你的意思。更大的隧道意味着更大的野兽。"

    old "But who knows where those beasts are by now? This tunnel could have been made days or even weeks ago. The large beast that carved it out may be long gone by now. And if we have to fight, we'll fight."
    new "But who knows where those beasts are by now? This tunnel could have been made days or even weeks ago. The large beast that carved it out may be long gone by now. And if we have to fight, we'll fight.\n但谁知道那些野兽现在在哪？这条隧道可能是几天甚至几周前留下的。凿出它的大野兽如今可能早已远去。而如果必须战斗，我们就战斗。"

    old "Perhaps we should leave it for [protag] to make the decision."
    new "Perhaps we should leave it for [protag] to make the decision.\n也许我们该让[protag]来做决定。"

    old "We'll take the wider path. If we have to fight, we fight. And if we have to fight, I'd prefer to have freedom of movement. There's nothing as terrified as being caught in a tight enclosed space when enemies might be lurking nearby."
    new "We'll take the wider path. If we have to fight, we fight. And if we have to fight, I'd prefer to have freedom of movement. There's nothing as terrified as being caught in a tight enclosed space when enemies might be lurking nearby.\n我们走更宽的那条路。若必须战斗，我们就战。而若要战斗，我宁愿有活动自如的空间。当敌人可能潜伏在附近时，没有什么比被困在狭窄密闭空间里更可怕的了。"

    old "I'll lead the way."
    new "I'll lead the way.\n我来带路。"

    old "Kusho leads us down the path carefully. The path twists and turns, making it difficult to see what lies ahead, and Kusho keeps poking his head around, all while keeping his hand on his weapon, ready to draw at a moment's notice. Eventually pass through the brush into a small clearing."
    new "Kusho leads us down the path carefully. The path twists and turns, making it difficult to see what lies ahead, and Kusho keeps poking his head around, all while keeping his hand on his weapon, ready to draw at a moment's notice. Eventually pass through the brush into a small clearing.\nKusho 领着我们小心地沿路前行。小径蜿蜒曲折，很难看清前方，Kusho 一直伸头张望，同时手按武器，随时准备拔刀。最终，我们穿过灌木，进到一片小空地里。"

    old "Kusho raises a finger to his lips, hushing us, and he points to a woodcrasher, standing in the clearing with its back facing us."
    new "Kusho raises a finger to his lips, hushing us, and he points to a woodcrasher, standing in the clearing with its back facing us.\nKusho 竖起一根手指到唇边，示意我们噤声，然后指向空地上一头背对着我们的 woodcrasher。"

    old "Kusho draws his weapon, and Vaeril and I stand beside him, assuming aggressive postures as we creep into position behind the beast. It's massive, and there's no doubt that it could do serious damage to any one of us, especially in this tight clearing. Retreat isn't an option. But we can get in a pre-emptive strike."
    new "Kusho draws his weapon, and Vaeril and I stand beside him, assuming aggressive postures as we creep into position behind the beast. It's massive, and there's no doubt that it could do serious damage to any one of us, especially in this tight clearing. Retreat isn't an option. But we can get in a pre-emptive strike.\nKusho 拔出武器，Vaeril 和我站到他身旁，摆出进攻姿态，悄然摸到那头野兽身后。它体型庞大，毫无疑问能对我们任何一人造成重创，尤其是在这片狭小的空地里。撤退不是选项。但我们可以先发制人。"

    old "Well, we've survived."
    new "Well, we've survived.\n好了，我们活下来了。"

    old "It's a wretched beast. This stench, it's like nothing I've ever encountered in this forest."
    new "It's a wretched beast. This stench, it's like nothing I've ever encountered in this forest.\n真是头可憎的野兽。这股恶臭，是我在这森林里从未遇到过的。"

    old "Maybe it's because we're close to the source of the forest's corruption."
    new "Maybe it's because we're close to the source of the forest's corruption.\n也许是因为我们接近了森林腐化的源头。"

    old "Maybe."
    new "Maybe.\n也许吧。"

    old "We'll take the narrower path. I'd rather suffer the cuts and scrapes of the brush than face whatever beast formed that massive hole."
    new "We'll take the narrower path. I'd rather suffer the cuts and scrapes of the brush than face whatever beast formed that massive hole.\n我们走更窄的那条路。我宁可被灌木割出几道口子、擦破点皮，也不愿面对凿出那个大洞的什么野兽。"

    old "The path through the bramble is narrow, and as we step through it, I grow aware of the crunching sound of twigs beneath our feet. I whisper to Vaeril."
    new "The path through the bramble is narrow, and as we step through it, I grow aware of the crunching sound of twigs beneath our feet. I whisper to Vaeril.\n穿过荆棘的小径很窄，当我们走进去时，我渐渐意识到脚下树枝被踩断的嘎吱声。我低声对 Vaeril 说。"

    old "We're making a lot of noise."
    new "We're making a lot of noise.\n我们弄出的动静很大。"

    old "Let's hope that anything that hears the noise is more afraid of us than we are of it."
    new "Let's hope that anything that hears the noise is more afraid of us than we are of it.\n只希望听到动静的东西，比我们怕它更怕我们。"

    old "At several points, the path becomes too narrow for me to pass through without positioning my body sideways, and as I sidle my way through, the thorns and briar of the forest grip my clothing and cut the skin on my face and hands."
    new "At several points, the path becomes too narrow for me to pass through without positioning my body sideways, and as I sidle my way through, the thorns and briar of the forest grip my clothing and cut the skin on my face and hands.\n有几处，小径窄得我必须侧过身子才能通过，当我侧身挤过去时，森林的尖刺和荆棘勾住我的衣服，划破我脸上和手上的皮肤。"

    old "I grit my teeth and power through the pain. This will be over soon enough."
    new "I grit my teeth and power through the pain. This will be over soon enough.\n我咬紧牙关，忍着疼痛硬闯。这一切很快就会过去。"

    old "I let out a yelp as a thorny branch catches my shoulder and tears across my arm, leaving a nasty cut."
    new "I let out a yelp as a thorny branch catches my shoulder and tears across my arm, leaving a nasty cut.\n一根带刺的树枝勾住我的肩膀，横着划过我的手臂，留下一道难看的伤口，我不由得叫了一声。"

    old "I'll survive."
    new "I'll survive.\n我死不了。"

    old "Once we're through this, I'll have my healing magic to patch you up."
    new "Once we're through this, I'll have my healing magic to patch you up.\n等我们穿过这里，我会用治疗魔法给你包扎好。"

    old "We make it to the end of the tunnel, but not without taking some damage from the bramble."
    new "We make it to the end of the tunnel, but not without taking some damage from the bramble.\n我们抵达了隧道的尽头，但也没少被荆棘弄得挂彩。"

    old "Finally we pass through the brush into a small clearing. I open my mouth to speak, but Vaeril turns around and raises a lip to his mouth, hushing me. I peak over his shoulder and see what he sees: a woodcrasher slumbering in the clearing. Vaeril whispers to me."
    new "Finally we pass through the brush into a small clearing. I open my mouth to speak, but Vaeril turns around and raises a lip to his mouth, hushing me. I peak over his shoulder and see what he sees: a woodcrasher slumbering in the clearing. Vaeril whispers to me.\n终于，我们穿过灌木，进到一片小空地。我张口想说话，但 Vaeril 转过身，把一根手指竖到唇边，示意我噤声。我越过他的肩膀看去，看到了他所见的：一头 woodcrasher 正在空地中酣睡。Vaeril 对我低声说。"

    old "It looks like a youngling. I think that we could take it on."
    new "It looks like a youngling. I think that we could take it on.\n看起来是头幼体。我想我们能对付它。"

    old "I eye the ground of the clearing. It's covered with broken twigs. Could we sneak around it without waking it with our footsteps, I wonder?"
    new "I eye the ground of the clearing. It's covered with broken twigs. Could we sneak around it without waking it with our footsteps, I wonder?\n我打量着空地的地面。上面铺满了断枝。我暗自思忖，我们能绕过去，而脚步不惊醒它吗？"

    old "I whisper to Vaeril and Kusho."
    new "I whisper to Vaeril and Kusho.\n我低声对 Vaeril 和 Kusho 说。"

    old "Let's move in for a pre-emptive strike."
    new "Let's move in for a pre-emptive strike.\n我们摸上去，先发制人。"

    old "I whispker to Vaeril and Kusho."
    new "I whispker to Vaeril and Kusho.\n我低声对 Vaeril 和 Kusho 说。"

    old "Let's try to sneak around without disturbing it."
    new "Let's try to sneak around without disturbing it.\n我们试着悄悄绕过去，不惊动它。"

    old "We begin walking around the clearing, attempting to place our footsteps gingerly, and we seem we made it."
    new "We begin walking around the clearing, attempting to place our footsteps gingerly, and we seem we made it.\n我们开始绕空地而行，努力把脚步放轻，看起来我们成功了。"

    old "Looks like we managed to avoid this fight."
    new "Looks like we managed to avoid this fight.\n看来我们成功避开了这场战斗。"

    old "We begin walking around the clearing, attempting to place our footsteps gingerly, but the dried brush crunches and crumbles under our footsteps. I tense up, and the youngling woodcrasher blinks awake."
    new "We begin walking around the clearing, attempting to place our footsteps gingerly, but the dried brush crunches and crumbles under our footsteps. I tense up, and the youngling woodcrasher blinks awake.\n我们开始绕空地而行，努力把脚步放轻，但干枯的灌木在我们脚下嘎吱作响、簌簌碎裂。我绷紧了身子，那头 woodcrasher 幼体眨了眨眼，醒了过来。"

    old "I've never seen a woodcrasher so small."
    new "I've never seen a woodcrasher so small.\n我从没见过这么小的 woodcrasher。"

    old "This is where they spawn. You didn't think they were born huge, did you?"
    new "This is where they spawn. You didn't think they were born huge, did you?\n这里就是它们滋生的地方。你总不会以为它们生来就很大吧？"

    old "You have a point."
    new "You have a point.\n你说得有道理。"

    old "Kusho pulls out his map."
    new "Kusho pulls out his map.\nKusho 掏出他的地图。"

    old "Based on our movement and the position of the sun, I think that we're very near to the source of the blight. The question is, can we get closer?"
    new "Based on our movement and the position of the sun, I think that we're very near to the source of the blight. The question is, can we get closer?\n根据我们的行进和太阳的位置，我想我们已经离枯萎之害的源头非常近了。问题是，我们能再靠近些吗？"

    old "I scan the clearing. We seem to be completely surrounded by bramble, except for the the tunnel we just came through."
    new "I scan the clearing. We seem to be completely surrounded by bramble, except for the the tunnel we just came through.\n我扫视空地。除了我们刚穿过的那条隧道，我们似乎完全被荆棘包围了。"

    old "Over here. There's a small gap."
    new "Over here. There's a small gap.\n这里。有个小缺口。"

    old "Could one of us fit through that? It looks to small for any of us to squeeze through."
    new "Could one of us fit through that? It looks to small for any of us to squeeze through.\n我们当中谁能挤过去吗？它看起来太小了，谁也钻不过去。"

    old "I wonder..."
    new "I wonder...\n我在想……"

    old "I grab the brier on either side of the narrow gap, and try to pull it apart. As I spread my arms apart, I can see what looks like a passageway."
    new "I grab the brier on either side of the narrow gap, and try to pull it apart. As I spread my arms apart, I can see what looks like a passageway.\n我抓住窄缺口两边的荆棘，试着把它们掰开。当我双臂向两边撑开时，我看到了一个像是通道的东西。"

    old "This may be a place where a woodcrasher came through, and then the brush continued to grow, covering the gap where it left. But if we pull the brush apart, it might be wide enough to get through."
    new "This may be a place where a woodcrasher came through, and then the brush continued to grow, covering the gap where it left. But if we pull the brush apart, it might be wide enough to get through.\n这可能是一头 woodcrasher 曾经穿过的位置，之后灌木继续生长，把它留下的缺口盖住了。但如果我们把灌木拉开，也许就能宽到可以穿过去。"

    old "I release my hold, and the brush snaps back into place, sealing the entrance."
    new "I release my hold, and the brush snaps back into place, sealing the entrance.\n我一松手，灌木弹回原位，封住了入口。"

    old "We might be able to force it open, but it could trap us inside."
    new "We might be able to force it open, but it could trap us inside.\n我们也许能强行把它撑开，但它可能把我们困在里面。"

    old "How about this: one of you stays here to hold it open, and I'll poke around and see what I can find."
    new "How about this: one of you stays here to hold it open, and I'll poke around and see what I can find.\n不如这样：你们其中一人留在这里把它撑开，我进去探探，看能找到什么。"

    old "I can try to hold the gap open...but my arms can only separate so far."
    new "I can try to hold the gap open...but my arms can only separate so far.\n我可以试着把缺口撑开……但我的手臂也只能分开到这种程度。"

    old "Maybe both of us should stay."
    new "Maybe both of us should stay.\n也许我们俩都该留下。"

    old "Kusho and Vaeril each grab one side of the brier, and begin pulling the two sides away from each other, opening up a gap for me to step through."
    new "Kusho and Vaeril each grab one side of the brier, and begin pulling the two sides away from each other, opening up a gap for me to step through.\nKusho 和 Vaeril 各抓住荆棘的一边，开始把两边向相反方向拉开，为我撑出一个可以钻过去的缺口。"

    old "What am I looking for?"
    new "What am I looking for?\n我要找什么？"

    old "At this point? Information. We don't know what's inside of this massive network of brier and bramble."
    new "At this point? Information. We don't know what's inside of this massive network of brier and bramble.\n眼下？信息。我们不知道这片庞大的荆棘网络里有什么。"

    old "I step through the gap and begin walking. It's a tight fit, and I'm not more than a few feet in before I find myself almost completely enveloped in darkness."
    new "I step through the gap and begin walking. It's a tight fit, and I'm not more than a few feet in before I find myself almost completely enveloped in darkness.\n我穿过缺口，开始前行。里面很挤，还没走几英尺，我就发现自己几乎完全被黑暗吞没。"

    old "I glance behind me, and see the reassuring form of Vaeril and Kusho. I keep pressing on, and I think I see a light."
    new "I glance behind me, and see the reassuring form of Vaeril and Kusho. I keep pressing on, and I think I see a light.\n我回头看了一眼，看到 Vaeril 和 Kusho 令人安心的身影。我继续前行，我想我看到了一束光。"

    old "Eventually, the gap grows so narrow that the only way through is on the ground, and I have to crawl on hands and knees to make it through. The light goes brighter, and brighter, and I push until I find myself standing in a small clearing in the brush, a hollowed out opening."
    new "Eventually, the gap grows so narrow that the only way through is on the ground, and I have to crawl on hands and knees to make it through. The light goes brighter, and brighter, and I push until I find myself standing in a small clearing in the brush, a hollowed out opening.\n最终，缺口变得极窄，唯一的通路只能贴着地面，我不得不手脚并用地爬过去。那光越来越亮，我一直向前，直到发现自己站在灌木中的一片小空地里，一个被掏空的开口处。"

    old "I crawl back out of the bramble the way I came, and soon I find myself back in the clearing with Vaeril and Kusho."
    new "I crawl back out of the bramble the way I came, and soon I find myself back in the clearing with Vaeril and Kusho.\n我沿着来时的路爬出荆棘，很快便回到了 Vaeril 和 Kusho 所在的那片空地。"

    old "Another smaller woodcrasher arrived while you were away, so we had to fight and kill it."
    new "Another smaller woodcrasher arrived while you were away, so we had to fight and kill it.\n你离开时，又有一头较小的 woodcrasher 来了，我们只得与它战斗并杀死了它。"

    old "I see. Glad you're both all right."
    new "I see. Glad you're both all right.\n明白了。很高兴你们俩都没事。"

    old "[protag], what did you see in there?"
    new "[protag], what did you see in there?\n[protag]，你在里面看到了什么？"

    old "What took you so long?"
    new "What took you so long?\n你怎么去了这么久？"

    old "I saw...vampires from N'Mar."
    new "I saw...vampires from N'Mar.\n我看到了……来自 N'Mar 的 Vampires。"

    old "What? Let's get ready to fight, then!"
    new "What? Let's get ready to fight, then!\n什么？那我们准备战斗吧！"

    old "They've already left, Kusho. And, as odd is it might seem, I don't think they mean us harm. In fact, one of them claimed to be on our side."
    new "They've already left, Kusho. And, as odd is it might seem, I don't think they mean us harm. In fact, one of them claimed to be on our side.\n他们已经走了，Kusho。而且，说来可能有些奇怪，我觉得他们无意伤害我们。事实上，其中一个还声称站在我们这边。"

    old "How could that be true?"
    new "How could that be true?\n那怎么可能是真的？"

    old "Some kind of vampire civil war, perhaps?"
    new "Some kind of vampire civil war, perhaps?\n也许是某种 Vampire 内战？"

    old "That may be the case. Then again, he may have been lying. I think the proof will come in the coming days and weeks."
    new "That may be the case. Then again, he may have been lying. I think the proof will come in the coming days and weeks.\n也许是这样。但话说回来，他也可能在撒谎。我想证据会在未来的几天、几周内见分晓。"

    old "The vampire claimed that he could dispel the corruption that has been seeping through the forest. That's why he came here."
    new "The vampire claimed that he could dispel the corruption that has been seeping through the forest. That's why he came here.\n那个 Vampire 声称自己能驱散一直在森林里渗透的腐化。这就是他来此的原因。"

    old "It sounds unbelievable. And yet..."
    new "It sounds unbelievable. And yet...\n听起来难以置信。然而……"

    old "I think I may have discovered the source of the magic that is corrupting the forest. And I think it may be at an end."
    new "I think I may have discovered the source of the magic that is corrupting the forest. And I think it may be at an end.\n我想我可能已经找到了腐蚀森林的魔法的源头。而且我想，它可能已经终结了。"

    old "Look."
    new "Look.\n看。"

    old "Vaeril points to the carcass of the woodcrasher we fought and defeated earlier. Its body seems to be dissolving, disintegrating."
    new "Vaeril points to the carcass of the woodcrasher we fought and defeated earlier. Its body seems to be dissolving, disintegrating.\nVaeril 指向我们先前战斗并击败的那头 woodcrasher 的尸体。它的身体似乎在溶解、崩解。"

    old "Vaeril points to the carcass of the woodcrasher they fought while I was away. Its body seems to be dissolving, disintegrating."
    new "Vaeril points to the carcass of the woodcrasher they fought while I was away. Its body seems to be dissolving, disintegrating.\nVaeril 指向我离开时他们战斗过的那头 woodcrasher 的尸体。它的身体似乎在溶解、崩解。"

    old "What is happening?"
    new "What is happening?\n发生什么了？"

    old "The woodcrasher carcass continues to deform, until all that remains is a pile of fine dust."
    new "The woodcrasher carcass continues to deform, until all that remains is a pile of fine dust.\n那头 woodcrasher 的尸体不断变形，直到最后只剩下一堆细尘。"

    old "Perhaps the corruption has already begun to subside. Whatever it was that fueled the spawning of these creatures is no more. And without the source of their very essence removed from the forest..."
    new "Perhaps the corruption has already begun to subside. Whatever it was that fueled the spawning of these creatures is no more. And without the source of their very essence removed from the forest...\n也许腐化已经开始消退了。无论是什么在滋养这些生物的滋生，如今都已不复存在。随着它们本质的源头从森林中消失……"

    old "The mass of bramble around us begins to shake, and I hear the sound of splintering and shattering around me. The bramble, the vines, the thorns...they all begin shattering around us."
    new "The mass of bramble around us begins to shake, and I hear the sound of splintering and shattering around me. The bramble, the vines, the thorns...they all begin shattering around us.\n我们周围的荆棘丛开始颤动，我听见四周传来断裂、碎裂的声响。荆棘、藤蔓、尖刺……它们开始在我们周围纷纷碎裂。"

    old "...is it over?"
    new "...is it over?\n……结束了吗？"

    old "It's incredible how quickly the dark magic that covered the land has been undone."
    new "It's incredible how quickly the dark magic that covered the land has been undone.\n覆盖这片土地的黑暗魔法，消散得如此之快，真是令人难以置信。"

    old "The magic itself may be ended. The woodcrashers, the bramble, and whatever spawned them may be gone. But to say that the dark work has been undone..."
    new "The magic itself may be ended. The woodcrashers, the bramble, and whatever spawned them may be gone. But to say that the dark work has been undone...\n魔法本身或许已经终结。woodcrashers、荆棘，以及滋生它们的一切，或许都已消失。但要说那黑暗的杰作已被彻底消除……"

    old "Vaeril looks at Kusho, and the two share a nod as they cast a forlorn gaze over the forest that surrounds us."
    new "Vaeril looks at Kusho, and the two share a nod as they cast a forlorn gaze over the forest that surrounds us.\nVaeril 看向 Kusho，两人点了点头，一起把哀伤的目光投向环绕我们的森林。"

    old "Trees that have stood for hundreds of years have been trampled down by those woodcrashers."
    new "Trees that have stood for hundreds of years have been trampled down by those woodcrashers.\n矗立了数百年的树木，已被那些 woodcrashers 践踏倒地。"

    old "The ground that was covered by this bramble...the life may be completely choked out of it. I wonder if another tree will ever grow on the ground we stand on."
    new "The ground that was covered by this bramble...the life may be completely choked out of it. I wonder if another tree will ever grow on the ground we stand on.\n被这荆棘覆盖过的土地……其中的生机可能已被彻底扼杀。我在想，我们脚下的这片地上，还能不能再长出树来。"

    old "The magic may be done. But the damage that has been done here will take years, decades, perhaps centuries to undo, if it can be undone at all."
    new "The magic may be done. But the damage that has been done here will take years, decades, perhaps centuries to undo, if it can be undone at all.\n魔法或许已经结束。但这里造成的损害，需要数年、数十年，甚至数个世纪才能修复——如果真能修复的话。"

    old "Still. Good has been done here."
    new "Still. Good has been done here.\n尽管如此。这里终究成就了善举。"

    old "Indeed."
    new "Indeed.\n确实。"

    old "Kusho turns to Vaeril and extends a hand. Vaeril looks at him with a surprised expression before taking the hand and shaking it."
    new "Kusho turns to Vaeril and extends a hand. Vaeril looks at him with a surprised expression before taking the hand and shaking it.\nKusho 转向 Vaeril，伸出一只手。Vaeril 带着惊讶的表情看着他，然后握住那只手握了握。"

    old "Vaeril, I owe you an apology. I hunted you down, believing that you were the source of the blight. That single-minded focus diverted my attention from the true root of the problem. Perhaps if I had acted sooner, the forest..."
    new "Vaeril, I owe you an apology. I hunted you down, believing that you were the source of the blight. That single-minded focus diverted my attention from the true root of the problem. Perhaps if I had acted sooner, the forest...\nVaeril，我欠你一个道歉。我追杀你，是相信你是那场枯萎之害的源头。那执迷的专注，让我偏离了问题的真正根源。也许如果我早点行动，森林……"

    old "What's done is done. We can't repair the damage that has been done to the forest. But..."
    new "What's done is done. We can't repair the damage that has been done to the forest. But...\n木已成舟。我们无法修复森林已经遭受的损害。但是……"

    old "But we can avenge it."
    new "But we can avenge it.\n但我们可以为它复仇。"

    old "[protag], you wanted my assistance in ridding the lands of N'Mar of the corruption of the undead. You said you wanted capable fighters. I think we may have found one."
    new "[protag], you wanted my assistance in ridding the lands of N'Mar of the corruption of the undead. You said you wanted capable fighters. I think we may have found one.\n[protag]，你想让我协助清除 N'Mar 土地的亡灵腐化。你说你需要能干的战士。我想我们也许找到了一位。"

    old "I hope I've been useful to you. And if I can continue to be useful to you, I'll gladly join you."
    new "I hope I've been useful to you. And if I can continue to be useful to you, I'll gladly join you.\n希望我对你有用。而如果我能继续对你有用，我会很乐意加入你们。"

    old "What do you think? I'd say this man has earned his freedom. Even if elves may frown upon his ways, I'd say we have a much greater menace to face. We need all the friends we can get."
    new "What do you think? I'd say this man has earned his freedom. Even if elves may frown upon his ways, I'd say we have a much greater menace to face. We need all the friends we can get.\n你觉得呢？要我说，这个人已经赢得了他的自由。即便 Elves 或许对他的行事方式不以为然，我想我们面前还有大得多的威胁。我们需要尽可能多的朋友。"

    old "Vaeril, it would be an honor to have you continue to travel and serve with us."
    new "Vaeril, it would be an honor to have you continue to travel and serve with us.\nVaeril，能让你继续与我们同行、效力，将是我的荣幸。"

    old "As Kusho said, the damage that has been done here cannot be undone. But we can make sure that something like this never happens again."
    new "As Kusho said, the damage that has been done here cannot be undone. But we can make sure that something like this never happens again.\n正如 Kusho 所说，这里已经造成的损害无法挽回。但我们可以确保，这样的事永不再发生。"

    old "Let us join forces, then. For the good of the forest. For the good of all of Aravorn."
    new "Let us join forces, then. For the good of the forest. For the good of all of Aravorn.\n那么，让我们联手吧。为了森林的福祉。为了整个 Aravorn 的福祉。"

    old "[protag], when we first met, you told me that you were infiltrating the castle of N'Mar. Something about fighting the undead. I told you that I found the offer intriguing, but at the time I was preoccupied with other things."
    new "[protag], when we first met, you told me that you were infiltrating the castle of N'Mar. Something about fighting the undead. I told you that I found the offer intriguing, but at the time I was preoccupied with other things.\n[protag]，我们初次见面时，你告诉我你正潜入 N'Mar 的城堡。是要对抗亡灵之类的事。我说过我觉得那提议很吸引人，但当时我正忙于别的事。"

    old "Now that I see Vaeril is not the source of the infestation of the forest, that has changed. I am free to join you in your mission. If the invitation is still open, I would like to accept it."
    new "Now that I see Vaeril is not the source of the infestation of the forest, that has changed. I am free to join you in your mission. If the invitation is still open, I would like to accept it.\n如今，看到 Vaeril 并非森林侵扰的源头，情况变了。我可以自由地加入你的使命。如果邀请仍然有效，我愿意接受。"

    old "We'd be glad to have you with us, Kusho."
    new "We'd be glad to have you with us, Kusho.\n能有你加入，我们很高兴，Kusho。"

    old "I must confess, at the time, that I considered the mission you described as a bit of an abstraction. An interesting diversion from my usual activities. But now...now I understand that something much greater is at stake."
    new "I must confess, at the time, that I considered the mission you described as a bit of an abstraction. An interesting diversion from my usual activities. But now...now I understand that something much greater is at stake.\n我必须承认，当时我把你描述的那项任务，看作有点抽象的事。一场从我日常活动中岔开的有趣消遣。但现在……现在我明白，事关重大得多。"

    old "Though this forest is miles away from the plains of N'Mar, its very fate may rest in your hands, and the hands of your companions. I count myself lucky to be among them."
    new "Though this forest is miles away from the plains of N'Mar, its very fate may rest in your hands, and the hands of your companions. I count myself lucky to be among them.\n虽然这片森林离 N'Mar 的平原远隔数里，但它的命运，也许就握在你和你同伴们的手中。我庆幸自己身在其中。"

    old "Now, let's get out of here and start slaying vampires, shall we?"
    new "Now, let's get out of here and start slaying vampires, shall we?\n那么，我们离开这里，开始猎杀 Vampires，好吗？"

    old "The night before the invasion, I try to force myself to stay up late. If I want to be awake and alert on the night of the full moon, then staying up late tonight, and forcing myself to get tomorrow's sleep during the morning or afternoon, seems like the best course of action."
    new "The night before the invasion, I try to force myself to stay up late. If I want to be awake and alert on the night of the full moon, then staying up late tonight, and forcing myself to get tomorrow's sleep during the morning or afternoon, seems like the best course of action.\n进攻前夜，我努力让自己熬夜。如果我想在满月之夜保持清醒警觉，那么今晚熬夜，强迫自己把明日的睡眠挪到上午或下午，似乎是最佳做法。"

    old "Grimoire is quiet tonight. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised."
    new "Grimoire is quiet tonight. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised.\n今晚的 Grimoire 很安静。我想我不该感到意外。"

    old "The townspeople seem to be increasingly aware of the danger that is coming the night of the full moon, and even if the vampires aren't expected tonight, something about the thought of vampires would be enough to scare most people into locking their doors at night and answering the door for no one."
    new "The townspeople seem to be increasingly aware of the danger that is coming the night of the full moon, and even if the vampires aren't expected tonight, something about the thought of vampires would be enough to scare most people into locking their doors at night and answering the door for no one.\n镇民们似乎越来越意识到满月之夜即将到来的危险，即便今晚并没有 Vampires 来袭的预期，但一想到 Vampires，就足以让大多数人夜里锁紧房门，谁也不给开门。"

    old "My guess is that most businesses shuttered early so that their owners could retire early, well in advance of dusk."
    new "My guess is that most businesses shuttered early so that their owners could retire early, well in advance of dusk.\n我猜大多数店铺都提前打烊了，好让店主们赶在天黑之前早早歇下。"

    old "I tread softly through the city streets. By now, my eyes have grown used to seeing the city in this slumbering, midnight state. Even though I know that doom looms on the horizon, something about seeing houses full of sleeping people puts me in a state of ease. "
    new "I tread softly through the city streets. By now, my eyes have grown used to seeing the city in this slumbering, midnight state. Even though I know that doom looms on the horizon, something about seeing houses full of sleeping people puts me in a state of ease. \n我轻轻走过城市街道。到如今，我的眼睛已习惯看这座城市沉睡的午夜模样。尽管我知道灾祸正逼近地平线，但看到一栋栋房子里睡满熟睡的人们，还是让我感到一种安心。"

